a5cc05d3-7989-490a-bce1-c7b270a44de4,,Steer AI Agents to Write Tests You Can Trust,"THIS IS A FREE, PRE-RECORDED TUTORIAL SERIES","**THIS IS A FREE, PRE-RECORDED TUTORIAL SERIES**
Please, find it here (https://shiftsync.tricentis.com/upskilling-tutorials-84/steer-ai-agents-to-write-tests-you-can-trust-2968?utm_source=ssnetwork&utm_medium=multi&utm_term=meetup_Ind&utm_content=Steer).

In this free upskill session, you will learn how to steer AI coding agents in Cursor to write, debug and maintain tests you can trust.

• **Work with your agent:** use chat, inline edits, the agents window and ask mode, and give the agent the right context to get reliable results.
• **Spot and fix hallucinations:** see why AI invents methods, selectors and root causes, and how to catch them before they reach your suite.
• **Set guardrails with rules and skills:** write AGENTS.md files, scoped rules and reusable skills, then evaluate whether they actually improve your agent's output.
• **Manage context and connect tools:** keep your context window lean, and choose between MCP servers and CLI tools for browser work.
• **Link tests to test management and CI:** sync your tests and results with Tricentis qTest through the qTest MCP Server, and turn a failed CI run into a reviewed pull request.

**Your instructor:**
***Filip Hric (https://www.linkedin.com/in/filip-hric/)****started his career by sharing what he learned about testing. And somehow it took off. His blog has surpassed 2 million reads, thousands of developers and testers have completed his courses, and he has become one of the names people reference in the world of testing and quality engineering.*
*Today he works as a DevRel at Qodo, helping development teams build quality directly into their process, speaks at conferences around the world, and strives to ensure that the AI era isn't something to fear for those who care about software that actually works. He lives in Slovakia with his wife and four children. He runs and plays guitar.*
