99b3ccce-d2ab-4ed7-9e91-6fe143d3b110,,"🌿 FREE SUNDAY PRE-LUNCH HIKE – Mole Gap Magic: River, Forest & Ancient Woods",🕙 Meeting Time: 10:00 a.m for a sharp 10:15 a.m start!,"🕙 **Meeting Time:** 10:00 a.m for a sharp 10:15 a.m start!
📍 **Start & Finish Point:** Outside Leatherhead Train Station (back exit next to car park / platform 2 exit)

📝 Overview

Join us for a scenic **up to 15 km circular hike** through the Surrey Hills, an Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty. This route offers a rich mix of landscapes — peaceful riverside paths, historic woodlands, rolling chalk downs, and vineyard views.

We’ll start from Leatherhead, following the **River Mole** through Mole Gap, cross into the picturesque hamlet of **Westhumble**, and loop across the open hills of **Norbury Park**. Expect sweeping countryside views, ancient woodlands, and plenty of fresh air.

🌟 Highlights

• Riverside walking along the **River Mole**.
• Pass by **Druids Grove**, with its ancient yew trees.
• Open landscapes of **Norbury Park** with stunning views of the Downs.
• A glimpse of the **Denbies Wine Estate**, one of England’s largest vineyards.

🥪 Break

We’ll aim to finish **before lunch**, but bring a small snack to enjoy mid-hike.

🥾 Difficulty

• Distance: ~up to 15 km
• Difficulty: ~Moderate – generally good paths, some uneven woodland, hills and chalky trails.

This hike is suitable for most fitness levels, but be prepared for a steady pace (medium to medium–fast). I always give breaks, wait for people to catch up, and make sure no one is left behind, so don't worry.

📌 What to Bring

• Comfortable hiking shoes with good grip.
• Water and light snacks.
• Weather-appropriate clothing (layers + waterproof if rain is forecast).
• A positive spirit — and don’t forget your best smile 😊

🚆 Travel

Leatherhead is easily accessible by train from London (about 45 min from London Waterloo or Victoria).

🍻 Post-Hike Social

Optional stop at a pub near Leatherhead station for a social drink and maybe a nice lunch, depending on what's on the menu.

⚠️ Important Notes

• Please stay with or behind the hike leader. This helps to manage group pace and cohesion.
• Participation is free, but you are responsible for your own safety and well-being. No risk/liability is inferred or accepted by the organiser.
• Please be mindful of others, respect the countryside, and keep the group spirit positive.
• Read the **About Us** section before joining:
👉 About Us (https://www.meetup.com/free-hiking-outdoor-fitness-and-social-activities/)

📲 **Contact:**
If you’re running late, lost, or need to reach me on the day, message/WhatsApp me at **07830 374 629**.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/7/f/d/b/highres_530492731.jpeg,2026-11-22 10:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Leatherhead station,"Station Approach, Surrey, KT22 7SQ",Leatherhead,c06699ed-62e0-4957-bcb4-080c5271da9a,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/free-hiking-outdoor-fitness-and-social-activities/events/317117359/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-26 03:22:56.772649+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/free-hiking-outdoor-fitness-and-social-activities/events/317117359/,event_317117359@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-26 03:22:56.772649+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.397771+00,,,,,f,GB
