cfbee1e4-03d5-4699-9e9b-e22fbc3cf817,,Woldingham circular walk - approx 13.5Miles - hilly/Strenuous,"Join us for a challenging but rewarding 13-mile circular hike starting and finishing at Woldingham station, taking in some of the finest scenery along the North Downs.","Join us for a challenging but rewarding 13-mile circular hike starting and finishing at Woldingham station, taking in some of the finest scenery along the North Downs.

This route combines steep climbs, rolling ridges, and sweeping valley views – perfect for those looking to stretch their legs and enjoy a good workout in the Surrey countryside. We’ll follow a mix of woodland trails, chalky downland paths, and open fields, with plenty of ups and downs along the way.

Highlights include:

Panoramic views across the North Downs escarpment.

Picturesque stretches through ancient woodland and quiet farmland.

There will be several steep ascents that will get the heart pumping – but worth it for the vistas at the top!

We’ll walk at a steady pace with breaks to catch our breath, take in the views, and stop for a packed lunch en route. Expect a full-day hike with a fair bit of elevation – good fitness and sturdy footwear are recommended.
This walk is not suitable for beginner hikers!!

Distance: 13.5 miles (24 km)
Terrain: Hilly, with steep ascents and descents, a mix of trails and tracks
Start/Finish: Woldingham station (easy access from London)
Duration: Approx. 6.5 hours including breaks

This is a sociable walk with plenty of opportunity to chat while enjoying the landscape. If you’re up for a bit of a challenge and some spectacular countryside, this hike is for you!

Meet at Woldingham rail station outside the station. I will join the train at Clapham junction so will meet you all at Woldingham.

Outward travel: Get the 09:21 train from London Bridge to Woldingham arr 09:55. Buy a day return ticket to Woldingham , the cost should be £9.35 with a groupsave or network railcard.

Walk starts at 10am from Woldingham station.

Walk ends at approx 16:30 at Woldingham station.

Please don't buy any tickets in advance in case I have to make changes to the schedule.

We will walk at a medium pace although the finish time may vary depending on the speed of the group.
We will do a pub stop around half way, might not have time to order food so bring a packed lunch/sandwiches.

*How to join?*
• The walk is entirely free of charge;
• You only arrange for your own travel and pub expenses;
• Understand our terms and conditions below (the ""IMPORTANT"" part);
• Understand how to stay safe outdoors, as you will be responsible for yourself. See our quick safety tips:
http://www.meetup.com/Free-Outdoor-Trips-From-London/about/
• Please answer the RSVP question; Guests with missing or incorrect answers will be removed from the list!

*What to bring*
• Plenty of water, 1-2 litres recommended
• Enough snacks and packed lunch to keep you energized along the walk
• Extra snacks and an extra packed lunch just in case
• Rainproof (ideally waterproof) clothing, sturdy shoes/boots you don't mind getting muddy
• Spare socks
• Walking poles and/or an umbrella :-)
• Yourself...
• ...and your camera!
• Cash for train ticket
• Cash for pub at the end of the walk?

Feel free to ask any questions in the comments section!

IMPORTANT
Please bear in mind this is a free of charge, self-guided trip with a hobby group. It is not organized by a business nor any entity with commercial purposes.
Any trip details, travel advice, route planning, instructions and other content in our group merely represent our shared personal knowledge, research and suggestions as outdoor enthusiasts. As this is no business, there is no ""product"", ""service"" or ""package"" and also no ""tour guide"", ""operator"" or ""walk leader"".
Each participant is responsible for their own safety. Even if some of us are very experienced walking outdoors, nobody assumes responsibility for any kind of injury, damage or loss that may happen.
Despite this, we take extreme precautions and all trips we plan are very safe, fun, highly educational and popular. Our experienced members volunteer their time and effort to shape a pleasant and quality adventure for everyone :-)
By participating you acknowledge and agree with this disclaimer.

Here are our tips on staying safe during outdoor trips:
http://www.meetup.com/Free-Outdoor-Trips-From-London/about/

TRAVEL, ACCOMMODATION, INSURANCE
Although we provide detailed suggestions, each participant is expected to arrange their own travel - this gives everyone the freedom and choice. Anyone interested in travel or outdoor insurance should also arrange this on their own. As mentioned above we always take extreme precautions, but some people may still feel safer if covered.
As most of our trips are confirmed or postponed very close to the event date - heavily depending on the weather forecasts - we advise not to buy this until the last minute. People getting tickets from the same station are encouraged to meet early on the day to benefit from discounts such as GroupSave.

Any questions, feel free to ask below or send a private message!",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/d/0/b/c/highres_530513436.jpeg,2026-11-22 09:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,London Bridge station,London Bridge station,London,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/free-outdoor-trips-from-london/events/317130056/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-27 03:22:58.978128+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/free-outdoor-trips-from-london/events/317130056/,event_317130056@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-27 03:22:58.978128+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.486349+00,,,,,f,GB
200b9878-5d42-49c3-9bb1-d873bb67fc58,,LEGO® SERIOUS PLAY® Online Live erleben,"Die meisten Online-Formate laufen gleich ab: Jemand teilt den Bildschirm, alle schauen zu, am Ende bleibt ein Chat voller Herzchen und keine einzige eigene Erkenntnis.","Die meisten Online-Formate laufen gleich ab: Jemand teilt den Bildschirm, alle schauen zu, am Ende bleibt ein Chat voller Herzchen und keine einzige eigene Erkenntnis.

Bei diesem Intro ist das anders. Du baust selbst mit, live vor der eigenen Kamera, mit LEGO-Steinen, die Du Dir vorher bereitlegst. LEGO SERIOUS PLAY dreht das übliche Prinzip um: Jede Person im Call bringt ihr Wissen ein, wird gehört und hat eine Stimme, nicht nur die lauteste im Raum.

Eine Stunde reicht nicht für eine Ausbildung. (🤫 2 Tage auch nicht!)

Aber für ein erstes echtes Gefühl.

Nach der Stunde weißt Du: Passt. Oder passt nicht.

**Spoileralarm:** LEGO SERIOUS PLAY ist keine Spielerei. Die Methode wird seit über 20 Jahren in Unternehmen weltweit eingesetzt und hat dazu beigetragen, dass LEGO noch existiert.

📅 **Wann:** Dienstag, 03. November 2026, 18:30 bis 19:30 Uhr
💻 **Wo:** Online via Zoom

**Was Du brauchst**
👉 Zwei Handvoll LEGO-Steine, mehr nicht. Kein Set, keine Anleitung, keine Vorkenntnisse.

**Was Dich erwartet**

• Ankommen und kurzer Rahmen
• Interaktiver LEGO SERIOUS PLAY Workshop, live und gemeinsam, für ein echtes Gefühl für die Methode
• Offener Austausch und Raum für Fragen

**Für wen ist dieses Meetup?**

• Für Führungskräfte und Entscheider:innen, wenn Meetings Energie kosten statt Klarheit schaffen.
• Für Coaches und Trainer:innen, wenn ein Thema zu heiß oder zu komplex für Diskussion ist.
• Für Change- und HR-Verantwortliche, wenn auf die Frage nach Bedenken im Projekt nur Schweigen kommt.

**Anmeldung**
Die Plätze sind begrenzt. Melde Dich hier für den Zoom-Call an:
https://us06web.zoom.us/meeting/register/rcMoj46OQZeb98cK7zy_Cg

**Dein Trainer: Matthias Renner**
Matthias Renner arbeitet seit über 10 Jahren mit LEGO SERIOUS PLAY, mit Unternehmen, Behörden und NGOs in Europa, Nord- und Zentralamerika. Er ist seit 2016 zertifiziert und der einzige autorisierte Trainer in Deutschland für das offizielle Foundation Training der Association of Master Trainers. Er wurde direkt von den Entwicklern der Methode, Robert Rasmussen und Per Kristiansen, ausgebildet. Er ist Co-Autor von zwei Fachbüchern zu LEGO SERIOUS PLAY, erschienen bei Springer und Dunod.

