77a0bcf1-54a6-42f4-b78b-80f081957611,,The Artist’s Way – Free Weekly Online Support Group & Book Club for Creatives,"Hi everyone,","Hi everyone,

Thank you for being part of the Playmakers journey — whether you’re brand new or you’ve been with us already, we appreciate you.

Playmakers is a creative community built around one simple idea: play isn’t just for children — it’s a powerful way for adults to connect, recharge, and grow. Over time, we’ll be hosting in-person workshops and events that blend theatre, movement, games, music, writing, and other creative activities to help people develop skills and build community.
For now, we’re keeping things simple.

As a low-barrier entry point into the Playmakers space, we’re running a free weekly online workshop. (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf9mHEnC3L9PpeMpaRVcsNqQ6EpVR7Bb7HJb8OV1UlGrFIhSg/viewform?usp=dialog) It’s a creative book-club-style group centred around *The Artist’s Way*, where we explore ideas together, share reflections, and gently challenge ourselves in a supportive environment.
Each session stands on its own, so you can join at any point in the year. It doesn’t matter how far we are in the book — there’s no catching up required. Just come as you are and start where we are.
It’s relaxed, welcoming, and you can engage at your own pace. No pressure — just curiosity, creativity, and connection.

**New here?** You can find all the details and sign up via This link - Book Club Sign up Form (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf9mHEnC3L9PpeMpaRVcsNqQ6EpVR7Bb7HJb8OV1UlGrFIhSg/viewform?usp=dialog) (you’ll receive the Google Meet link after submitting)

**Returning?** You don’t need to fill the form again — just join using the usual link you’ve already received or keep an eye out for our weekly emails.

**Quick favour:** even if you’re a regular, please hit **Attend / RSVP**. It helps the Meetup algorithm push the event to more people and grow the community

**Event details**
**Sundays | 10:30–11:30am**
**Platform:** Google Meet
**What to bring:** something to write with (notebook + pen or Notes app)

For any questions or further info, hit me up at **Taurean@theplaymakersproject.com**.
Looking forward to building this with you.

— Taurean

The Playmakers Project",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792984815/orbit/event-covers/sources/oabswdi65dy9p5ql41d3.jpg,2026-12-13 10:30:00+00,2026-12-13 12:00:00+00,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,books,creative,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/playmakers-play-creativity-community/events/317144666/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/playmakers-play-creativity-community/events/317144666/,event_317144666@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,meetup:playmakers-play-creativity-community:the artist s way free weekly online support group book club for creatives,"Every week on Sunday until February 14, 2027",f,
94acdc4f-73ab-4dce-a6d6-138279a0a699,,🎃 Seven Sisters Spooky Stroll,Hike the Iconic Seven Sisters Cliffs with Me!,"**Hike the Iconic Seven Sisters Cliffs with Me!**

Looking for the ultimate day adventure from London? Join me for a 20km coastal hike along the breathtaking Seven Sisters Cliffs -one of the most spectacular walks in the UK.

Picture this: rolling white chalk cliffs, sweeping sea views, lunch at the dreamy Cuckmere Haven, and fish & chips in Eastbourne to finish. I’ve done this hike six times and it never gets old — it’s pure magic when the weather’s right.

Route: Seaford to Eastbourne
Guide Fee: £15
Tickets: Please purchase an off-peak return ticket from London Bridge to Eastbourne (approx. 1.5-hour journey). Prices are around £25 with a Railcard.

Distance: Approximately 22 km (hilly terrain), with two short breaks planned.

Travel options:

• Train (recommended): Return ticket to Eastbourne
• Alternative: Travel via ground transport or drive

Whether you’re craving fresh air, stunning views, or just a really good reason to get outside — this is the hike for you.

DM me to join or ask questions! Limited spots. Let’s go cliffside 🌿☀️

#SevenSistersHike #DayTripFromLondon #HikingUK #CoastalAdventure #NatureFix #GetOutside #GroupHike",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/d/f/8/highres_528340440.jpeg,2026-10-31 08:30:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,"London Bridge, London, SE1",London Bridge,London,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/thenikoutcollective/events/317128373/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-27 03:22:58.978128+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/thenikoutcollective/events/317128373/,event_317128373@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-27 03:22:58.978128+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.486349+00,,,,,f,GB
