59bea00b-422f-4612-96ab-c6bb763fd7e1,,"Fit and Happy Indoors- Healthy heart, lungs and body- online Class","Even if you cannot join our outdoor classes,I still want to help you stay motivated, happy, strong, fit and healthy.","Even if you cannot join our outdoor classes,I still want to help you stay motivated, happy, strong, fit and healthy.

We are now leading some walks, but we still have several classes per week online, using Zoom.

When you join us live, you can get my encouragement, and you can see and chat with the others, almost as if we are in the same room. And we can stick around for a chat after the session.

What you need for this session:
• ca 1.5x1.5 meter space to move around.
• tablet, laptop or computer screen with internet connection
• two waterbottles, cans or small hand weights
• straight kitchen or dining room chair without armrests.

Session Price: £10 per session, £100 for a 10-session card or £70 unlimited sessions per month. Session cards and pay Monthly can be used in any of our outdoor walks or indoor Zoom classes sessions (except for the Parkinson's sessions).

Pay What Works:
The price shown above is the “true” value of the session that best reflects the work I put into preparing and leading your session. However, I understand that not everyone can afford to pay full price, and I don’t want that to stop you from joining us.

In an effort to find a balance between more financial accessibility and sustainable pricing, I now offer a “Pay What Works” model. This allows for financial flexibility while still valuing and respecting the work and energy I provide in creating and delivering these classes.

Then send an email to ailien@fitandhappyoutdoors.com with the heading “INVOICE please”- followed by “FAHO 1” to pay full price as quoted below, “FAHO 2”, for 20% off, or “FAHO 3” for 50% off.

Please do tell me if you want to pay for 10 sessions, or if you’d like to pay monthly.
I prefer payment by bank transfer, but if that is not possible you could pay in cash. No cheques please, the queues by the banks are just too long.

Once you sign up for this class, I will send you a message with the links and passwords you need.

Never used Zoom before? A bit of a technophobe? Get in touch before your first class and I will be happy to talk you through it!",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/e/7/2/highres_490124658.jpeg,2027-01-13 09:30:00+00,2027-01-13 10:30:00+00,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/fit-and-happy-outdoors/events/trwwstykccbrb/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-25 03:22:59.993096+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/fit-and-happy-outdoors/events/trwwstykccbrb/,event_trwwstykccbrb@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-25 03:22:59.993096+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.486349+00,,,meetup:fit-and-happy-outdoors:fit and happy indoors healthy heart lungs and body online class,Every week on Wednesday,f,
895bf941-d05b-43e7-8c22-3586e59f268e,,From Bot to Business App — The UiPath Coded Apps Story,"In this session, we will cover:","In this session, we will cover:

🔹 What are UiPath Coded Apps? Understand Coded Apps, how they work, and where they fit into the UiPath automation ecosystem.

🔹 Where Can Coded Apps Be Used? Explore practical scenarios where Coded Apps can provide a better experience for users and complement traditional RPA and automation solutions.

🔹 Live Demo: Build a real-world Coded App from scratch and see how it can interact with UiPath automations, data, and business processes.

🔹 Build It Yourself: Walk through the key steps involved in creating a Coded App, including designing the app, adding logic, connecting to resources, and making it available to users.

Who should attend: UiPath Developers, RPA Professionals, Automation Engineers, Technical Leads, Solution Architects, and anyone interested in building modern applications with UiPath.

Prerequisite: Basic UiPath knowledge is helpful, along with some familiarity with programming concepts, but no prior Coded Apps experience is required.

👉 Join us and discover how UiPath Coded Apps can help you turn automation capabilities into powerful, user-friendly applications.",,2026-10-22 13:30:00+00,,Asia/Kolkata,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,{technology},,external,https://www.meetup.com/agentic-ai-community-pune/events/316896840/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 03:22:46.934486+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/agentic-ai-community-pune/events/316896840/,event_316896840@meetup.com,,2026-10-22 03:22:12.257+00,,2026-10-22 03:22:46.934486+00,2026-10-22 03:22:46.934486+00,,,,,f,
8be97f45-9020-45c3-a9ea-df81e8346bd1,,"Badminton 1-4pm, £9.00 Per Person. Regarding Car Park charge Please read below","We accommodate intermediate and advance badminton players and also beginners, (Please message us if you are a beginner).","We accommodate intermediate and advance badminton players and also beginners, (Please message us if you are a beginner).
We also accommodate single players who want to play Singles badminton games. Singles is an option if there is a spare badminton court and the opponent is willing to have a singles game.

**We are just an 8-minute drive from Hounslow Middlesex Badminton Dome.**

**Details how to get to the badminton club by Public Transport are at the bottom.**

• a). £9.00 Per Person Pay & Play - Cash Payment Only.
• b). Time: 1:00pm - 4:00pm
• c). Please bring your own water.
• d). 3 Badminton Courts every week - **Depending on numbers attending we can increase or decrease the badminton courts, (To book more badminton courts we must know by Tuesday evening how many members are attending. Please RSVP early).**
• *e). Feather shuttlecocks are provided by the club.* **(PLEASE NOTE: We do not use plastic shuttlecocks because potentially plastic shuttlecocks could give you a tennis elbow).***
• f). **Venue Address:**
Cranford Community College Sports Hall,
High Street, Cranford, TW5 9PD
• g). Please RSVP if you are attending the Badminton Club
• h). Please ensure that you update your RSVP status ASAP if for any reason you are unable to attend the badminton club so the next member on the wait list can attend. **(If you cancel your RSVP last minute, we will not charge you).**

If for any reason you cannot RSVP on meetup. Please send Harry a text on 0771 182 4977 with your name to state you will be attending badminton and you will be added as a guest on meetup.

• ***CAR PARKING CHARGE*** at the school for the whole day is £2.90 **- Evology App** - PAY FOR PARKING BY PHONE. Please download Evology App onto your phone and make payment through this app. Instructions for this are at the car park and outside the school reception area.
• There is a 20-minute grace period for drops offs and pick before the charge applies.
• Street parking is free outside the school or on Brabazon Road, Heston, TW5 9LP, which is a 10-minute walk to the venue.
• If the car park is full, - You can park for free on the following road: - Brabazon Road, Heston, TW5 9LP. (**Don’t forget the 20-minute grace period to exit the car park).**

*Heathrow Spidernets Badminton Kit is available to buy from the following website: **www.pbteamwear.co.uk*** (http://www.pbteamwear.co.uk%2A%2A%2A/)

Heathrow Spidernets Badminton Club takes No Responsibility and will not be responsible for any personnel injuries, damage or loss of property.

Members will be responsible and are required to be members of Badminton England for insurance purposes. Website: www.badmintonengland.co.uk (http://www.badmintonengland.co.uk/)

**Transport:**
***Cars:***
There is a large Car Park, Car Parking charge at the school is £2.90 for the day - **Evology App** - PAY FOR PARKING BY PHONE.
Drive through the Blue gates up to the barrier which will then open automatically. **If the car park is full**,
Park Free on the following road: Brabazon Road, Heston, TW5 9LP.(Remember there is a 20 minute grace period to exit the car park).

***Buses:***
***105***, **H28** - will drop you outside Cranford Community College in Cranford
***111*** - will drop you outside The Queens Head Pub, Cranford go towards the mini roundabout when you come off the bus, it is a 2 minute walk.

***81, 222, H98*** - from Bath Road, Cranford
10-15 Minute walk from the Bath Road.
Come off the bus on the Bath Road in Cranford outside DoubleTree Hotel or Ibis Budget Hotel.
At the traffic lights go down the road called **'The Avenue'** walk to the end of the road. Mini roundabout take a right, walk straight down cross the road at the traffic lights or take the footbridge to cross the road. Then carry on straight down and you will see The Queens Head Pub on your right carry on straight down to the mini roundabout. Then carry on straight down and you will approach a blue fence on your left, go to the end of the blue fence and entrance to the school is on your left before the mini roundabout and bridge.

**285 Bus from Feltham to Cranford Community College**
Take 285 bus from Feltham Station towards Heathrow Airport. Get off at Harlington Corner. Take the 105 bus heading towards Greenford Station or 111 bus heading towards Kingston from outside Best Western Hotel/Marriott-Court Yard Hotel. 105 bus will drop you outside the school. 111 bus will drop you outside the Queens Head Pub which is a 2 minute walk to the school.

***Underground:***
Take the Piccadilly line to Hounslow East Station.
Outside Hounslow East Underground station take the*** 111 Bus*** heading towards Heathrow Airport come off the bus in Cranford outside Queens Head Pub go towards the mini roundabout when you come off the bus, from there it is a 2 Minute walk to Cranford Community College Sports Hall.

**Elizabeth Line:**
Take the Elizabeth Line to **Hayes & Harlington Station**.
