cea3b0e5-c275-470f-95eb-c87113f7d422,,"AIDataTech Connect: Global Virtual Networking Event for AI, Data & Tech Pros","Are you working in artificial intelligence, data science, or machine learning? Whether you're a developer, researcher, startup founder, or aspiring tech enthusiast — AIDataTech Connect is your go-to…","Are you working in artificial intelligence, data science, or machine learning? Whether you're a developer, researcher, startup founder, or aspiring tech enthusiast — **AIDataTech Connect** is your go-to **AI networking event online** designed to foster career growth, real-time collaboration, and innovation exchange in a dynamic, community-driven environment.

This event brings together a global **virtual AI community meetup** hosted on a flexible Slack-style platform that supports group discussions and **1-1 video or text chats**, making it perfect for professionals looking to connect, collaborate, and build with others in the AI ecosystem.

🎥 **Watch how it works:**
👉 https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NRUTXUOFKm4

**💬 What to Expect:**
At AIDataTech Connect, attendees are encouraged to explore, share, and engage across multiple interactive channels designed to support learning, networking, and opportunity discovery:

• **General** – A central hub for orientation, announcements, and community-wide discussions.
• **Intros** – Introduce yourself, your background, and your AI/tech journey. Spark meaningful introductions.
• **Networking** – Share your resume, startup, or project pitch. Meet employers, peers, or collaborators.
• **Help Wanted** – Ask for help or offer support on coding, data, research, or AI model deployment.
• **Industry Room Tech** – Discuss AI frameworks, tools, and the latest tech trends in data and development.
• **Project Showcase** – Perfect for those seeking a **machine learning career fair** experience or showcasing real-world work through our **AI project showcase platform**.
• **Collaboration Pods** – Jump into discussions around **collaboration for AI specialists**, including open-source partnerships, research pods, and co-building opportunities.

**📍 Where:**
Join virtually at:
👉 https://events.tao.ai/pod/ai.bharath.club/q4j5imq9qjs9
**🕔 When:**
Event runs globally from **5:00 PM – 7:00 PM local time** — designed for participation across time zones.

**👥 Who Should Join:**

• AI professionals, ML engineers, and data scientists
• Tech founders, entrepreneurs, and product leaders
• Students, job seekers, and aspiring AI talent
• Recruiters, employers, and hiring managers in AI/tech
• Researchers, open-source contributors, and peer mentors

**🧠 Why Attend:**

• Engage in a truly global **virtual tech networking event**
• Discover AI jobs, freelance gigs, or partnership opportunities
• Connect with experts and peers in AI, ML, and data
• Explore AI applications and get feedback on your models or tools
• Network directly via 1-on-1 video or text chats
• Collaborate on new ideas, research papers, or open-source projects

**❓ Questions or Suggestions?**
We’re here to help. Drop us a note at:
👉 https://noworkerleftbehind.org/event_support

**🔖 Hashtags:**
#AIDataTechConnect #AINetworkingEventOnline #VirtualAICommunityMeetup #MachineLearningCareerFair #AIProjectShowcasePlatform #CollaborationForAISpecialists #DataScienceMeetup #MLJobs #AIResearchNetworking #GlobalTechNetworking #TechCollaborationEvent",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/6/f/e/highres_526205886.jpeg,2026-10-22 11:30:00+00,2026-10-22 13:30:00+00,Asia/Kolkata,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,careers,ai,entrepreneurship}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/ai-blr/events/316255457/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 03:22:46.934486+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/ai-blr/events/316255457/,event_316255457@meetup.com,,2026-10-22 03:22:12.257+00,,2026-10-22 03:22:46.934486+00,2026-10-22 17:09:36.380806+00,,,meetup:ai-blr:aidatatech connect global virtual networking event for ai data tech pros,"Every 4th Thursday of the month until December 24, 2026",f,
d8f353ab-3dfb-438c-b7dd-b4460de8cd31,,🌙✨ Nightly Journaling Circle✨,🌙✨ Nightly Journaling Circle | Online | 9 PM – 10 PM,"🌙✨ **Nightly Journaling Circle | Online | 9 PM – 10 PM**

Looking for a peaceful way to end your day? Join us every evening for a cozy online journaling session where we pause, reflect, and set intentions for a better tomorrow.

From **9:00 PM to 10:00 PM**, we'll spend time writing down our thoughts, practicing gratitude, and sharing general reflections in a warm, supportive, and judgment-free space. Whether you're celebrating small wins, processing your day, or simply seeking calm, you're welcome here.

💛 **What to expect:**
• Guided journaling prompts
• Quiet reflection time
• Optional sharing and meaningful conversations
• A positive and supportive community
• Small daily habits for personal growth and well-being

📖 **Bring along:**
• A journal or notebook
• A pen
• An open heart and mind

No writing experience is needed—just come as you are.

**Because healing, self-discovery, and growth happen one page at a time.** 🌿✨

*""Write your thoughts today, create a better tomorrow.""*

*# Journaling Session Ground Rules*

*To create a safe, focused, and meaningful space for everyone, please keep these guidelines in mind:*

1. **This is a journaling-focused session.** *Please keep all discussions related to the prompts and personal reflections from today's session.*

2. **No work or workplace discussions.** *This is a space to disconnect from work and reconnect with yourself. Please avoid conversations about your job, colleagues, office, or workplace situations.*

3. **Respect everyone's time.** *Stay on topic and avoid side conversations so we can make the most of our time together.*

4. **No unrelated subjects.** *Please refrain from discussing politics, current affairs, gossip, business, or other topics unrelated to the journaling experience.*

5. **Share with kindness, not advice.** *If participants choose to share, listen with empathy. Avoid giving unsolicited advice or trying to solve someone else's experiences.*

6. **Confidentiality matters.** *What is shared in this session stays in this session. Please respect everyone's privacy.*

7. **Share only what feels comfortable.** *There is no pressure to speak. You're welcome to simply journal and listen.*

8. **Be present.** *Silence your notifications, minimize distractions, and give yourself this hour to reflect and be fully engaged.*",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792620962/orbit/event-covers/sources/cuebbhsi72crkdo488pv.jpg,2026-10-26 17:00:00+00,2026-10-26 18:00:00+00,Asia/Dubai,online,Online event,,,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,wellbeing,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/dlrc-walk-and-talk/events/316871072/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:15:29.416216+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/dlrc-walk-and-talk/events/316871072/,event_316871072@meetup.com,,2026-10-22 03:21:50.591+00,,2026-10-21 22:15:29.416216+00,2026-10-22 03:22:11.100007+00,,,meetup:dlrc-walk-and-talk:nightly journaling circle,Every week on every day,f,
