68489784-2168-4ccd-8ff4-66ad16a3c96b,,Socratic Seminar #54,"Join us for the next London BitDevs Socratic Seminar! We'll be covering the latest research, ideas, and developments in Bitcoin and related protocols. This is a highly interactive evening where…","Join us for the next London BitDevs Socratic Seminar! We'll be covering the latest research, ideas, and developments in Bitcoin and related protocols. This is a highly interactive evening where participants are encouraged to share their insights, ask questions, and collaborate.

**We've moved!** This seminar is taking place at Antidote (https://antidotebtc.com/), instead of our usual location in Westminster.

What to Expect

Our discussions are technical, and we don't shy away from diving into the nitty-gritty details. However, each topic will be briefly introduced for those less familiar with the subject matter.
Whether you're an experienced contributor or simply curious to learn more, you're welcome to join the conversation. As long as you have a basic understanding of how Bitcoin works, you'll find something interesting to take home.

Topics & Suggestions

We will announce the final discussion topics shortly before the event on londonbitdevs.org (https://londonbitdevs.org/). If you have a specific topic you'd like to dive into, please leave a comment on the appropriate pull request in our GitHub repo (https://github.com/londonbitdevs/londonbitdevs-website).

Event Details

• Doors Open: 18:40
• Seminar Starts: 19:00
• Late Entry Cutoff: 19:10 *(We cannot let you in after this time, so please arrive promptly!)*
• Scheduled End Time: 21:00
• 📍 Venue: The Bindery, 51-53 Hatton Garden, London EC1N 8HN

Rules

• We enforce a strict no-photo and no-video policy and adhere to Chatham House Rule (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chatham_House_Rule), to ensure everyone feels comfortable to attend and speak freely.
• This is a technical, Bitcoin only event. Other projects and non-technical topics are not discussed.

