e6cb5544-5d7f-4008-8e04-2f8123e98f86,,"Cambridge and Grantchester, In the Footsteps of Poets, Beginner Hike","Join our friendly group for a walk from Cambridge to Grantchester and return, a classic, scenic riverside hike that follows the River Cam through open green spaces and quiet nature reserves.","Join our friendly group for a walk from Cambridge to Grantchester and return, a **classic, scenic riverside** hike that follows the River Cam through open green spaces and quiet nature reserves.
This walk starts with a **City Centre** tour of the **University Colleges**, before leading past historic **punting spots**, and into **Coe Fen and Sheep's Green** where cattle and sheep often graze right next to the water.
We follow the meandering **River Cam** to **Grantchester Meadows**. A wide, open expanse of grass framed by weeping willows, famous for inspiring **Pink Floyd**'s song ""Grantchester Meadows"" and **Poets Lord Byron, Ted Hughes, Silvia Plath and Rupert Brooke.**
We arrive at **Grantchester Village**, a postcard-pretty English village featuring thatched-roof cottages and the 12th-century Church of St Andrew and St Mary.
Here we will have time to visit the **Orchard Tea Garden,** established in 1897, this historic tea room lets you sit under apple trees for **coffee, tea, and scones** - following in the footsteps of famous historical figures like Rupert Brooke, **Virginia Woolf, E.M. Forster**.
After lunch we make our way back through the meadows to Cambridge. There you can join the group for a drink at a local pub, or take a train directly back to London.

**GRADE**: Beginner, 14km
3.30hrs walking time not including breaks.
Flat. Pavement, footpaths, grass meadows, and riverside towpaths. Can be muddy after rain.
**PACE**: Social with regular breaks
**MEETING TIME**: 08:55 at London Kings Cross Station. By the ticket machines near platforms 9-11.
**TRAINS**: 09:24 From London Kings Cross to Cambridge, arriving 10:14, journey time 50 mins.
Train tickets are not included and are available on the day or in advance.
**TICKETS**: Super off-peak day return ticket to Cambridge. Group save tickets can be bought with 3-9 together from the ticket machines.
**WALK STARTS**: 10:15 at Cambridge station
**LUNCH**: Packed lunch
**WALK FINISHES**: approx 15:30 at Cambridge Station. Trains to London Kings Cross every 30mins at .42 and .12, journey time 51mins.
**HIKE LEADER:** Natalie
**ADDITIONAL INFO:** n/a

**What to Bring**
Full kit list- Click Here (https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FLjSAczjgbZ26OKE4Iy_zX2IFqkybdXCmK9AkVfqI1w/edit?usp=sharing)
✅ Hiking boots or sturdy shoes
✅ Suitable clothing and layers for changing weather
✅ Packed lunch, snacks and water
✅ Train ticket
Stay Connected
📱 WhatsApp: 07968585224
📩 Mailing List: https://www.golondonhiking.co.uk/contact
🌐 Website: https://www.golondonhiking.co.uk (https://www.golondonhiking.co.uk/)
📸 Instagram: https://www.instagram.com/golondonhiking/
👍 Facebook Page: https://www.facebook.com/GoLondonAdventure/

