adbc0216-9560-44c9-80d5-5aa330f0b2c0,,#5 - semiotics ideation worskhop,Meet likeminded UX professionals and experience a new way to ideate with a researcher at UAL.,"**Meet likeminded UX professionals and experience a new way to ideate with a researcher at UAL.**

Our next event is a bit different - one of our members, Mary, is working on her thesis project for UAL's MA in User Experience Design and is hosting a session at the university for us to try it out.

She's built a card-based ideation method that uses visual symbolism and semiotics to trigger unexpected ideas - almost like tarot meets design thinking!

There's also a custom AI agent she's developed that plays the role of an ""idea psychic,"" helping you reframe problems and push past obvious solutions.

She needs people to use it on a real brief so she can observe what works and what doesn't. You’ll get to try an unusual creative method and help shape a member’s research project, while also having the opportunity to meet and spend time discussing with other creatives.

**The Details:**

• **Location:** London College of Communication (UAL), Elephant & Castle, London SE1 6SB
• **Capacity:** We’re keeping this to a small group to ensure everyone can connect and contribute. Please ensure your RSVP is up to date and let us know if you're unable to attend.
• **What to bring:** **Bring some ID on the day for entry to UAL.**
• **Vibe:** Friendly and relaxed!

**Why Join?**
If you’re a designer or researcher who wants to use your skills for more than just conversion, come say hi.
It’s a chance to meet like-minded people and consider how design can solve universal human problems.

**Who is this for?**
Our events are for UX designers, researchers and other strategic and creative thinkers who are passionate about using their skills for social good, not just profit. Please note that this is not a networking event, or a place to find a job.

**Who are the hosts?**

Mary is a UX designer from Iran, currently based in London pursuing her masters in Experience Design at UAL.

Max is a London based design researcher. Until recently he was based in Tokyo, where he ran a small design agency and spent over 10 years as a meetup organizer. He's exploring ways to bring designers together to use our skills to work on meaningful problems.

