594cff7d-5f8b-4ab3-b26e-016ba4340dec,,Securing Kubernetes Cluster with Kubescape,🔐 Kubernetes Security: A Practical Look at Kubescape,"**🔐 Kubernetes Security: A Practical Look at Kubescape**
Kubernetes helps teams build flexible and scalable infrastructure, but it also introduces new security challenges. How can you identify vulnerabilities and misconfigurations and systematically strengthen the security of your Kubernetes workloads?

**📅 On October 27,** join us to explore Kubescape — an open-source tool from the CNCF ecosystem for auditing, monitoring, and strengthening Kubernetes security.

**🎤 Maxat Akbanov (https://www.linkedin.com/in/maxat-a-970770151/),** a DevOps Engineer at Magnum Cash & Carry Kazakhstan, will share his hands-on experience with Kubescape and discuss:
🔹 how to audit a Kubernetes cluster
🔹 how to identify misconfigurations and vulnerabilities
🔹 what to consider when integrating the tool
🔹 what value Kubescape can bring to your team and organization

**🔗 Register here (https://people-andersenlab.com/events/kubernetes-security?utm_source=meetup.com&utm_medium=meetup&utm_campaign=2710)**
Registration is required to attend the event. Please register via the website to receive the event details.

**Event details:**
**⏰ Time: 16:00 (CET)**
**🕒 Duration: 1 hour**
**🗣️ Language: English**
