e555e595-6c21-40a8-bb48-dce4df00069e,,"The Thames Path, Part 4. (14 Miles/22KM)",Do this walk because - its a great way to see the River Thames and follow its flow from the beautiful Cotswolds towards London.,"**Do this walk because** - its a great way to see the River Thames and follow its flow from the beautiful Cotswolds towards London.

We plan to complete the 292 km distance in about 20 single-day walks over a 24 month period. Estimated completion is May 2028.

We're doing this hike with Variety is the Spice (https://www.meetup.com/variety-is-the-spice-meetup-group/) Meetup group. Carl R will lead the walk.

**Walk facts (Stage 4)**
**Form:** Linear walk from Newbridge to Oxford.
**Distance:** Approximately 14 miles / 22km
**Duration:** Walking time circa 5.5 hours.
**Grade:** Easy. During wet weather the paths can become muddy.
**Donation to GOSH (https://www.gosh.org/):** £5 cash on the day.
**What to take**: A packed lunch and plenty of water.
**Also, we're not insured, so please have your own insurance for this type of activity.**

**Walk Description**
Our route will generally follow the Thames Path. We will be walking in the direction of flow of the River Thames.

**Meeting at**
Outside The Rose Revived (https://www.chefandbrewer.com/pubs/oxfordshire/rose-revived) pub, Newbridge.
We'll be outside The Rose Revived at 10:45am.
We'll start walking at 10:50am.

**Travel to the start of the walk**
The start location for this walk is very difficult to get to with public transport.
It may be possible to join Carl at Reading and travel by car to the start of the walk (subject to space in the car). Please contact Carl if you’d like a lift.
A £5 donation is requested for the return journey to help cover costs (this is separate to your walk donation to GOSH).

**Travel home after the walk**
Public transport options from Oxford are quite good.

**KEY INFORMATION**
YOU MUST READ THE THREE SECTIONS BELOW - if you join this trip, you're confirming that you have.

1. The perilous bit (https://1drv.ms/w/s!Amm1USRcx4vIguYmnugrVTjSPTyGAQ?e=KEtxLW)
2. Our FAQs (https://1drv.ms/w/s!Amm1USRcx4vIguYnTkTcg0qmj9tSzw?e=RtfXnP), including an explanation of Group save tickets which will save you money.
3. See here for what to wear and take (https://1drv.ms/w/s!Amm1USRcx4vIguYkeUPX7cpM0ZrmIA?e=Bn1d7g). Specifically make sure you bring good hiking boots and that you are ready for muddy conditions . Please - no trainers, they are not suitable for walking in the wintry muddy conditions.

**AND FINALLY**

• We're raising money for Great Ormond Street Hospital for Children (https://www.gosh.org/)

We’ll deduct Meetup fees but all the profits will go to GOSH. After each hike, we’ll let you know exactly how much we’ve all raised. And if you’d like to join us and raise money by leading some hikes, please get in touch – the more the merrier 😊",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/6/0/b/highres_534849739.jpeg,2026-10-31 10:45:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,,,,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/hike-for-charity/events/316196492/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/hike-for-charity/events/316196492/,event_316196492@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.486349+00,,,,,f,
