998cb187-02fb-46c2-965a-69e063b3c2aa,,Meetup #19 - The Agentic Web Explained,"Shaping our future with AI. Creating opportunity through AI fluency, connection and community.","Shaping our future with AI. Creating opportunity through AI fluency, connection and community.
No jargon. No hype. No confusing terminology.

**Join us for our next in-person meetup in London on Tuesday 27th October.**

The theme of this meetup is **""Building awesome agents""** and we're thrilled to have Tara Ojo Agyemang from Google joining us to explain the Agentic Web and the role of WebMCP.

Tara is followed by Nick Ferrel who is hands on building Agentic solutions are Focused. Nick isn't going to show us a magical ""hello world"" of building agents, instead he's going to talk about the final 10%, the important overlooked work that takes a great demo and makes it a production ready product.

**Where and When?**

• Tuesday, October 27th
• Doors open at 18:00
• Talks start at 19:00
• AutogenAI, 123 Pentonville Rd, London N1 9LG

**Talk 1: Building For The Agentic Web With WebMCP**

AI agents are starting to use the web on our behalf, booking tickets, filling in forms and comparing products. Today most of them do it the hard way, by reading screenshots and guessing at the DOM. It works until a button moves or a layout changes, and it leaves site owners with no say in how agents interact with their product.

WebMCP proposes a different approach. In this talk we'll look at what WebMCP is and how it differs from what's available today.

**About Tara:**
Tara Ojo Agyemang is a Developer Relations Engineer on the Google Chrome team, based in London. After ten years as a software engineer, she now helps developers adopt new web platform capabilities in an increasingly agentic world.

**Talk 2: The Last ""10%"" - Converting your agentic system from a demo to reliable, profitable production app**
We will talk through the most common gaps we've seen in production agentic systems and the most impact full ways to cover those gaps. We will dig a bit deeper into evals and observability and ask the audience for some of their pain points and interests. Lastly I will show examples of what everyone should look at for the near future to improve accuracy and reduce costs.

**About Nick:**
Nick Ferrell is a Senior Lead Software Engineer at Focused. Helping companies and engineers build systems that matter. Nick is focussed on agentic solutions that are production-ready, scalable, and built to last. Turning ambitious ideas into software that works in the real world.

**Thanks!**
We'd like to thank our sponsors Focused.io (http://focused.io/) for supporting the community and making this event happen. We'd also like to thank our amazing hosts Autogen.

**Code of Conduct**
This event has a code of conduct that you can review here. (https://aifortherestofus.live/code-of-conduct) By joining the community and registering for this event you agree to abide by our code of conduct.

**Providing Your Name and Email**
To register for this event you'll be asked to provide your email address. After the event you will be automatically subscribed to the newsletters from *AI for the rest of us* and Focused. You can unsubscribe at any time (But why would you? They are really very good!)",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/b/8/0/highres_536535232.jpeg,2026-10-27 18:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,AutogenAI,"123 Pentonville Rd, London N1 9LG, UK",London,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,ai}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/ai-for-the-rest-of-us-london/events/316926189/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,t,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/ai-for-the-rest-of-us-london/events/316926189/,event_316926189@meetup.com,8005a504-2ee0-4893-a5e7-2f156356d102,2026-10-26 03:23:00.233+00,,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,2026-10-26 03:23:36.1552+00,,,,,f,GB
