A free session for PMs, engineers, designers, founders, and operators who are building with AI and want honest peer accountability, not another product demo.
Most AI content is hype. This session isn't.
A small group of builders gets together to have the conversation that doesn't happen in Slack or LinkedIn. The real one about what AI tools are actually saving time, what looked promising but flopped, and what workflows are genuinely changing how we work.
**What we cover**

• Which tools people are actually using week-to-week (not just testing)
• Adoption blockers. What's getting in the way at work or in your team
• Workflow patterns that are working across different roles
• How to build AI-native habits that stick
• Open Q&A and peer problem-solving

**How it works**

• We open by checking in on how we are doing on AI adoption or review what you said you'd try last time
• We compare notes openly, including the failures
• You leave with one specific thing you'll test before the next session
• Next time, we hold each other to it

**Format**

• 60 minutes, online via Zoom
• Small group (max 30 people) so everyone can contribute
• Facilitated by Patricia Juarez, Staff AI Engineer with 9 months of experience leading AI adoption programs on AWS. No slides, no pitch, no selling.
• Montly cadence. With option to every 2 weeks.

**Who it's for**
PMs, engineers, designers, founders, operators, and team leads already using AI tools in some form who want to get more intentional about it. You don't need to be an expert. Show up curious and willing to share honestly.
**What this is NOT**

• A product demo
• A sales webinar
• A lecture

**This IS**

• A peer conversation among people who are figuring this out together
• A place to say ""I tried X and it failed"" without judgment
• A way to shortcut 3 months of trial and error by hearing what others are learning

**Host**
Patricia Juarez Muñoz. Senior Engineer at AWS, AI adoption lead, and founder of WonderLead. Patricia ran AI literacy programs across teams at AWS in Berlin, turning weekly learning sessions into a 6-month community of practice across organizations. She's been where you are, and she facilitates these sessions so the group does the talking.
**Register**
Free. Spot is yours once you sign up. We'll send a reminder 48 hours before and a Zoom link the morning of.
**What People Say**
*“What started as a series of demo and sharing sessions quickly evolved into a lasting community of learning that continued for more than six months.”*
