What changes when AI becomes part of the product—and sometimes starts making decisions or taking actions on behalf of users?
We'll explore questions such as:

• Are we solving the **right problem** with AI?
• What decision is the AI actually helping the user make?
• What context does AI need to make useful decisions?
• What happens when AI is **wrong**?
• Why can a highly accurate AI still create a poor product experience?
• How much autonomy should an AI agent have?
• Where should humans approve, override or intervene?
• How do we design **trust, control and explainability**?
• And importantly, **where should UX professionals contribute across AI SDLC?**

Beyond Screens & Interfaces

UX for AI is not only about designing a chatbot, copilot or AI interface.
As AI becomes more autonomous, UX increasingly involves designing:
**Human-AI workflows • Decisions • Context • Trust • Control • Failure & Recovery • Adoption • Business Outcomes**
The masterclass will introduce you to the emerging **Dreamworx UX for AI SDLC framework** and show how familiar UX and product practices need to evolve for AI-enabled products.

Who Should Attend?

For professionals involved in **designing, building, testing or managing AI-enabled products**, including:
UX/UI & Product Designers • UX Researchers • Product Managers • Business Analysts • Developers • QA/Test Professionals • Product & Technology Teams • Startup Founders • IT Professionals
**You don't need to be an AI expert.**
This is not a prompt-engineering or AI-tools session. It is about developing the **UX and product thinking needed to build useful, trustworthy and valuable AI-enabled products.**

About the Facilitator

**Nandhakumar V**
**Founder & UX/CX Director, Dreamworx**
Nandhakumar brings over two decades of experience across UX, experience strategy, product thinking and digital product development. His current work focuses on integrating UX and human-centered product development into AI SDLC.

Join the Free Masterclass

If AI is changing how products are built, perhaps the bigger question isn't:
**“How do I use more AI?”**
It is:

**“How do we make sure we're building the right AI experience in the first place?”**

Join the upcoming **FREE UX for AI SDLC Masterclass** to explore where UX belongs in this new development lifecycle.
**AI gives speed. UX gives direction.**
If AI is changing how products are built, the bigger question may not be:
**“How do I use more AI?”**
but:
**“How do we make sure we're building the right AI experience in the first place?”**
