817aaa51-c198-4505-b729-72a73ce80afd,,AI This Week: Open Circle,"AI moves fast. Something new drops every week, and it's hard to keep up alone.","AI moves fast. Something new drops every week, and it's hard to keep up alone.

AI This Week: Open Circle is our weekly open circle for developers, builders, and anyone curious about where AI is headed. There are no slides and no fixed speaker. We bring the week's biggest AI news, new model releases, tools worth trying, and whatever questions you're stuck on, and we talk it through together.
**What we usually cover:**
• The AI news that actually matters this week
• New models, frameworks, and tools people are testing
• Real problems from your projects or work
• Quick live demos when someone has something cool to show
**Who should come:**
Engineers, data folks, founders, students, and career switchers. All levels are welcome. You don't need to present anything. Just show up with curiosity.
Bring a topic, a question, or just listen in. Some of our best conversations start with ""Has anyone tried...?""
Hosted by AgentVersity, a community of 30,000+ developers learning to build with AI.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/8/3/0/highres_536182576.jpeg,2026-11-27 04:00:00+00,2026-11-27 05:30:00+00,Asia/Kolkata,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,ai}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/bengaluru-artificial-intelligence-group/events/316732373/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 03:22:47.855553+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/bengaluru-artificial-intelligence-group/events/316732373/,event_316732373@meetup.com,,2026-10-22 03:22:12.257+00,,2026-10-22 03:22:47.855553+00,2026-10-22 03:22:57.615225+00,,,meetup:bengaluru-artificial-intelligence-group:ai this week open circle,Every week on Friday,f,
5eb82c4c-b1f8-4819-8690-52fa5aef0ef0,,Umbraco Builders Day,"Umbraco Builders Day brings Umbraco community and HQ folks together for a relaxed day of building - helping each other shape ideas, get unstuck and find people to team up with. Regulars will know it…","Umbraco Builders Day brings Umbraco community and HQ folks together for a relaxed day of building - helping each other shape ideas, get unstuck and find people to team up with. Regulars will know it as our virtual hackathon (new name, same friendly faces!), and if you’ve never been to one, it’s the perfect first event.

Hack together on anything that extends or uses an Umbraco product. Bring an idea, find collaborators, build something.

Drop in and out whenever you like. Come for an hour or stay all day, it’s completely up to you.

**What to expect**

• A relaxed day of building. No pitches, no judges, no pressure.
• Umbraco HQ people around all day to help or point you to the right person.
• Other builders to team up with, or just to keep you company on your screen while you work on your own thing.
• We'll run a casual show-and-tell throughout the day for anyone who wants to share what they built. Totally fine to skip it.

**What can you build?**
Anything that touches an Umbraco product. A package, an integration, a starter kit, a fix for something that’s been bugging you, a weird experiment with AI, or a feature you wish existed. Small is great. Unfinished is great too.

**What to bring**

• An idea, a problem you’ve been meaning to solve, or nothing at all. We’ll help you find something, or you can join someone else’s project.
• Your curiosity. Ask questions, poke at things, try something you haven’t tried before.

**It’s a workday, so ask your boss**
Builders Day is on a Friday, so have a chat with your employer about blocking out the day (or part of it). It’s hands-on learning with the people who build Umbraco, and you’ll come back with new skills, new contacts and maybe even something you can use at work. That’s an easy sell, right? 😉

**First time?**
This is the perfect one to start with. You don’t need to be an Umbraco expert, you don’t need a team, and you don’t need a plan. Plenty of people come along just to learn, ask questions and see what others are working on. Everyone was new once, and the people in the room are genuinely happy to help.

**Not good for your timezone?**
We are currently planning to run the event from 10am to 1am (CET). If you're keen to be involved but these times don't work well for you then please contact the Umbraco Developer Relations team (https://community.umbraco.com/connect/the-developer-relations-team/contact-devrel/) and let's see what we can do!",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/6/d/0/highres_536585840.jpeg,2026-11-13 09:00:00+00,,Europe/Copenhagen,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,{technology},,external,https://www.meetup.com/umbraco-virtual/events/316959484/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/umbraco-virtual/events/316959484/,event_316959484@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.493162+00,,,,,f,
