9f3bdf73-e671-4052-afea-f0a34f8f4c02,,Stay fit with Parkinson's (Zoom class),"Exercise can slow down the progression of Parkinson’s, and Covid 19 Quarantine is no reason not to move! Join our fun outdoor class and stay fit and healthy.","Exercise can slow down the progression of Parkinson’s, and Covid 19 Quarantine is no reason not to move! Join our fun outdoor class and stay fit and healthy.

Our ‘Nordic Neuro Magic’ is a new exercise class designed for people in the early stage of Parkinson’s and their friends or partners who can walk, are at a low risk of falls and have no major other health concerns .

Our exercise classes can really help improve your gait, balance and posture. They are also an excellent way to get fitter and stronger.
Inspired by PD Warrior, we run these especially designed classes, full of fun exercises, designed to slow down the progression of Parkinson’s.

Our members love it, and we can really see the difference in the members who have been with us for a while!

The classes are based around 7 key principles:
o Powerful
o Complex
o Frequent
o High effort
o Meaningful in daily life
o Specific to symptoms
o Fun!

New to Fit and Happy Outdoors? Please email me on ailien@fitandhappyoutdoors.com or send me a personal message through Meetup at least 24 hours before the session you would like to join.

That will give me enough time to get back to you and discuss your needs and find out a bit more about you.

Once signed up we will send you a link to our Zoom meeting, as well as the password.

Cost: £150 per 10 sessions or £90 per month for unrestricted access to all our classes. Your partner can join your session for free.

Pay What Works:
The price shown above is the “true” value of the session that best reflects the work I put into preparing and leading your session. However, I understand that not everyone can afford to pay full price, and I don’t want that to stop you from joining us.

In an effort to find a balance between more financial accessibility and sustainable pricing, I now offer a “Pay What Works” model. This allows for financial flexibility while still valuing and respecting the work and energy I provide in creating and delivering these classes.

Then send an email to ailien@fitandhappyoutdoors.com with the heading “INVOICE please”- followed by “FAHO 1” to pay full price as quoted below, “FAHO 2”, for 20% off, or “FAHO 3” for 50% off.

Please do tell me if you want to pay for 10 sessions, or if you’d like to pay monthly.
I prefer payment by bank transfer, but if that is not possible you could post me a cheque, made out to Ailien Rhijnsburger.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/4/4/4/highres_490858436.jpeg,2026-12-03 11:00:00+00,2026-12-03 12:00:00+00,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/fit-and-happy-outdoors/events/jmrnvryjcqbfb/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/fit-and-happy-outdoors/events/jmrnvryjcqbfb/,event_jmrnvryjcqbfb@meetup.com,,2026-10-27 03:22:34.801+00,,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,2026-10-27 03:22:59.22745+00,,,meetup:fit-and-happy-outdoors:stay fit with parkinson s zoom class,Every week on Thursday,f,
a4f15543-7917-407c-82b0-cd3d28aa6a46,,What Day-2 Kubernetes looks like when it's done right,"Platform teams are expected to deliver Kubernetes as a reliable internal platform, without multiplying tools or operational overhead. In this demo‑driven session, see how Nutanix Kubernetes Platform…","Platform teams are expected to deliver Kubernetes as a reliable internal platform, without multiplying tools or operational overhead. In this demo‑driven session, see how Nutanix Kubernetes Platform (NKP) reduces complexity and enables teams to run Kubernetes at scale with a unified, production‑ready approach.

Attendees will learn how to:
1. **Reduce operational complexity** with built‑in automation that simplifies Kubernetes lifecycle management and eliminates fragmented tooling.
2. **Operate Kubernetes and VM workloads together** through a unified platform, enabling consistent Day‑2 operations and smoother modernization.
3. **Run scalable, production‑ready Kubernetes** including stateful applications, on an open platform, with a brief look at built‑in data services such as Nutanix Data Services for Kubernetes (NDK).",,2026-11-19 18:00:00+00,,Asia/Kolkata,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,{technology},,external,https://www.meetup.com/platform-engineers-bangalore/events/316781876/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 03:22:47.855553+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/platform-engineers-bangalore/events/316781876/,event_316781876@meetup.com,,2026-10-22 03:22:12.257+00,,2026-10-22 03:22:47.855553+00,2026-10-22 03:22:47.855553+00,,,,,f,
4ab40600-de9f-441a-a50f-548f7bc23fd1,,"Social @ Tate Britain Lates! DJ Music, Activities & After-Party 🎨🎶🎨🎶","Join our social group for a meetup at Tate Britain Late — a perfect blend of cultural discovery, meaningful connections, and pure fun.","**Join our social group for a meetup at Tate Britain Late** — a perfect blend of cultural discovery, meaningful connections, and pure fun.
We’ll wander through the museum’s grand halls together, taking in masterpieces by Turner, Hockney, and centuries of British art that have inspired generations. Then we’ll head to the high-energy DJ party for drinks, music, and dancing till 21:45.
Looking forward to exploring and celebrating with the group!

**Tate Britain Late** promises a perfect blend of **cultural discovery**, **meaningful connections**, and **pure fun**. Wander through the museum’s grand halls filled with masterpieces by Turner, Hockney, and centuries of British art that have inspired generations, then experience the high-energy DJ party for drinks, music, and dancing till 21:45.

🎨✨ **How It Works**
Welcome! This event is all about **meeting new people, making connections, and enjoying art together**. 💬🤝

**📍 *Phase 1: Meet & Mingle (The Most Important Part!)***
Our first meeting point is where the magic begins! ✨
Please take this opportunity to:
• 👋 Say hello to as many people as you can.
• 💬 Introduce yourself and have a few conversations.
• 😊 Be open, friendly, and welcoming—everyone is here to meet new people too!
The more people you chat with at the start, the more fun the rest of the event will be.

***🖼️ Gallery Exploration***
Once everyone has had a chance to mingle, I'll lead you to a designated area of the gallery. From there:
• 👥 You'll split into your groups.
• 🎭 Explore the exhibition together at your own pace.
• 💡 Share your thoughts, discover your favourite pieces, and enjoy getting to know your group.
There's no right or wrong way to experience the gallery—just have fun and enjoy the conversations!

***📍 Meet Back Up***
we'll all reconvene at our **original meeting point**. This is a great chance to catch up with people you met earlier and make sure everyone is ready for the next stop. 🎉
Most importantly… relax, be yourself, and have an amazing time! 🥳🎨✨

**AFTER PARTY**
After party is at Tamesis Dock on a walk-in basis. So go here and find each other. Arrival 10pm onwards.
https://maps.app.goo.gl/fVRARZuYBkTAffvH9

***Route from Tate Britain***
https://maps.app.goo.gl/thmPTACLqym9y2MB7

Important Details ℹ️

**Dress Code**: Smart casual; no athletic tracksuits or sports trainers. 👗 **Bring ID** for entry to the bar venues. 🆔 **More Info**: Check the event page for additional details. 🌐
**Join up now** — if we have a lot of sign-ups, we may introduce a fee for any additional new joiners (through the Meetup RSVP system). Avoid this by signing up early! ⏰
Don’t miss this chance to explore world-class British art, make new friends, and dance the night away in the heart of London. Join us for an evening that’s as enriching as it is exhilarating! 🎉

**Some Tips:**

1. **Let’s all commit to updating our RSVPs if plans change**—it helps us plan better and ensures great attendance for everyone. If you RSVP “yes” but don’t attend and don’t update your RSVP, you may be removed from the group to keep things fair. No stress, though—you can rejoin for a small £10 fee! Just send me a DM, and I’ll share the PayPal details to get you back in.
2. **Turn Up on Time at the start!** This helps the quality of the event and helps you.
3. If you are struggling with the **app**, use the web page instead, that's what I use.
4. **Attendee Numbers & Guest Lists:** We have this event listed at least on two groups and the guest list includes attendees from all. You can see the list of attendees here:
https://www.meetup.com/zensingles/
https://www.meetup.com/cityzenlondon/
https://www.meetup.com/LoveLife
1. Join our **social media**:
**Instagram**: https://www.instagram.com/cityzen.london/
**X:** https://x.com/CityZenLondon
1. **Our WhatsApp group:** [See private comment in the comments section below]. We have a few rules including no ads, no DMs unless recipient is in the ""Direct Messaging List"" or risk removal and £10 rejoin fee.
2. **Support Our Amazing London Event Hosts! 🙌**
Our incredible crew of hosts is the heartbeat of London’s buzzing meetup scene, bringing people together for unforgettable experiences that spark connection, growth, and fun! 🌟 From museum adventures to flirty dating mixers, these rockstar hosts pour their energy, time, and passion into creating events that level up your social and communication skills. But hosting isn’t easy—it takes resources, effort, and heart. 💖
Please consider supporting our hosts with a donation to keep the good vibes flowing and help us make London the ultimate social hub! 🚀 Below, meet our hosts for this event and see how you can chip in to fuel their amazing work.
1. To encourage signing up early to events and regulate the number of attendees a late joiner/overflow fee may be applied to an event for any **additional** people wanting to join the event. This may happen on the day or even an hour before the event. So there may be people who…",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/b/3/1/c/highres_535605852.jpeg,2026-11-13 18:45:00+00,2026-11-13 21:45:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Tate Britain,Millbank,London SW1P 4RG,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,socialising,music,arts,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/cityzenlondon/events/315446575/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/cityzenlondon/events/315446575/,event_315446575@meetup.com,,2026-10-27 03:22:34.801+00,,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,2026-10-27 03:22:59.22745+00,,,meetup:cityzenlondon:social tate britain lates dj music activities after party,"Every 2nd Friday of the month until January 1, 2027",f,GB
