d9e12960-26c5-4b1a-a3fc-59d5271a764d,,"North London’s Green Corridor: Highgate, Hampstead and Ally Pally fireworks","Join us for an interesting, varied walk through North London’s historic leafy trails, culminating near Alexandra Palace, where we can stay for a glimpse of one of London’s finest November firework…","Join us for an interesting, varied walk through North London’s historic leafy trails, culminating near Alexandra Palace, where we can stay for a glimpse of one of London’s finest November firework displays.

Starting in Finsbury Park, we’ll pick up London’s longest linear nature reserve, following a former railway line and passing a folklore-inspired sculpture that has become its unofficial guardian.

We’ll climb through Highgate, with its attractive village streets and famous cemetery, before reaching Parliament Hill for views across London to St Paul’s, the Shard and Westminster.

We’ll cross the ponds, meadows and woodland of Hampstead Heath to Kenwood House, the elegant neoclassical villa that is home to the Iveagh Bequest and paintings by Rembrandt and Vermeer.

We’ll finish by passing through Highgate Wood, a 70-acre section of the ancient Hornsey Wood, before heading towards Alexandra Palace for a well-earned drink or two and the option to stick around for the fireworks later.

**NB** The event does not include entry into the official firework venue. If you are interested in attending this, tickets are available on the link below. The walk Host won't be attending the fireworks event due to an early start the next day (😂) but do post in the Comments section below if you want to co-ordinate with others to attend. www.alexandrapalace.com/whats-on/fireworks-drone-festival (https://www.alexandrapalace.com/whats-on/fireworks-drone-festival/)

**SUMMARY (all info is approximate!)**

**Distance**: 16km/10 miles linear route
**Ascent**: 250 metres
**Duration**: 4.5 hours walking
**Grade**: Beginners/Intermediate, largely flat, along good paths, with plenty of short stops and options to leave part-way through if you get tired.

**COST AND LOGISTICS**

**Cost**: £12
**Meet:** 10:30am - Costa Coffee, Finsbury Park Station https://maps.app.goo.gl/NMjh9WfKBaK1YU1Z8
**Start**: 10.45am
**Finish:** 4.30pm Hornsey Station / Great Northern Railway Tavern
**Both stations are within the Oyster/Contactless Zone**

**REVIEWS**
Trip Advisor (https://www.tripadvisor.co.uk/Attraction_Review-g186338-d19994843-Reviews-AAA_Hiking_Outdoor_Group-London_England.html) | Facebook (https://www.facebook.com/AAAHikingUK/reviews) | MeetUp (https://www.meetup.com/aaa-outdoor-hiking-adventure-travel/feedback-overview/)

**PRICE INCLUDES**

• Guided walk planned and led by an experienced AAA leader, trained in Outdoor First Aid.

**PRICE DOES NOT INCLUDE**

• Travel costs
• Lunch, drinks or any refreshments
• PayPal fees

**RECOMMENDED KIT LIST** ( (https://mailchi.mp/aaalondongroup.com/kitlist)[complete list](www.aaahiking.co.uk/kit-lists)) (https://mailchi.mp/aaalondongroup.com/kitlist)

• Suitable walking shoes or boots
• Packed lunch and snacks
• Water - Minimum 1 litre recommended
• Waterproof jacket and trousers
• Warm windproof layer e.g. Down/Primaloft/Fleece
• Wicking base layer e.g. Polyester/Tencel/Merino

**CANCELLING/REFUNDS**

If you can no longer join the walk, please message the Host listed on here, and update your RSVP status to 'Not going', to allow others to take your place. If the event is full, and you have messaged us and have changed your RSVP to 'Not going', we will refund you, less the PayPal/Meetup fees. To obtain this, please email info@aaalondongroup.com **after the event**, with the email address you use on your PayPal account and transaction reference. If the hike is not full, unfortunately we will not be able to provide any refund.

**QUESTIONS**
If you have any other questions, please check visit our FAQ page (https://mailchi.mp/aaalondongroup.com/frequently-asked-questions). If you are still unsure, contact the event Host shown on this page.

We’ve run over 1,000 trips in the last 18 years, so you’re in good hands. That said, all participants (members and their guests) in any AAA Hiking event or activity are personally responsible for their fitness, safety and welfare, and must be equipped accordingly. If you have signed up for the event, you acknowledge and accept the AAA London Group Terms and Conditions (https://www.aaahiking.co.uk/terms-and-conditions).

© AAA London Group Ltd. Errors and Omissions Excepted

