0438da4c-7b67-4170-9dad-a2ae9ac64ed1,,🌙✨ Nightly Journaling Circle✨,🌙✨ Nightly Journaling Circle | Online | 9 PM – 10 PM,"🌙✨ **Nightly Journaling Circle | Online | 9 PM – 10 PM**

Looking for a peaceful way to end your day? Join us every evening for a cozy online journaling session where we pause, reflect, and set intentions for a better tomorrow.

From **9:00 PM to 10:00 PM**, we'll spend time writing down our thoughts, practicing gratitude, and sharing general reflections in a warm, supportive, and judgment-free space. Whether you're celebrating small wins, processing your day, or simply seeking calm, you're welcome here.

💛 **What to expect:**
• Guided journaling prompts
• Quiet reflection time
• Optional sharing and meaningful conversations
• A positive and supportive community
• Small daily habits for personal growth and well-being

📖 **Bring along:**
• A journal or notebook
• A pen
• An open heart and mind

No writing experience is needed—just come as you are.

**Because healing, self-discovery, and growth happen one page at a time.** 🌿✨

*""Write your thoughts today, create a better tomorrow.""*

*# Journaling Session Ground Rules*

*To create a safe, focused, and meaningful space for everyone, please keep these guidelines in mind:*

1. **This is a journaling-focused session.** *Please keep all discussions related to the prompts and personal reflections from today's session.*

2. **No work or workplace discussions.** *This is a space to disconnect from work and reconnect with yourself. Please avoid conversations about your job, colleagues, office, or workplace situations.*

3. **Respect everyone's time.** *Stay on topic and avoid side conversations so we can make the most of our time together.*

4. **No unrelated subjects.** *Please refrain from discussing politics, current affairs, gossip, business, or other topics unrelated to the journaling experience.*

5. **Share with kindness, not advice.** *If participants choose to share, listen with empathy. Avoid giving unsolicited advice or trying to solve someone else's experiences.*

6. **Confidentiality matters.** *What is shared in this session stays in this session. Please respect everyone's privacy.*

7. **Share only what feels comfortable.** *There is no pressure to speak. You're welcome to simply journal and listen.*

8. **Be present.** *Silence your notifications, minimize distractions, and give yourself this hour to reflect and be fully engaged.*",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792620962/orbit/event-covers/sources/cuebbhsi72crkdo488pv.jpg,2026-10-23 17:00:00+00,2026-10-23 18:00:00+00,Asia/Dubai,online,Online event,,,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,wellbeing,fitness,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/dlrc-walk-and-talk/events/316829663/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:15:29.416216+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/dlrc-walk-and-talk/events/316829663/,event_316829663@meetup.com,,2026-10-22 03:21:50.591+00,,2026-10-21 22:15:29.416216+00,2026-10-22 03:22:11.100007+00,,,meetup:dlrc-walk-and-talk:nightly journaling circle,Every week on every day,f,
d4ad6115-8cac-478e-8763-80cf9c80c280,,MarTech London: Building an Experimentation Practice That Delivers Value,How do you build an experimentation practice that delivers value today and prepares your business for what comes next?,"How do you build an experimentation practice that delivers value today and prepares your business for what comes next?

Join us at MarTech London on the 19th of November to hear from Stuart Clare of The AA and Barry Lennon of VodafoneThree UK, exploring how to build a strong experimentation practice, prepare for personalisation and improve confidence in the data behind digital decisions.

Stuart will share his perspective on bringing teams together, building support for experimentation, and making testing part of everyday decision-making. Drawing on experience from The AA, adidas and Vistaprint, he’ll explore how customer insight and experimentation can improve customer experiences and drive business growth.
He’ll also discuss how AI is changing the landscape and what that means for organisations taking their next steps towards personalisation.

Barry will explore quality assurance (QA) for digital analytics and experimentation, the implications of data quality issues and practical lessons from implementation. He’ll also discuss how automation can support QA, helping teams identify issues and build greater confidence in their measurement.

Join fellow marketing, digital and MarTech leaders for practical insights, questions and discussion with time to connect over drinks and nibbles.

