9681682d-6c71-4f28-a026-bea714211d2b,,Sunday Walk from Hampstead Heath Station,"This walk takes us all around and across Hamstead Heath in a 6.15 mile route, taking in the glorious Autumn scenes of this unique location. We'll visit the main points of interest; Kenwood House,…","This walk takes us all around and across Hamstead Heath in a 6.15 mile route, taking in the glorious Autumn scenes of this unique location. We'll visit the main points of interest; Kenwood House, Parliament Hill and the Henry Moore sculpture. There are a few elevations, it is quite up and down. Hampstead Heath is the overground station where we start; Belsize Park and Hampstead tube, Northern Line are both 10 to 15 minutes walk away at the most. Walking time approx 2.5 hours.

The price for the walk is £2 cash to cover costs.

After the walk there's the option to stay for a drink, chat and refreshments at a nearby hostelry.

**Free Parking**
Allow 15 minutes for parking to be on the safe side.

There's free roadside parking on Sundays; you may find some on South Hill Park Gardens, Parliament Hill, Nassington Road and Tanza Road, and the main road, South End Road. There's also ample paid parking at East Heath Car Park on East Heath Road, London NW3 1TH.

Please note that this walk is not led by a qualified leader and, as such, isn't covered by insurance. Be sure to wear suitable boots and clothing.
The organiser cannot be held responsible for any injuries, however caused. Members are expected to take responsibility for their own preparation and safety including adequate fluids, weather protection and a snack. Please be sure to make me aware if you have any medical conditions.

Dogs are welcome as always but please be mindful to keep them on leads for roads and around other animals. These events are not for children.
