13c3ab7f-e197-4638-8acc-8c52760f321a,,"Midhurst, Woolbeding and River Rother stunning countryside walk",Let's go with the flow and do this fabulous 9 mile walk in the stunning West Sussex countryside !,"Let's go with the flow and do this fabulous 9 mile walk in the stunning West Sussex countryside !

Things to bring : packed lunch, water, snacks etc and waterproof jacket and walking shoes/boots/trainers.

We shall buy group train tickets at 10am for the 10.30am train that arrives at Haslemere at 11.20am.

Train ticket: Return to Petersfield

At 11.42am we shall take the no 70 bus to Midhurst and shall alight by Midhurst ( Easebourne ) Community Hospital so that we can walk past Cowdray House and Cowdray Ruins - the remains of one of England's most important Tudor houses -

Or you may decide to drive.

Midhurst houses medieval streets filled with timber-framed buildings, local cafes and boutique shops.

June Lane separates Midhurst from the stunning Woolbeding countryside and we shall walk by the River Rother and all the ancient trees.

You should have adequate and appropriate insurance for this type of activity and be able to walk 2.5 miles per hour.

We shall have a drink at the end of the walk.

Likely train back from Petersfield at 5.18pm that arrives in London at around 6.20pm after first taking no 92 bus at 4.46pm from Trotton.

Please only post photos of others with their consent.

