62b14162-3962-4c4a-93bd-3dceefe52ad7,,Samir Abu Ghosh: Business Agility Under Pressure in the Middle East,"Operating in increasingly complex, fast-changing, and uncertain environments, organizations must continuously adapt while delivering strategic outcomes.","Operating in increasingly complex, fast-changing, and uncertain environments, organizations must continuously adapt while delivering strategic outcomes.
Drawing on transformation initiatives across the Middle East (such as Saudi Arabia, UAE, and Qatar), this session explores the realities of achieving sustainable agility in fast-growing economies pursuing ambitious national visions.
Why do some transformations succeed where others struggle? We need to move beyond agile frameworks and methodologies and examine enterprise agility as an organizational capability rather than a delivery practice.
We will share lessons on some capability levers that enable sustainable business agility.

About our speaker:

Samir Abu Ghosh (https://www.linkedin.com/in/samir-abughosh/) is a senior transformation leader with over 20 years of experience helping organizations accelerate enterprise transformation and improve strategy execution. He is the founder of Ontario Consulting, a boutique management consulting firm specializing in business agility, innovation labs activation, and AI solutions co-creation. The firm focuses primarily on the public and financial sectors, serving clients across Canada, the Middle East, and North Africa.

About our hosts:

Markus Willner

Thoralf J Klatt (https://www.linkedin.com/in/tjklatt/)
Thoralf serves as a Product and Agile Coach. His motto is: be at the center of value. He started his career developing medical devices like CT scanners and became a Certified Scrum Master in 2007. Based on many years of experience in diverse domains, Thoralf qualified as SPC in 2016, as Scrum@Scale and Scrum Inc. Trainer with Jeff Sutherland in 2019, and as Mobius Navigator Coach with Gabrielle Benefield in 2020. He has been translating her new book (https://www.amazon.com/Mobius-Outcome-Delivery-Quickstart-decisions-ebook/dp/B0DX1SHB2Y/) on Mobius Loop to German and he has been organizing several charity fundraiser training during pandemic and Ukraine crisis (giving to MSF). Thoralf recently became a genAI Practitioner Trainer for Scrum Inc and has been a Neural Network & AI geek since studying at MIT and is currently using AI for better Discovery using JTBD. Reach out for speakerships.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/3/f/b/highres_535138363.jpeg,2026-11-05 18:00:00+00,,Europe/Berlin,online,Online event,,,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,growth,entrepreneurship,careers}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/business-agility-meetup-berlin/events/315626400/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-25 03:22:33.838204+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/business-agility-meetup-berlin/events/315626400/,event_315626400@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-25 03:22:33.838204+00,2026-10-28 03:22:27.129706+00,,,,,f,
