24b3b6ca-a7d5-49a8-bf4e-859465d0a3b1,,Canal Walk - Angel to Victoria Park Cafe / Market,We will enjoy a leisurely walk (approx 45 mins - 1 hour) along Regent's Canal from Angel station and ending at the fabulous Victoria Park Market. This event usually runs on the 4th Sunday of each…,"We will enjoy a leisurely walk (approx 45 mins - 1 hour) along Regent's Canal from Angel station and ending at the fabulous Victoria Park Market. This event usually runs on the 4th Sunday of each month, unless there is bad weather or exceptional circumstances. We are a welcoming group, so feel free to mix around and say hello other people.

There is a wondering food market in Victoria Park, and most of us will get something to eat together. We usually sit on the grass or public benches (if available) near the Bonner Gate entrance, behind the Dogs of Alcibiades statue. This is at the intersection of foodstalls running north/south and east/west. If it is raining or the market is closed, we can either go to the Pavillion cafe, or The Crown pub on Grove Road instead.

Please note a few points:
1. There is currently no charge for this group. I will need to review this again later in 2026.

2. WE WILL WAIT ONLY ABOUT 10 MINUTES AFTER THE START TIME. If you are running late, please catch us up along the canal. Please note, I will not be checking for meetup or whatsapp messages after the walk starts.

3. The nearest tube station to Victoria Park is Bethnal Green station (central line). Please check Google Maps or similar.

4. You are responsible for yourselves on the walk, so please bring appropriate footwear etc. Please be mindful of those around you, especially where the canal gets narrow in places.

Whatsapp group here: https://chat.whatsapp.com/IJd6MJfVDPC6jUw6iW77ZY

Previously, there was a separate walk on the 3rd Sunday of the month, which started at Limehouse Basin, and then ran along the same canal to Victoria Park. Please note, the walks starting from Limehouse on the 3rd Sunday of the month are now cancelled for the foreseeable future.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/f/2/e/highres_520768462.jpeg,2027-04-25 11:00:00+00,2027-04-25 14:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Angel Station,A1,London,c06699ed-62e0-4957-bcb4-080c5271da9a,"{sport,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/canal-walk-run-food-markets/events/315791974/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-26 03:21:15.822395+00,source:cba1b9d2-d09d-4c19-a89e-50bdbe5525a0,https://www.meetup.com/canal-walk-run-food-markets/events/315791974/,event_315791974@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:20:38.34+00,,2026-10-26 03:21:15.822395+00,2026-10-28 03:21:15.930389+00,,,meetup:canal-walk-run-food-markets:canal walk angel to victoria park cafe market,"Every 4th Sunday of the month until July 25, 2027",f,GB
efa626e9-6cdd-4eaa-83ab-fcd7ea1ba162,,AIoT Hub - (Re)-engineering AI,"AIoTHub (formerly IoT North) Community meetup are pleased to present Blesson Varghese in ""(Re)-engineering AI""","AIoTHub (formerly IoT North) Community meetup are pleased to present Blesson Varghese in ""(Re)-engineering AI""

Abstract:
The widespread deployment of AI beyond the cloud and onto smaller, resource-constrained devices presents a fundamental engineering challenge. While considerable attention has focused on developing increasingly capable models, making ML systems practical in real-world environments requires us to rethink how we engineer them.
In this talk, I will discuss three fundamental challenges that arise when deploying ML systems at scale: they do not run efficiently on small devices, they have inherent sequential dependencies that limit efficient execution, and they are highly memory-intensive. I will present research solutions we have developed to address these challenges, drawing on our experience in designing and deploying distributed and edge AI systems.
Rather than focusing on a particular model or application, the talk will explore the underlying systems problems and the engineering principles behind our solutions. I will show how rethinking the way ML systems are designed and executed can make AI more practical for deployment across resource-constrained environments.

Bio:
Blesson Varghese is a Professor of Computer Science at the University of St Andrews, UK, with over 15 years of UK and international experience designing, developing and deploying large-scale distributed computer systems. His research focuses on edge computing and distributed systems, with an emphasis on translating research into practical systems. He was the recipient of the 2021 IEEE Rising Star Award and held a Royal Society fellowship in partnership with British Telecommunications plc, supporting the translation of his research into real-world applications. He directs the Edge Computing Hub, funded by Rakuten Mobile, Japan, and co-leads research within the UK’s National Edge AI Hub. He has filed over ten patents arising from his research. His research has featured in a New Scientist video series and the documentary *Clouded*, where he has contributed to raising public awareness of emerging computing technologies.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/6/7/7/highres_536314423.jpeg,2026-11-03 18:00:00+00,2026-11-03 19:00:00+00,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,ai}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/aiotmcr/events/316720792/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/aiotmcr/events/316720792/,event_316720792@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.493162+00,,,meetup:aiotmcr:aiot hub re engineering ai,"Every 1st Tuesday of the month until November 30, 2027",f,
0db26239-659d-4e30-b11e-0896cd1932b0,,Webinar on Cost Optimisation for AI Agents by Chandan Varshney,"We're excited to announce the upcoming TTTribeCast Webinar on ""Fewer Tokens, Similar Results: Cost Optimisation for AI Agents"" by Chandan Varshney","We're excited to announce the upcoming TTTribeCast Webinar on ""**Fewer Tokens, Similar Results: Cost Optimisation for AI Agents""** by Chandan Varshney

**When is it happening?** **22nd October 2026** | Thursday | 9:00 PM IST | 8:30 AM PT | 11:30 AM ET | 5:30 PM CEST

**What will Chandan speak about?**

Fewer Tokens, Similar Results: Cost Optimisation for AI Agents

Your chatbot answers in one call. Your AI agent might make 20 calls for the same job, and re-read everything it has seen before each one. That's why agent bills surprise so many teams.

**You'll walk away with:**
✅ Why agent costs grow faster than the number of steps
✅ The six hidden cost drivers most teams miss
✅ Five practical ways to cut spend: caching, model routing, context trimming, budgets, and right-sized multi-agent designs
✅ A real-world example: a test-failure triage agent made 25× leaner
✅ Why cost per successful task beats cost per call

**About the speaker:**
Chandan Varshney (https://www.linkedin.com/in/chandan-varshney-b1ba3721/?utm_source=luma)is a seasoned Test Automation Architect with 16 years of experience designing enterprise-grade automation frameworks for web and API testing using Java, Selenium, Cucumber, Rest Assured, and Karate. He brings deep expertise in AI and ML-driven testing strategies to drive innovation and efficiency in QA.

**About The Test Tribe:**
The Test Tribe, established in 2018, is the **world's largest software testing community** and an EdTech startup. We empower testing professionals globally with expert courses, memberships, events, and community initiatives, fostering collaboration, learning, and growth. With over **950+ events** and a global reach of **173K+** testers from **130+ countries,** our mission is to provide life-altering growth to every testing professional.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/e/a/2/highres_536504706.jpeg,2026-10-22 15:30:00+00,,Europe/Berlin,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,ai}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/the-test-tribe-frankfurt-meetup/events/316893394/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/the-test-tribe-frankfurt-meetup/events/316893394/,event_316893394@meetup.com,,2026-10-21 22:16:27.132+00,,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,2026-10-22 09:28:23.916645+00,,,,,f,
