6268d23d-22f9-44a8-bdda-9cddfe2b572d,,Hastings to Rye Coastal 22k (Small Group),Come explore my happy place! :-),"**Come explore my happy place! :-)**

We’ll be tackling **Hastings to Rye along the Saxon Shore Way**, one of the UK’s most scenic coastal walks. This linear route is part of the iconic 160-mile long-distance path linking Gravesend to Hastings. Along the way, you’ll enjoy dramatic sandstone cliffs, wild coastal heath, ancient gill woodland, lowland meadows, and sustainably managed farmland — all shaped by the sea over millions of years. Expect a day full of history, nature, and seaside charm.

**Hike Details – Hastings to Rye**

• **Distance:** 12.4 miles
• **Estimated Time:** 5–6 hours
• **Elevation:** 1,614 ft
• **Meeting Point:** London Bridge or Hasting Train Station
• **Cost:** £10 guiding fee
• **Travel:** purchase return ticket with National rail card -£25 open return.

⚠️ **Important: Refund Policy & Weather Notice**

• No refunds will be processed.
• Rain or shine. Spots can be transferred with 48h notice.

There are plenty of opportunities to stop for refreshments along the way, whether in Hastings or Rye. This hike is all about connection and adventure - we’ll keep the group small and friendly so you can enjoy the company and make new friends while soaking in one of the most picturesque coastal walks in the UK.

Once we reach the minimum number of registrations, I’ll set up a WhatsApp group so we can all vote on highlights and share tips for the hike. It’s your chance to connect, plan, and maybe even challenge yourself with the full adventure!

