ec68289e-e22c-4e3f-bf0d-0a33d02a19e7,,"FINAL SPACES! THE CAPE PENINSULA, SOUTH AFRICA (31 OCT - 7 NOV)",Final spaces! (twin share and single occupancy available - please enquire),"**Final spaces! (twin share and single occupancy available - please enquire)**

Join us for an epic week of hiking and exploration on South Africa’s Cape Peninsula, based in Noordhoek, a coastal gem with beachfront accommodation overlooking endless white sand.

*Note: the organiser will arrive in Cape Town 2 days before the trip and anyone is welcome to join early to explore this amazing city!*

**Duration:** 7 nights
**Group size:** 18
**Accommodation:** twin share rooms in private group accommodation (limited single occupancy places available - please enquire)
**Meals:** 7 breakfasts, 7 lunch packs and 4 dinners
**Transport:** Private minibus for our 6 days of activity
**Trip cost:** £875

Our group accommodation, reserved exclusively for us, is situated just below Chapman’s Peak Drive and offers splendid mountain and ocean views — the perfect place to relax and socialise together after a day on the trails.

From this idyllic base, we will hike along rugged mountain ridges and dramatic coastlines, taking in sweeping ocean views and discovering some of the Cape’s most iconic sights.

There’s no shortage of trails to explore, from the cliffs above Chapman’s Peak to the legendary Table Mountain range. Beyond the trails, enjoy a scenic excursion to Cape Point, where the Atlantic and Indian Oceans meet, visit Boulders Beach to see its famous colony of African penguins, and go wine tasting in the surrounding valleys.

Back at our accommodation, meals are prepared in-house by a talented chef known for heartfelt, home-cooked dishes that showcase fresh, locally inspired flavours. Each meal is crafted with care and a touch of sophistication, celebrating South African ingredients and tradition.

Experience an unforgettable week of hiking and adventure in South Africa's Cape Peninsula!

**DIFFICULTY:**

Hikes on this trip are challenging, with some significant elevation gains and steep climbs/descents, and this trip is therefore best suited for fit, experienced hikers. The trails are not technical, but may involve some moderate scrambling and you should be comfortable on rough, rocky, and uneven terrain.

**ITINERARY:**

**Sat 31/10** (-/-/D) - Arrival in Noordhoek.

**Sun 01/11** (B/LP/-) - Hike from Noordhoek to Chapman's Peak and East Fort (11km, 750m up/down).

**Mon 02/11** (B/LP/D) - Hike from Kirstenbosch to Table Mountain via the Skeleton Gorge (10km, 1000m up/800m down).

**Tue 03/11** (B/LP/-) - Two ocean's circuit hike in Cape Point nature reserve (13km, 400m up/down) and visit Boulder's Beach to see the penguins.

**Wed 04/11** (B/LP/D) - Vineyard area walk and visit to one of the Cape's famous wineries.

**Thu 05/11** (B/LP/-) - Echo Valley hike to Boomslang Cave and the Amphitheatre from Kalk Bay (12-15km, 750m up/down).

**Fri 06/11** (B/LP/D) - Hike to be decided — there’s no shortage of incredible trails to choose from! Or enjoy a relaxed day soaking up the sun on the beach.

**Sat 07/11** (B/LP/-) - Trip finishes in Noordhoek.

*This itinerary is subject to change.*

**INCLUDED:**

• Accommodation: 7 nights accommodation in twin or single occupancy rooms
• Meals: 7 breakfasts, 7 lunch packs, 4 dinners
• Epic Adventure Club trip leader
• Transport to/from hikes and sightseeing places (we have the use of a private minivan with driver for our group for our 6 hiking/sightseeing days)
• Full itinerary for our 6 hiking/activity days
• National Park entrance fees (daily conservation fee) for Boulder's Beach and Cape Point (around £35)
• Financial protection in accordance with the Package Travel Law 1992

**NOT INCLUDED:**

• Flights and airport transfers (see below)
• Any other meals not specified. On 3 nights we can enjoy dinner in local restaurants
• Other entrance fees not mentioned above (hike/activity dependent)
• Travel Insurance

**FLIGHTS:**

There are direct flights to Cape Town with British Airways, Virgin Atlantic, and Norse Atlantic Airways (on select days), as well as indirect flights with numerous other airlines.

Our accommodation is about a 50-minute drive from the airport. Those arriving or departing on the same flight can share airport transfers. Taxis are affordable and the Uber/Bolt ride sharing apps are widely used. The accommodation can also organise transfers.

We highly recommend extending your stay with a few days in beautiful Cape Town before or after the trip.

