06e24186-9a18-4f33-99c0-efb5899ce04d,,Autumn colours of the North Downs and the Temple of the winds,WhatsApp Gary 07968585224,"WhatsApp Gary 07968585224
This beautiful hike explores the **northern edge of the South Downs National Park and the Sussex Weald**, following sections of the **Serpent Trail** through some of West Sussex’s finest heathland, woodland and open countryside.
We begin by crossing **Marley Common**, a peaceful mix of broadleaf and chestnut woodland, open heath and grazing land. Now managed by the National Trust, the common is home to **Belted Galloway cattle** and offers a wonderfully rural start to the walk.
From here, we continue towards **Fernhurst** before climbing steeply towards the **Temple of the Winds**. The effort is rewarded with sweeping views across the **South Downs**, and on a clear day it may even be possible to see as far as the **English Channel**.
Our route then takes us across **Black Down**, the highest point in the historic county of Sussex. The area has strong literary connections with **Alfred, Lord Tennyson**, who bought nearby land in the 19th century and built **Aldworth House** as his summer home.
From Black Down, we continue through the rolling Sussex countryside towards the attractive market town of **Haslemere**, where the hike finishes.
Afterwards, you are welcome to join us for a well-earned drink in a local pub before catching the train back to London.

**🕘 Schedule & Meeting Info**

• **Meeting Time:** 09:00 at London Waterloo Station, underneath the main clock. *(alternatively you can meet us at the hike start point)*
• **Trains:** 09:30 from London Waterloo to Haslemere, arriving at approximately 10:20. Journey time approximately 50 mins.
• **Tickets:** Return ticket to Haslemere
• **Hike Start:** 10:25 at Haslemere Station
• **Lunch:** pack lunch
• **Estimated finish:** 17:30 at Haslemere Station
• **Return to London:** Regular trains to London Waterloo

📍 **Hike Overview**

• **Grade:** Intermediate **🥾🥾**
• **Hiking time:** Approx 6 hours, excluding breaks
• **Distance:** 19km / 12 miles
• **Ascent:** Approx 600m
• **Terrain:** Woodland, heathland and countryside tracks with several steep hills and climbs
• **Pace:** Steady with regular breaks
• **Hike Leader:** Gary 07968585224

🎒 **What to Bring**
**✅** Hiking boots or sturdy hiking shoes ✅ Waterproof jacket ✅ Suitable layers for the weather and conditions ✅ Packed lunch & water ✅ Return train ticket to Haslemere

💬 **What to Expect**
Our hikes are social, inclusive, and fun. Expect a welcoming community of Londoners, expats, solo walkers, professionals, and nature lovers. Most people join solo – and leave with new friends.
🧭 **Qualified, Insured Hike Leaders**
All GO London events are led by qualified, experienced, and fully insured hike leaders, trained in outdoor safety, navigation, and group management.

✅ **RSVP Now**
Spaces are limited – RSVP “Yes” to secure your place.
Full event details, reminders, and updates will be emailed in advance.
