0543a81d-71ce-4198-952e-0e6668a5e612,,Nobody Asked for the Cookie Banner: The Mistake We Can’t Afford with AI,"Last month our founder, Sandra Gonzalez (https://lnkd.in/p/ejjWC6fG), delivered a thought-provoking keynote at The Barbican for The Flux Convergence conference. She is bringing the extended version…","Last month our founder, Sandra Gonzalez (https://lnkd.in/p/ejjWC6fG), delivered a thought-provoking keynote at The Barbican for The Flux Convergence conference. She is bringing the extended version this talk to the UX for Change community.

Curious about the title? Here is the the premise. No law has ever required a cookie banner. The rules asked for informed consent and left the interface to us, and what our design profession built, collectively, is the most disliked pattern on the web. This talk is about what happened and why it can be happening again right now, as the EU AI Act starts to be rolled out. Last time the worst case scenario was a better-targeted advert. This time the stakes are much higher. Sandra will walk you through six real, documented cases and show how each one maps to a law built to prevent these type of cases to happen again, and which of those protections are already in force and which won’t arrive until 2027 or later.

This won’t be a lecture you sit through politely. It’s a provocation our founder invites the community to wrestle with, because the UX community is well positioned to be at the forefront of not making the same mistakes.

Come for the talk. Stay for the conversation.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/3/7/a/highres_536518234.jpeg,2026-11-17 17:30:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Rivington Place,"Rivington Place, 1 Rivington Pl, London EC2A 3BA, UK",London,7aa69eeb-df8c-40ae-b929-a4324f936266,"{technology,ai}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/ux-for-change-london/events/316909771/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/ux-for-change-london/events/316909771/,event_316909771@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.493162+00,,,,,f,GB
62595cec-7e28-4098-9869-8df9b1d3e042,,DevFest 2026 Ahlen ONLINE,DevFest 2026 Ahlen,"DevFest 2026 Ahlen
Build, secure, scale: Developers and builders in the agentic era
This DevFest season we invite you to reflect on some major shifts in the developer landscape. The role of professional developers is evolving from writing to reviewing code and orchestrating autonomous agents. You can do more, faster, with models and tools that are getting more and more powerful. At the same time, AI is opening the doors for everyone to be a solution builder. It means more people can solve more problems, bringing more diverse ideas to life than ever before.

""Builders"" use their skills and AI assistance to build apps, automate, optimize workflows and create solutions for any industry. They use developer tools but can work in different roles including product management or design. Gartner predicts that 80% of technology products and services will soon be built by people who are not professional software developers. In this world, a secure-by-default mindset is more important than ever. So is choosing the right models, platform and tools that match your needs and goals.

DevFest is the world's largest community-driven tech conference, bringing together developers and builders to learn, build and connect https://youtu.be/T8RBES766fk?si=i_AdripqRuqQZ7pg
This is a hybrid event. Join the event virtually at https://gdg.community.dev/events/details/google-gdg-ahlen-presents-devfest-2026-ahlen-online-2/
or in person at

Initiative Bürgerzentrum Schuhfabrik e.V. - 7 Königstraße, Ahlen 59227

Agenda

12:00 PM: Speaker Sathyaram Sannasi: Anatomy of a Data Agent: What's Actually Inside an Agent That Queries Your Data

12:45 PM: Speaker David Aniebo: From Clicks to Tool Calls: Building Agent-Ready Web Applications with WebMCP

AI agents are becoming capable of doing more than generating text; they can search, make decisions, and take actions on behalf of users. This creates a new challenge for web developers: how should web applications be designed when an AI agent becomes another type of user?

For years, websites have been built around human interaction: users navigate pages, click buttons, fill out forms, and complete workflows through visual interfaces. AI agents, however, need more reliable ways to understand what an application can do and invoke those capabilities.

In this session, we’ll explore how to build agent-ready web applications using modern Web APIs and WebMCP, an emerging web standard that enables websites to expose structured tools that AI agents can discover and invoke.

Through a practical example, we’ll transform a conventional web application into one that can support both human users and AI agents. We’ll examine how to design meaningful tools, define structured inputs and outputs, handle authentication and authorization, introduce user confirmation for sensitive actions, and build secure boundaries around agent-driven operations.

We’ll also look at challenges such as prompt injection, unpredictable agent behavior, error handling, and evaluating whether agents can reliably complete real-world workflows.

The goal is not to build another chatbot. It is to understand how the Web Platform is evolving for an agentic world and give developers a practical framework for building applications that are ready for both humans and machines.

Speakers

Sathyaram Sannasi

Sathyaram Sannasi is a Google Developer Expert and a data practitioner specializing in using Data and AI/ML for business outcomes primarily on Google Cloud Platform. As a freelancer, he advises and implements solutions that transform data into decisions and products.

David Aniebo - Greenplaces (Software engineer)

David Aniebo is a Software Engineer. He focuses on crafting high-performing and scalable solutions that exceed both business and user expectations. He continually seeks to enhance his skills and deepen his knowledge of software development through various courses and practical experience.

Host

Anna Muzykina - GDG Ahlen Organizer (Founder CTO & CEO @ Proofa)

I’m a dedicated Developer with a strong focus on community building and empowering women in technology. As the GDG Organizer for Ahlen and Münster, I actively foster tech communities and mentor women entering the industry. As a Women in Data Science (WiDS), I provide guidance and support to aspiring women technologists.
With a deep expertise in Dart, Firebase, and AI ecosystems, I specia…

