9358a9ab-a2bc-4c7d-9bdc-408205ce1b8b,,Teach the Nation: Introduction to Data Management,About this workshop:,"**About this workshop:**
Join us for a practical introduction to how data is stored, managed, and used in the real world.
You'll explore core concepts around data architecture and get hands-on with SQL (Structured Query Language), learning how to query and update information using a database system.
Whether you're curious about IT, data analytics, or business systems, this session will help you build a strong foundation in data management – no prior experience needed.

**In this workshop, you'll learn:**

• What data management means and how it works
• How to perform basic SQL operations (CRUD: Create, Read, Update, Delete)
• The difference between SQL and NoSQL systems
• How data supports business decisions

**Who should attend?**

• Anyone interested in understanding how data is stored, managed, and used
• Individuals looking to broaden their digital and technical knowledge
• Those curious about databases and keen to learn something new

**What you'll need:**

• Laptop or desktop computer
• Stable internet connection
• Web browser (e.g. Chrome, Edge, Firefox)

This workshop is structured in a way that's easy to understand for any background and level of knowledge
