92af918d-de2a-4485-85d3-4b7e8c364bf3,,The Ugly Stories of Business Transformations (and What to Do About Them),From Car Crashes to Train Wrecks: The Ugly Stories of Business Transformations (and What to Do About Them),"**From Car Crashes to Train Wrecks: The Ugly Stories of Business Transformations (and What to Do About Them)**

Most conferences celebrate success stories and often paint the grass green.

This session keeps us all grounded in the realities of change. It's messy. It's thankless. It's sometimes plain ugly. But only when we recognise the problems, we can work on the effective solutions.

Every year, organisations spend billions on transformation programmes, agile transformations, digital initiatives, operating model redesigns, AI adoption, and culture change efforts. Yet many fail to deliver the promised outcomes. Some quietly disappear. Some survive long enough to be declared a success before slowly evaporating. Others become expensive exercises in organisational theatre that consume energy, attention, and goodwill without creating lasting change.

**Why is it so difficult to make change stick?**

Why do so many well-funded and well-intentioned transformation efforts struggle to achieve their goals?

Why do organisations repeatedly encounter the same obstacles despite decades of accumulated experience, frameworks, methodologies, and expert consultants?

**And most importantly: what can we learn from these stories?**

In this special LeanTech Circles panel discussion, we will explore the uncomfortable realities of business transformation. Rather than focusing on polished case studies and success narratives, we will examine real experiences of initiatives that underperformed, stalled, lost momentum, or failed entirely.

Together, we will explore recurring patterns, including:

• Transformation as theatre rather than genuine change
• Leadership behaviours that unintentionally undermine change
• The gap between strategy and execution
• Organisational inertia and resistance
• Why adoption remains harder than implementation
• The challenge of sustaining improvements over time
• The hidden costs of large-scale transformation programmes
• How organisations create complexity faster than they eliminate it
• What successful change efforts do differently

This session is not about assigning blame. It is about learning from reality.

Through candid discussion, audience participation, and collective reflection, we will identify the patterns that repeatedly derail transformation efforts and explore practical approaches for creating change that survives beyond the launch event, steering committee, or programme closure report.

**Panel discussion**

For this session, we are bringing very experienced change professionals who will share their experience of the challenges and the solutions.

• **Karl Scotland** : 20+ years as an advocate of Lean and Agile approaches. Karl helps businesses become Learning Organisations through outcome-oriented, continuous transformation, engaging everyone, everywhere.
• **Morten Elvang** : Managing Partner of Thinking Twice Works. or more than two decades, his work has revolved around a deceptively simple problem: how do organizations keep acting with strategic intent when reality refuses to stand still?
• **John Clifford** : StrataMapping inventor, StrataTree® creator. Leading organizations from chaos to delivery with effective process and planning.

**Accessing the meetup:**
Please note that, following some disruption at past meetups, we have changed our policy for accessing our meetups. From now on, attendees will need a valid Zoom account (a free account is OK) and must be logged in to access our meetups.
We believe that, for professionals in our line of work, you probably already have a Zoom account, so it shouldn't be an issue for you to join.
For the disruptors, who access sessions from anonymous web links, it will create an additional hurdle to access, and we can more effectively report and ban them.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792621067/orbit/event-covers/sources/vvplj1ug3qdyoamqt0xb.jpg,2026-10-23 11:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,entrepreneurship,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/leantech/events/315085223/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/leantech/events/315085223/,event_315085223@meetup.com,,2026-10-23 03:23:03.153+00,,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,2026-10-23 03:23:43.045297+00,,,,,f,
