04f94d04-183e-44bc-afc2-bb804fd5e3fa,,Play Badminton for fun... social badminton with a competitive edge!,"Welcome to Grove Park Badminton! Come and play at our bi-weekly sessions, please RSVP your attendance and bring along your racket.","Welcome to Grove Park Badminton! Come and play at our bi-weekly sessions, please RSVP your attendance and bring along your racket.
**MIDDLE INTERMEDIATE LEVEL AND ABOVE ONLY (INCLUDING VISITORS)** - Sorry, NO beginners, this club is not suitable for players who cannot serve, smash, hold a strategic rally and clear a shot from the back of the court. We play with quality, feather shuttlecocks only. Please do not attend Badminton if you are feeling unwell at all, or if you or anyone in your household currently has symptoms of any virus.

**INFORMATION:** Sessions cost: £13 for regulars and 'First Timers'* (cash or bank transfer, always pay before you play) for 2 hours. Please do not attend unless you have RSVP to reserve a space. If circumstances change, update your RSVP 24 hours before the session so others can fill the space. *If you do not attend or cancel after midday on the day of the session, then you will be expected to pay the full £13 cancellation fee on your next visit.*
*First Timers - you will receive a message with bank details to make your first payment of £13. Failure to send payment by midday of the day of your session will result in your name being moved to the 'Not Going' list, this in turn means if there is a 'WaitList', then another player will automatically fill your space.

**TRAVEL:** Free car park and main entrance accessed via Staveley Road. Walk through the side gate, towards sports hall and entrance is on your right hand side. Buses: E3 bus stop opposite the entrance. Chiswick Station: South West Trains - 7 minutes walk Please ring if you get lost - 07811 331030.

**ATTENDANCE, LATE DROP-OUTS AND NO-SHOWS:** Regular players: First no-show - You'll be expected to pay full price for the missed session. Second no-show - £15.00 penalty Third no-show - you will be removed from the group. This is to ensure basic courtesy to those playing and those waiting who can attend and want to play! First Timers: First no-show - you will be removed from the group.

**INSURANCE:** Any injury or loss incurred will be the individual’s responsibilities. The club will hold no responsibility or liability for any loss or injury. Because of this we encourage you to warm up appropriately, wear appropriate clothing including non-marking footwear and STRETCH off before and AFTER the games.
We hope you’ll have fun and an enjoyable time at this session! **PLAYING BADMINTON IS A GREAT WAY TO GET FIT AND HAVE FUN!!!**

**Note:** Please ensure you have all you belongings (and rubbish) before leaving at the end of the evening. There are bins situated just outside the hall for any rubbish. Thank you.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792812087/orbit/event-covers/sources/yzmvuwqk5buczdmcg3ww.jpg,2026-11-20 20:00:00+00,2026-11-20 22:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Grove Park Badminton Club,"Chiswick School Sports Hall, Free Car Park and entrance off Staveley Road",London,c06699ed-62e0-4957-bcb4-080c5271da9a,"{sport,fitness,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/grove-park-badminton-club/events/316408217/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-24 03:21:20.750761+00,source:cba1b9d2-d09d-4c19-a89e-50bdbe5525a0,https://www.meetup.com/grove-park-badminton-club/events/316408217/,event_316408217@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:20:38.34+00,,2026-10-24 03:21:20.750761+00,2026-10-28 03:21:15.930389+00,,,meetup:grove-park-badminton-club:play badminton for fun social badminton with a competitive edge,"Every week on Friday until December 20, 2030",f,GB
d0305745-7846-4514-95af-81ef18fddd5e,,Mushroom University,Develop skills on how to identify fungi in these co-learning identification sessions with Fabrice Boltho and friends.,"Learn how to identify fungi at our identification sessions with Fabrice Boltho and friends. Bring your specimens and photos and we’ll teach you how to identify local fungi. This is a co-learning space of mixed abilities.

Drop-in activity. All abilities welcome.

Time: 5.30-7.30pm

Cost: Non members £5, SLBI members by donation. You can become one for £25/year. (https://www.slbi.org.uk/join/)

These sessions are focused on responsible collecting for education and not oriented towards harvesting for food. British Mycological Society has guidance on picking fungi whichcan be found here (https://www.britmycolsoc.org.uk/conservation.html)

**Access**

Our building is not wheelchair accessible and the workshop is on the first floor. Please contact us at info@slbi.org.uk if you have any access needs.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792660156/orbit/event-covers/sources/cpqp3urhr9epguatbngk.jpg,2026-11-30 17:30:00+00,2026-11-30 19:30:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,The South London Botanical Institute,323 Norwood Road,London,c17c4a77-8c19-42da-a932-7fd57ad27fc7,"{gaming,arts,hobbies,socialising}",,external,https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/mushroom-university-tickets-2001048482879,Register on Eventbrite,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 09:09:07.508932+00,source:692118d3-2638-432e-9973-25e783168a55,https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/mushroom-university-tickets-2001048482879,eventbrite-2001048482879,,2026-10-22 09:08:39.438+00,,2026-10-22 09:09:07.508932+00,2026-10-22 09:09:17.169824+00,51.442086,-0.105341,eventbrite-series-2001048100736,,f,GB
