5a1197bb-0f5b-470c-bd8b-97a4fbd014d5,,🎉 Friday Night Zen Social at the National Gallery + After Party! 🎉,🎉 Friday Night Social at the National Gallery London 🎉,"🎉 Friday Night Social at the National Gallery London 🎉

**Art. Connection. Adventure.**
Join us for an unforgettable evening at one of the world’s most iconic art museums—the National Gallery in Trafalgar Square! With its late-night opening hours and legendary collection, this is your chance to explore masterpieces, meet new people, and enjoy a relaxed social vibe in the heart of London 🌆.

🖼️ About the National Gallery

Founded in 1824, the National Gallery houses over 2,300 paintings spanning from the 13th to the early 20th century. From da Vinci’s ethereal brushwork to Van Gogh’s swirling sunflowers, this museum is a treasure trove of Western European art. And the best part? Admission is free! 🆓
Whether you're an art aficionado or just curious, the Gallery offers a welcoming space to wander, reflect, and connect. It’s a place where history meets inspiration—and tonight, it meets community.

🗓️ Event Schedule

**6:45pm – Meet & Mingle**
📍 INSIDE the Sainsbury Wing entrance in the Foyer next to one of the thick giant columns.
We’ll gather here for 30 minutes (6:45-7:15PM) to chat, introduce ourselves, and kick off the evening with our icebreaker:
**“What kind of artwork are you drawn to?”** 🎭
No name tags—just good conversation and friendly faces.
**7:15pm – Leave meeting point to Explore the Gallery**
🎨 We’ll head inside to explore these stunning rooms:

• Room 32: Carracci, Caravaggio, Guercino
• Room 34: Reynolds, Gainsborough, Turner, Constable
• Room 45: Van Gogh 🌻

Feel free to roam in small groups—if you get separated, check these rooms to reconnect.
**8:15pm – Reconvene AT ORIGINAL MEETING POINT**
Then in your groups make your own way to the optional after-party:
**8:30pm – Afterparty at ZEBRANOS IN SOHO🍸**
18 Greek St, London W1D 4DS
Let the social vibes continue at a lively spot for drinks, music, and more mingling.
Mention ZEN on entry. Bring ID
Route: https://maps.app.goo.gl/9FhUkidjkcCKJGmA8?g_st=ac

🎟️ Tickets & Entry

This is a **free event**, but you’ll need a ticket to enter the Gallery.
Grab yours from the National Gallery website (https://www.nationalgallery.org.uk/) before they run out!
If tickets are unavailable, don’t worry—we’ll share a group ticket in the WhatsApp group and Meetup page 📲.

👗 Dress Code & Essentials

• **Smart Casual** (no athletic track suits or sports trainers)
• **Bring your ID** for the bar
• A curious mind and a friendly spirit 💫

Ready to mix art with social magic? Let’s make Friday night a masterpiece 🖌️💃

**Some Tips:**

1. **Let’s all commit to updating our RSVPs if plans change**—it helps us plan better and ensures great attendance for everyone. If you RSVP “yes” but don’t attend and don’t update your RSVP, you may be removed from the group to keep things fair. No stress, though—you can rejoin for a small £10 fee! Just send me a DM, and I’ll share the PayPal details to get you back in.
2. **Turn Up on Time at the start!** This helps the quality of the event and helps you.
3. If you are struggling with the **app**, use the web page instead, that's what I use.
4. **Attendee Numbers & Guest Lists:** We have this event listed at least on two groups and the guest list includes attendees from all. You can see the list of attendees here:
https://www.meetup.com/zensingles/
https://www.meetup.com/cityzenlondon/
https://www.meetup.com/LoveLife
1. **Join our** **social media**:
**Instagram**: https://www.instagram.com/cityzen.london/
**X:** https://x.com/CityZenLondon
1. **Our WhatsApp group:** [See private comment in the comments section below]. We have a few rules including no ads, no DMs unless recipient is in the ""Direct Messaging List"" or risk removal and £10 rejoin fee.
2. **Support Our Amazing London Event Hosts! 🙌**
Our incredible crew of hosts is the heartbeat of London’s buzzing meetup scene, bringing people together for unforgettable experiences that spark connection, growth, and fun! 🌟 From museum adventures to flirty dating mixers, these rockstar hosts pour their energy, time, and passion into creating events that level up your social and communication skills. But hosting isn’t easy—it takes resources, effort, and heart. 💖
Please consider supporting our hosts with a donation to keep the good vibes flowing and help us make London the ultimate social hub! 🚀 Below, meet our hosts for this event and see how you can chip in to fuel their amazing work.

**Disclaimer, Liability Waiver & Media Consent**
By attending this event, you acknowledge and agree to the following:
**Organiser Identity** – The organiser operates under the community name **“ZEN”**, which is used as an alias for privacy and branding purposes. By joining, you understand that “ZEN” refers to the organiser and/or designated hosts of this event. **Assumption of Risk** – You understand and accept that participation in any social, recreational, or group activity involves inherent risks, including but not limited to personal injury, illness, property damage, or other…",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/0/a/2/highres_535872450.jpeg,2027-01-01 18:45:00+00,2027-01-01 21:45:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,The National Gallery Sainsbury Wing,"Trafalgar Square,",London WC2N 5DN,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,socialising,arts,fitness,travel}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/cityzenlondon/events/316983644/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-26 03:22:56.772649+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/cityzenlondon/events/316983644/,event_316983644@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-26 03:22:56.772649+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.486349+00,,,meetup:cityzenlondon:friday night zen social at the national gallery after party,"Every 1st Friday of the month until April 2, 2027",f,GB
4450f3e1-f333-4237-807f-ef78f3d19338,,FREE HIKE - Surrey Hills Area Circular Hike 12 miles. FREE to join picturesque..,Please 🙏 Read Details Carefully to avoid Disappointment.,"**Please 🙏 Read Details Carefully to avoid Disappointment.**

This is a Free Hiking event.

You only pay for your return train tickets with groupsave its around £12 or £13.

However there are rules on this meetup
group so please read them carefully to avoid being banned from this meetup group.

**This event has been posted on 2 other meetup groups. So you will see more faces from other meetup groups joining us at this event.**

**To join WhatsApp Group txt.**

**07590 919391 via** WhatsApp Only....

One of the most popular Hiking Events In the Surrey Hills Area. And one of the most beautiful Hikes that can be done in the Surrey Hills Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty.

Not to be missed. This event is only done once per year. We will not repeat it again for at least another 12 months.

Full of natural beauty and natural history. Very beautiful Scenic picturesque views.
Bring your best 📷 camera and dress appropriately for the weather forecast. Hiking shoes are absolutely necessary.

Please read carefully and pay attention to details.

**Meeting Point.**

Meet under the main Central Clock at
London Waterloo station 8.20 am prompt - for the 9.00am train to guildford. Try to get there earlier than 8:20 am so you will have time to find the group.

From Guildford Station we will walk The North Downs Way to Martha’s Hill and more. Enjoy the Outdoors. Relaxed pace) (2 miles per hour).

.............

We will meet under the Main Central Clock. WhatsApp group communication is important so you can find the meeting point and the group.

**By purchasing the Train tickets in groups of 3 or more people together we will save 30% on Train tickets.**

**Your return group train travel will be approx. £12 or £14 per person from London Waterloo Station.**

I will update this Via WhatsApp nearer the date with any changes.

£14 each. Group Return Train ticket from London Waterloo- to- Guildford.

For the purchase of train tickets Please bring your money in cash only. No Bank transfer is allowed. No time.

You can also meet us at Guildford train station at 9.30 or travel by car and park in various paid car parks in Guildford. This is down to you to find and meet us outside Guildford Train Station at 9.35 am Promptly. There are FREE car parks on the roads 5 to 10 minutes walking distance from Guildford train station.

Planned arrival time back to London Waterloo station will be between 6:30 to 7:30 pm.

Please join the whatsApp Group. So you can communicate with each other on the day of the event and share photos.

Whether you are a serious hiker or just want something light and easy this hike has it all, from a gentle stroll along the River Way, to challenging hill climbs with fantastic views. We will not leave anyone behind and you will have frequent water stops and photo opportunities. .

Guildford is a beautifully charming town in Surrey, The hike will take us out along the River way, before heading up to Chantries Wood, Chilworth Gunpowder Mills, and back down to newlands corner with fantastic views across the Surrey Hills & The North Downs Way, before returning we will be able to visit St Martha’s Hill Church.

Our hike will take us through beautiful countryside, expansive open woodlands along the River Way. Guildford is famous for its historic buildings and cobbled street, of which we will see many, there are truly breathtaking views from St Martha’s Hill for as far as you can see.

.............

**Difficulty level**

**Intermediate Level**

Hiking time.
6 hours moving time and maybe 7.5 hours with the added breaks.
Distance 12 miles Approx.

**Food.**

We will stop during the hike for a snack lunch so please bring packed lunches and drink. Water stops will be frequent please bring 2 litres of water.

**What to bring.**

Suitable hiking clothes & footwear - ideally hiking shoes. Hat gloves if cold, water proof jacket and trousers. Dress appropriately for the weather.
Hiking boots are advisable. Some areas during the hike will be dense and muddy.

Clarification on the weather will be posted Via WhatsApp nearer to the walk.

Probability of rainfall is not important. Volume of rainfall expected is more important information than probability of rainfall. This event will not be cancelled regardless unless there is an emergency situation.

**Terms and Conditions**

