8ee22a51-a727-4135-945c-517e0d2aa637,,AUTUMN COLOURS HIKES PART 3: Leith Hill,"It's Autumn, it's romantic, it is still sunny, the woods are slowly changing colours so let's get sweaty in these beautiful woods and climb a few hills along with some doggy and dodgy friends! If…","It's Autumn, it's romantic, it is still sunny, the woods are slowly changing colours so let's get sweaty in these beautiful woods and climb a few hills along with some doggy and dodgy friends! If you don't have a loved one to enjoy the colours of autumn, well, take your dog or your friends so that you have someone to cuddle...

This is going to be the first edition of a few hikes where you will be able to bring your dog or your dodgy friends or where you will be able to hike with these lovely pets if you do not have one, obviously if you are allergic or if dogs worry you, I would not recommend. BUT for those who just want a nice hike with some lovely hikers and their furry friends, this is the one you want to join. People have been asking to bring their dogs for quite a while now so why not give it a go?!Our lovely Zoe is a regular puppy on our walk and everyone is crazy about her.
I am not expecting hundreds of dogs so this will just be a non-pets discriminatory hike with some gorgeous woodlands dressing up slowly for the autumn...

You do not need to have a dog to join this trip though but only need to love them or at least not have an issue with it as there will be more hikers than creatures...

Leith Hill is the second highest point in Southeast England, I will walk you through woods, more woods and some woods till you get sick of it!
It is beautiful though, take you boyfriend, your wife or your fiance and enjoy a time in the forest by my side! Woodlands in the UK are absolutely stunning, it sometimes feels as if you were in Canada or other beautiful places.

When we reach the summit, you will be able to climb Leith Hill Tower, an 18th Century Gothic building for a small fee, if you wish. It is claimed that on a clear day, you will be able to see 13 counties from the hilltop.

Come on, let's burn some calories before Christmas or just use this trip as an excuse to gather together and have some fun in the woods not too far from London.

This hike is not hard but there will be a couple of short steep inclines, most of you should be fine😄

INFORMATION:

Distance:12 miles/18km
Difficulty: Average, a couple of steep hills to climb

MEETING POINT:

08:15 am by the ticket office in the main hall at London Victoria station.

COST:

£17 via PayPal for the guide's fee

The fee is non-refundable, but you may resell and you can try to find someone to take your place.

About £12 in cash for the train.

Doggies travel for free, your dodgy friends don't.

PLEASE PM ME IF YOU BRING YOUR DOG, SO THAT I ROUGHLY KNOW HOW MANY WILL JOIN AND LET ME KNOW IF YOU HAVE AN ISSUE WITH OTHER PEOPLE PETTING IT,
IT IS YOUR RESPONSABILITY TO BRING FOOD AND WATER FOR YOUR PET.
Also please, only bring dogs that behave with other dogs and other people to avoid some unnecessary issues...

We will buy a group return ticket at the station for those who wish to get a 34% group discount.

INCLUDED:

Guided hike

A great time with lovely people

A lot of sweat and a forced diet to be ready for the summer

NOT INCLUDED:

Train

Anything not mentioned above

WHAT TO BRING:

Waterproof shoes for the hike, preferably hiking shoes, otherwise good trainers;

Weather appropriate clothes, including waterproofs if there is a chance of rain;

Water bottle;

Packed lunch and snacks.

Food and drinks for your pet

ATTENTION:

Our trips will not be cancelled due to weather conditions so please ensure that you do wear and carry appropriate clothing. 😄

POLICIES:

1: This group is designed for the pleasure and enjoyment of all of us, we do not accept any derogatory comments or behaviours towards anyone. Racism, discrimination and other unacceptable behaviours will only lead to your rejection of any of our trips and this is without exception. Everyone is welcome, we have religious and non-religious people, gay, straight, bisexual people, all shades and colours or nationalities, people of all ages, sex and political beliefs and mutual respect is the fundamental spirit of this group.

2: Our trips are only refundable up to 30 days before departure, if you wish to cancel after that, you will be offered a transfer to another trip for the same price or you may resell your slot to somebody else.

3: If we do cancel the entirety of the trip on our site, you will be fully refunded.
4:In the eventuality that our transport are delayed, or cancelled which is out of my control, I do not pay for taxis or alternative route, if this happens, you will be able to claim delay repay from the train companies who will reimburse your train ticket and some eventual costs occurred. By signing up to my events, you agree to this.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/c/1/4/highres_498695860.jpeg,2026-11-15 08:15:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Victoria Station,Victoria Train Station,London,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/jons-trails/events/316353797/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/jons-trails/events/316353797/,event_316353797@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.486349+00,,,,,f,GB
99c1e7fb-bcf8-42e8-a73b-1d00a81ca43b,,"Happy valley circular walk - extended version, approx 15 Miles","This is a countryside walk within the borders of Greater London, with remarkably unspoiled countryside considering its within London zone 6. This is a moderate walk with some steep hills. It might…","This is a countryside walk within the borders of Greater London, with remarkably unspoiled countryside considering its within London zone 6. This is a moderate walk with some steep hills. It might be muddy so wear appropriate footwear with good grip.

Due to the short days during the winter we will have to walk at a brisk pace of 2. 5 - 3mph, and there are some steep hills, so this walk is not suitable for beginner hikers.

Walk starts at 09.25 at Coulsdon South Station. Walk ends around 4.30pm at Coulsdon South railway Station. Get the 08.55 train from London Bridge to Coulsdon South arr. 09:22. Day return cost £11 with railcard or one day travelcard or use oyster card zone 6. Pub stop for lunch, bring a packed lunch as there might not be time to order food. *How to join?* - The walk is entirely free of charge; - You only arrange for your own travel and pub expenses; - Understand our terms and conditions below (the ""IMPORTANT"" part); - Understand how to stay safe outdoors, as you will be responsible for yourself. See our quick safety tips: http://www.meetup.com/Free-Outdoor-Trips-From-London/about/ - Please answer the RSVP question; Guests with missing or incorrect answers will be removed from the list! *What to bring* - Plenty of water, 1-2 litres recommended - Enough snacks and packed lunch to keep you energized along the walk - Extra snacks and an extra packed lunch just in case - Rainproof (ideally waterproof) clothing, sturdy shoes/boots you don't mind getting muddy - Spare socks - Walking poles and/or an umbrella :-) - Yourself... - ...and your camera! - Cash for train ticket - Cash for pub at the end of the walk? Feel free to ask any questions in the comments section! IMPORTANT Please bear in mind this is a free of charge, self-guided trip with a hobby group. It is not organized by a business nor any entity with commercial purposes. Any trip details, travel advice, route planning, instructions and other content in our group merely represent our shared personal knowledge, research and suggestions as outdoor enthusiasts. As this is no business, there is no ""product"", ""service"" or ""package"" and also no ""tour guide"", ""operator"" or ""walk leader"". Each participant is responsible for their own safety. Even if some of us are very experienced walking outdoors, nobody assumes responsibility for any kind of injury, damage or loss that may happen. Despite this, we take extreme precautions and all trips we plan are very safe, fun, highly educational and popular. Our experienced members volunteer their time and effort to shape a pleasant and quality adventure for everyone :-) By participating you acknowledge and agree with this disclaimer. Here are our tips on staying safe during outdoor trips: http://www.meetup.com/Free-Outdoor-Trips-From-London/about/ TRAVEL, ACCOMMODATION, INSURANCE Although we provide detailed suggestions, each participant is expected to arrange their own travel - this gives everyone the freedom and choice. Anyone interested in travel or outdoor insurance should also arrange this on their own. As mentioned above we always take extreme precautions, but some people may still feel safer if covered. As most of our trips are confirmed or postponed very close to the event date - heavily depending on the weather forecasts - we advise not to buy this until the last minute. People getting tickets from the same station are encouraged to meet early on the day to benefit from discounts such as GroupSave. Any questions, feel free to ask below or send a private message!",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/0/f/c/highres_494004828.jpeg,2026-11-08 08:30:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,London Bridge Station,London Bridge Station,London,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/free-outdoor-trips-from-london/events/316999911/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/free-outdoor-trips-from-london/events/316999911/,event_316999911@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.486349+00,,,,,f,GB
2bbe3025-b3a6-4818-987f-0d65ed8ee984,,Play Badminton for fun... social badminton with a competitive edge!,"Welcome to Grove Park Badminton! Come and play at our bi-weekly sessions, please RSVP your attendance and bring along your racket.","Welcome to Grove Park Badminton! Come and play at our bi-weekly sessions, please RSVP your attendance and bring along your racket.
**MIDDLE INTERMEDIATE LEVEL AND ABOVE ONLY (INCLUDING VISITORS)** - Sorry, NO beginners, this club is not suitable for players who cannot serve, smash, hold a strategic rally and clear a shot from the back of the court. We play with quality, feather shuttlecocks only. Please do not attend Badminton if you are feeling unwell at all, or if you or anyone in your household currently has symptoms of any virus.

**INFORMATION:** Sessions cost: £13 for regulars and 'First Timers'* (cash or bank transfer, always pay before you play) for 2 hours. Please do not attend unless you have RSVP to reserve a space. If circumstances change, update your RSVP 24 hours before the session so others can fill the space. *If you do not attend or cancel after midday on the day of the session, then you will be expected to pay the full £13 cancellation fee on your next visit.*
*First Timers - you will receive a message with bank details to make your first payment of £13. Failure to send payment by midday of the day of your session will result in your name being moved to the 'Not Going' list, this in turn means if there is a 'WaitList', then another player will automatically fill your space.

**TRAVEL:** Free car park and main entrance accessed via Staveley Road. Walk through the side gate, towards sports hall and entrance is on your right hand side. Buses: E3 bus stop opposite the entrance. Chiswick Station: South West Trains - 7 minutes walk Please ring if you get lost - 07811 331030.

**ATTENDANCE, LATE DROP-OUTS AND NO-SHOWS:** Regular players: First no-show - You'll be expected to pay full price for the missed session. Second no-show - £15.00 penalty Third no-show - you will be removed from the group. This is to ensure basic courtesy to those playing and those waiting who can attend and want to play! First Timers: First no-show - you will be removed from the group.

**INSURANCE:** Any injury or loss incurred will be the individual’s responsibilities. The club will hold no responsibility or liability for any loss or injury. Because of this we encourage you to warm up appropriately, wear appropriate clothing including non-marking footwear and STRETCH off before and AFTER the games.
We hope you’ll have fun and an enjoyable time at this session! **PLAYING BADMINTON IS A GREAT WAY TO GET FIT AND HAVE FUN!!!**

**Note:** Please ensure you have all you belongings (and rubbish) before leaving at the end of the evening. There are bins situated just outside the hall for any rubbish. Thank you.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792812087/orbit/event-covers/sources/yzmvuwqk5buczdmcg3ww.jpg,2026-11-06 20:00:00+00,2026-11-06 22:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Grove Park Badminton Club,"Chiswick School Sports Hall, Free Car Park and entrance off Staveley Road",London,c06699ed-62e0-4957-bcb4-080c5271da9a,"{sport,fitness,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/grove-park-badminton-club/events/316408215/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-24 03:21:20.750761+00,source:cba1b9d2-d09d-4c19-a89e-50bdbe5525a0,https://www.meetup.com/grove-park-badminton-club/events/316408215/,event_316408215@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:20:38.34+00,,2026-10-24 03:21:20.750761+00,2026-10-28 03:21:15.930389+00,,,meetup:grove-park-badminton-club:play badminton for fun social badminton with a competitive edge,"Every week on Friday until December 20, 2030",f,GB
36fa9fe2-d90a-455f-a438-65d1b80d1540,,Addison Exiles Weekly Club Night,"Welcome to our regular club night session for intermediate level players and above! Sessions cost £10 for Members, and £12 for Guests; please contact an organiser to discuss becoming a Member.…","Welcome to our regular club night session for intermediate level players and above! Sessions cost £10 for Members, and £12 for Guests; please contact an organiser to discuss becoming a Member. Session are held at:

