7b2c73c6-cd64-4d74-8c6b-40aff94ce26d,,Nordic Walking Brockwell Park,Ready to get outside? Our Friday morning Nordic Walk in Brockwell Park is back!,"Ready to get outside? Our Friday morning Nordic Walk in Brockwell Park is back!

At this moment we can meet with up to 30 people (of more than two households) to do outdoor exercise and walks. However, i like to keep our exercise groups small, so I have set the maximum participants at 12.

For now this walk is for our experienced Nordic Walkers only, who already used to Nordic Walk with us regularly before Covid 19 kept us indoors, and who have their own Nordic Walking poles.

As this session is outdoors, we will not ask you to wear a face mask, but we do ask you to keep 2 meters apart. Some of our walkers might be immune compromised or more at risk, so please help us keep everyone safe!

Please do not come to the session and stay at home if:
• you know you have been in contact - in the last 2 weeks- with someone with symptoms of possible Covid, or if you have been in contact with someone who tested positive.
• you have any of the following symptoms: (new) Loss of smell/taste, Persistent cough, Fatigue, Loss of appetite, Skin rash, Hives, Fever, Severe muscle pain, Shortness of breath, Diarrhoea, Delirium, Abdominal pain, Chest pain, Hoarse voice, Eye soreness, Sore or painful throat, Nausea or vomiting, Headache, Dizziness or light headedness

We meet by the Blackbird bakery in Herne Hill, between the station and the park.

Session Price: £10 per session, £89 for a 10-session card or £70 unlimited sessions per month. Session cards and Pay Monthly can be used in any of our outdoor walks or indoor Zoom classes sessions (except for the Parkinson's sessions).

Pay What Works:
The price shown above is the “true” value of the session that best reflects the work I put into preparing and leading your session. However, I understand that not everyone can afford to pay full price, and I don’t want that to stop you from joining us.

In an effort to find a balance between more financial accessibility and sustainable pricing, I now offer a “Pay What Works” model. This allows for financial flexibility while still valuing and respecting the work and energy I provide in creating and delivering these classes.

Then send an email to ailien@fitandhappyoutdoors.com with the heading “INVOICE please”- followed by “FAHO 1” to pay full price as quoted below, “FAHO 2”, for 20% off, or “FAHO 3” for 50% off.

Please do tell me if you want to pay for 10 sessions, or if you’d like to pay monthly.
I prefer payment by bank transfer, but if that is not possible you could pay in cash. No cheques please, the queues by the banks are just too long.

We walk in all safe weather conditions – if a walk is cancelled, we will contact you to let you know. Please check for text messages or Meetup messages before leaving home!",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792698887/orbit/event-covers/sources/v0emjd6ekqqgxwve3ka1.jpg,2026-11-27 10:00:00+00,2026-11-27 11:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Blackbird Bakery,230 Railton Road,London,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/fit-and-happy-outdoors/events/fjpqgsyjcpbkc/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,10.00,10.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:54:30.136455+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/fit-and-happy-outdoors/events/fjpqgsyjcpbkc/,event_fjpqgsyjcpbkc@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-22 19:54:30.136455+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.486349+00,51.452682,-0.102277,meetup:fit-and-happy-outdoors:nordic walking brockwell park,Every week on Friday,f,GB
a729efca-845d-497e-b226-08b858d93061,,London Walk : Two Towers Walk,This 5 mile heritage walk from Westminster to the Tower of London features two towers with top views over London: three palaces and several unique features of the history of London. We start at…,"This 5 mile heritage walk from Westminster to the Tower of London features two towers with top views over London: three palaces and several unique features of the history of London. We start at Parliament Square at the base of the statue of Churchill, from where we can take in Westminster Abbey, the Palace of Westminster and Whitehall. We then walk east passing the Watergate where we can appreciate how far the width of the Thames has been reduced to accommodate the Embankment and Bazlegette's innovation. We can explore the Georgian splendour of Somerset House built around one of the most beautiful courtyards in Europe (free tour if we have time). We then cross over Waterloo Bridge to take in the South Bank with a visit to Gabriel's Wharf where we might be lucky enough to see some sand sculptors at work. After seeing the Globe Theatre we then head over London Bridge to climb to the top of the Monument (built after the great fire of London in 1666). There is a climb of the 331 steps for great views across London. We then rejoin the Thames Path to walk alongside the Tower of London taking in this the oldest Royal Palace in England. The walk ends at the world famous Tower Bridge where our tickets will allow us to discover the Bridge's fascinating history from Victorian times to the present day through films, animations and interactive displays. We will climb the towers and walk along the high-level walkway over the river (glass floor to add to the vertiginous thrill) with stunning views up and down the Thames. Option to finish walk at the Dickens Inn in St Katherine's Dock for refreshments whilst we admire the yachts and the Thameside views. A joint ticket for the Monument and Tower Bridge can be purchased prior to the event, can also buy on the day.

Refreshments -- Cafes and shops are to be found along our walk with pub at the end

Travel - Nearest station to start: Westminster, on Jubilee, District and Circle lines. Nearest station to end: Tower Hill, on District and Circle lines.

Start--10:45am prompt at Churchill statue, Parliament Square, postcode SW1A 0AA

FinishAround 3:00pm at Tower Bridge, postcode E1W 1BA

Event arranged by our main group (www.hawog.org.uk (http://www.hawog.org.uk/)). All walks are free to full members. It is just £10 for 12 months & we have free walks every weekend (only a selection is shown on meet up). Please join today by PayPal via link: http://www.hawog.org.uk/membership.php . If not joining please pay the £5 walk fee via PayPal after you rsvp. Any questions please mail meetup@hawog.org.uk",,2026-11-07 10:45:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Parliament Square,Parliament Square,London,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,fitness,travel,arts}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/ealing-ruislip-harrow-walking-social-group/events/316531661/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:54:30.136455+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/ealing-ruislip-harrow-walking-social-group/events/316531661/,event_316531661@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-22 19:54:30.136455+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.75405+00,,,,,f,GB
b089cd38-4d6d-4973-b8d9-19b34f0346b9,,Baker Street to Hampstead Walk,"A linear 10 mile walk starting from Baker Street station and ending at Hampstead station. The route takes in several notable viewpoints over London: Primrose Hill, Waterlow Park and Parliament Hill.…","A linear 10 mile walk starting from Baker Street station and ending at Hampstead station. The route takes in several notable viewpoints over London: Primrose Hill, Waterlow Park and Parliament Hill. The parks and Hampstead Heath provide a lot of green spaces to enjoy. We will stop momentarily to pay respects to George Michael by looking at his former home in Highgate Village. There are numerous blue plaques on route which link people of the past with buildings of the present - now run by English Heritage. Great fun trying to spot as many as you can! There will be a pub stop at the end in Hampstead.

Refreshments
Cafes on way, pub at end. Option to bring packed lunch.
Travel
Baker Street is on Metropolitan, Circle, Jubilee and Bakerloo lines. Hampstead is on Northern line, also Hampstead Heath station near end on Overground line.This is our first training event for the year. We are
Start
10:00am prompt at Baker Street station, postcode NW1 5LJ. Meet next to Starbucks cafe inside station.
Cost of event is £10. This includes full membership for 1 year , the workshop and follow up training walks. Just £10 now, balance when booking. Event arranged by main group,(www.hawog.org.uk (http://www.hawog.org.uk/)) All day walks are free to full members. Please rsvp & pay via paypal link. We will send you confirmation mail on booking. Any questions please mail meetup@hawog.org.uk",,2026-11-14 10:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Baker Street,Marylebone Road,London,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,fitness,travel}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/chiltern-and-thames-valley-walking-group/events/316390973/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-25 03:22:59.993096+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/chiltern-and-thames-valley-walking-group/events/316390973/,event_316390973@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-25 03:22:59.993096+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.75405+00,,,,,f,GB
