5240ddbf-9220-4a77-8295-be8b3bbbc0c9,,The Conscious Perimenopause Café,Details,"**Details**
**📅** Tuesday, **Nov 24** · 12:30 – 13:30
**📍 FREE online event -** *Hosted by Womanship Professional Dr Ghiselle Panneflek.*
👉 Reserve Your Spot (https://belong.womanship.co/c/upcoming-workshops/the-conscious-perimenopause-cafe-07a5a3) 👈

👋 **Do you feel like you no longer recognize yourself?**
• The mood swings that hit out of nowhere.
• Anxiety with no clear cause.
• Brain fog so thick you second-guess yourself at work.
• A body that suddenly feels unfamiliar.
You've seen doctors. They said everything's fine. But you know it isn't.
This has a name, and a far better path forward than most women are ever shown.

Most approaches treat perimenopause as symptoms to manage. We believe it's a transition to be *navigated*: physical, emotional, and deeply personal, all at once.
Through **Conscious Perimenopause**, I guide women through three stages of awareness, from *""what's wrong with me?""* to *""something deeper is happening""* to finally, *""my body is guiding me.""*

🤝 **Meet Dr. Ghiselle**
A Medical doctor, hormone specialist, and **founder of Conscious Perimenopause™**. Born in Curaçao, based in Amsterdam, and a practicing GP for nearly 20 years.
This work isn't from a textbook, it's from her own story.

Almost a decade ago, perimenopause hit her hard: burnout, anxiety, heavy bleeding, migraines, weight gain, fibroids. Even as a doctor, the system failed her. That experience became the foundation of everything she does now.
**She looks at the whole picture, not just estrogen and progesterone, but cortisol, thyroid, and insulin too.** Not just physical symptoms, but the emotional shifts and identity questions underneath them. She treats symptoms as signals, not inconveniences.

*-Your body is whispering. She's here to help you listen.* 🌸 -

👉 **Ask Dr. Ghiselle**
***Got a question you've never quite known how to ask?*** Send it in before the session, anonymously if you'd rather. She'll answer as many as she can live during the Café.
No question is too small. No symptom too embarrassing. No feeling too hard to put into words.
This is a safe space. Come as you are. 🌸

👀 **What to expect**
A warm space with women who truly understand what you're moving through. Honest, grounded perspectives from a doctor who's lived it herself. Your questions answered with real depth, never dismissed.
**Room to reflect, share, or simply listen, no preparation, no prior knowledge, no pressure to participate.**
*""Just come as you are, dushi. 🌿""*

