1d217eeb-d237-429a-b121-c8fb2e022b23,,Canal Walk - Angel to Victoria Park Cafe / Market,We will enjoy a leisurely walk (approx 45 mins - 1 hour) along Regent's Canal from Angel station and ending at the fabulous Victoria Park Market. This event usually runs on the 4th Sunday of each…,"We will enjoy a leisurely walk (approx 45 mins - 1 hour) along Regent's Canal from Angel station and ending at the fabulous Victoria Park Market. This event usually runs on the 4th Sunday of each month, unless there is bad weather or exceptional circumstances. We are a welcoming group, so feel free to mix around and say hello other people.

There is a wondering food market in Victoria Park, and most of us will get something to eat together. We usually sit on the grass or public benches (if available) near the Bonner Gate entrance, behind the Dogs of Alcibiades statue. This is at the intersection of foodstalls running north/south and east/west. If it is raining or the market is closed, we can either go to the Pavillion cafe, or The Crown pub on Grove Road instead.

Please note a few points:
1. There is currently no charge for this group. I will need to review this again later in 2026.

2. WE WILL WAIT ONLY ABOUT 10 MINUTES AFTER THE START TIME. If you are running late, please catch us up along the canal. Please note, I will not be checking for meetup or whatsapp messages after the walk starts.

3. The nearest tube station to Victoria Park is Bethnal Green station (central line). Please check Google Maps or similar.

4. You are responsible for yourselves on the walk, so please bring appropriate footwear etc. Please be mindful of those around you, especially where the canal gets narrow in places.

Whatsapp group here: https://chat.whatsapp.com/IJd6MJfVDPC6jUw6iW77ZY

Previously, there was a separate walk on the 3rd Sunday of the month, which started at Limehouse Basin, and then ran along the same canal to Victoria Park. Please note, the walks starting from Limehouse on the 3rd Sunday of the month are now cancelled for the foreseeable future.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/f/2/e/highres_520768462.jpeg,2027-02-28 12:00:00+00,2027-02-28 15:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Angel Station,A1,London,c06699ed-62e0-4957-bcb4-080c5271da9a,"{sport,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/canal-walk-run-food-markets/events/315791960/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:49:59.056229+00,source:cba1b9d2-d09d-4c19-a89e-50bdbe5525a0,https://www.meetup.com/canal-walk-run-food-markets/events/315791960/,event_315791960@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:20:38.34+00,,2026-10-22 19:49:59.056229+00,2026-10-28 03:21:15.930389+00,,,meetup:canal-walk-run-food-markets:canal walk angel to victoria park cafe market,"Every 4th Sunday of the month until July 25, 2027",f,GB
38195e9d-3632-434c-b9e6-7906f250929b,,Pinner to Ruislip Walk,"Easy linear walk from Pinner to Ruislip Manor Farm site. Route will follow the Celandine Route through Memorial Park, meadows and allotments. We will explore Eastcote House gardens, with a coffee…","Easy linear walk from Pinner to Ruislip Manor Farm site. Route will follow the Celandine Route through Memorial Park, meadows and allotments. We will explore Eastcote House gardens, with a coffee break at the cafe. We then follow footpaths through local parks before ending at the Ruislip Manor Farm heritage area. The Christmas market is taking place, the Barn is open and many food stalls set up. Ruislip Station is 10 minutes' walk away.
Refreshments
Coffee and cake at Eastcote House. Lunch at the Christmas Market, lots of food stalls.
Travel
Pinner and Ruislip are both on Metropolitan Line. Free parking on Sundays at start and finish of walk. Local buses stop at start.
Start
10:00am prompt outside Pinner Station, postcode HA5 5LZA
