c15c45f7-2533-491c-9b7b-ebce1296891b,,"SalsaTrain weekly classes Salsa for beginners, improvers/improver + level","Join us at SalsaTrain for a fun-filled evening of dancing and learning the art of salsa, suitable for all levels! SalsaTrain is in its 5th year now.","Join us at SalsaTrain for a fun-filled evening of dancing and learning the art of salsa, suitable for all levels! SalsaTrain is in its 5th year now.
All aboard! The SalsaTrain every Weds @ the Selhurst Railway Club in South London right by Selhurst Train station. Salsa classes every Weds night from 6.30-11pm.

The classes are fun & interactive with Dominic Insta(Salsa_Legend) with over 20 years salsa experience, and Trish with 10 years teaching experience. Dominic's style is Predominately L.A. on 1/ cuban fusion. He was placed 1st in the Tropicana Tropics World Open Salsa Championship (Ama Division) 2003, has performed with a team of dancers at the 2005 UK salsa congress and placed as runner up in the European Open Salsa Championships (Cab 2007). He has also performed at the Scandinavian Salsa Congress 2009 in Sweden; as part of a team at one of the New York Salsa Congresses and instructed for many salsa promoters within the UK and Internationally.
During lockdown, Dom launched his weekly music show ""Sundown Salsa Live"" on Mixcloud and has played regularly on OSSR radio every Friday 10am-12pm. Trish teaches the beginner class and has had experience teaching with another Salsa Group.

All lessons (45 mins long) include party. No partner necessary.
Free stop - 6.30-7pm Bachata Time (Music and Dance for 30 mins). There will be Bachata Tasters - (Beginners steps - 30 mins - Subject to change).
1st stop - 7-7.45pm Beginners & Improvers
2nd stop - 8-8.45pm Improvers plus level
3rd stop - 9-11pm - PartyTrain Social dancing
Homeward Bound 11pm
£10 for 1 class, £12.50 for 2 classes, £5 for party only. Early bird tickets for beginners Salsa class only for £8.50 & for 2 classes including party train for £10.00 inc Eventbrite fee available until 6.30pm each Tuesday - 24 hours before SalsaTrain.
Boarding from 6.30pm.

Get your tickets via www.latindianevents.com (http://%5Bhttp://www.latindianevents.com%5D(http://www.latindianevents.com) ""http://www.latindianevents.com"") which leads to the following eventbrite link - [https://salsa-train-selhurst.eventbrite.co.uk/ (https://salsa-train-selhurst.eventbrite.co.uk/)](https://eur02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fsalsa-train-selhurst.eventbrite.co.uk%2F&data=05%7C02%7CA.Kapadia%40mdx.ac.uk%7Cfdc1b99d8569432c544008de4ebfb677%7C38e37b88a3a148cf9f056537427fed24%7C0%7C0%7C639034782480290305%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=bK7omfXlIt1Thr9F%2BZ4ZzCfdEWF9B27DChx7%2FsEcOIU%3D&reserved=0 ""https://eur02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fsalsa-train-selhurst.eventbrite.co.uk%2F&data=05%7C02%7CA.Kapadia%40mdx.ac.uk%7Cfdc1b99d8569432c544008de4ebfb677%7C38e37b88a3a148cf9f056537427fed24%7C0%7C0%7C639034782480290305%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=bK7omfXlIt1Thr9F%2BZ4ZzCfdEWF9B27DChx7%2FsEcOIU%3D&reserved=0"")
(WE ALSO ACCEPT PAYMENT BY CARD ON THE NIGHT)
You will be refunded or have your ticket transferred to another night providing you inform either of the contacts below by 7pm on the day you are coming.

More info please contact Abs 07507634241 or Dom 07939587944
Venue details and information.
Selhurst Railway Club is a stones throw from Selhurst train station - well connected by London Victoria, Clapham Junction and East Croydon. Upon arrival please press the buzzer and wait to be let in. You will need to show your pre paid ticket on your phone & asked to give your details to the club management.
You will then be escorted into the room to board the SalsaTrain.
The venue has a fully stocked bar at extremely reasonable prices & crisps, nuts. It is a very spacious venue and has a very comfortable feel with great wooden floor for dancing.
All aboard!!!!",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/3/d/7/c/highres_532575740.jpeg,2026-12-16 18:30:00+00,2026-12-16 23:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Selhurst Club,42 Dagnall Park,London,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/colombian-professionals-in-london/events/sgfdxtyjcqbvb/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/colombian-professionals-in-london/events/sgfdxtyjcqbvb/,event_sgfdxtyjcqbvb@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,2026-10-28 03:22:27.129706+00,,,meetup:colombian-professionals-in-london:salsatrain weekly classes salsa for beginners improvers improver level,"Every week on Wednesday until December 16, 2026",f,GB
8a885eeb-c2c2-40e1-8347-ddfc8d2a68d6,,Helvellyn & Fairfield Adventure – Lake District,Register your interest now! Limited spaces available.,"**Register your interest now! Limited spaces available.**

**Day 1 - Arrival & Welcome**

**Day 2 - Glenridding & Helvellyn Circular**

**We begin our Lake District adventure in the beautiful village of Glenridding for a full-day mountain hike through some of the most iconic scenery in the Lakes.**

**The route takes us on a challenging circular towards Helvellyn, with panoramic ridge views, dramatic landscapes, and classic Lakeland terrain throughout the day. Depending on weather and mountain conditions, the route may be adapted for safety and group ability.**

**Expect a rewarding day on the fells with steep ascents, uneven terrain, and plenty of opportunities to take in the scenery and connect with fellow hikers.**

**Hike Details:**

• **Distance: Approx. 18–20 km**
• **Duration: 7–8 hours**
• **Difficulty: Challenging**
• **Terrain: Mountain trails, rocky paths, steep ascents/descents**

**⸻**

**Day 3 - Fairfield Horseshoe Adventure**

**On day three, we head into the stunning Eastern Fells for a classic hike around Fairfield. This route offers a completely different feel to day one - quieter trails, rolling ridgelines, and spectacular views across the Lake District.**

**The Fairfield route is a fantastic mountain day with a steady challenge throughout, taking us across high passes and scenic ridge paths before descending back into the valley.**

**This is the perfect way to round off the weekend with another unforgettable day in the mountains.**

**Hike Details:**

• **Distance: Approx. 15–17 km**
• **Duration: 6–7 hours**
• **Difficulty: Moderate to Challenging**
• **Terrain: Fell paths, rocky sections, exposed ridges**

**⸻**

**Important Information**

**Participation Fee**

**The hiking organising & guiding fee is £75 per person.**

**Please note that the fee does not include:**

• **Travel or train tickets (if applicable)**
• **Accommodation**
• **Food or drinks**
• **Personal hiking insurance**
• **Hiking equipment or clothing**
• **Any additional personal expenses**

**⸻**

**Estimated Additional Costs**

• **Hostel accommodation: approximately £38 per night**
• **Taxi to/from the mountain start point: approximately £15**
• **Food, snacks, and drinks for the weekend**
• **Travel costs to the Lake District**

**Please note that prices may vary depending on availability and bookings.**

**⸻**

**Food & Preparation**

**Participants must bring packed lunches for both hiking days, along with enough snacks and water for full days in the mountains. Opportunities to purchase food during the hikes will be limited or unavailable.**

**We strongly recommend bringing:**

• **Minimum 2 litres of water**
• **High-energy snacks**
• **Waterproof clothing**
• **Proper hiking boots with good grip**
• **Warm layers suitable for changing mountain weather**

**⸻**

**Fitness & Experience**

**Participants should have:**

• **A good level of fitness**
• **Previous hill-walking experience**
• **Confidence walking for several hours in mountainous terrain**

**⚠️Safety & Responsibility⚠️**

**While this is a guided group hiking experience, all participants are responsible for their own personal safety and wellbeing throughout the trip. By joining the hike, participants acknowledge the risks associated with mountain walking, including uneven terrain, changing weather conditions, and physical exertion.**

