e1b69433-df45-45be-b3f5-cbde2184b8e9,,"📖 Careless People: A Cautionary Tale of Power, Greed, and Lost Idealism","Join the UX Book Club on Wednesday 9 November where we'll chat about Careless People: A Cautionary Tale of Power, Greed, and Lost Idealism by Sarah Wynn-Williams.","Join the UX Book Club on Wednesday 9 November where we'll chat about *Careless People: A Cautionary Tale of Power, Greed, and Lost Idealism* by Sarah Wynn-Williams.

//ABOUT THE BOOK //
This memoir is an insider's account of working at Facebook during its rise. Sarah Wynn-Williams describes a world of private jets and meetings with world leaders, but also sexism, double standards and a toxic workplace culture.
She covers key moments in the company's history, along with the strain of being a working mother in a high-pressure job, while Sheryl Sandberg told women to ""lean in"".

👉🏽 Learn more: https://www.panmacmillan.com/authors/sarah-wynn-williams/careless-people/9781035065967

Join our meet-up where we'll chat about key topics and themes from the book, and try some of the gamestorming techniques with fellow book club members!

// FAQ //
Q. I've no background in UX, is it ok for me to attend?
A. Yes, The UX Book Club is open to anyone who wants to read more, learn together, network or talk with more confidence in professional discussions.
Q. What do you do at UX Book Club meetups?
A. We have a short intro to the book in focus, talk about it, and sometimes there are questions. Breakout rooms are sometimes used to help make larger events a little more personal :)
Q. How Do I Attend?
A. You can join our online book clubs via Zoom and we'll message participants with a meeting link before the event.
Q. What if I haven't read or finished the book?
A. Come anyway!
Q. Do you have a Code of Conduct?
A. Yes, you can find it here:
https://www.meetup.com/theuxbookclub/messages/boards/thread/53097975
Message the organisers and we'll do our best to answer your questions.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/7/6/2/highres_536718274.jpeg,2026-11-18 08:00:00+00,,Europe/Dublin,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,books}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/theuxbookclub/events/316859325/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/theuxbookclub/events/316859325/,event_316859325@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.689062+00,,,,,f,
28023c60-c16d-4674-8314-2541e93ef523,,My favourite plugin 16th November Zoom 7pm UK WP Cambridge,"Dear All,","Dear All,
Join us on **Monday 16 November at 7pm UK time** for a friendly WordPress discussion on Zoom: **“My favourite plugin.”**

Which plugin makes your WordPress life easier? Perhaps it saves you hours, solves a tricky problem, or does one small thing brilliantly. It might be a well-known favourite with a setting others have overlooked, or a hidden gem that deserves more attention.

Come along to share your recommendation, discover something useful, or ask for help finding the right plugin. **You don’t need to bring a favourite to take part — curiosity is enough!**

Reserve your spot:
https://www.meetup.com/wordpress-cambridge/events/317133426

What we might explore?

If you’d like to show us a plugin in action, you’re welcome to share your screen. No slides or prepared presentation needed. Maybe you'd like to share:

• **Your must-have plugin:** What does it do, and why you keep using it?
• **Hidden features:** Is there a useful setting or clever trick others might have missed?
• **Lessons learned:** Have you replaced a plugin, solved a conflict, or found a simpler alternative?
• **Recommendations wanted:** What would you like your WordPress site to do better?

We encourage everyone to ask questions and/or propose solutions. Hence, our discussions are always interesting and valuable.

**We're a discussion meeting**
There is no ""expert"" speaker, however Chris and Simon will, as usual, start by briefly describing the issue, just to start and inspire a discussion.

Beginner or advanced, we’re here to learn from one another. As always, our friendly regulars from the UK, Europe, and the USA will be joining in.

**Evening's Schedule:**
**7:00 PM** – Quick hellos and intros: Share your WordPress journey in 10 seconds!
**7:15 PM** – Open discussions with live Q&A and contributions from attendees. Feel free to share your screen.
**8:30 PM** – Brainstorm ideas for next month’s topic.
**9:00 PM** – Official close, but you’ll leave inspired and more connected with our WordPress community!

**Why Attend?**
From the UK to the US and across Europe, our meetups bring together a diverse group of WordPress enthusiasts. You’ll tap into a wealth of knowledge and get real-world tips and solutions for your design projects.
**🔗 Reserve Your Spot Today!**
https://www.meetup.com/wordpress-cambridge/events/317133426

