7735ccaf-6917-48e5-b639-ea40fee73a1d,,"Norfolk SEAL PUPS, Britain's most magical wildlife spectacular!",It is this time of the year again and I am taking you on a journey into a world of cuteness where not carrying your camera will not be allowed.,"It is this time of the year again and I am taking you on a journey into a world of cuteness where not carrying your camera will not be allowed.
LET'S GO SEE THE BABY SEALS!

ATTENTION, BOOKINGS WILL CLOSE A WEEK BEFORE DEPARTURE AND IT IS ON A FIRST COME FIRST SERVE BASIS as this trip is limited to 12 people.

Due to the popularity of this trip I have decided to do it again.
Norfolk is THE place where you can see one of Britain's most fantastic show; the grey seal breeding season.

Norfolk holds the world's two largest Atlantic grey seals colonies and I am taking you there. You will be able to observe at often just a couple of metres away the 7000 seals that come to these sandy beaches every year to give birth to those gorgeous white furry creatures.
You will not get enough of it, believe me.

We will be able to observe seals of every ages from the tiny few hours old white pups, to the full fat adolescents and up to the big males who weight hundreds of kilos and who will be fighting a bit further down on the sand. Volunteers will be there to answer all our questions and to keep us from getting too close to those beautiful creatures, often unsuccessfully as those cubs being of a curious nature will approach us often far too close to inspect us.

The seals will be the highlight of or trip but will not be our only journey as we will hike the dunes of Norfolk which are home to a pair of barn owl and where shorties spend the winter.
We meet at 08.00 am at Liverpool Street station, and off we go, we should be back in London by 9.30pm.
Due to other commitments, I can only do this one trip to Norfolk this year so book your spot asap if you want to see the cutie balls of fur.
As always we will grab a meal at the end of the trip before we head back to London with a few hundred photos. I have a professional camera and will share it with you.
We will not rush for this trip, we will stop for plenty of photos so if you are coming for a hardcore hike I would not recommend.
There are no dogs allowed on this trip I am afraid for obvious reasons.

Attention, this is a whole day out, we should be back after 9pm, I cannot change the train time.

TRANSPORT:
VIA train and bus (about 3 hours)
COST:
£ 75
I tried to keep it as cheap as possible but the train prices went up as well as buses and in this case my costs too.
The fee is refundable up to 2 weeks before departure and non-refundable after that, but you may resell and you can try to find someone to take your place.

INCLUDED:
Guided hike
Fast train to Norfolk and back and a short bus journey
A great time with lovely people

NOT INCLUDED:
Food and drinks
Anything not mentioned above
WHAT TO BRING:
Waterproof shoes for the hike, preferably hiking shoes, otherwise good trainers
Weather appropriate clothes
Water bottle;
MEETING POINT:
Liverpool Street Station. At 7am

A WHATSAPP GROUP WILL BE CREATED A FEW DAYS BEFORE DEPARTURE WITH MORE INFO.

ATTENTION:
Our trips will not be cancelled due to weather conditions so please ensure that you do wear and carry appropriate clothing. 😄

POLICIES:
1: This group is designed for the pleasure and enjoyment of all of us, we do not accept any derogatory comments or behaviours towards anyone. Racism, discrimination and other unacceptable behaviours will only lead to your rejection to any of our trips and this without exception. Everyone is welcome, we have religious and non-religious people, gay, straight, bisexual people, all shades and colours or nationality, people of all ages, sex and political believes and mutual respect is the fundamental spirit of this group.
2: Our trips are only refundable up to 14 days before departure, if you wish to cancel after that, you will be offered a transfer to another trip for the same price or you may resell your slot to somebody else.
3: If we do cancel the entirety of the trip on our side, you will be fully refunded
4:In the eventuality that our trains are delayed, or cancelled which is out of my control, I do not pay for taxis or alternative route, if this happens, you will be able to claim delay repay from the train companies who will reimburse your train ticket and some eventual costs occurred. By signing up to my events, you agree to this.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/e/8/6/highres_506496486.jpeg,2026-11-14 07:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Liverpool Street Station,Liverpool Street Station,London,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/jons-trails/events/316353503/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-24 03:22:51.513176+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/jons-trails/events/316353503/,event_316353503@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-24 03:22:51.513176+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.75405+00,,,,,f,GB
d5c45c77-763c-421c-8e23-3acc1af81b77,,Osterley Park Walk,"6-mile scenic amble through the grounds of Osterley Park, currently displaying flowers in the Bloom Trail. Walk starts at the 1930's station (historical information on the concourse). We will reach…","6-mile scenic amble through the grounds of Osterley Park, currently displaying flowers in the Bloom Trail. Walk starts at the 1930's station (historical information on the concourse). We will reach the NT car park at 10:45am to meet the people who drove there, and then can admire the Robert Adam designed Osterley House with its classical entrance facade. Walk takes in the lake, meadows and deer park of this rare surviving country estate within London. Walk includes section of the Grand Union Canal through Hanwell with stops at the impressive Hanwell Flights of six locks and Brunel's engineering marvel of the Three Bridges. NT members can visit the House itself for free, others can visit for the admission price.
Refreshments
Bring packed lunch. Cafe at Osterley Park, pub stop on walk.
Travel
Osterley is on Piccadilly line. Free car park for NT members at Osterley House entrance.
Start
