05923a1e-08dd-45e7-b1b5-dd780b868c48,,Toasted Fig | October Hike | Godalming to Guildford | Sat 24 Oct,October Group Hike | Godalming to Guildford | Sat 24 Oct,"**October Group Hike | Godalming to Guildford | Sat 24 Oct**

Autumn by the water 🍂
A gentle riverside walk along the River Wey from Godalming to Guildford, passing Guildford Castle with an optional pub stop at the end.

**About this hike**
A flat, easy walk along the River Wey. Expect water meadows, old locks, narrowboats and autumn colour. Ideal if you’re new to group hiking or just fancy a relaxed Saturday outdoors.

**The route**
From Godalming station we follow the river north through countryside towards Shalford, passing traditional locks along the way. In Guildford we head up towards the castle and its gardens, finishing in Guildford town centre with an optional pub stop. Guildford station is nearby, with direct trains to Waterloo (and back to Godhalming if driving).

**The details**
📍 Meet outside Pret inside London Waterloo from 08:40–08:50 for the 09:00 train (arrives Godalming 10:09), or join us at Godalming station at 10:09

🚶 ~9km / ~5.5 miles

⏱ ~2 hours moving time

🍻 Optional pub stop in Guildford

💷 £10 per person

**What’s included**
✔️ A guided hike led by a qualified outdoor first aider
✔️ A healthy homemade marshmallow snack
✔️ A friendly group (capped at 20)

**What’s not included**
✖️ Train ticket
✖️ Food or drink you purchase along the way (or at the pub)

**How to pay**
After you RSVP, I’ll message you bank details. Please pay £10 by bank transfer within 48 hours (or before the hike, if sooner) to confirm your spot. Unpaid spots will be released after a friendly reminder. Bank transfer only, no cash.

**Refund policy**
Full refund up to 24 hours before the hike, paid within 48 hours. No refunds within 24 hours of the start.

**What to bring**
Sturdy footwear, plenty of water and a snack if you think you'll get hungry

**The vibe**
Relaxed pace, good company and time in nature, with a shared love of the outdoors, good food and looking after yourself. No fitness pressure. Solo or with a friend, you’ll be made welcome from the moment you arrive.

**Safety**
I’m a qualified outdoor first aider, so you’re in safe hands 🙌

**Any questions?**
Message me on Meetup, or on 07759894981 on the day if you need help finding us.

