4a4d89ed-b77f-4ccc-99de-e3c72df15cb3,,Kew Gardens Walk,"This 6-mile autumn nature walk takes in Richmond, Thames Path and Kew Gardens. On Tuesdays Kew Gardens offer a discount ticket of just £10. After coffee at Tide Tables we follow the river path north…","This 6-mile autumn nature walk takes in Richmond, Thames Path and Kew Gardens. On Tuesdays Kew Gardens offer a discount ticket of just £10. After coffee at Tide Tables we follow the river path north past the lock bridge with scenic views of Isleworth and Brentford on the way. Reaching Elizabeth Gate on Kew Green we enter Kew Gardens. The walk continues through Kew Gardens taking in seasonal highlights such as the autumn colours, berries and autumn crocus displays. We can explore all the features of Kew Gardens including the treetop walkway. Can buy tickets at the entrance gate of Kew Gardens.
Refreshments
Bring a packed lunch if you like. Cafe at beginning of walk and in Kew Gardens.
Travel
Richmond and Kew Gardens are on District and Mildmay lines. Southwestern trains also stop at Richmond. Payable parking near start.
Start
