c3304b8d-9f3f-4252-aca9-fb0aabc66b1c,,.NET Liverpool Lightning Talks,"Join us for this meet-up, presented by our attendees and the local community! It's a fantastic opportunity to support first-time public speakers as they share their passions and experiences. Come…","Join us for this meet-up, presented by our attendees and the local community! It's a fantastic opportunity to support first-time public speakers as they share their passions and experiences. Come out and show your support—there are some exciting topics on the agenda!

**Details**
Every year in October, we host a series of lightning talks from the community - 10/15 minute slots for our members to talk about something interesting within the .NET ecosystem!

Each speaker will have 15 minutes to present, and then we'll have a 5 minute break in-between for questions and equipment prep.

**Talks**
18:30 - Introductions
18:40 - (Simon Jackson) - THE 3.7 BILLION TOKEN DIET
19:00 - (Christopher Devine) - Supervise jobs, not clocks: Production CI
19:20 - (Stephen Mills) - C# is finally getting union types. So what?
**Break** 10 min
19:50- (Joseph Tossell) - Guardrails that aren't fallible
20:10 - (Mohmoud Elbadwi) - When Sensors Lie: Building Data Pipelines You Can Actually Trust
20:30 - (Samson Nwizugbe) - Building a Recommendation Engine without training data
20:50 - (Speaker Name) - Slot Available TBD

