2cfbf7a1-0f35-4f53-a245-15e407ce0d69,,Typelevel Open Source Hack,"Calling all Scala enthusiasts! Join us for a fun night of hacking, collaborating, and contributing to Typelevel open-source projects (https://typelevel.org/). Whether you’re a seasoned Scala…","Calling all Scala enthusiasts! Join us for a fun night of hacking, collaborating, and contributing to Typelevel open-source projects (https://typelevel.org/). Whether you’re a seasoned Scala developer or just getting started, this is the perfect opportunity to level up your skills, meet like-minded coders, and contribute to Open Source!

**Agenda**
10:00am - 🥐 Doors open. Come along, mingle and grab some breakfast.
10:30am - 💻 Quick introduction & find your hackmates!
1:00pm - 🥙 Lunch: Join us for some free food and drinks! Vegan and vegetarian options are provided. Let us know if you'd like something special - we'd be happy to accommodate.
2:00pm - 💻 Keep hacking!
3:30pm - 🥤 Join up and share what we've been working on.
4:00pm - ☕ Join us in a coffee shop to keep going!

**What will happen on the day?**
After a quick introduction, we will help everyone find a project they want to work on and disperse into groups.
At end of the afternoon we'll gather up and share what we've done and learned that day :)

**Frequently Asked Questions**
***I am a novice Scala developer, is this the right event for me? 📚***
Yes! One of the best ways to improve your Scala skills is by working on Open Source library and projects!

***I don't know what projects I should contribute to.. ↔️***
We have a list of Typelevel-related projects that would love to have some contributions. Other than get-work-done libraries, we have cool projects like game engine, frontend framework, synthesiser!

***I have an idea for a Open Source project but it's a bit daunting. Can you help? 🏔️***
Yes! We'd love to see more open source Scala projects and contributors! We can help you get started and provide technical guidance whenever you need it.

***Help! I'm stuck outside the building / somewhere!***
Joining our discord is probably the best way to be heard!

Discord server invite link:
https://discord.com/invite/aRCVCHmHES

**Donations**
The Typelevel foundation is a charity and is looking for funding! You can donate to it via Global Giving (https://www.globalgiving.org/projects/typelevel/).

📜 This event operates under the Typelevel Code of Conduct: https://typelevel.org/code-of-conduct/.
We encourage each of you to report the breach of the conduct, either anonymously through this form (https://forms.gle/9PMMorUWgBnbk1mm6) or by contacting one of our team members. We guarantee privacy and confidentiality, as well as that we will take your report seriously and react quickly.",,2026-10-24 09:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,SiriusXM,36 High Holborn,London,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,food}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/london-scala/events/315196780/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/london-scala/events/315196780/,event_315196780@meetup.com,,2026-10-24 03:22:55.871+00,,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,2026-10-24 03:23:30.869937+00,,,,,f,GB
02c8c1f1-5f45-4bc6-a933-bcd680d1260c,,BOOKCLUB: Annihlation - Jeff Vandermeer,"This month we will be reading/discussing Annihilation by Jeff Vandermeer. (https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/17934530-annihilation?ref=nav_sb_ss_1_5) If you have not read the book, you are more…","This month we will be reading/discussing ***Annihilation by Jeff Vandermeer. (https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/17934530-annihilation?ref=nav_sb_ss_1_5)*** If you have not read the book, you are more than welcome to join. Be aware, there will be spoilers!

18:30 - 18:45 - Meet, get drinks, get settled (at the back and upstairs)
18:45 - 19:45 - Discuss the book
19:45 onwards - pick book for next meet and socialize

**The Venue: Shinner and Sudtone (https://shinnerandsudtone.co.uk/)** (https://shinnerandsudtone.co.uk/)

A lovely little pub with a variety of craft beer. Usually quiet on a Monday and we get the upstairs area. They serve food and dogs are most welcome.

**The Book:** ***Annihilation by Jeff Vandermeer. (https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/17934530-annihilation?ref=nav_sb_ss_1_5)***
Area X has been cut off from the rest of the world for decades. Nature has reclaimed the last vestiges of human civilization. The first expedition returned with reports of a pristine, Edenic landscape; the second expedition ended in mass suicide, the third in a hail of gunfire as its members turned on one another. The members of the eleventh expedition returned as shadows of their former selves, and within weeks, all had died of cancer. In *Annihilation*, the first volume of Jeff VanderMeer's *Southern Reach Trilogy*, we join the twelfth expedition.

The group is made up of four women: an anthropologist; a surveyor; a psychologist, the de facto leader; and our narrator, a biologist. Their mission is to map the terrain, record all observations of their surroundings and of one another, and, above all, avoid being contaminated by Area X itself.

They arrive expecting the unexpected, and Area X delivers—but it’s the surprises that came across the border with them and the secrets the expedition members are keeping from one another that change everything.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/0/c/4/highres_536180676.jpeg,2026-11-09 18:30:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Shinner and Sudtone,67 High Street,Sutton,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising,books,food,hobbies}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/sutton-bookclub/events/316593183/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/sutton-bookclub/events/316593183/,event_316593183@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,,,f,GB
