4cbf2b50-4a06-4b2f-8b63-b134796fb2a0,,Builders Foundry #6 - Vibe Coding to Agentic Engineering & MCP,Agenda:,"**Agenda:**

6 PM Doors Open & Networking, **Pizza and drinks as always**
6.30 Introduction & Welcome
6.40 PM First talk- **Your Existing Applications Are Ready for AI Agents - Here's How MCP Makes It Possible**
(Arin Roy, Principal Architect & Azure AI, MVP , Capgemini)
7.20 PM 10min break
7.30 PM Second talk **- Going from vibe coding to Agentic engineering, a step-by-step guide** (Matteo Emili, Director of Platform engineering @Zema Global)
8.10 PM Networking & Wrap up

Talk Details:-

**Your Existing Applications Are Ready for AI Agents - Here's How MCP Makes It Possible**

(Arin Roy, Principal Architect & Azure AI, MVP , Capgemini)

Learn how to expose existing APIs through MCP servers so AI agents can discover and invoke business capabilities, with guidance on design, security, governance, and observability.

####

Your organization has invested years building applications that power its most important business processes. As AI agents become part of modern software, the challenge is no longer building new AI applications—it's making those existing systems accessible to them.

This session explores how the Model Context Protocol (MCP) helps bridge that gap. Rather than rebuilding applications or creating bespoke AI integrations, MCP enables existing capabilities to be exposed as discoverable tools that AI agents can understand and invoke at runtime.

Starting from an existing API, we'll build an MCP server, connect it to an LLM, and demonstrate how agents can dynamically discover and execute business capabilities. Along the way, we'll explore when APIs are sufficient, when MCP adds value, and the practical considerations for adopting MCP in production, including tool design, security, governance, discoverability, and observability.

Attendees will leave with a practical understanding of how to make existing applications agent-ready, how MCP complements rather than replaces APIs, and the architectural patterns and best practices for introducing MCP into real-world systems.

**Going from vibe coding to Agentic Engineering, a step-by-step guide**

(Matteo Emili, Director of Platform engineering @Zema Global)

A step-by-step guide to evolving from vibe coding to governed agentic engineering through AI collaboration, workflows, standards, and process discipline.
AI-augmented software development is evolving from “vibe coding”, where intuition and spontaneous creativity drive progress, to ""agentic engineering"", a more regulated and governed approach. In this new paradigm, AI agents collaborate with developers not only to unlock creativity, but also to ensure adherence to best practices and organizational guidelines. By harnessing agentic workflows, teams can capture the imaginative potential of AI while embedding robust standards, governance, and process discipline into everyday coding. This session explores how agentic engineering blends innovation with accountability to reshape the future of software development.

####",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/0/a/6/highres_536817510.jpeg,2026-11-19 18:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Civo Tech Junction,"First Floor, 32-37 Cowper St, London EC2A 4AW, UK",London,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,ai}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/the-builders-foundry/events/317147946/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-28 03:23:34.220625+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/the-builders-foundry/events/317147946/,event_317147946@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-28 03:23:34.220625+00,2026-10-28 03:23:36.424969+00,,,,,f,GB
c545ed1a-0f2c-416c-bf94-6387f6c0585f,,London Search Week Meetup: Building Flexible Search Pipelines & More,"Tesco have kindly offered to host us again - doors will open at 6.30pm and we will finish by 9pm, with food and drinks available. This will be an in-person event (but we will try to record the talks…","Tesco have kindly offered to host us again - doors will open at **6.30pm** and we will finish by 9pm, with food and drinks available. This will be an in-person event (but we will try to record the talks and share the videos later). **Our Meetup is part of [London Search Week](www.londonsearchweek.com) - check out the other events this week!**

Our first talk will come from Natália Sumida, a Software Engineer on the Search team at iFood (https://www.ifood.com.br/), Latin America's largest food delivery platform: *""Beyond Retrieval: Building Flexible Search Pipelines:*
*Search pipelines power critical user experiences, and their reliability depends on how easily we can model, test, and evolve each stage. In this talk, I'll share practical patterns for designing flexible search pipelines, drawn from lessons learned building search at a large-scale food delivery marketplace. We'll look at how to structure the pipeline into clear, testable components (query understanding, candidate generation, ranking, and post-processing) and how to validate each layer independently.""*

Second talk to be announced!

We'll also make time for Q&A on all things search and AI and some general networking. Our Search Meetup is organised by [The Search Juggler](www.thesearchjuggler.com), OpenSearch (https://opensearch.org/) and Eliatra (https://eliatra.com/).

