a9b2cf2e-66ea-4312-875c-2db07e0c5c52,,Lunch & Learn: The Harness Wore a Trenchcoat - Building a Rust MCP Server,"This talk is from Michelle Rojas, one of the head organizers of Rust NYC, and it addresses the unglamorous problem at the center of every AI agent: how do you give a language model safe access to a…","This talk is from Michelle Rojas, one of the head organizers of Rust NYC, and it addresses the unglamorous problem at the center of every AI agent: how do you give a language model safe access to a real filesystem without also handing it the ability to burn the house down? Michelle will build falcon-mcp live, a sandboxed Rust MCP server exposing tools across five categories (filesystem, cargo, git, prompt-safety linting, and exec) to any MCP-compatible client, including Gemini CLI. The goal is to make every tool call a boring, predictable event instead of an open door.

Attendees will leave with a concrete blueprint for sandbox boundaries (root jail, binary allowlist, read-only mode, per-tool timeouts), an understanding of why a single Rust binary with dual stdio and HTTP transports is the right shape for both local agent harnesses and hosted deployments, and guidance on treating the tool surface exposed to a model as a security boundary, not just an API.

️When: **Jun 23, 13:30 - 14.15 GMT, 8.30 - 9.15 ET (please note this is intentionally 30 mins later to accomodate time zones)**
Where: **Online**

--

**FAQs**
**Are there any House Rules?**
At SurrealDB, we are committed to providing live and online events that are safe and enjoyable for all attending. Please review our website for more information: https://surrealdb.com/legal/code-of-conduct

**Is Women in Rust only for women?**
We set up Women in Rust to foster a more inclusive and diverse Rust community by providing a dedicated space for women to connect, learn, and grow. Our online and in-person events are designed to support this mission. However, we also want to contribute to the wider Rust community, which is why all of our talks will be available to watch on **Youtube (https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCSW88H3WD7F96DJsM3Uq6iA)** after the event. We also welcome you to use our **Notion Resources page (https://www.notion.so/surrealdb/Women-in-Rust-Learning-Resources-ff83fd56ec4146d1b19b114490b953cb?pvs=4)*,*** where you can find useful articles, reading materials and advice to help you on your journey in learning Rust.

**How can I get involved with Women in Rust?**
We’re always excited to welcome new contributors! You can get involved by:

• **Speaking at our events**: Share your expertise or experience with the community.
• **Hosting online workshops**: Lead interactive sessions to help others learn and grow.
• **Spreading the word**: Help us reach more people by sharing our events and initiatives.

Simply fill out this form to express your interest: https://surrealdb.typeform.com/to/B2gk7bzz. We’ll be in touch to explore how we can collaborate.
Let’s grow together—your involvement makes a difference!",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792621023/orbit/event-covers/sources/ymw72h6ovetnfznpbqnq.jpg,2026-11-17 13:30:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,{technology},,external,https://www.meetup.com/women-in-rust/events/315719313/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:16:55.997298+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/women-in-rust/events/315719313/,event_315719313@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-21 22:16:55.997298+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.689062+00,,,,,f,
