cc0ed483-c658-40fd-a934-e9b8f9d17ecf,,The Power of Public Speaking: How Communication Builds Careers,"Hi everyone 👋 Thanks for joining. Great to have you here! Introduce yourself, Title","Hi everyone 👋 Thanks for joining. Great to have you here! Introduce yourself, Title
Public Speaking & Your Career: An Evening with Two TEDx Speakers
Description
Tickets are sold on Eventbrite: https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/the-power-of-public-speaking-how-communication-builds-careers-tickets-2003568269629
Saturday 24 October, doors 6:30pm, finishing 10pm
Mint Leaf London, near Bank
How does the way you communicate shape your career? Join us for an evening of short talks, live Q&A, an open mic and real networking, hosted by the London Networking Community.
Meet the speakers
Moe Musa, TEDx speaker and UK national public speaking winner, is the co-founder of Pathwei, a startup helping graduates land their first job in a competitive market. From managing £700K of procurement at Jaguar Land Rover to leading go-to-market strategy at startups, he'll speak on how the ability to sell an idea in the room, not just on the slide, has shaped his career and his company.
Iain Messore, TEDx speaker and public speaking coach, is a former president of the Public Speaking Society at the University of Nottingham and now a Civil Service Fast Streamer working as an Operations Manager at HMRC. Having coached people across the UK, he'll speak on how communication underpins leadership and why anyone can build it.
Open mic: story first
After the talks, the floor is yours. Step up to the mic and tell the room a story first: a lesson, a mistake, or a problem you're stuck on. Then, in one sentence, say what you're building and the one thing you need from the room. Two minutes each. Want a slot? Message us on WhatsApp at +44 7469 804955.
Agenda
6:30pm: Doors open, drinks and networking
8:00pm: Welcome from the host
8:05pm: Moe Musa (8 min talk + 5 min Q&A)
8:20pm: Iain Messore (8 min talk + 5 min Q&A)
8:35pm: Open mic (about 25 min)
9:00pm: Networking continues
10:00pm: End of the official part. Optional afterparty nearby, for those who want to keep the night goingask questions, or share anything useful before we meet at the event.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/e/a/6/highres_536724230.jpeg,2026-10-24 17:30:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Mint Leaf,"Bank, 12 Angel Ct, London EC2R 7HB, UK",London,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,growth,careers,entrepreneurship}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/london-networking-community/events/317070949/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/london-networking-community/events/317070949/,event_317070949@meetup.com,,2026-10-24 03:21:51.18+00,,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,2026-10-24 03:22:26.369051+00,,,,,f,GB
256187ce-bcb5-4a4d-b807-ad5be49bfb0f,,The Monsters Among Us,"How a Hidden Minority Preys on Organisations, Societies, and Nations — and How We Stop Them","How a Hidden Minority Preys on Organisations, Societies, and Nations — and How We Stop Them

There are people in this world whose psychology is profoundly abnormal — organisational predators driven by extreme psychopathy and narcissism. They are few in number, perhaps less than one percent of the population, yet their impact is devastating. They infiltrate organisations, manipulate culture, erode trust, and quietly seize influence. When enabled, they become monsters — unseen, applauded, protected — leaving destruction in their wake.

For decades, Gearóid Carey has studied these individuals and the catastrophic effects they have on teams, communities, governments, and entire nations. In this groundbreaking book, he reveals their psychology, their methods, and the predictable pattern of infiltration, grooming, and colonisation that they use to gain power.

But The Monsters Among Us is not a book about despair — it is a book about the cure.
Carey introduces two revolutionary frameworks capable of stopping organisational predators: Organisational Hygiene and Anti-Tyrannical Measures. When these principles are applied, predators lose their power, organisations recover, and societies thrive. When they are absent, corruption spreads, misery rises, and tyrannous rule emerges.

Inside this book, you will learn:
• How organisational predators think, behave, and manipulate
• Why good people fail to recognise them until it’s too late
• The three stages of organisational capture: infiltration, grooming, colonisation
• How networks of predators coalesce into the powerful superclass
• Why tyranny has been the default condition of civilisation for 10,000 years
• Why liberal democracy is the first real antidote — and why it is under attack
• The essential anti-tyrannical safeguards every free society must defend
• How to apply organisational hygiene to protect teams, institutions, and nations

A warning. A diagnosis. A blueprint for victory.
This book exposes how the superclass manipulates economies, healthcare, food systems, education, and government to serve their own interests — regardless of human suffering. Yet it also offers a path to rebuild integrity and restore freedom.

A call to action
If we understand the monsters, we can defeat them. If we defend liberal democracy and organisational hygiene, their age ends — and the age of human flourishing begins.
This is the end of tyranny — if we are brave enough to defend the light.

For readers of:
Matt Goodwin, Ayaan Hirsi Ali, Jordan Peterson, Douglas Murray, and Robert F. Kennedy Jr.

About the Author
Gearóid Carey is a counsellor, researcher, and writer with over 20 years of experience helping people recover from trauma, addiction, and mental-health crises. He is the creator of the Recovery Tracker and an advocate for transforming society through measurable wellbeing, integrity, and freedom.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792698511/orbit/event-covers/sources/stcimytiovboslu05wwi.jpg,2026-12-06 19:00:00+00,2026-12-06 19:30:00+00,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/journey-to-democracy/events/fvrpbvyjcqbjb/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,0.00,0.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:37.169472+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/journey-to-democracy/events/fvrpbvyjcqbjb/,event_fvrpbvyjcqbjb@meetup.com,,2026-10-27 03:19:10.711+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:37.169472+00,2026-10-27 03:19:46.873136+00,,,meetup:journey-to-democracy:the monsters among us,"Every week on Sunday until October 8, 2028",f,
33506809-3a2c-4653-bb12-c3a35874a1d0,,Make New Friends At A Bookshop,Do you want to meet new people in a relaxing chill atmosphere surrounded by new books? Do you dislike loud and smelly places like pubs and clubs? This is the event for you.,"Do you want to meet new people in a relaxing chill atmosphere surrounded by new books? Do you dislike loud and smelly places like pubs and clubs? This is the event for you.

Science and Philosophy Book Club is creating a new kind of meetup where people who love books and knowledge can meet new friends in a big book shop. We will explore around different sections of the book shop together as a group while making interesting conversations with each other. We will go to both fiction and non-fiction areas.

If you feel shy and feel nervous to come alone, I will make sure you will feel comfortable and accomodate to your needs. I will help introduce you to others so you can go over the barrier of anxiety when approaching a new person.

