The Friday WFH Club is a hosted coworking morning for 6 women, founders, freelancers, marketers, writers, anyone whose Friday is remote, around the dining table of a beautiful home right on Portobello Road, Notting Hill, London. Bring your actual work. This is not a workshop, it is your WFH day with better coffee, better company, and no laundry staring at you.

THE MORNING
9:15 Arrive, proper coffee, quick hellos
9:30 Deep work: heads down, phones away, music low
11:00 Coffee break and the good kind of shop talk
11:30 Second sprint
12:45 Wrap: one thing you shipped, one thing you learned

THE BONUS
I build with AI every day and I am on hand all morning. Bring your questions about whether AI could do a bit of your job, and leave with working answers.

DETAILS
6 seats. Great coffee and pastries included. Fast wifi, big table, actual daylight. Exact address sent after booking.

35 pounds. Less than you would spend camping in a cafe all morning, and you will get more done.

Hosted by Sarah. Fridays are better with company.

