92b4cc97-aeeb-42d0-b3ae-c2ed8df47dbb,,Navigating Corporate Trauma,Navigating Corporate Trauma,"Navigating Corporate Trauma

From Surviving to Thriving: Reclaim Your Confidence, Your Voice & Your Power

Have you ever walked away from a workplace feeling less confident, less valued, or questioning your own abilities?

Perhaps you’ve experienced a toxic boss, workplace bullying, discrimination, gaslighting, betrayal, burnout, or a corporate culture that slowly chipped away at your confidence.

Maybe you left that environment behind, but the impact followed you into your next role, your relationships, or even the way you see yourself.

You’re not alone. And your workplace experiences do not have to define your future.

Join Women on the RISE for an empowering, thought-provoking, and practical evening dedicated to understanding, navigating, and recovering from corporate trauma.

This isn’t another traditional networking event or leadership seminar. It’s an opportunity to have the conversations that too often go unspoken in the corporate world.

What You’ll Discover

During this interactive three-hour workshop, we’ll explore:

• Recognising Corporate Trauma: Understand how toxic workplace experiences, bullying, discrimination, exclusion, and chronic stress can affect your confidence, identity, and career.
• Breaking Free from Self-Doubt: Explore how workplace experiences can contribute to imposter feelings, perfectionism, people-pleasing, and fear of speaking up.
• Rebuilding Your Confidence: Discover practical techniques to reconnect with your strengths, trust your judgment, and reclaim your professional voice.
• Setting Healthy Boundaries: Learn strategies for recognising red flags, protecting your wellbeing, and navigating challenging workplace dynamics.
• Moving from Surviving to Thriving: Develop a personal action plan to move forward with greater clarity, resilience, and purpose.

What Makes This Workshop Different?

We believe that professional success should never come at the expense of your wellbeing.

This workshop creates space for real conversations, meaningful connections, practical strategies, and personal reflection.

You’ll have opportunities to connect with other ambitious women who understand the pressures of professional life, share experiences if you choose, and learn strategies you can apply immediately.

You won’t be expected to disclose personal experiences. Participation is always your choice, and the session is designed to be supportive and respectful.

Who Should Attend?

This event is for women at every stage of their professional journey, particularly those who:

• Have experienced toxic or challenging workplace environments.
• Are recovering from burnout or a difficult professional experience.
• Feel their confidence has been affected by workplace experiences.
• Are navigating a career transition or returning to work.
• Want to become more resilient, self-assured leaders.
• Lead teams and want to create psychologically safer workplaces.

Whether you’re an emerging leader, senior executive, entrepreneur, or woman navigating your next chapter, this evening is for you.

Event Details

Date: Wednesday, 18 November 2026
Time: 5:30 PM – 8:30 PM
Location: Central London (exact venue to be announced)
Hosted by: Women on the RISE
Theme: Heal • Reset • Lead • Thrive

Come for the Conversation. Leave with a New Perspective.

Imagine walking into a room filled with ambitious, accomplished women who understand that behind every successful career is a story that isn’t always visible.

Imagine leaving with renewed confidence, practical tools, meaningful connections, and a clearer vision of the leader you want to become.

Your past workplace experiences may have shaped your journey, but they don’t have to determine your destination.

At Women on the RISE, we believe in lifting one another, rising together, and soaring beyond the limitations placed upon us.

Reserve your place and join us for an evening of reflection, connection, empowerment, and growth.

Women on the RISE — Lift. Rise. Soar.

Real Conversations. Practical Strategies. Lasting Change.

I would position this on Meetup and LinkedIn as a premium, interactive leadership and wellbeing workshop, rather than a trauma support group. That helps attract corporate professionals, managers, senior leaders and women in career transition while keeping the subject approachable.

One important distinction: unless a qualified trauma professional is facilitating, the event should be presented as an educational, supportive workshop rather than therapy or a promise of trauma healing.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/9/6/2/highres_536646498.jpeg,2026-11-18 17:30:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,University Women’s Club,2 Audley Mayfair,London,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,{technology},,external,https://www.meetup.com/london-women-on-the-rise-meetup-group/events/317024013/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/london-women-on-the-rise-meetup-group/events/317024013/,event_317024013@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.493162+00,,,,,f,GB
29ea878e-6a94-49a3-bd7f-e691f575c04a,,PostgreSQL Fireside Chat,"Join Pat Wright, Advocate at Redgate, and Pavlo Golub, PostgreSQL expert and developer at CYBERTEC for an hour of unscripted conversation about where Postgres is headed and what it means for the…","Join Pat Wright, Advocate at Redgate, and Pavlo Golub, PostgreSQL expert and developer at CYBERTEC for an hour of unscripted conversation about where Postgres is headed and what it means for the people running it.

What we will cover

• Real-world stories from people who work with PostgreSQL every day, not just the theory.
• Why PostgreSQL is the right call for your relational database needs, with examples from the field.
• Where PostgreSQL and AI are heading, and what that shift means for your day-to-day work.
• How the PostgreSQL community can help you do your job better, and how to get more involved.

Speakers

**Pat Wright**
Advocate at Redgate
Pat Wright is an Advocate with Redgate Software. He has been a database professional for 25 years, specializing in PostgreSQL for the past 10 years, after a long career with SQL Server. He has worked across large-scale SaaS platforms, early-stage startups, and a wide range of consulting engagements over the past decade. Pat currently serves as the Sponsor Coordinator for PGUS and as President of Utah Geek Events, and is a frequent speaker in both the PostgreSQL and SQL Server communities. His sessions draw on deep real-world experience with performance, automation, and operational best practices. Outside of tech, he enjoys photography, classic cars, and cycling.

Pavlo Golub
Senior Developer & Consultant at CYBERTEC
Pavlo is a PostgreSQL expert and developer at CYBERTEC, PostgreSQL contributor and GSoC Org Admin. He’s been working with PostgreSQL since 2002. He has an M.Ed. with an emphasis in Mathematics and Computer Science from the Central Ukrainian State Pedagogical University, and previously worked as a professor at the Kirovograd Medical Professional College. He is the co-founder of PostgreSQL Ukraine. He develops and maintains the PostgresDAC and pgxmock libraries, as well as the pgwatch, pg_timetable, and vip_manager projects.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/1/8/3/highres_536300867.jpeg,2026-10-27 13:00:00+00,,Europe/Vienna,online,Online event,,,7aa69eeb-df8c-40ae-b929-a4324f936266,{technology},,external,https://www.meetup.com/cybertec-meetups/events/316705497/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/cybertec-meetups/events/316705497/,event_316705497@meetup.com,,2026-10-21 22:16:27.132+00,,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,2026-10-22 09:28:23.916645+00,,,,,f,
