e7e1a5ad-4ace-49eb-93de-12f1c2e9cfaf,,Does One Off-Plan Meal Turn Into an Off-Plan Week?,Does One Off-Plan Meal Turn Into an Off-Plan Week?,"**Does One Off-Plan Meal Turn Into an Off-Plan Week?**

You eat something you hadn’t planned. Then comes the thought: “I’ve ruined it now. I might as well start again on Monday.”

One meal turns into several days of choices that leave you feeling further from your weight-management goals. Each restart feels a little harder, and your confidence takes another knock.

You want to enjoy flexibility around food and trust yourself to carry on when things don’t go to plan.

In this free live webinar, we’ll explore:

• How all-or-nothing thinking can turn one choice into a longer setback.
• Why one meal doesn’t erase your progress—and your next choice still matters.
• How to return to your intentions without punishment or overcompensating.

**You’ll leave with a simple plan to interrupt the “I’ve ruined it” cycle:** recognise the thought, put the meal into perspective and choose a manageable next step.

Imagine enjoying an unplanned meal, then carrying on without needing another Monday restart. How much time and energy would that give you back?

Hosted by **Gaelle Joseph and Philip Perre**.

If you’d like ongoing support to put these ideas into practice, we’ll also share details of our **Mind and Body Reset membership**.
Explore Mind and Body Reset (https://www.weightharmony.co.uk/mind-and-body-reset-membership)

Want to explore what keeps getting in your way and how support could help?
Book a discovery call (https://calendar.google.com/calendar/u/0/appointments/schedules/AcZssZ0NXWkvTJDKtZVPzii5WO9FgQN7ldMEEwja_t-4EfRU8NFQUXJ846KBeWsfbl3IKfJcX4Om4qp1)

**What do you tend to tell yourself after eating something you hadn’t planned—and how does that affect your next choice?** Share in the comments below. We’d love to hear from you and bring your questions into the session.

***Please note:*** This webinar is for educational and self-development purposes only and is not intended to replace medical, nutritional or psychological advice, diagnosis or treatment.

