1b23bfe8-62d7-4b68-a2c4-610f9365410c,,Build & Learn: From Data Science to AI Engineering Week 7(ONLINE DEMO),📅 Week 7: Demo Day,"**📅 Week 7: Demo Day**

This is the final event in our seven-week AI Engineering program and we are doing it online.

After building an end-to-end AI application step by step, it’s time to share what you created.
This week, we’ll focus on presenting our projects and reflecting on the full development journey:

This is the final event in our seven-week AI Engineering program. This week is about sharing what you built, explored or learned—the project does not need to be complete.

You can **choose** what you would like to present yourself, here is a list of possibilities :

• Demo your complete AI application.
• Focus on one technical component, such as LLM calls, RAG, APIs, databases, evaluation or deployment.
• Share a challenge you faced and how you approached it.
• Explain an experiment that worked—or one that didn’t.
• Talk about your most important learning from the seven weeks.
• Present your architecture or development process.
• Share what you would improve or build next.
• Present your own project, even if it differs from the shared build.

The goal is not to deliver a polished or production-ready product. It is to reflect on your progress, communicate what you learned and learn.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/4/b/7/highres_532445303.jpeg,2026-11-14 09:00:00+00,,Europe/Berlin,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,data,ai,science}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/build-learn-data-science-saturdays/events/316622518/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/build-learn-data-science-saturdays/events/316622518/,event_316622518@meetup.com,,2026-10-21 22:16:27.132+00,,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,2026-10-22 09:28:23.916645+00,,,,,f,
4c57e9f2-069d-4869-b17f-a69076eb7b47,,Canal Walk - Angel to Victoria Park Cafe / Market,We will enjoy a leisurely walk (approx 45 mins - 1 hour) along Regent's Canal from Angel station and ending at the fabulous Victoria Park Market. This event usually runs on the 4th Sunday of each…,"We will enjoy a leisurely walk (approx 45 mins - 1 hour) along Regent's Canal from Angel station and ending at the fabulous Victoria Park Market. This event usually runs on the 4th Sunday of each month, unless there is bad weather or exceptional circumstances. We are a welcoming group, so feel free to mix around and say hello other people.

There is a wondering food market in Victoria Park, and most of us will get something to eat together. We usually sit on the grass or public benches (if available) near the Bonner Gate entrance, behind the Dogs of Alcibiades statue. This is at the intersection of foodstalls running north/south and east/west. If it is raining or the market is closed, we can either go to the Pavillion cafe, or The Crown pub on Grove Road instead.

Please note a few points:
1. There is currently no charge for this group. I will need to review this again later in 2026.

2. WE WILL WAIT ONLY ABOUT 10 MINUTES AFTER THE START TIME. If you are running late, please catch us up along the canal. Please note, I will not be checking for meetup or whatsapp messages after the walk starts.

3. The nearest tube station to Victoria Park is Bethnal Green station (central line). Please check Google Maps or similar.

4. You are responsible for yourselves on the walk, so please bring appropriate footwear etc. Please be mindful of those around you, especially where the canal gets narrow in places.

Whatsapp group here: https://chat.whatsapp.com/IJd6MJfVDPC6jUw6iW77ZY

Previously, there was a separate walk on the 3rd Sunday of the month, which started at Limehouse Basin, and then ran along the same canal to Victoria Park. Please note, the walks starting from Limehouse on the 3rd Sunday of the month are now cancelled for the foreseeable future.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/f/2/e/highres_520768462.jpeg,2026-10-25 12:00:00+00,2026-10-25 15:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Angel Station,A1,London,c06699ed-62e0-4957-bcb4-080c5271da9a,"{sport,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/canal-walk-run-food-markets/events/315650747/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:49:59.056229+00,source:cba1b9d2-d09d-4c19-a89e-50bdbe5525a0,https://www.meetup.com/canal-walk-run-food-markets/events/315650747/,event_315650747@meetup.com,,2026-10-24 03:20:44.813+00,,2026-10-22 19:49:59.056229+00,2026-10-24 03:21:21.677232+00,,,meetup:canal-walk-run-food-markets:canal walk angel to victoria park cafe market,"Every 4th Sunday of the month until July 25, 2027",f,GB
18cbcf0e-957a-4a26-9954-2cc953df70d5,,Docs in Practice: Behind the State of Docs,"This month, we're joined by GitBook (https://www.gitbook.com/), one of the most widely used and recognised platforms for publishing documentation. Join us for an evening with Addison Schultz…","This month, we're joined by **GitBook (https://www.gitbook.com/),** one of the most widely used and recognised platforms for publishing documentation. Join us for an evening with Addison Schultz (https://www.linkedin.com/in/addisonschultz/) (Developer Relations Lead), Tal Gluck (https://www.linkedin.com/in/tal-gluck-32464131/) (Developer Advocate), and Stephen Ashby (Content Marketing Lead) for an exclusive behind-the-scenes at how they do documentation themselves.

In the first half, they’ll take us inside the tooling and workflows from docs.gitbook.com (http://docs.gitbook.com). Then, they’ll take us through the widely distributed **State of Docs Report (https://www.gitbook.com/blog/state-of-docs-2026)**: How they ran the global survey, the industry trends it revealed, and where they believe documentation is headed.

**🗒️ Agenda**
**When:** Thursday, 19 November from 6:00pm
**Where:** Wallacespace Spitalfields: 15 Artillery Ln, London E1 7HA
**What:**
**18:00 - 18:30** Arrival
**18:30 - 18:40** Welcome & Housekeeping
**18:40 - 19:10** Talk 1: How GitBook runs its own docs
**19:10 - 19:40** Break (with drinks and nibbles 🫒)
**19:40 - 20:10** Talk 2: Behind the State of Docs
**20:10 - 20:30** Q&A
**20:30 - 21:00** Networking
**All times are approximate.**

**📍 How to find us**
