c906b160-4158-4df3-8bd5-4e542b386504,,Building an Internal Developer Platform for Kubernetes,"In this webinar, we’ll demonstrate how you can build an internal developer platform using meshStack, empowering your development teams to focus more on delivering value and less on managing…","In this webinar, we’ll demonstrate how you can build an internal developer platform using meshStack, empowering your development teams to focus more on delivering value and less on managing infrastructure.

**Language: English**
**Where: Google Meet**
To get the webinar link, **please, register on our website**: https://www.meshcloud.io/en/company/events/building-an-internal-developer-platform-with-meshstack/

**Who is this webinar for?**
This is a workshop for platform engineers, aiming at building a container-based platform to their developers and empowering them to focus more on delivering value and less on managing infrastructure.

**Our IDP Reference Architecture**
Within this workshop, we’ll use a reference architecture, comprising AKS, GitHub for Version Control and Github Actions for CI/CD, as well as a PostgreSQL database.

**Reducing Cognitive Load for Developers**
The primary goal is to reduce the cognitive load for your developers. By providing an out-of-the-box setup for building containerized applications, we ensure that developers can get started quickly without needing to worry about the complexities of the underlying infrastructure. This streamlined approach accelerates development time and enhances productivity.

**Enabling Consistent Infrastructure for Day 2 Operations**
While simplifying the developer experience, it’s also critical that the underlying infrastructure remains consistently configured. This consistency ensures that the platform can scale smoothly and support day 2 operations. As a platform team, we need to make sure that the integration of all components is seamless and manageable over time.

**Managing the Lifecycle of Integrated Components**
Juggling the integration and lifecycle management of various components can be challenging for platform teams. In this workshop, we’ll show you how meshStack simplifies this process, allowing your platform team to efficiently manage and maintain the entire lifecycle of your platform’s components, from development to production.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/f/e/5/highres_533840453.jpeg,2026-11-04 09:00:00+00,,Europe/Berlin,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,{technology},,external,https://www.meetup.com/cloud-foundation-community/events/316879621/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/cloud-foundation-community/events/316879621/,event_316879621@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.493162+00,,,,,f,
