6e565988-4d7f-47c3-9f9d-5ca34faf4ffc,,👁️🎬 CLAYFACE (A DC HORROR EXPERIENCE),"🗿 Some monsters are made, not born. And when the face in the mirror is no longer your own, the nightmare has just begun…","**🗿 Some monsters are made, not born. And when the face in the mirror is no longer your own, the nightmare has just begun…**

👋 **What's up, guys!** Looks like DC is taking horror seriously for a change, as this won't be your stereotypical superhero flick. The buzz around this one is that it will lean heavily into body dysmorphia, identity and psychological unease, pushing the DC universe in a much darker direction.

This body horror setup is directed by **James Watkins** and based on the eponymous **DC Comics** character. The story follows an up-and-coming actor whose face is disfigured by a gangster. As a last resort, he turns to a scientist who transforms his body into clay, with horrifying consequences.

For now, at least, **Clayface** stands as a standalone genre piece within the **DC Universe**, blending horror and tragedy rather than traditional superhero spectacle. But who knows what the future holds?

**The Meetup:** We'll be meeting for drinks at **8:00 pm** at the **Victory House Wine Bar** before heading to **VUE Cinema West End** for the **9:00 pm** screening. I'll be seated in **A13 (Screen 2)** if you'd like to sit nearby.

**After the film**, we'll regroup in the foyer at approximately **11:15 pm** to share our thoughts and review the film for **Letterboxd (https://letterboxd.com/movieroadhouse/)**. You'll also find the **full details, booking link and venue addresses below** to help you find your way.

If you're a fan of the eerie and the weird, then this should be an unsettlingly fun night out!

**See you guys there,**
**Jonny**

