ca2c2176-7d2c-4853-8ae5-b92d94391de9,,Harnessing AI in Capital Markets Engineering,"Correctness and precision in AI-augmented engineering featuring Jonny Press (CTO, Data Intellect) and Tom Dellmann (Director of Engineering, Chronicle).","**Correctness and precision in AI-augmented engineering featuring Jonny Press (CTO, Data Intellect) and Tom Dellmann (Director of Engineering, Chronicle).**

Doors at 6pm for a 6:30 start, two talks with time for questions, then food, drinks and networking.

**Jonny Press, Data Intellect**

Data Intellect is a consultancy built around KDB+ and Q, the high-performance database and language behind real-time analytics. Jonny is its CTO and has worked in the language his whole career, coming up through First Derivative and KX.

He'll make the case for Q in the age of AI. Coding models tend to churn out pages of code, but Q's terse primitives do more with less: less to read, review and explain to a regulator. Expect a live demo of analytics that are trivial in Q and awkward in SQL.

**Tom Dellmann, Chronicle Software**

Chronicle makes low-latency software for capital markets: messaging, FIX engines and the trading systems built on them. Tom is Director of Engineering and has stayed hands-on, leveraging AI to stay in contact with the code.

He'll resurrect Maude, an academic model checker he last grappled with at university, now made approachable with Claude. He'll live-demo using it to find real issues, including in Chronicle's own open source projects.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/b/3/c/highres_536555644.jpeg,2026-11-12 18:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,2 Pear Tree Court,"2 Pear Tree Ct, London EC1R 0DS, UK",London,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,data,ai}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/capital-markets-engineering-london/events/316936193/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/capital-markets-engineering-london/events/316936193/,event_316936193@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.493162+00,,,,,f,GB
2d998a32-8c93-4da0-8a5d-32d7b007e0a6,,Unlocking Flow - Making KFC a £1Bn Digital Business,"Digital transformation is often framed as a technology challenge. Organisations invest in platforms, applications, agile delivery methods, and transformation programmes in the hope of accelerating…","Digital transformation is often framed as a technology challenge. Organisations invest in platforms, applications, agile delivery methods, and transformation programmes in the hope of accelerating growth and improving customer experience.

Yet technology alone rarely creates business success.

Before COVID, digital was not a major priority for many Quick Service Restaurant businesses. Within a few years, home delivery, mobile ordering, kiosks, and digital customer journeys became critical growth channels across the industry. For KFC, this shift represented both a huge opportunity and a significant challenge.

The opportunity was clear. As home delivery and aggregator platforms grew, KFC needed to maintain a direct relationship with its customers rather than relying on third-party intermediaries. At the same time, its highly configurable menu made digital channels particularly effective at helping customers make choices and increasing basket size. The challenge was that the organisation itself was not structured to support a digital-first business.
The answer was not tighter delivery management.

Instead, KFC embarked on a journey to align its organisation around fast flow. Teams, responsibilities, decision-making, and operating practices were redesigned to optimise the customer ordering experience end-to-end. The result was greater autonomy, clearer ownership, faster delivery of digital capabilities, and ultimately the growth of digital channels to more than £1 billion in annual sales.

This transformation became one of the featured case studies in the second edition of *Team Topologies*.

In this special LeanTech Gemba session, KFC Digital’s Ben Richards, *Team Topologies* co-author Matthew Skelton, and Philippe Guenet, one of the transformation coaches behind the journey, will share the story behind the case study and the lessons learned along the way.

Together, they will explore:

• Why delivery management alone was not enough
• How customer flow became the organising principle for the business
• How Team Topologies influenced the design of teams and responsibilities
• How organisational design enabled greater autonomy and ownership
• The challenges encountered during the transformation
• The practical lessons learned from scaling digital capabilities
• What other organisations can apply from the experience

This is not a discussion about theory.
It is a real-world transformation story showing how organisational design, flow, and team structure can unlock business performance and enable sustained digital growth.

Who Should Attend?

Reducing siloes and enabling flow is ultimately a leadership challenge.
This session is particularly relevant to CTOs, CIOs, Heads of Engineering, Product Leaders, Delivery Leaders, Transformation Leaders, Digital Leaders, Architects, Engineering Managers, Team Coaches, and anyone responsible for improving organisational effectiveness.
Whether you work in a startup, scale-up, business unit, or large enterprise, this session will provide practical insights into designing organisations around customer value, enabling flow, and building the conditions for sustainable digital growth.

Speakers

Ben Richards **– System Coach, KFC Digital**

Ben supports leaders and teams to align on purpose, build confidence in their ways of working, and reduce friction across teams. Creating environments where continuous improvement isn’t just a practice, but a capability that delivers on today’s strategy while shaping tomorrow’s opportunities.
Ben is driven by a desire to see teams and individuals thrive through the utilisation of their collective intelligence and diverse experiences to accomplish exceptional results. Ben takes pride in observing individuals’ strengths and capabilities shine through in their work.
It's an approach recognised on some of the most credible stages in the field. Ben has spoken at Atlassian's flagship Team conference, been recognised with an award from the Agile Business Consortium and featured as a published case study in *Team Topologies.*

Matthew Skelton **– Co-author of *Team Topologies***

Matthew provides leaders with the levers and language to **enhance decision-making**, **reshape operating models**, **redesign capability placement**, and create cultures that **enable sustainable high performance without burnout**.

As co-author of the award-winning book ‘Team Topologies’ and CEO at Conflux, Matthew’s ideas and practices have been adopted by organizations worldwide to transform how they deliver value. Recognized by Book Authority as one of the “Best Product Management Books of All Time,” Team Topologies has become a reference point for leaders looking to **scale with clarity, reduce friction and improve value flow**.

Drawing on **Team Topologies**, **Adapt Together™** and related approaches, Matthew works with executives and teams to integrate organizational design, platform thinking and humane leadership, demonstrating that **business performance and…",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/9/9/0/highres_536727024.jpeg,2026-11-19 12:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,d529a6f8-b2d5-4689-bad4-376fffe4d42a,{technology},,external,https://www.meetup.com/leantech/events/315470544/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/leantech/events/315470544/,event_315470544@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.689062+00,,,,,f,
ca1f9811-2faa-4c59-b579-48dcea6b027e,,Film Discussion: The Life of Chuck,Join us for a friendly discussion of the film The Life of Chuck directed by Michael Flanagan based on Steven King's book with the same name.,"Join us for a friendly discussion of the film The Life of Chuck directed by Michael Flanagan based on Steven King's book with the same name.

