bc485e74-d4fc-49e0-a94b-0f8ad3e15bfc,,"Hiking to Windsor Castle, the Thames path and Magna Carta Monument",Any Questions WhatsApp Gary 07968585224,"**Any Questions WhatsApp Gary 07968585224**

This beautiful and historic hike follows the Thames towards **Runnymede**, one of the most important historic sites in England. It was here in **1215** that **King John sealed the Magna Carta**, the document that placed limits on royal power and helped shape the development of modern democracy.
From Runnymede, we climb through woodland before entering the magnificent **Windsor Great Park**, hiking through ancient oak trees, open parkland and rolling countryside. We’ll then join the famous **Long Walk**, with superb views towards **Windsor Castle** as we make our way into Windsor.
**Windsor Castle** has been a royal residence for almost 1,000 years, while the surrounding Great Park was once the traditional hunting ground of generations of kings and queens.
Our hike finishes in **Windsor**, where you are welcome to join us for a well-earned drink and refreshments before making your way home.

**🕘 Schedule & Meeting Info**

• **Meeting Time:** 09:10 London Paddington Station next to the ticket office near platform 1
• **Trains**: **09:37:** Depart **London Paddington** **09:51:** Arrive at **Slough**
**10:10:** Depart **Slough 10:16:** Arrive at **Windsor & Eton Central** 40 mins
• **Tickets:** Contactless accepted or Return ticket London to Eton and Windsor Central Station or
• **Hike Start:** 10.16 Windsor and Eaton Central Station
• **Lunch:** pack lunch (water,snacks and lunch)
• **Estimated finish:** 17:00, Windsor and Eton Central Station
Return Trains to London every 20–30 minutes

**🎫** Train fare is not included please purchase your own return ticket in advance or on the day.

**📍 Hike Overview**

• **Grade: Beginner 🥾**
• **Hiking time:** 5-5.5 hrs excluding breaks
• **Distance:** 19 km
• **Accent:** 140m
• **Terrain:** Riverside paths, woodland trails, parkland and well-maintained tracks.
• **Pace:** Steady with regular breaks

👣 **Hike Leader:** Gary📱 07968585224📧 [golondongary@hotmail.co.uk](mailto:golondongary@hotmail.co.uk)

**What to Bring**
✅ Hiking boots or sturdy shoes
✅ Waterproof jacket & layers
✅ Packed lunch, snacks & water
✅ Sun protection (exposed cliffs)
✅ Train ticket / Railcard

**💬 What to Expect**
Our hikes are social, inclusive, and fun. Expect a welcoming community of Londoners, expats, solo walkers, professionals, and nature lovers. Most people join solo – and leave with new friends.

**🧭 Qualified, Insured Hike Leaders**
All GO London events are led by qualified, experienced, and fully insured hike leaders, trained in outdoor safety, navigation, and group management.

