5e6f7cad-32c6-43e4-8aa0-6cb390fed3a2,,Startup Pitch & Networking in London,📍 Registration is on Luma — Meetup is not our RSVP platform. Please register here to secure your spot: https://luma.com/2h86s6ht,"📍 **Registration is on Luma — Meetup is not our RSVP platform.** Please register here to secure your spot: https://luma.com/2h86s6ht

🚀 **Join our event in London!**

We design Pitch and Networking nights to help founders sharpen their thinking through direct, candid feedback and to give strong investors access to serious teams.

**Our pitch night is complemented by a structured networking session before and after the pitch session.**

▶ **See how our pitch nights look:** https://vimeo.com/877496618

**💡 What to expect:**

• **Startups pitch live and receive focused feedback** from angels and VC partners
• **Structured networking session** before and after the pitches
• Entrepreneurs, startup founders, and operators are joining to network, exchange ideas, and build strong connections
• Active investors and venture scouts joining to discover the best startups early

**🤝 Who you will meet at the event:**

• Founders
• Investors, VC partners, Venture Scouts
• Marketers, Salespeople, Business Advisors
• Industry Disruptors
• AI Experts
• Entrepreneurs from Europe, Asia, and the United Kingdom

**💼 We Welcome New Investors:**

We invite investors to our event to expand their network, get acquainted with new startups, evaluate them, share feedback, and participate in discussions with early-stage and serial founders.

We offer **complimentary tickets to institutional investors, angels, and venture scouts** with a proven track record.

Please apply via Luma (https://luma.com/2h86s6ht) or send us an email so we can issue the ticket.

If you'd like to **access our database of promising startups** or **provide mentorship support to our best startups**, please fill out this short Investor Application Form (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdn1s8f5_R3iaqYoJ4aU2q1IxcFXIZIQElD6cEcv8YkRQhaUA/viewform), and our team will contact you.

**🎤 Want to Pitch?**

A limited number of founders will have the opportunity to pitch their startup or business **to a panel of investors and experts.**

4-6 selected founders will pitch their startup, followed by a short Q&A where participants can ask questions and share feedback.

Apply by filling out the Pitch Application Form (https://forms.gle/CuscVQibyXBbi1Fv7) and sending us your pitch deck.

Spots are limited, and we select founders in advance.

To maintain high-quality pitches, you are required to present with a pitch deck. We will share our **pitching guide** and, if you'd like, **coach you** so you're fully prepared for pitch night.

🏆 **The best startups will be featured** across our social media and included in our **investor newsletter.**

**Requirements for attendees:**

• Dress code: smart casual. Bring good energy.

**🎟 Join our event and secure your ticket today!**

**About us:**

Startup Valley (https://startupvalley.club/) is a global event organizer hosting pitch nights in 25 cities since 2023. Since then, **we have hosted 850 events for 40,000 attendees**. Over these years, we connected countless outstanding early-stage startups to serious investors, and we are not planning to stop. We maintain strategic partnerships with VC funds in the US, Europe, and Asia to support our community.

Do you have a **question, a partnership proposal, or want to clarify something**? Reach us at hello@startupvalley.club

**Agenda**

• 18:00–18:30 — **Registration**: Guests register, receive badges, and event programs. This is an opportunity for casual networking, making first connections, and preparing for the event.
• 18:30–19:00 — **Event Kickoff & Interactive Networking**: Official welcome from the organizers with a brief overview of the event goals and schedule. Interactive networking session to connect with key contacts.
• 19:00–19:50 — **Startup Pitch Session**: Startups present their projects to investors and experts. Each team has 5 minutes to pitch, covering the project’s core idea, business model, and target market.
• 19:50–21:00 — **Chill & Networking**: Participants enjoy casual conversations with investors, discuss collaboration opportunities, and exchange ideas over refreshments.

**FAQ**

**Can I pitch?**
Yes! To pitch, please purchase a Pitch Ticket and fill out the Pitch Application Form. We will contact you to discuss and approve your pitch. The pitch duration is 5 minutes. You will also have some time to answer questions from the audience.

**How does the pitch go?**
Selected founders present on stage to the audience and the investors in the room. You get 5 minutes to pitch your idea, business model, target market, and investment ask, followed by a short Q&A. The best startups are featured across our social media channels and in the investor newsletter.

**Who will I meet?**
Founders, angel investors, VC partners, venture scouts, AI experts, engineers, operators, marketing and sales experts, and international entrepreneurs from across Europe, Asia, and the US.

**Do investors get free tickets?**
Yes! Please apply via Luma (the link is in the event…",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/f/3/f/highres_536052095.jpeg,2026-11-10 18:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,The Earls Court Community Hub (10th Fulham Scouts),"1a Aisgill Ave, London W14 9NF",London,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,entrepreneurship,finance}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/startups-tech-events-in-london/events/316469593/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/startups-tech-events-in-london/events/316469593/,event_316469593@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.493162+00,,,,,f,GB
0249a52e-0165-4754-874c-019678e28110,,Body-Doubling | THURSDAY 09:00 - 16:00,Update:,"Update:

👉Aufgrund von Terminen mit Kunden, werde ich zu teilen an der Donnerstags-Session nicht selbst anwesend sein, d.h. die Gruppe ist offen zur selbstorganisation.

👉 Due to client appointments, I won’t always be present during the Thursdays session, so the group is open to self-organisation.

🇩🇪 **Deutsche Version, English below**

**Fokus Body-Doubling: Gemeinsam in Stille ins Tun kommen**
Egal ob du arbeitest, studierst, liest oder Papierkram erledigst, oder deine Wohnung aufräumst – in dieser Session konzentrieren wir uns gemeinsam.

**Ablauf:**

• **ca. 5–10 Min** Check-in & wer mag, teilt mit, was in dieser Session erledigt werden sollte
• **ca. 60 Min.** Fokuszeit (Mikro aus zu jeder Zeit, gerne gegenseitig erinnern – auch mich :D )
• Ganz kurzer Check-in nach 60 Min
• **Pausen:** Es hat sich gezeigt, dass die Teilnehmer*innen sich selbst zu den Pausen organisieren: Sich beispielsweise was zu essen machen, mit dem Hund gehen und dann wiederkommen – das ist o.K.
• **ca. 5–10 Min** Check-out & Nachbesprechung

👉Wer nach Start dazukommt, wird kommentarlos hereingelassen, in der nächsten Check-In-Runde geht’s dann gerne mit ins Gespräch.
👉 Wenn die Möglichkeit besteht, einen 2. Bildschirm (Handy & Laptop) zu nutzen, perfekt. Es macht viel aus, einander zu sehen.

**Wichtig:**
🎯 **Fokus ist Fokus:** In den Body-Doubling-Sessions gibt es bewusst keine Break-out-Sessions oder umfangreiche Socials.
**📵 Keine Teilnahme aus öffentlichen Umgebungen,** wo Fremde mithören- und sehen. Bitte schützt unseren gemeinsamen Raum.
**🎥 Kamera ist Pflicht**
**👋 Wenn du kurz weg musst: kein Problem, kein Abmeldeszenario.**
**⏱️ Verlängerung auf Wunsch –** gib mir ein Zeichen, wenn du noch bleiben magst, ich, aber auch andere, gehe gerne mal in die Verlängerung.

Ich freue mich auf dich, **""lets get things done together""!**

Die Sessions sind und bleiben free, wer mag darf mir einen Coffee spendieren. Ganz ohne Verpflichtung, einfach als Dankeschön. 💚 Tip für einen Kaffee (https://ko-fi.com/bodydoublingforeveryone)☕️.

🇬🇧 **English Version**

**Focus Body-Doubling: Let’s Get Things Done**
Whether you're working, studying, reading or doing paperwork – this session helps you stay focused and productive.

**Agenda:**

• **ca. 5–10 min Check-in** & optional sharing of what you’d like to get done in this session
• **ca. 60 min Focus Time** (mic off at all times; feel free to remind each other – me too :D)
• **Quick check-in after 60 min**
• **Breaks:** Participants usually manage their own breaks – grab food, walk the dog, and come back when ready. That’s perfectly fine.
• **ca. 5–10 min Check-out & reflection**

👉 If you join after we’ve started, you’ll be let in without comment and can join the next check-in round.
👉 If possible, use a second screen (phone & laptop) – it really makes a difference to see each other.

**Important:**

• 🎯 **Focus is focus:** In Body-Doubling-Sessions there are deliberately no breakout rooms or extended socials.
• 📵 **No participation from public spaces** where strangers could listen or watch. Please protect our shared space.
• 🎥 **Camera is required**
• 👋 If you need to step away for a moment: no worries, no need to announce it.
• ⏱️ **Extension optional:** If you’d like to stay longer, just let me know. I – and often others – am happy to extend.

The sessions are going to stay for free. But if u fancy it - leave a donation for me: coffee tip (https://ko-fi.com/bodydoublingforeveryone)☕️

Looking forward having you around **""lets get things done together""!**",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/b/7/d/highres_531983421.jpeg,2026-12-17 08:00:00+00,2026-12-17 15:00:00+00,Europe/Berlin,online,Online event,,,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/online-body-doubling-coworking/events/xdckxtyjcqbwb/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:14:19.427857+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/online-body-doubling-coworking/events/xdckxtyjcqbwb/,event_xdckxtyjcqbwb@meetup.com,,2026-10-21 22:13:45.894+00,,2026-10-21 22:14:19.427857+00,2026-10-22 19:53:35.38298+00,,,meetup:online-body-doubling-coworking:body doubling thursday 09 00 16 00,"Every week on Thursday until December 30, 2026",f,
