dc05e667-ccde-494c-9148-96a5b1bf4a91,,FREE Hike Surrey Hills St Martha’s Church and River Wey 12 miles Beauty😍,Please 🙏 Read Details Carefully to avoid Disappointment.,"**Please 🙏 Read Details Carefully to avoid Disappointment.**

This is a Free Hiking event.

You only pay for your return train tickets with groupsave its around £12 or £13.

However there are rules on this meetup
group so please read them carefully to avoid being banned from this meetup group.

If you RSVP as attending and fail to show-up you will be banned from this meetup group for time wasting operation. The ban will be permanent.

This event has been posted on 2 other meetup groups. So you will see more faces from other meetup groups joining us at this event.

**To join WhatsApp Group txt.**

**07590 919391 via** WhatsApp Only....

One of the most popular Hiking Events In the Surrey Hills Area. And one of the most beautiful Hikes that can be done in the Surrey Hills Area of Outstanding Natural Beauty.

Not to be missed. This event is only done once per year. We will not repeat it again for at least another 12 months.

Full of natural beauty and natural history. Very beautiful Scenic picturesque views.
Bring your best 📷 camera and dress appropriately for the weather forecast. Hiking shoes are absolutely necessary.

Please read carefully and pay attention to details.

**Meeting Point.**

Meet under the main Central Clock at
London Waterloo station 8.20 am prompt - for the 9.00am train to guildford. Try to get there earlier than 8:20 am so you will have time to find the group.

From Guildford Station we will walk The North Downs Way to Martha’s Hill and more. Enjoy the Outdoors. Relaxed pace) (2 miles per hour).

.............

We will meet under the Main Central Clock. WhatsApp group communication is important so you can find the meeting point and the group.

**By purchasing the Train tickets in groups of 3 or more people together we will save 30% on Train ticket.**

**Your return group train travel will be approx. £12 or £14 per person from London Waterloo Station.**

I will update this Via WhatsApp nearer the date with any changes.

£14 each. Group Return Train ticket from London Waterloo- to- Guildford.

For the purchase of train tickets Please bring your money in cash only. No Bank transfer is allowed. No time.

You can also meet us at Guildford train station at 9.30 or travel by car and park in various paid car parks in Guildford. This is down to you to find and meet us outside Guildford Train Station at 9.35 am Promptly. There are FREE car parks on the roads 5 to 10 minutes walking distance from Guildford train station.

Planned arrival time back to London Waterloo station will be between 6:30 to 7:30 pm.

Please join the whatsApp Group. So you can communicate with each other on the day of the event and share photos.

Whether you are a serious hiker or just want something light and easy this hike has it all, from a gentle stroll along the River Way, to challenging hill climbs with fantastic views. We will not leave anyone behind and you will have frequent water stops and photo opportunitie

Guildford is a beautifully charming town in Surrey, The hike will take us out along the River way, before heading up to Chantries Wood, Chilworth Gunpowder Mills, and back down to newlands corner with fantastic views across the Surrey Hills & The North Downs Way, before returning we will be able to visit St Martha’s Hill Churc

Our hike will take us through beautiful countryside, expansive open woodlands along the River Way. Guildford is famous for its historic buildings and cobbled street, of which we will see many, there are truly breathtaking views from St Martha’s Hill for as far as you can see.

.............

**Difficulty level**

**Intermediate Level**

Hiking time.
6 hours moving time and maybe 7.5 hours with the added breaks.
Distance 12 miles Approx.

**Food.**

We will stop during the hike for a snack lunch so please bring packed lunches and drink. Water stops will be frequent please bring 2 litres of water.

**What to bring.**

Suitable hiking clothes & footwear - ideally hiking shoes. Hat gloves if cold, water proof jacket and trousers. Dress appropriately for the weather.
Hiking boots are advisable. Some areas during the hike will be dense and muddy.

Clarification on the weather will be posted Via WhatsApp nearer to the walk.

Probability of rainfall is not important. Volume of rainfall expected is more important information than probability of rainfall. This event will not be cancelled regardless unless there is an emergency situation.

**Terms and Conditions**

**By participating you understand that the host and organiser is not liable or responsible for your health and safety. This is a hobby group. You as an individual bear full responsibility for your own safet**

**If your profile photo or your profile name does not comply with the terms and Conditions set by admin which are stated on the first page of this meetup group. Then your profile will be removed and banned permanently from all future events from this meetup group.**

.............

