a03bb7d4-d7f2-4d1f-9067-23debfdaf810,,NEW HIKE: Autumnal colours Part 1: Is this Surrey or Canada?,"There is a magical place not too far from good old London where the colours of the trees seem straight out of a fairy tale, it will allow us to take the most gorgeous pictures both mental and…","There is a magical place not too far from good old London where the colours of the trees seem straight out of a fairy tale, it will allow us to take the most gorgeous pictures both mental and physical, a trip that I could make many times and never get tired of.

The hike will take us through stunning woodlands, villages and in places straight out of a book from the Grimm brothers

Red, yellow, green, orange, all these colours will charm us. Take your lover, meet one or just enjoy the nature with our awesome hikers, whatever the reason, this is a pretty place that I will teach you to love.

This hike will have a couple of hills and is a bit longer than my usual ones and will feature tons of varied landscapes and views to remember.
This is a remodeling of one of my first ever hikes in the UK.

If the public right of way is still open, we might even have a peak for free at the Winkworth A rboretum (The owner has been trying to close the public right of way for many years and as I haven't been in4 years, I cannot promise access, but nevertheless, we will have a try.

The rest of the hike though is an absolute stunner, you will see so many different landscapes and types of woodlands that you can only fall in love with it!

As always, you will have the opportunity to grab some food in a nice restaurant in Godalming after the trip.

PLEASE HAVE WATERPROOF SHOES WITH A GOOD GRIP, YOU WON'T BE ABLE TO DO THIS HIKE WITH TRAINERS AS IT WILL GET REALLY MUDDY.

INFORMATION:

Distance: 15 Miles/23 km
Time:5-6 hours
Hills: 2
Steepness: Medium

PRICE:
£15 for the guide's fee via paypal

About £20 in cash for the train ticket, we will buy a group return ticket together to save about 35%

INCLUDED:

Guided hike

A great time with lovely people

NOT INCLUDED:

Train

Anything not mentioned above

WHAT TO BRING:

Waterproof shoes for the hike, preferably hiking shoes, otherwise good trainers;

Weather appropriate clothes, including waterproofs if there is a chance of rain;

Water bottle;

Packed lunch and snacks.

MEETING POINT:

London Waterloo Station at 08.15 am

ATTENTION:

Our trips will not be cancelled due to weather conditions so please ensure that you do wear and carry appropriate clothing. 😄

POLICIES:

1: This group is designed for the pleasure and enjoyment of all of us, we do not accept any derogatory comments or behaviours towards anyone. Racism, discrimination and other unacceptable behaviours will only lead to your rejection of any of our trips and this is without exception. Everyone is welcome, we have religious and non-religious people, gay, straight, bisexual people, all shades and colours or nationalities, people of all ages, sex and political beliefs and mutual respect is the fundamental spirit of this group.

2: Our trips are only refundable up to 30 days before departure, if you wish to cancel after that, you will be offered a transfer to another trip for the same price or you may resell your slot to somebody else.

3: If we do cancel the entirety of the trip on our site, you will be fully refunded",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/b/0/e/highres_535931022.jpeg,2026-10-24 07:15:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Waterloo,York Road,London,c06699ed-62e0-4957-bcb4-080c5271da9a,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/jons-trails/events/316354295/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/jons-trails/events/316354295/,event_316354295@meetup.com,,2026-10-23 03:22:35.713+00,,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,2026-10-23 03:23:01.453296+00,,,,,f,GB
