354557a2-51e0-41be-86a1-b115606f7a46,,"Putting ""Think and Grow Rich"" Into Action",Chapter 8 - Decision: the Mastery of Procrastination,"**Chapter 8 - Decision: the Mastery of Procrastination**
What if the single biggest obstacle standing between you and your dreams is not a lack of opportunity, but a lack of decision? In this powerful discussion of Chapter Eight from *Think and Grow Rich*, we tackle Decision: The Mastery of Procrastination, where Napoleon Hill reveals how indecision is the silent killer of success and why the ability to make clear, unwavering choices separates the achievers from the dreamers. Are you ready to break free from hesitation, take control of your destiny, and step boldly into the life you were meant to lead?

Every week, we delve into one of the **13 principles of success**, exploring how to incorporate it into our daily actions to meet our objectives. Our sessions include a live online study group where participants can engage and learn together to gain valuable insights on how to utilize this knowledge for your own success.
Think and Grow Rich was the first book to boldly ask, ""What makes a winner?"" The man who asked and listened for the answer, Napoleon Hill, is now counted in the top ranks of the world's winners himself.

**Group Guidelines:**
This group is meant to be interactive. Having your video on is encouraged but not required. Come with questions and an open mind. My goal is to provide a safe and engaging environment for us to learn from each other and walk away feeling empowered to take action. Please practice kindness and respect. We'll summarize key takeaways from previous weeks, so don't worry if you missed the last one; drop in at any point in the book!

“There’s something really powerful about groups and shared experiences. People might be skeptical about their ability to change if they’re by themselves, but a group will convince them to suspend disbelief. A community creates belief.” — Charles Duhigg
Let's think and grow rich together!

Looking forward to meeting with you,
Dave and Doug",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/0/1/2/highres_536277362.jpeg,2026-11-17 19:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/london-e-business-owners-meetup-group/events/316958906/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:14:19.927193+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/london-e-business-owners-meetup-group/events/316958906/,event_316958906@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-21 22:14:19.927193+00,2026-10-28 03:22:27.129706+00,,,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02:putting think and grow rich into action:online,,f,
31d551db-9d0c-4f05-9083-fb376001c723,,Icebreaker & Launch Session: Meet the Community,"Welcome to our very first online gathering! This session is all about breaking the ice, setting a comfortable rhythm for future events, and meeting fellow members in a relaxed, low-pressure…","Welcome to our very first online gathering! This session is all about breaking the ice, setting a comfortable rhythm for future events, and meeting fellow members in a relaxed, low-pressure environment.
Whether you want to introduce yourself on mic, type in the chat, or simply grab a seat and listen in, you are 100% welcome. Zero pressure, zero forced call-outs.
**What We’ll Cover (30–45 Mins)**

• **Welcome & Concept Overview (5 mins):** A quick intro to how our upcoming financial briefings and presentation practice sessions will work.
• **Casual Intros & Light Chat (20 mins):** Share a bit about your background, profession, or general interests—only if you feel like speaking up. Mics, cameras, and chat box are all optional. Anonymous/quiet participation is fully respected!
• **Upcoming Session Preview (10 mins):** An introduction to how our content-sharing format works. We will open the floor for voluntary sign-ups for our next session (volunteers receive their short narration script via email 3 days in advance).
• **Wrap-Up & Q&A (5 mins):** Final thoughts and offline next steps.

**Event Details**

• **Location:** Online (Meeting link will be visible upon RSVP)
• **Duration:** 45 to 60 minutes
• **What to Bring:** Just yourself! No prior preparation or financial background required.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792639290/orbit/event-covers/sources/z5apjeqnegmhyvt7e8hn.jpg,2026-12-05 04:30:00+00,2026-12-05 05:30:00+00,Asia/Kolkata,online,Online event,,,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/public-speaking-forum-economy-and-finance-narration/events/317050004/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 03:21:15.028412+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/public-speaking-forum-economy-and-finance-narration/events/317050004/,event_317050004@meetup.com,,2026-10-22 03:20:45.416+00,,2026-10-22 03:21:15.028412+00,2026-10-22 19:53:37.886591+00,,,meetup:public-speaking-forum-economy-and-finance-narration:icebreaker launch session meet the community,"Every week on Saturday until February 16, 2027",f,
0f0b0678-b098-497a-8fb4-d6678fdc784f,,South London Tech Community Days: November 2026 Brunch,"This event is open to anyone who works in or is interested in the tech industry, whether you are a developer, designer, engineer, entrepreneur, student, or hobbyist. You can meet new people, share…","This event is open to anyone who works in or is interested in the tech industry, whether you are a developer, designer, engineer, entrepreneur, student, or hobbyist. You can meet new people, share your experiences, learn from others, and find potential collaborators or mentors.

