a384642c-58ad-436c-aeb8-1ab162a5a405,,"Copilot, Power Platform & Dynamics Coffee Talk!","Welcome to our first Copilot, Power Platform & Dynamics Coffee Talk!","Welcome to our first Copilot, Power Platform & Dynamics Coffee Talk!

This will be a relaxed meetup where we can get to know each other, exchange ideas, and decide together which topics we would like to explore in future events.
We can discuss Microsoft Copilot, Copilot Studio, AI agents, Microsoft Foundry, Power Platform, Dynamics 365, Dataverse, business automation, governance, security, and responsible AI. We can also exchange project experiences, talk about new and upcoming features, and help each other with practical questions and implementation challenges.

There is no formal presentation planned for this first meetup. You do not need to prepare anything or be an expert. Simply bring your questions, experiences, and ideas.

If someone would like to present a topic, use case, or demo in the future, we can plan a dedicated online or in-person session based on the topic and the number of interested participants.

Agenda
• Arrival and introductions
• Brief introduction to the community
• Open discussion about Copilot, AI agents, Power Platform, and Dynamics 365
• Collection of ideas for future topics
• Planning the next meetup
• Informal networking

German will normally be our main language.
If more English-speaking participants attend, we can hold the conversation in English so everyone can participate.
Everyone is welcome, from curious beginners to experienced professionals.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/d/e/4/7/highres_536636903.jpeg,2026-11-18 17:30:00+00,2026-11-18 19:30:00+00,Europe/Berlin,online,Online event,,,7aa69eeb-df8c-40ae-b929-a4324f936266,"{technology,food}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/copilot-power-platform-dynamics-coffee-talks/events/317016500/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/copilot-power-platform-dynamics-coffee-talks/events/317016500/,event_317016500@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.493162+00,,,meetup:copilot-power-platform-dynamics-coffee-talks:copilot power platform dynamics coffee talk,Every 3rd Wednesday of the month,f,
98b0d9bd-ce31-4685-ac2b-2ea211aaef89,,City Photowalk,"We had a great turnout last time and would love to keep the momentum. Given that the weather is getting a bit iffy, I’m going to come up with a Plan A for the actual walk and Plan B if it literally…","We had a great turnout last time and would love to keep the momentum. Given that the weather is getting a bit iffy, I’m going to come up with a Plan A for the actual walk and Plan B if it literally rains on our photography parade.
See you guys soon!

**Photowalk Code of Conduct**

Our club is a welcoming, inclusive and judgment-free space for photographers of every background and experience level.

1. Everyone is equal. Treat every member with the same respect, regardless of age, race, ethnicity, nationality, religion, gender, sexuality, disability, appearance, experience or equipment.
2. Be kind. Bullying, harassment, discrimination, intimidation, exclusion or deliberately making someone uncomfortable will not be tolerated.
3. No shaming. Never shame anyone for their photographs, ability, camera, phone, editing style, knowledge or level of experience.
4. Do not make negative comments about ability. Everyone is here to enjoy photography and develop at their own pace. Constructive feedback should only be given when someone asks for it, and it must be respectful and helpful.
5. Respect different styles. Photography is subjective. You do not have to like someone’s work, but you must respect their creative choices.
6. Help, don’t compete. Celebrate other people’s progress, share knowledge generously and make newer members feel welcome. This club is a community, not a competition.
7. Respect personal boundaries. Ask before photographing another member or sharing an identifiable photograph of them. If someone asks not to be photographed, respect that immediately.
8. Include everyone. Do not form cliques, deliberately leave people behind during walks or make anyone feel that they do not belong.
9. Take responsibility for your impact. Jokes and comments should not come at somebody else’s expense. If someone tells you that your behaviour made them uncomfortable, listen and respond respectfully.
10. Speak to an organiser if something happens. Concerns will be taken seriously and handled as fairly and discreetly as possible. Serious or repeated breaches may result in removal from the club.

The basic rule: be kind, be inclusive and never make another person feel small.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/5/c/highres_535502652.jpeg,2026-12-05 14:00:00+00,2026-12-05 16:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Liverpool Street,Liverpool Street,London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,creative,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/photowalk-club/events/316040966/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/photowalk-club/events/316040966/,event_316040966@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,meetup:photowalk-club:city photowalk,Every 1st Saturday of the month,f,GB
8b0e76bd-a729-4576-8aba-34c0b3af4162,,DevOps for Fabric - Git & Deployment Pipelines,"🎯 The Problem: Someone overwrote the production report. Again. No one knows what changed. There's no way to roll back. Manual deployments at 11 PM on Friday - because that's when ""no one is using…","**🎯 The Problem:** Someone overwrote the production report. Again. No one knows what changed. There's no way to roll back. Manual deployments at 11 PM on Friday - because that's when ""no one is using the system.""
**💡 This Evening:** We'll bring professional DevOps to Fabric. Git integration, deployment pipelines, variable libraries - the practices that make BI enterprise-ready.
**⏱️ Save yourself:** The 3 AM ""we broke production"" calls. Proper CI/CD means confident deployments, every time.
**What you'll learn:**
🏷️ **Sensitivity Labels** - Data classification and protection, and WHY labels flow with the data, not the container (data stays protected when copied)
🔐 **Microsoft Purview** - Unified governance across Azure and Fabric, and WHY Purview is the governance control plane (one place for all policies)
📂 **Git Integration** - Source control for Fabric items, and WHY Git enables collaboration and rollback (version history for everything!)
🚀 **Deployment Pipelines** - Dev → Test → Prod promotion, and WHY pipelines beat manual deployments (one click, no errors)
📋 **Variable Libraries** - Environment-specific configurations, and WHY hardcoded values kill maintainability (connection strings, paths)
**DevOps Flow:** Developer → Git Commit → PR Review → Merge → Deployment Pipeline → DEV → TEST → PROD (each with its own Variables)
**Who should attend:** Developers adopting DevOps for BI, Platform teams building CI/CD, Security teams implementing governance
**Agenda:**

• **18:30** - Welcome & Networking
• **18:45** - Sensitivity Labels & Purview
• **19:05** - Git Integration Demo
• **19:25** - Deployment Pipelines
• **19:40** - Variable Libraries & Best Practices
• **19:55** - Q&A and Discussion
• **20:00** - Networking",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/b/c/a/b/highres_532008299.jpeg,2026-11-10 17:30:00+00,,Europe/Berlin,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,{technology},,external,https://www.meetup.com/ai-and-intelligent-cloud-hamburg/events/312635991/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/ai-and-intelligent-cloud-hamburg/events/312635991/,event_312635991@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.493162+00,,,,,f,
