cfe5b09f-2b5e-42c5-ad4c-d5cf2609b384,,City Photowalk,"We had a great turnout last time and would love to keep the momentum. Given that the weather is getting a bit iffy, I’m going to come up with a Plan A for the actual walk and Plan B if it literally…","We had a great turnout last time and would love to keep the momentum. Given that the weather is getting a bit iffy, I’m going to come up with a Plan A for the actual walk and Plan B if it literally rains on our photography parade.
See you guys soon!

**Photowalk Code of Conduct**

Our club is a welcoming, inclusive and judgment-free space for photographers of every background and experience level.

1. Everyone is equal. Treat every member with the same respect, regardless of age, race, ethnicity, nationality, religion, gender, sexuality, disability, appearance, experience or equipment.
2. Be kind. Bullying, harassment, discrimination, intimidation, exclusion or deliberately making someone uncomfortable will not be tolerated.
3. No shaming. Never shame anyone for their photographs, ability, camera, phone, editing style, knowledge or level of experience.
4. Do not make negative comments about ability. Everyone is here to enjoy photography and develop at their own pace. Constructive feedback should only be given when someone asks for it, and it must be respectful and helpful.
5. Respect different styles. Photography is subjective. You do not have to like someone’s work, but you must respect their creative choices.
6. Help, don’t compete. Celebrate other people’s progress, share knowledge generously and make newer members feel welcome. This club is a community, not a competition.
7. Respect personal boundaries. Ask before photographing another member or sharing an identifiable photograph of them. If someone asks not to be photographed, respect that immediately.
8. Include everyone. Do not form cliques, deliberately leave people behind during walks or make anyone feel that they do not belong.
9. Take responsibility for your impact. Jokes and comments should not come at somebody else’s expense. If someone tells you that your behaviour made them uncomfortable, listen and respond respectfully.
10. Speak to an organiser if something happens. Concerns will be taken seriously and handled as fairly and discreetly as possible. Serious or repeated breaches may result in removal from the club.

The basic rule: be kind, be inclusive and never make another person feel small.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/5/c/highres_535502652.jpeg,2027-01-02 14:00:00+00,2027-01-02 16:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Liverpool Street,Liverpool Street,London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,creative,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/photowalk-club/events/316040967/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/photowalk-club/events/316040967/,event_316040967@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,meetup:photowalk-club:city photowalk,Every 1st Saturday of the month,f,GB
