06babd8a-963d-4db7-bf95-c5d861036bed,,The Mask & The Mirror: Mindful Art Workshop Online via Zoom,"The week before Halloween, the whole city puts on a face. Shop windows, costumes, strangers you almost recognise.","The week before Halloween, the whole city puts on a face. Shop windows, costumes, strangers you almost recognise.
For two hours, with a plain white mask in front of you, you'll make a mask of your own: with paint, colour, and whatever wants to come out. No one tells you what it should look like, or what it should mean.

This isn't an art class; it's a guided space to meet the versions of yourself with curiosity rather than judgement, and to notice what's quietly asking for more room. You share only what you want to. The rest stays with you.
You'll leave with the mask in your hands and, often, with a slightly different sense of the person wearing it.
**The evening includes**

• A small, unhurried group
• Guided facilitation
• Quiet time to create, and space to share if you choose
• A finished mask to keep

**Materials to prepare:**
• A4 paper + any art material/medium you feel called to explore.
**Language:** English · Open for Adults 18+ · No experience needed
**Price**: 15 euros via transfer, Payment confirms your seat.

**Led by Aida Akoury** Psychologist and mindful art facilitator, with postgraduate training in Art Therapy and Community Art. She founded Fluid Art & Wellness to build experiences where creativity, reflection, and real connection meet.

*Come as you are. Paint the mask. See what looks back.*
