54d56824-cb11-48e0-9ebc-36a9b3da12ab,,UX Beers Antwerp October @ Plein Magazijn with Humix,Welcome to our October UX Beers in Antwerp!,"**Welcome to our October UX Beers in Antwerp!**
This time, we will host our event on Tuesday the 27th of October with our host Humix at Plein Magazijn in Antwerp.
Ariad (https://www.ariadgroup.com/) and Creative Skills (https://www.creativeskills.be/) sponsor our events.
Follow the event online? We stream live via Youtube (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EBqyTDAyQBw)

UX TALKS

**Talk 1 : Back to pen and paper: why the best UX ideas still start with a sketch**
Mieke Van Gils (https://www.linkedin.com/in/miekevangils/?isSelfProfile=false), UX Strategist @Humix
Kato Thys (https://www.linkedin.com/in/kato-thys/), UX Designer @Humix

Our tools make it easier than ever to jump straight into polished screens. But the faster we get to pixels, the easier it is to skip the part where we actually understand the problem. In this talk, Kato and Mieke from Humix show us where good old pen and paper still make a difference, bringing real stories from their daily practice and a few honest lessons on what changes when you take a moment to put the screen aside.

Expect practical takeaways, a little science on why your brain remembers what your hand writes, and one honest question: where do you still pick up a pen? Come ready to sketch.

**Talk 2: Bringing Interfaces to Life: Getting Started with UX Animation**
Sander Spolspoel (https://www.linkedin.com/in/sanderspolspoel/), Freelance motion/3D designer

Today’s web and mobile applications are just as complex as desktop software. To keep users from feeling overwhelmed, motion design can elegantly visualize concepts and preserve context within tight layouts. Animation is also a powerful tool for brand personality — just think of how much Duolingo relies on its animated characters to delight users.

Join Sander, an animator and developer since 2008, as he breaks down how to get started with UX animation. You will learn which motion elements add real value (or a bit of cuteness) to your digital products. If you are already familiar with Figma’s Smart Animate, the new Timeline feature will take your skills to the next level. We will also explore how Lottie bridges the gap between motion software and modern UX workflows.

SCHEDULE
18:00 - Doors open. Drinks & snacks
19.00 - 19.15 - Introduction to UX Belgium Meetup, announcements
19.15 - 19:45 - Talk #1
19:45 -20:15 - BREAK
20:15 - 20:45 - Talk #2
20:45 - 21:30 - Socialize

SLACK CHANNEL
We have our own UX Belgium slack channel.
Come join us and say hi! (https://join.slack.com/t/ux-belgium/shared_invite/zt-1bjpnuiog-T4Di4flXYPWgbT9KrZ53CA)

YOUTUBE CHANNEL
All our livestreams and talks are recorded and available on our UX Belgium youtube channel (https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCno7V18T-EglYXprgrUZQ7A).

ABOUT UX BELGIUM
UX Belgium is a growing community of User Experience (UX) professionals in and around Belgium.
Look for these types of events:

UX Beers
Periodically, we gather at a different agency or venue to drink beers, network and listen to speakers on various themes in the world of UX and digital design.
UX Antwerp: Each last Tuesday of the month
UX Brussels: Each second Tuesday of the month, 4x per year

UX Workshops
Now and then we organize events to dive deeper into specific skills and techniques in UX. These are smaller, hands-on workshops designed to boost your UX toolbox.

