f048f64a-200e-43f3-b11d-1013720676c8,,Millwall FC History and Heritage Tour - The First 25 Years (1885-1910),"Join us for a fun and informative walking tour exploring the early years of Millwall FC existence on the Isle of Dogs, before moving south.","**Join us for the Millwall FC History and Heritage Tour - The First 25 Years (1885-1910)!**

Join us to explore the early years of one of the most iconic football clubs in London. Discover the roots of Millwall Football Club and learn about the key moments that shaped the club's history during its first quarter-century.

This in-person event will start from the esplanade at West India Quay, conveniently located near the West India Quay DLR Station. Get ready to immerse yourself in the rich heritage of Millwall FC with our knowledgeable guides.

Don't miss this unique opportunity to delve into the past of a beloved football institution. See you there!

Have you Walked the Walk yet?

Why not do it during the next international break of 2026.

Come and join us on our 12th Out of the Blue event - a special trip back in time to discover all of the key highlights of our famous old football club’s early existence on the Isle of Dogs (1885-1910).

Discover the very place where we were founded, the pub culture instilled from day one, the workplaces of our fan base, our club headquarters, plus all 4 sites of our very first football grounds in that 25-year time space before we moved across the river.

This is a history and heritage tour which explores Millwall’s life on the Isle of Dogs - the early days, the rapid progress, the highs and the lows of the once leading light of London football.

Learn how an amazing FA Cup run led to our old nickname ‘Dockers’ would lead to us being known as the ‘Lions’.

The Isle of Dogs has an interesting history too which is interwoven into the very fabric of our DNA, you will hear some myths debunked, some less known secrets plus plenty of amusing anecdotes to keep you smiling!

We finish in a pub which was our previous HQ, and have a quiz (with prizes) which is always great fun.

Anyone who ‘Walks the Walk’ will also receive a souvenir booklet, and if you join us on this tour we shall endeavour to provide you with both a memorable London tour experience, but also a unique insight into the history and heritage of Millwall Football Club.

Let ‘em come!

**Check out our many Testimonials:**

*""A great walking tour bringing Millwall's early history to life Really enjoyable few hours around the Isle of Dogs. Rob and Mike are great guides and really help bring the history to life* *Tour is wider than purely club history and talks about the changes in that part of London and the fascinating history in this once vital world port. Learnt a lot but all done in an enjoyable and interactive way""**** - Mark Fairbrother ( Managing Director Millwall Football Club)***

*“I really enjoyed it. You were a brilliant guide. You and Mike cleared up my confusion over ‘Rear of Lord Nelson'and Millwall Park""* *-* ***Jeff Burnige (former Club Chairman)***

*""Thank you for a really great day, from Linda and myself. Enjoyed it, and were great hosts""* *-* ***Bryan King (Legendary Goalkeeper making 380 appearances 1967-1975)***

*“Great day, great people, thanks to Mike and Rob""* *-* ***Phil Coleman (Ex-player and Captain of the FA Youth Cup Winners in 1979)***

*“A great tour yesterday, very interesting, and with a great bunch of people made it an enjoyable afternoon, rounded off with a couple of pints in the Nelson!”* *-* ***Dave Sullivan (Millwall Stadium Tour Historian and Author of ‘Millwall in the FA Cup - The Road to the Millennium)***

*“Great day, and thanks for all your hard work""* *-* ***Chris Bethell (Club Historian and Co-Author of 'Millwall Football Club 1885-1939')***

*“This tour shines more light on the life of the fan base in the docks and gave a great insight to our club history back then”* *-* ***Micky Simpson (former Millwall Fan on the Board)***

*""It was an excellent experience. Supported the club since 68/69 and learnt found out some new stuff today. A great few hours and a must for Lions fans""* *-* ***Adrian Wisson (former Millwall Kit Man)***

*“So what did you do during the international break?* *In my case, it was to go on a walking tour around the docks on the #Millwall history and heritage tour. Fascinating stuff, well worth a wander!” -* ***Karl Bates (BBC Radio and Millwall TC Commentator)***

*""A great time was had by all. It was really informative. I would recommend that Millwall supporter’s when you get the opportunity to go make sure you do”* *-* ***Stan Godwin (No One Likes Us Talkin' show pundit)***

*""This is a terrific walking tour of the original sites from which Millwall FC began in the Victorian and Edwardian eras. A very absorbing and entertaining mix of social and football history, this will interest any Millwall fan who wants to understand the industrial and dockland origins of our great club. Highly recommended""* - ***Nick Hart (Auctung! Millwall Podcast)***

*""Thank you for a great day, learnt a few things and had a drink in a pub my Grandad Tiny Joyce may have had the odd pint or three! The tour was well presented and we had a few laughs.I'm more than happy to…",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792660174/orbit/event-covers/sources/xcwtes6camu0ivnxs2nw.jpg,2026-11-14 11:00:00+00,2026-11-14 14:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,West India Quay,"West India Quay Esplanade, Canary Wharf",London,c17c4a77-8c19-42da-a932-7fd57ad27fc7,"{gaming,arts,hobbies,socialising}",,external,https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/millwall-fc-history-and-heritage-tour-the-first-25-years-1885-1910-tickets-1996432830338,Register on Eventbrite,f,,t,,16.96,16.96,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 09:09:07.357991+00,source:692118d3-2638-432e-9973-25e783168a55,https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/millwall-fc-history-and-heritage-tour-the-first-25-years-1885-1910-tickets-1996432830338,eventbrite-1996432830338,,2026-10-28 03:23:43.538+00,,2026-10-22 09:09:07.357991+00,2026-10-28 03:24:07.409619+00,51.5073678,-0.0219012,,,f,GB
31166de3-cc51-48af-81f8-c67e989aac47,,London Society FOOD CRAWL - Tooting Market,"Have you ever wanted to explore and savour as many food places within an event? If so, this may be the right one for you.","Have you ever wanted to explore and savour as many food places within an event? If so, this may be the right one for you.

Welcome to another one of the FOOD CRAWLS where you have the opportunity to explore and savour the food from some of the places we may visit.
  With this particular event, we will be exploring an array of cuisine revolving around Mauritius, Guyana and England however, it’ll be the first time that we’re doing this in a food market. The market that has been chosen is ‘Tooting Market’. We will also be savouring what they may deliver.
Based on research and experience, the places we are to visit have some unique delicacies which has brought joy to the world.

Here are the food places we’ll be visiting:

• Mange de Iles (Mauritian)
• Pepi’s (Guyanese)
• Candycane Lounge (English)

So the plan is extremely simple. We’re to visit each food place with the market and savour their unique delicacies hence the term ‘food crawl’.

This is the opportunity to explore the Food places, eat, drink, make new friends but most importantly, have an enjoyable yet memorable experience.

My fellow explorers, if you enjoyed the event, I’m more than happy to accept any donations which of course are optional but will go a long way to help me unlock and deliver even more exciting and engaging events and resources: https://www.paypal.me/calvinjoy
  WHAT - Food Crawl WHERE - Tooting Market WHEN - 4pm - 6pm MEETING POINT - Outside Tooting Broadway Station NEAREST STATION - Tooting Broadway Station REQUIREMENTS - Just your good behaviour is all and whatever is listed above for the walk.  
Disclaimers:

Please be on your best behaviour and respect one another. This group doesn’t tolerate any misbehaviour and misconduct. Should such a thing take place, you will be removed.

If you ask a question that either already has the answer to it or doesn’t relate to the event at all, I won’t respond.

Whenever an event takes place, I will cut off contact 20 minutes after the event commences. If you message even 1 minute after the cut off time, I won’t be available as I’m conducting the event.

There will be photography and videography by myself so if you are photo conscious and/or do not want to be in the video, do kindly inform me and I’ll try my utmost best to not involve you in the picture.

Let’s all be responsible but please be aware you come at your own risk. Do be mindful of your possessions, belongings and most importantly, your safety. The ‘London society of explorers’ accept no risk of liability at this event.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/f/f/4/highres_536728660.jpeg,2026-11-07 16:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Tooting Broadway Station,"London SW17 9PA, UK",London,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,fitness,food}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/london-society-of-explorers/events/317076224/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/london-society-of-explorers/events/317076224/,event_317076224@meetup.com,,2026-10-26 03:22:31.993+00,,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,2026-10-26 03:22:57.415853+00,,,,,f,GB
