7742a661-6708-4fb5-8879-11b4a9df0855,,Seven Sisters Coastal Hike | Seaford to Eastbourne | 22 km,"Join us for one of the most spectacular coastal walks in southern England, following the famous Seven Sisters cliffs from Seaford to Eastbourne.","**Join us for one of the most spectacular coastal walks in southern England, following the famous Seven Sisters cliffs from Seaford to Eastbourne.**
Expect dramatic sea views, rolling South Downs countryside and a full day outdoors with a friendly international group of hikers from London.

🥾 Key information

**Route:** Seaford → Seven Sisters → Eastbourne
**Distance:** 22 km / 14 miles
**Difficulty:** Medium – 6/10
**Ascent:** approx. 500 m
**Walking time:** approx. 6 hours
**Meeting point:** London Victoria Station
**Meeting time:** 8:30 AM
**Hiking fee:** **£12**

💳 RSVP now — no advance payment required

Simply click **Going** to reserve your place.
There is **no advance payment required through Meetup**.
The **£12 guided hiking fee is payable on the day**, either **by card or cash**.

🚆 Transport

Transport is **not included** in the £12 hiking fee.
You can arrange your own train tickets, or, when a transport option is available, book it separately through our website:
**https://www.hikinginlondon.co.uk/seaford-to-eastbourne-seven-sisters-walk.html**

👥 Meetup attendee numbers

We also receive bookings through our **website and other channels**, so the Meetup attendee list does not always represent the total number of people joining the walk.
Many people come to our hikes on their own, especially for their first event, so don't worry about coming alone — you'll be very welcome.

📍 Meeting point

We meet inside **London Victoria Station**, near the ticket machines, close to **Boots (unit 27), WHSmith and LEON**.
Please arrive in good time so the group can travel together.
If you have any difficulty finding us, call or text Maria:
**07535 295739**

🌊 About the hike

We travel from London to **Seaford**, where our walk begins.
From Seaford, we'll follow the spectacular Sussex coastline across the **Seven Sisters**, with beautiful views over the English Channel and repeated climbs and descents across the famous chalk cliffs.
The route continues through the **South Downs towards Beachy Head**, before finishing in **Eastbourne**.
This is a rewarding full-day hike with some steep sections, so a reasonable level of fitness is required.

🎒 What to bring

• Hiking boots or walking shoes with good grip
• Waterproof jacket
• Water
• Packed lunch and snacks
• Suitable clothing for the weather
• Card or cash for the £12 hiking fee

Please check the weather forecast before travelling.

⭐ About Hiking in London

Hiking in London is a friendly international hiking community with **12,000+ members on Meetup and more than 35,000 people across our wider community**.
Our walks are a great way to **explore the countryside, meet new people and enjoy a day outdoors**.
Many members attend their first hike alone.
**Come alone or bring a friend — you'll be very welcome.**",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/3/b/b/highres_536381915.jpeg,2026-11-21 08:30:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Victoria Station,"London, UK",London,c06699ed-62e0-4957-bcb4-080c5271da9a,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/hiking-in-london/events/316775545/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/hiking-in-london/events/316775545/,event_316775545@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-22 19:54:29.549376+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.486349+00,,,,,f,GB
