aa82a033-c8c9-4728-959a-1524fa9370e7,,Free Terrible Football @ Regents Park Sunday at 10:30am,Hey Terrible Footballers!,"Hey Terrible Footballers!

We play in Regent Park. See the map above or follow the below whatsapp link. Leave a message and someone will respond on Saturday night. Sometimes we have openings as late as that and this is when final list is finalised.So feel free to add your name to the waitlist.

Everyone is welcome! That means every skill level, gender, sexuality etc. Just gotta be over 18!

No one gets upset if we miss a pass.... or the ball altogether! Skills vary from old semi-pro players all the way to never kicked a ball. We weren’t fibbing when we said inclusive.

Please bring a BLACK and WHITE tshirt. Please aim to arrive at 10:15 (ideally 10:15am to help out in the setting up) as we want to kickoff at 10:30.

(If you arrive late after kick off, you may have to wait around half hour for the next half).

Please sign up early (during the week if possible), check the meetup page for the week and our Whatsapp group for any last minute changes.

Follow this link to join us on whatsapp:

https://chat.whatsapp.com/HLps3JK0kSmHR2vuJj1VDu

The game will normally go ahead come rain or shine if we have the numbers.

Some important information:

• Age 18+

• Terrible Football meet-ups are extremely popular but unfortunately we have limited spaces. If you end up on the waiting list, please wait and see if a spot becomes available. We will have to check who has RSVP-ed if too many show up and will have to turn people away if they’re not on the list.

• Please show up on time! If you have RSVP-ed but don’t show up on time, we will have to give your spot to someone else! If you show up after we have started playing, and no one else has taken your spot, you might still be asked to sit the first half out in order to prevent confusion. There is nothing worse for organisers than people showing up late!

• As mentioned above, we don’t charge, however, if you are a regular, we do ask you to donate some money once or twice a year for the upkeep and new equipment.

For any questions, please contact one of the organisers.

See you there! TFC Team",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/a/0/a/highres_525327146.jpeg,2026-12-20 10:30:00+00,2026-12-20 12:30:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Regents Park,NW1 4NR,London,c06699ed-62e0-4957-bcb4-080c5271da9a,"{sport,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/terrible-football-in-london/events/315975307/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:49:59.056229+00,source:cba1b9d2-d09d-4c19-a89e-50bdbe5525a0,https://www.meetup.com/terrible-football-in-london/events/315975307/,event_315975307@meetup.com,,2026-10-25 03:20:46.537+00,,2026-10-22 19:49:59.056229+00,2026-10-25 03:21:28.4898+00,,,meetup:terrible-football-in-london:free terrible football regents park sunday at 10 30am,Every week on Sunday,f,GB
ccfe5b5a-fd1e-4353-aabb-195d7c0b37d3,,"TEXTILE REPAIR - PATCHING- SASHIKO, BORO, APPLIQUÉ – 1 DAY",Bookable via our website ➡️ https://www.thegoodlifecentre.co.uk/events/patching-sashiko-boro-applique-1-day-2/,"**Bookable via our website ➡️** https://www.thegoodlifecentre.co.uk/events/patching-sashiko-boro-applique-1-day-2/
**⋆⋆⋆**

**Course:** Textile Repair workshop: Patching – Sashiko, Boro, Appliqué – 1 day

Demystify the art of sashiko along with other patching techniques used to mend and alter clothing or accessories.

Sashiko is a traditional Japanese technique which transforms mends into visually striking additions to your well-loved clothing using repeated stitches. Translated to “little stabs”, the craft originated 400 years ago as a means to preserve clothing and embrace damage through creative stitch patterns.

If you’ve ever wanted to try your hand at this practical, yet aesthetic mending technique but didn’t know where to start, this is the perfect course for you.

During the course, you will learn about the tools and materials necessary to start your mending journey as you are guided through a range of techniques which include sashiko and appliqué by experienced textile artist Selina Latour. You will learn other patching methods using hand stitch techniques used in patching such as herringbone, whip, slip and blanket stitches.

Bring along a piece of clothing or two to practice the new techniques on and mend throughout the day!

Visit our website for more information: https://www.thegoodlifecentre.co.uk/textile-repair-workshops/",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792812017/orbit/event-covers/sources/hozf2ry7kcymyl3ywjop.jpg,2026-11-22 10:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,The Goodlife Centre,49/55 Great Guildford Street,London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising,hobbies}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/thegoodlifecentre/events/316653802/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,140.00,140.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-24 03:19:48.126338+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/thegoodlifecentre/events/316653802/,event_316653802@meetup.com,,2026-10-24 03:19:10.673+00,,2026-10-24 03:19:48.126338+00,2026-10-24 03:20:18.381173+00,51.503124,-0.096614,,,f,GB
092b5d6f-7168-4f07-8877-20df874ba124,,Artist's Way Free Course,The Artist’s Way – weekly creative circle,"**The Artist’s Way – weekly creative circle**
Each Tuesday we work through one chapter of Julia Cameron’s *The Artist’s Way* together.

**Before each session:**

• Read (or listen to) that week’s chapter
• Keep up your morning pages
• Take your artist date

**Please bring:**
Your book, a notebook and a pen.

**How the session runs:**

• **Check-in:** how your morning pages and artist date went, and anything significant from your week
• **Tasks:** we work through the chapter’s tasks together as quiet writing exercises
• **Reflection:** a short share at the end, only if you’d like to

**A safe space**
This is a peer-led circle, not a class or therapy group. We’re all in it together, including me.
What’s shared here stays here. You don't have to share, and nobody will be fixed or critiqued. Different views are welcome, shared with kindness.

Cameras on, at least during check-in and sharing - seeing each other helps us all feel safe and connected. You can turn them off during quiet writing time. If you need yours off at some point, just let us know at the start of the session.
Sessions are not recorded.

This work can sometimes bring things up. If it does, please be gentle with yourself and reach out to someone you trust, or to a professional if you need more support.

**Schedule**

• 27 Oct – Week 2: Recovering a Sense of Identity
• 3 Nov – Week 3: Power
• 10 Nov – Week 4: Integrity
• 17 Nov – Week 5: Possibility
• 24 Nov – Week 6: Abundance
• 1 Dec – Week 7: Connection
• 8 Dec – Week 8: Strength
• 15 Dec – Week 9: Compassion
• 22 Dec – Week 10: Self-Protection
• 29 Dec – Week 11: Autonomy
• 5 Jan – Week 12: Faith

Dates around Christmas may change; I’ll confirm nearer the time.
However your week went - seven days of pages or none - you are welcome to join. Just come as you are.

**WhatsApp group**
We also have a WhatsApp group for support between sessions - sharing pages done, artist date ideas and little breakthroughs. Please see under **Event Chat** to join. Please note that members can see each other’s phone numbers.

Dom",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1793071190/orbit/event-covers/sources/uijudafh6qsrvpavufjw.jpg,2026-12-15 19:30:00+00,2026-12-15 21:30:00+00,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising,books}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-givbfttm/events/317079303/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,0.00,0.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-27 03:19:45.380416+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-givbfttm/events/317079303/,event_317079303@meetup.com,,2026-10-27 03:19:10.711+00,,2026-10-27 03:19:45.380416+00,2026-10-27 03:20:35.626139+00,,,meetup:meetup-group-givbfttm:artist s way free course,"Every week on Tuesday until January 12, 2027",f,
