b20dcaab-3eb8-4a62-b3fe-752d130df2b6,,Women in Data & AI London Lunch | At The Table,At The Table,"At The Table

**A small networking lunch for women in Data, AI & beyond**

At The Table is an intimate networking lunch for women working across data, AI, governance, risk, technology, transformation, policy and related fields.

This is deliberately small.
Just six women around one table, including the host.

The purpose is to make meaningful professional connections while giving everyone enough time to understand what the other women actually do, what they are working towards and where there might be opportunities to support, introduce, collaborate or help one another.

Whether you're building your career, growing a business, considering your next move or simply want to expand your professional circle, this is a chance to meet women working in and around some of the same spaces.

There are no panels, presentations or formal pitches.
No speed networking.
No pressure to work a room.

**It is networking, just around one table rather than across a crowded room.**

Who is it for?

Women working across areas such as data, AI, governance, risk, compliance, technology, digital transformation, cybersecurity, product, policy, research, consulting and adjacent fields.

You do not need to have “AI” or “data” in your job title. What matters is that your work, business or professional interests meaningfully touch this space.

What to expect

Each table is limited to **five guest places**, with six women in total including the host.

Keeping the gathering small means everyone has the opportunity to take part in the conversation and leave knowing more than simply another person's name and job title.

Expect a polished but relaxed setting, intelligent conversation, professional networking and a mix of discussion about careers, business, work, ideas and whatever else naturally comes up around the table.

The aim is simple: **leave with a handful of meaningful professional connections rather than dozens of introductions you barely remember.**

The details

**Group size:** 6 women, including the host
**Format:** Networking lunch
**Location:** The Delaunay, 55 Aldwych, London WC2B 4BB
**Date:** Sunday 15 November 2026
**Time:** 1:30 pm–3:30 pm
**Food and drinks:** Guests order and pay for their own food and drinks directly with the restaurant.

Event fee

There is a **£10 event fee** to reserve your place.
The fee helps cover the platform and administration costs involved in running At The Table. Food and drinks are paid for separately at the restaurant, and the event fee is not deducted from your restaurant bill.

Finding us

The reservation will be under **At The Table – Bess**.
I’ll be there a little before 1:30 pm. When you arrive, simply ask the restaurant team for the At The Table reservation.",,2026-11-15 13:30:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,The Delaunay,"55 Aldwych, London WC2B 4BB, UK",London,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,growth,technology,careers,data,ai}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/the-women-s-data-ai-table/events/316882869/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/the-women-s-data-ai-table/events/316882869/,event_316882869@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,2026-10-28 03:22:26.899552+00,,,,,f,GB
43fadd78-3c01-4d29-a75e-ceab4dc2e5cf,,🚀 Start Your Online Business with AI: A Practical Launchpad for Beginners,🚀 Start Your Online Business with AI: A Practical Launchpad for Beginners,"🚀 Start Your Online Business with AI: A Practical Launchpad for Beginners

Interested in starting something online, but not sure what

to sell, where to begin or how AI could actually help?

For many beginners, the biggest challenge isn't a lack of ideas — it's

knowing how all the pieces of an online business fit together. Products,

websites, marketing, technology and sales can quickly feel overwhelming.

Join **Paul Chuter** for this **free, beginner-friendly live webinar**

exploring practical ways AI and existing online business

models can help you take those first steps with greater clarity.

💡 What You'll Explore

During the webinar, Paul will cover:

✨ How to explore an online business without necessarily creating your own product or course from scratch

✨ How established webinars and partnership-based business models can work

✨ Ways AI can support research, ideas, offers, websites and marketing content

✨ How AI tools may simplify some of the technical and repetitive tasks involved in getting started

✨ The different components that go into creating an online business

✨ How training, guidance and a clear framework can help you stay focused as you learn

✨ What still requires **your input, decisions and consistent action**

👋 Is This Webinar for You?

This session is particularly suitable for **beginners, aspiring entrepreneurs and professionals** who are curious about creating an online business but aren't sure where to start.

You don't need to be an influencer, an experienced salesperson or an AI expert. The aim is to give you a **clear and realistic introduction** to some of the tools, models and approaches available today.

This is an opportunity to **learn, ask questions and explore the possibilities** before deciding what approach may be right for you.

🎟️ Free Live Online Webinar

