9cb66d8b-0f1b-4b7f-9bb3-654a9ded08d4,,💛 Navigating Chronic Pain & Fatigue: Practical Tools for Greater Wellbeing,"🌿 Living Well with Chronic Pain & Fatigue: Practical Strategies for Energy, Wellbeing & Daily Life","🌿 Living Well with Chronic Pain & Fatigue: Practical Strategies for Energy, Wellbeing & Daily Life

Living with chronic pain, fatigue, or a long-term health condition can be physically and emotionally challenging.

Many people find themselves caught in a cycle of pushing through on good days, only to experience setbacks, exhaustion, or increased symptoms afterwards.

**In this free online, webinar, hosted by Federica we'll explore practical, energy-conscious approaches that can help support wellbeing, resilience, and quality of life while living with ongoing health challenges.**

During this session, you'll discover:

✨ Why the nervous system can play an important role in how we experience stress, energy, and daily functioning

✨ Understanding the common ""Boom & Bust"" cycle and how it can impact wellbeing

✨ Practical strategies for managing energy more sustainably

✨ Tools that may help support emotional well-being, stress management, and self-awareness

✨ Ways to create a meaningful and fulfilling life while working within your current energy levels

Hosted by **Federica**, an ICF-Certified Coach with lived experience

of chronic illness, this session combines personal insight with

practical coaching principles designed to help individuals better

understand and navigate life with chronic health conditions.

Whether you're living with chronic pain, fatigue, or another

long-term condition, this webinar offers a supportive space to

learn, reflect, and explore new approaches that may help you

move forward with greater confidence and self-compassion.

🎁 All attendees will receive a complimentary practical guide containing

simple exercises and strategies to support their ongoing wellbeing journey.

**Please note:** This webinar is intended for educational and

informational purposes only and does not provide medical

advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Individual experiences will vary.

