8c4621bb-935a-4943-aeef-0a6233024119,,Operating Systems Book Club: Paging Mechanisms,Online Event - link visible to attendees,"***Online Event - link visible to attendees***

Welcome from Rust (not the game) and Cpp Cardiff! All levels welcome!

Join us as we continue our book club on the excellent Operating Systems: Three Easy Pieces (https://pages.cs.wisc.edu/~remzi/OSTEP/) by Remzi H. Arpaci-Dusseau and Andrea C. Arpaci-Dusseau. While the book is not strictly about Rust or C++, it described the fundamentals of operating systems which help you to get the most out of your software. Reading the chapter before hand is strongly recommended, but not required.

This session will cover three chapters: Translation Lookaside Buffers, Advanced Page Tables and Swapping Mechanisms.

Recordings of previous meetups are available on youtube (https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKre6QmGZ270Og0uLylTSVA). We also have a discord server for chatting between meetups - message any of the meetup organizers for the discord link.
