843a7a71-f00d-414d-b245-10069e192cc3,,Startup Pitch event - Validate your idea,🚀 Startup Pitch Event – Validate Your Idea!,"🚀 Startup Pitch Event – Validate Your Idea!

**Have a startup idea? Building a product? Looking for honest feedback before taking the next big step?**

Welcome to **Beyond the Founder – Startup Pitch & Idea Validation Event**, where ideas meet opportunities, feedback, and the right people!
Whether you have an early-stage idea, a working prototype, or an already launched startup, this is your chance to step forward, pitch your vision, and discover what others really think.

🎯 What's in it for you?

• 🚀 **Pitch Your Idea:** Showcase your startup, product, or business concept to an audience of entrepreneurs, professionals, and startup enthusiasts.
• 💡 **Validate Your Concept:** Get honest, constructive feedback from real people who could become your future customers.
• 🧪 **Find Your First Testers:** Connect with people willing to test your prototype, try your product, and share valuable insights.
• 🤝 **Meet Potential Co-founders:** Find collaborators, technical partners, and people who believe in your vision.
• 💰 **Connect with Potential Investors:** Build relationships that could open doors to future funding opportunities.
• 🎙️ **Get Featured on Our Podcast:** Selected founders may have the opportunity to share their stories on our weekly *Beyond the Founder* podcast and reach a wider audience.
• 🌍 **Build Your Community:** Find early supporters, create awareness, and start building a network around your startup.

Startup founders are ready to pitch, please register here :

https://forms.gle/yZvBPHpxsiDMGTEE8

👥 Who Should Attend?

Aspiring entrepreneurs, early-stage founders, students with innovative ideas, startup enthusiasts, potential investors, product testers, and anyone interested in discovering and supporting new businesses.

💬 No Perfect Pitch Required!

You don't need a registered company, a polished presentation, or even a finished product.
**All you need is an idea, the courage to share it, and an open mind to receive feedback.**
Come to pitch, listen, ask questions, share your expertise, or discover an exciting startup you could become part of.
**Your next customer, co-founder, tester, or investor might be sitting in the audience!**

🌟 Beyond the Founder

*Because great ideas don't grow in isolation. They grow through conversations, connections, and communities.*

**Join us. Pitch your idea. Validate your vision. Find your people.**",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/b/0/d/a/highres_536745274.jpeg,2026-11-07 11:00:00+00,,Europe/Berlin,online,Online event,,,168d49d1-9456-4c1f-a396-5bc9f2050d9d,"{carrer,growth,entrepreneurship}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/beyond-the-founder/events/317095836/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-24 03:22:25.885011+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/beyond-the-founder/events/317095836/,event_317095836@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-24 03:22:25.885011+00,2026-10-28 03:22:27.129706+00,,,,,f,
0c418036-7272-4a5d-a548-492de5c77376,,Sync Suffolk: What Are We Building Next?,Technology. Startups. Data. AI. Innovation.,"Technology. Startups. Data. AI. Innovation.
And the people making it happen in Suffolk.

Sync is returning as a place for Suffolk’s technology and innovation community to meet, share what they’re working on and have better conversations about what’s coming next.

We want developers and founders in the same room as data people.
Startups talking to established businesses.
Technical people meeting people with problems worth solving. Researchers meeting practitioners.

People experimenting with AI talking to people wondering what on earth they’re supposed to do with it and occasionally people from completely different worlds discovering that they should probably have met years ago.

Our first session back will be deliberately broad:

• What are we building next?
• What’s happening in Suffolk that more people should know about?
• What are you building, testing or researching?
