c17066b4-60c9-4574-a9b9-a6c8e8bad291,,SCOTLAND UNLEASHED: THE HIGHLANDS & ISLE OF SKYE,Four days. Three nights. One unforgettable Scottish adventure. New friends.,"**Four days. Three nights. One unforgettable Scottish adventure. New friends.**

**We’re heading into the Scottish Highlands and Isle of Skye for a small-group road trip filled with dramatic landscapes, historic castles, wild coastlines and cosy autumn evenings.**

**The adventure starts in Fort William, Scotland on Thursday, 29 Oct. Reserve your spot now.**

*Everyone will make their own travel arrangements to Fort William by train or plane. Once the group meets in Fort William, we’ll take care of the road trip- including hiring a large, comfortable vehicle for the group.*

The adventure includes:

• Glencoe & Rannoch Moor
• Loch Ness & Urquhart Castle
• Eilean Donan Castle
• The Old Man of Storr
• The Quiraing
• Fairy Glen
• Fairy Pools
• A special Halloween evening on Skye
• Beautiful, cosy accommodation
• An unforgettable Highland road trip

This is more than a sightseeing trip.
Estimated total cost: £750 per person

This includes:
🏠 Accommodation
🚐 Transport to and from Skye
🥐 3 breakfasts
🥪 1packed hiking lunches
🎃 Halloween nibbles
🗺️ Trip planning, organisation and guiding fee

Deposit:

As there are only 6 places available, a £400 deposit per person will be required.
This will allow me to cover the initial group bookings and up front.

Weekend itinerary:

Thursday: Arrival & Welcome (dinner optional)- Fort William
Friday: Old Man of Storr
Saturday: BIG Quiraing challenge, including the Three Sisters
Saturday Halloween Party
Sunday: Loch Ness, swimming/pool and Fort W

Dates: 29 October – 1 November 2026

Starting point: Fort William, Scotland
Travel to starting point: Organised individually by each guest (recommendations will be available)
Transport during the trip: Large group hire car
Group: Small and exclusive
WhatsApp

REFUND AND CANCELLATION POLICY

The estimated total cost of the trip is £750 per person. A £400 upfront payment is required to cover fixed costs and advance commitments, such as accommodation, transport and group bookings.

As these costs may be committed or non-recoverable once bookings are confirmed, cancellations may result in some or all of this payment being withheld to cover costs that cannot be recovered. Any refund will depend on the costs already incurred, amounts recoverable from suppliers and whether a replacement participant can be found.

If you can no longer attend, you’re welcome to arrange a suitable replacement, subject to approval and any supplier requirements. Once the replacement has been confirmed and any necessary transfer completed, we’ll review any recoverable costs and refund any amount due.

Please make sure you understand these terms before paying your deposit. We recommend taking out suitable travel insurance to protect against unexpected cancellations.

Places will be limited so we can keep the group small, relaxed and personal.

**Want to join us? Register your interest now.**

