5443e7b3-839b-44e7-961b-20c8bcc5c110,,Organisational Dark Matter - Stephen E. Morris,"The Future of Work Scotland team are delighted to welcome back Stephen E. Morris, author of Leaders, Believers and Expert Deceivers.","The Future of Work Scotland team are delighted to welcome back Stephen E. Morris, author of Leaders, Believers and Expert Deceivers.

For years we’ve been told that smarter strategies, North-star visions and new frameworks will make our products shine, teams thrive and transformations stick. In today’s landscape – where AI, geopolitical tensions, cost-of-living pressures and generational shifts collide – it’s ever more important to get it ‘right’, yet according to the stats:

• 70%+ of change initiatives don’t deliver (McKinsey, Gartner et al.)
• 95% of new products fail (Harvard Business School)
• 50% of employees quit to escape a bad manager (Gallup)

There’s clearly something going on, but that something isn’t simply the plan, the framework we chose or that ‘people are resistant’. The true cause is the hidden contexts – the organisational dark matter – that can quickly drain budgets, stall progress and erode loyalty. In this eye-opening talk, we’ll explore this dark matter and reveal how to work with the forces you never knew (or didn’t appreciate) were pulling the strings.

Key insights:
• The illusion of control: Why even the most detailed plans and frameworks are blind to the contexts that truly drive outcomes.
• From icebergs to dark matter: Why the physics-inspired metaphor reveals a far more useful picture of organisations and what holds them back.
• Detection as a key skill: How to surface hidden contexts, ask better questions and act with intention.

**Learning Objectives - what you'll take away from this session:**

For leaders and teams who refuse to be blindsided by what they cannot see, you’ll leave with:
• A new lens to think about organisations and to spot the invisible patterns shaping them.
• Practical principles to prime your team to detect what others miss.
• Actionable insights to benefit from these hidden contexts.

**Here's a little more about our guest speaker:**

Stephen is an author, speaker and accomplished and award-winning leader with over twenty years of experience in complex, uncertain and high-scale technical organisations. Across diverse sectors, including information technology, healthcare, banking, insurance, manufacturing, and government, Stephen has a track record of driving real success, backed by hands-on achievements and industry recognition.

Leadership highlights
• C-Suite leader during a period of extraordinary growth, achieving 400% YoY
• Leadership coach for a 300-million-dollar international software rollout
• Mentor and consultant for an international leadership team managing over 750 professionals through an organisational transformation
• Strategist for the successful launch of 50+ commercial cloud-based products and services, shaping the future of business technology
Awards
• Most Influential Business Leader, 2016 Agile Awards
• Most Improved Agile Team, 2016 Agile Awards
• Best Leadership and Agile Coaching Provider, 2020 UK Enterprise Awards",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/9/e/3/highres_536603011.jpeg,2026-11-18 19:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,{technology},,external,https://www.meetup.com/the-future-of-work-in-scotland/events/316975619/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/the-future-of-work-in-scotland/events/316975619/,event_316975619@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.689062+00,,,,,f,
83d5a6cd-3340-4b45-9f2c-49450ff20bd6,,How to Build an Unbreakable Mind — Free Live Training,FREE LIVE TRAINING · ONLINE · 1 HOUR · ONLY 10 SEATS,"FREE LIVE TRAINING · ONLINE · 1 HOUR · ONLY 10 SEATS
👉 Click ""Attend"" to save your seat. The Google Meet link shows on this page once you RSVP.
A free one-hour live training, online, with Gabriel von Knorring: former bomb disposal officer, army mental-resilience trainer and 100-mile ultrarunner.
Most men are told to ""be tougher"". Nobody shows them how. This is the how.
WHAT YOU'LL LEARN
• What an unbreakable mind really is, and what it is not
• Why most men quit on themselves after three good weeks, and how to stop the fade
• The habits that keep a man steady when things go sideways
