cc6d555c-cdbd-47a2-9cac-994de4ed50b5,,City Photowalk,"We had a great turnout last time and would love to keep the momentum. Given that the weather is getting a bit iffy, I’m going to come up with a Plan A for the actual walk and Plan B if it literally…","We had a great turnout last time and would love to keep the momentum. Given that the weather is getting a bit iffy, I’m going to come up with a Plan A for the actual walk and Plan B if it literally rains on our photography parade.
See you guys soon!

**Photowalk Code of Conduct**

Our club is a welcoming, inclusive and judgment-free space for photographers of every background and experience level.

1. Everyone is equal. Treat every member with the same respect, regardless of age, race, ethnicity, nationality, religion, gender, sexuality, disability, appearance, experience or equipment.
2. Be kind. Bullying, harassment, discrimination, intimidation, exclusion or deliberately making someone uncomfortable will not be tolerated.
3. No shaming. Never shame anyone for their photographs, ability, camera, phone, editing style, knowledge or level of experience.
4. Do not make negative comments about ability. Everyone is here to enjoy photography and develop at their own pace. Constructive feedback should only be given when someone asks for it, and it must be respectful and helpful.
5. Respect different styles. Photography is subjective. You do not have to like someone’s work, but you must respect their creative choices.
6. Help, don’t compete. Celebrate other people’s progress, share knowledge generously and make newer members feel welcome. This club is a community, not a competition.
7. Respect personal boundaries. Ask before photographing another member or sharing an identifiable photograph of them. If someone asks not to be photographed, respect that immediately.
8. Include everyone. Do not form cliques, deliberately leave people behind during walks or make anyone feel that they do not belong.
9. Take responsibility for your impact. Jokes and comments should not come at somebody else’s expense. If someone tells you that your behaviour made them uncomfortable, listen and respond respectfully.
10. Speak to an organiser if something happens. Concerns will be taken seriously and handled as fairly and discreetly as possible. Serious or repeated breaches may result in removal from the club.

The basic rule: be kind, be inclusive and never make another person feel small.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/5/c/highres_535502652.jpeg,2026-11-07 14:00:00+00,2026-11-07 16:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Liverpool Street,Liverpool Street,London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,creative,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/photowalk-club/events/316040965/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/photowalk-club/events/316040965/,event_316040965@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,meetup:photowalk-club:city photowalk,Every 1st Saturday of the month,f,GB
d73f27c2-71dc-4e89-b060-bab42ade9012,,DSOLG November Event,Details,"Details

Welcome to the DevSecOps London Gathering November Event on Wednesday 18 November! We bring you two more great speakers, as well as the usual conversations, pizza and beer!

📍 **Hosted at Adaptavist, Telephone House, 69-77 Paul Street, London, EC2A 4NQ**
📅 **Wednesday, 18 November 2026**
🕕 **6:00–8:00 PM**

**Talk** **Abstracts:**

**Talk 1 - Nobody inspects hop three — securing agent-to-agent messages**
Multi-agent AI pipelines split work across orchestrator, researcher, and writer agents — but most teams still only inspect the user prompt. Indirect injection arrives inside web fetches and inter-agent handoffs, and the last agent in the chain often holds the credentials. This session tells that story live: an attack that succeeds without protection, then the same pipeline secured with AgentGuard — open-source Python middleware (pip install inter-agent-guard) that inspects every hop with rules, optional ML scoring, Ed25519 trust attestation, YAML capability manifests, and a tamper-evident audit log.
You will see which defences are deterministic and deployable today (signatures and policy) versus probabilistic (ML with published limits). The demo uses IntelBrief, a three-agent LangGraph pipeline: poisoned web content and forged orchestrator messages blocked at the tool boundary and signature layer. Audience takeaway: deploy identity and capability controls immediately; treat ML as defence in depth with honest metrics; audit every block decision.

**Speaker Bio**:
Umme Nizba designed and built AgentGuard, an open-source firewall for the messages AI agents send each other — inspecting content, verifying Ed25519 signatures, enforcing YAML capability policy, and logging every decision in a tamper-evident audit trail. The library ships on PyPI and GitHub (v1.2.0) with IntelBrief, a live three-agent demo for indirect injection and impersonation attacks.

They hold an MSc in Information Security from Royal Holloway University of London and work as a software engineer in regulated financial services, with experience spanning secure system design, threat modelling, PCI-aware data pipelines at scale, authentication, and real-time platforms. Their talks emphasise what teams can deploy deterministically tomorrow — trust and policy — versus probabilistic ML with published limits.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/d/9/9/e/highres_536155710.jpeg,2026-11-18 18:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Telephone House,"69-77 Paul Street. Shoreditch, London EC2A 4NQ GB",London,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,ai}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/devsecops-london-gathering/events/316386425/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/devsecops-london-gathering/events/316386425/,event_316386425@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-22 19:56:05.832408+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.493162+00,,,,,f,GB
