40aa8002-6ac4-4e35-80e9-500c36471689,,Breaking Procrastination,We all have something we keep putting off.,"We all have something we keep putting off.

A goal we want to achieve. A project we need to start. A decision we need to make. Something we know matters, but somehow tomorrow always feels like a better time to deal with it.

**This free, interactive workshop is about breaking that cycle.**

Bring something you’ve been procrastinating on and spend an hour focused on getting yourself unstuck.

You’ll come away with greater clarity about what you really want, a stronger connection to why it matters, and the confidence to stop overthinking and start making progress.

No productivity hacks. No perfect plans. Just a practical, interactive session designed to help you move from **“I really need to do this”** to **“I’m actually doing it.”**

Come with something you’ve been putting off.

Maybe it’s a goal you genuinely want to achieve. A project you need to start. A decision you’ve been avoiding. A conversation you know you need to have. Or simply something that’s been sitting on your list for far too long.

You know it matters. You probably know you should do something about it.

**So why aren’t you doing it?**

That’s what this workshop is about.

This isn’t another session about time management, productivity hacks or building the perfect to-do list. Instead, you’ll take **one real thing you’ve been procrastinating on** and work on it throughout the session.

Through a series of guided exercises, personal reflection and conversations with other participants, you’ll start to uncover what’s actually keeping you stuck and what needs to change for you to move forward.

By the end of the workshop, you’ll have:

• **Greater clarity** about what you’re really avoiding
• **A stronger connection** to what you actually want
• **A practical way forward** that feels realistic rather than overwhelming
• **A clear next action** you’re ready to take

This is a practical, interactive workshop. You won’t just listen to someone talk about procrastination, **you’ll work on your own**.

Come with something you’ve been putting off.

**Leave knowing what you’re going to do about it.**

No perfect plans. No productivity guilt. Just an hour dedicated to finally getting something important moving.

**Leave ready to move it forward.**

**Frequently asked questions**

**Will the workshop be recorded?**
No, none of our workshops are recorded for privacy reasons.

