52464d45-7a5c-4d31-9b5f-0701c9548ef6,,A Fabulous Day in Paris – Seine River Lunch Cruise & Small Hosted Group,PARIS FOR THE DAY – SMALL HOSTED GROUP,"**PARIS FOR THE DAY – SMALL HOSTED GROUP**

We’re off to Paris for the day!

Join us for a fabulous hosted day trip to one of the most beautiful cities in the world, perfect for anyone who wants to enjoy Paris without the hassle of organising everything themselves.

We’ll travel from London to Paris by Eurostar and spend the day exploring the city together as a small hosted group.
A highlight of the day will be a relaxing lunch cruise along the River Seine, where we can enjoy our meal while taking in some of Paris’s most famous sights from the water.

During the day, we’ll also have time to see some of the city’s iconic landmarks, enjoy the Parisian atmosphere, take plenty of photos and have some free time to explore, shop or simply sit at a café and watch the world go by.

This trip is perfect for solo travellers, friends and couples. Most people attending our events come on their own, so you’ll be warmly welcomed and introduced to the group.
Expect a fun, relaxed and sociable day with good company, beautiful scenery, great food and the chance to experience Paris without needing to stay overnight.

A wonderful little escape from London and a chance to say: “I went to Paris for lunch on the river Seine!”

Let’s explore Paris together! I’ll be hosting and bringing everyone together throughout the day, but as I don’t know the city inside out, we’ll navigate Paris as a group and enjoy discovering the sights together.

Small hosted group, spaces will be limited.
**Maximum 12 guests**

Perfect if you’re coming solo, enjoy Paris without waiting for friends to travel with you.

**Minimum of 6 guests required for the trip to go ahead.**

Itinerary

**6:30am – Meet at London St Pancras International**

**8:01am – Eurostar London → Paris**
**Around 11:20am – Arrive Paris Gare du Nord**

11:30am

Go directly for lunch, this is beside the Eiffel Tower and where the lunch cruises depart.

12:15pm – Arrive at Eiffel Tower

Allow time to find the boat, check in and take a few photographs.

12:45–2:45pm – Seine River Lunch Cruise

This is the centrepiece of the day and gives everyone the chance to see many major Paris landmarks while having lunch.
You should see sights including the Eiffel Tower, Musée d'Orsay, Louvre area, Notre-Dame area and many of Paris's famous bridges.

2:45–3:15pm – Eiffel Tower photographs

Once you leave the boat, spend around 30 minutes around the Eiffel Tower and Seine.

3:15pm – Head to Arc de Triomphe

3:30–4:00pm – Arc de Triomphe

Photographs and a look around the famous monument.

4:00–5:30pm – Champs-Élysées

Walk down the Champs-Élysées, browse the shops, stop for coffee, wine, pastries or dessert and give everyone a little free time.
People who don't want to shop can simply enjoy the area and Paris atmosphere.

5:30–6:00pm – Optional drink / café stop

Have a final drink or coffee together before heading back.

6:00pm – Leave Champs-Élysées for Gare du Nord

We will aim to be at the station at approximately **6:30–6:45pm**.
That gives us a comfortable buffer for Eurostar ticket, security and passport checks. Eurostar says passengers should follow the recommended arrival time on their ticket, and Standard/Plus ticket gates close **30 minutes before departure**, so I wouldn't risk arriving close to 7:30pm.

8:00pm – Eurostar Paris → London

We should arrive back at London St Pancras at approximately **9:30pm UK time**, depending on the exact service.

**Early bird: £215 For the first 6 people**
**Standard price: £225pp**

**Price gone up by £10 Trian fees have increased Now £235 as from 13/10/2026**

**Price increase again NOW £250 as from 22/10/20326**
**As the date draws closer the price is increasing**

**Trip is non refundable unless cancelled minus booking fees**

**Pay via Meetup or via Eventbrite https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/1999847253971?aff=oddtdtcreator**

**Maximum: 12 guests**
**Minimum needed to go ahead: 6 paying guests**

**What's Included**
Return Train ticket
Lunch Cruise along the River Seine
Friendly host
Coming out of your comfort zone
Solo friendly
Meeting new people
Escaping the UK for the day

Meeting Arrangements

We will meet near the **Eurostar departures area at London St Pancras International**.
Please arrive **no later than 6:30am** so that we have plenty of time to meet as a group and complete the Eurostar check-in and security process together.
Once I have received **6 confirmed payments**, I will create a dedicated **WhatsApp group** for everyone attending the Paris trip.
The exact meeting point, final travel information and any important updates will be shared in the WhatsApp group before the trip.
Please make sure you arrive on time, as we will not be able to delay the Eurostar departure for late arrivals.

**Wrap up warm it maybe chilly wear comfortable footwear**

Hope you can join us for a great day out in Paris

