ef0c8a30-7ad0-4c42-9fb3-e48c9fe6e18c,,NODES 2026,"NODES, the biggest community gathering dedicated to engineering better intelligence returns on November 12, 2026, for its eighth year.","**NODES**, the biggest community gathering dedicated to engineering better intelligence returns on **November 12, 2026**, for its eighth year.
Join thousands of developers and data and AI practitioners for this free, 24-hour conference (https://neo4j.com/nodes/) to learn about the latest advancements in intelligent systems and gain insights from speakers who showcase their implementations, tools, and models.

The agenda is out (https://neo4j.com/nodes/agenda/#tab-europe-ai-engineering)!!! Here is a snapshot from the AI Engineering track

1. **From Vector Search to GraphRAG: Architecting AI Systems That Actually Work in Production**, Emmanuela Opurum, SoftNet Technologies
2. **Building an Explainable GraphRAG System: From Clinical Notes to Knowledge Graphs with Neo4j**, Joakim Nilsson, Capgemini & Johan Müllern-Aspegren, AI Futures Lab
3. **Sovereign Transaction Graphs – Adaptive Agents Without Context Leakage**: Mandy Goram, pmOne AG
4. **Why Did the Agent Do That? A Neo4j Decision-Trace Layer for AI Agents**: Alexis Ngoga
5. **Inside the AI Detective's Brain: Multi-Agent Deduction on Knowledge Graphs**, Paweł Gołąb & Michał Domański, BCNN

Check out the full agenda (https://neo4j.com/nodes/agenda/#tab-europe-ai-engineering) of unique live sessions

