d89bbf34-5b4e-4883-974c-f90645631d39,,Inside-Out Strategies: Making Agility Matter,"Digital and AI are accelerating uncertainty faster than organisations can plan for. We'll explore Inside-Out Strategy: making adaptability, experimentation, and learning strategic capabilities.…","***Digital and AI are accelerating uncertainty faster than organisations can plan for. We'll explore Inside-Out Strategy: making adaptability, experimentation, and learning strategic capabilities. Using Wardley Mapping, we’ll explore how organisations build advantage through continuous adaptation.***

Most organisations still approach strategy as if the future can be predicted and committed to upfront.

But digital acceleration, AI, shifting customer expectations, and unstable markets are making many landscapes too uncertain for heavy strategic plans to remain reliable for long.

As uncertainty increases, strategic advantage shifts away from prediction and toward the ability to sense change, learn continuously, and adapt faster than competitors.

This is where Inside-Out Strategy emerges.
Rather than treating adaptability as a supporting capability, adaptability itself becomes the strategy.

The organisation focuses less on maintaining certainty about the future and more on improving its ability to detect threats, identify opportunities, and reorganise around what it learns.

This is not about Agile theatre or another transformation programme. It is about taking a structured approach to build organisational responsiveness, learning speed, and operational effectiveness, and creating performance.

Using Wardley Mapping (no prior experience needed), we’ll explore:

• How clarity of the value chain helps organisations design operating models for adaptability
• How innovation emerges from sensing and experimentation
• How successful innovations evolve into scalable and standardised capabilities
• How organisations can improve responsiveness without losing coherence

Expect a practical session with live mapping, strategic discussion, and real-world patterns from technology and product organisations operating in uncertain environments.

You’ll walk away with:

• A clearer understanding of balancing Inside-Out and Outside-In strategies
• New perspectives on organisational capabilities as strategic advantage
• Greater confidence using Wardley Maps to connect internal change with business outcomes",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792621059/orbit/event-covers/sources/onbb6kiogmqrqraioypx.jpg,2026-11-06 12:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,entrepreneurship,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/leantech/events/314866123/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/leantech/events/314866123/,event_314866123@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-21 22:16:55.807095+00,2026-10-28 03:23:34.689062+00,,,,,f,
a57bc99f-4ef1-4e49-96fc-8897b9f127b1,,Blood on the Clocktower @OtterChaos,Join OverBoard to play the brilliant social deduction game Blood on the Clocktower in person at the brand new board game cafe Otter Chaos in Brixton.,"Join OverBoard to play the brilliant social deduction game Blood on the Clocktower in person at the brand new board game cafe Otter Chaos in Brixton.

If you haven’t heard of Blood on the Clocktower before it is an evolution of classic party games like Mafia/Werewolf where a hidden evil team takes on the good team by lying and killing. The good team has a few tricks up their sleeve but will have to work together to deduce who the evil doers are in their midst.

**This is a beginner friendly event so no experience with the game is necessary.**

Please note that a gaming cover charge of ~£5 will be payable by each attendee to the venue so that we can make use of the space. We also encourage you to buy food and drink from the bar so we are supporting the business (I can highly recommend their pizzas!)

If you want to know more about the rules of the game check out this video:
