**30-Day Writing Challenge 2026**
*Hosted by A Write & a Pint*

Do you miss NaNoWriMo?

We do too!

💭 This is our second year hosting A Write & a Pint’s 30-Day Writing Challenge, an exciting alternative to NaNoWriMo but in the same tradition!

Last year, we had just over 30 people join us to make progress on their writing. This year, well, we're ready for however many want to be part of the challenge!

If you’d like to join us throughout November 🍂, you’ll build momentum on your writing project in community with others 🤝. We’ll have live weekly online workshops 💻, workshop recordings 🎥, online accountability 📲, and social events 🎉 with other writers to help hone your skills and focus on your writing.

**Who is this for?** 🤔

If you’re a writer or would-be writer working on a book of prose, poetry, or just any writing project, this is for you!

It might be fiction ✨, memoir 📝, biography 👤, autofiction 🔄, autoethnography 🌍, a collection of short stories or poems 📚, or anything in between.

You just need something to work on that you want to make tangible progress on over 30 days 📆, with support and in community 🌟.

**What is the challenge?** 🎯

The challenge – if you choose to accept it – is just like NaNoWriMo, and to write a full, 50,000+ word manuscript 🖊️ in 30 days (wild, we know! 😅).

And for anybody who makes it to **at least 10,000 words**, we invite you to submit your favourite 500-word excerpt ✨ to our competition.

The author of our favourite piece will win a **Penguin Mini Classics Box Set** 🎁 🐧 (RRP £100). *Note: organisers Sean and Shimrit + 2 × guest judges will be reading each piece and whittling them down to a short list before choosing a winner.*

That said, if you just want to join to be able to make meaningful progress on your writing in community, without needing to track wordcount, you are still very much welcome to join us! This is for anyone who wants to spend November committed to their writing, alongside others doing the same, and with support.

**How it works** ⚙️

Through November, you’ll join **8 live, online sessions** (1.5 hours each, twice a week) 🗓️.

In the first half hour, we’ll work through practical exercises to hone your writing skills. We’ll then have an hour of shared, quiet writing time, where you can actively focus on your work.

The sessions will cover topics such as **arc, plot, style, tone, character, dialogue, pace, and perspective** 🎭, and give you practical techniques and inspiration you can put to work straight away.

Depending on the tier you sign up for, you might also participate in:

• An all-day kick-off workshop at a London location 🍵 🥐 (with brunch + tea/coffee included)
• An online midway-point check-in 💬
• A final “Read & Pint” social at a London location 🍷 📖 (with a drink included)
• A 1.5-hour, one-to-one coaching session 🎓 to dive deeper into your writing
• Editorial feedback on up to 1,500 words ✍️ 📝

You’ll also have the option of joining a dedicated **WhatsApp group** of fellow writers who are participating in the challenge 📲, for daily inspiration and accountability. Once you’re part of the WhatsApp community, there may also be people who want to commit to additional shared quiet writing time, or to self-organise writing meet-ups with others. The adventure is yours to craft! 🌟

**Total Value at a Glance 📌**

• **12 hours** of live online workshops and focused writing time (All Tiers)
• **Midway online “check-in”** gathering, to share challenges and progress (All Tiers)
• **Designed journal** to accompany you through the month, including word tracker, worksheets, and daily pages (All Tiers)
• **Facilitated WhatsApp group**, for daily support (All Tiers)
• **1 full-day** in-person kick-off workshop in London, including brunch and a drink (Tiers 2 and 3)
• **Final “Read & Pint”** in-person social with a drink, in London (Tiers 2 and 3)
• **1.5-hour 1:1 coaching session** + feedback on up to 1,500 words (Tier 3)

All participants will also be given a **50% discount code to join our [Wake Up, Write membership (https://www.writeandpint.com/pricing-plans/list)**for the month, giving you access to our Morning Sessions up to three times a week, as an additional quite space to focus on your writing (All Tiers)

**Pricing & Tiers** 💷

**Tier 1 – Weekly Online Workshops (£85)**

• 8 x 1.5-hour live online sessions (twice a week) led by our facilitators, including skill-building exercises and focused writing time
• Mid-point online check-in: gather with others and our facilitators to share and work through your challenges, progress, and successes so far
• Dedicated journal to accompany you through the month
• Accountability and community with fellow book writers
• Membership of the WhatsApp group

