4bfced5a-363f-4eaa-b49f-f39e8bfbaefd,,Public Speaking Club with Early Bird Speakers,Who We Are,"**Who We Are**
Early Bird Speakers is one of London's best public speaking club for beginners and experienced speakers alike. Our fast-paced, engaging meetings help members develop confidence and refine their speaking skills in a supportive environment.

**What to Expect**
Each meeting follows a structured format with three key segments:

• **Prepared Speeches** – Members deliver speeches based on projects that enhance skills like storytelling, persuasion, and vocal variety.
• **Impromptu Speaking (Table Topics)** – Participants practice thinking on their feet with 1–2 minute speeches on surprise topics.
• **Evaluations** – Constructive feedback is given to foster continuous improvement.

**Why Join Us?**

• A **diverse and welcoming** community, including professionals, entrepreneurs, artists, and more.
• **Energetic and engaging** sessions designed to make learning enjoyable.
• A **structured yet fun** experience that builds confidence and skill.
• Optional **post-meeting coffee or breakfast** for networking and socialising.
• Each meeting is attend by 30-50 people

**Whether you’re terrified of public speaking or already confident at the mic,**
this club is the place to grow.
From first-time speakers to experienced presenters — everyone has something to gain here.

**Meeting Details**
📍 **Where:** Freemasons' Hall, 60 Great Queen Street, London, WC2B 5AZ
🕖 **When:** Every Thursday at 7:00AM - 8:45 AM
(Please try to be on time as reception downstairs will close shortly after the meeting has started)

Join us for free as a guest! Feel free to sign up on Meetup or **simply show up on Thursday.**

Whatever your speaking ability, you'll find a warm and supportive atmosphere to grow your skills.

📩 **Questions?** Send us a message on meetup, visit www.earlybirdspeakers.com (http://www.earlybirdspeakers.com/) or e-mail us on membership@earlybirdspeakers.com",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/0/b/d/highres_529396573.jpeg,2026-11-19 07:00:00+00,2026-11-19 09:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Freemasons' Hall,"60 Great Queen Street, London",WC2B 5AZ,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,growth,entrepreneurship}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/earlybirdspeakers/events/bbxlstyjcpbzb/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/earlybirdspeakers/events/bbxlstyjcpbzb/,event_bbxlstyjcpbzb@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,2026-10-28 03:22:26.899552+00,,,meetup:earlybirdspeakers:public speaking club with early bird speakers,"Every week on Thursday until December 10, 2026",f,GB
c8416bff-9d03-4915-8703-f36589fc312a,,Founders & Freelancers Meetup,Going it alone doesn't mean doing it alone.,"**Going it alone doesn't mean doing it alone.**
A relaxed monthly evening for founders and freelancers to meet each other. No pitching, no agenda, just good people and honest conversation.

**Whether you're building a startup, freelancing, running a side hustle, starting a charity, or just doing something ambitious outside of conventional employment, this group is for you.**

Being an entrepreneur or freelancer can be a lonely experience. You've got big decisions to make, have to keep the confidence of your clients and investors, and sometimes pretend everything is okay on LinkedIn when you're stressed out of your mind. This is a space where you don't have to do that.

**The format is deliberately relaxed: come along, grab a drink, meet some interesting people.** There'll be open networking, a business card bowl to make sure you leave with at least one new meaningful connection, and space for anyone who wants to share a current challenge or screw-up.

• 6:30:PM — doors open, drop your card in the bowl, drinks and open networking
• 7:20PM — optional: share a current challenge or screw-up with the group (sign up at the door). Gareth will share something to get the ball rolling
• 7:30PM — networking continues

This is the second event in what we hope becomes something really worthwhile. Help us shape what this becomes!

Hosted by Gareth Lewis, founder of Gareth Lewis Events (http://garethlewis.co/) and co-founder of PopUp Painting (http://popuppainting.com/) and The London Art Bar (http://londonartbar.com/). Questions? [hello@garethlewis.co](mailto:hello@garethlewis.co)",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/d/3/1/highres_535699761.jpeg,2026-11-04 18:30:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,The Anthologist,"58 Gresham St, London EC2V 7BB, UK",London,168d49d1-9456-4c1f-a396-5bc9f2050d9d,"{carrer,growth,entrepreneurship}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/founders-freelancers/events/316908798/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/founders-freelancers/events/316908798/,event_316908798@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,2026-10-28 03:22:26.899552+00,,,,,f,GB
