722a737e-39b0-4be5-b094-3e5fd24daf2c,,"Badminton 1-4pm, £9.00 Per Person. Regarding Car Park charge Please read below","We accommodate intermediate and advance badminton players and also beginners, (Please message us if you are a beginner).","We accommodate intermediate and advance badminton players and also beginners, (Please message us if you are a beginner).
We also accommodate single players who want to play Singles badminton games. Singles is an option if there is a spare badminton court and the opponent is willing to have a singles game.

**We are just an 8-minute drive from Hounslow Middlesex Badminton Dome.**

**Details how to get to the badminton club by Public Transport are at the bottom.**

• a). £9.00 Per Person Pay & Play - Cash Payment Only.
• b). Time: 1:00pm - 4:00pm
• c). Please bring your own water.
• d). 3 Badminton Courts every week - **Depending on numbers attending we can increase or decrease the badminton courts, (To book more badminton courts we must know by Tuesday evening how many members are attending. Please RSVP early).**
• *e). Feather shuttlecocks are provided by the club.* **(PLEASE NOTE: We do not use plastic shuttlecocks because potentially plastic shuttlecocks could give you a tennis elbow).***
• f). **Venue Address:**
Cranford Community College Sports Hall,
High Street, Cranford, TW5 9PD
• g). Please RSVP if you are attending the Badminton Club
• h). Please ensure that you update your RSVP status ASAP if for any reason you are unable to attend the badminton club so the next member on the wait list can attend. **(If you cancel your RSVP last minute, we will not charge you).**

If for any reason you cannot RSVP on meetup. Please send Harry a text on 0771 182 4977 with your name to state you will be attending badminton and you will be added as a guest on meetup.

• ***CAR PARKING CHARGE*** at the school for the whole day is £2.90 **- Evology App** - PAY FOR PARKING BY PHONE. Please download Evology App onto your phone and make payment through this app. Instructions for this are at the car park and outside the school reception area.
• There is a 20-minute grace period for drops offs and pick before the charge applies.
• Street parking is free outside the school or on Brabazon Road, Heston, TW5 9LP, which is a 10-minute walk to the venue.
• If the car park is full, - You can park for free on the following road: - Brabazon Road, Heston, TW5 9LP. (**Don’t forget the 20-minute grace period to exit the car park).**

*Heathrow Spidernets Badminton Kit is available to buy from the following website: **www.pbteamwear.co.uk*** (http://www.pbteamwear.co.uk%2A%2A%2A/)

Heathrow Spidernets Badminton Club takes No Responsibility and will not be responsible for any personnel injuries, damage or loss of property.

Members will be responsible and are required to be members of Badminton England for insurance purposes. Website: www.badmintonengland.co.uk (http://www.badmintonengland.co.uk/)

**Transport:**
***Cars:***
There is a large Car Park, Car Parking charge at the school is £2.90 for the day - **Evology App** - PAY FOR PARKING BY PHONE.
Drive through the Blue gates up to the barrier which will then open automatically. **If the car park is full**,
Park Free on the following road: Brabazon Road, Heston, TW5 9LP.(Remember there is a 20 minute grace period to exit the car park).

***Buses:***
***105***, **H28** - will drop you outside Cranford Community College in Cranford
***111*** - will drop you outside The Queens Head Pub, Cranford go towards the mini roundabout when you come off the bus, it is a 2 minute walk.

***81, 222, H98*** - from Bath Road, Cranford
10-15 Minute walk from the Bath Road.
Come off the bus on the Bath Road in Cranford outside DoubleTree Hotel or Ibis Budget Hotel.
At the traffic lights go down the road called **'The Avenue'** walk to the end of the road. Mini roundabout take a right, walk straight down cross the road at the traffic lights or take the footbridge to cross the road. Then carry on straight down and you will see The Queens Head Pub on your right carry on straight down to the mini roundabout. Then carry on straight down and you will approach a blue fence on your left, go to the end of the blue fence and entrance to the school is on your left before the mini roundabout and bridge.

**285 Bus from Feltham to Cranford Community College**
Take 285 bus from Feltham Station towards Heathrow Airport. Get off at Harlington Corner. Take the 105 bus heading towards Greenford Station or 111 bus heading towards Kingston from outside Best Western Hotel/Marriott-Court Yard Hotel. 105 bus will drop you outside the school. 111 bus will drop you outside the Queens Head Pub which is a 2 minute walk to the school.

***Underground:***
Take the Piccadilly line to Hounslow East Station.
Outside Hounslow East Underground station take the*** 111 Bus*** heading towards Heathrow Airport come off the bus in Cranford outside Queens Head Pub go towards the mini roundabout when you come off the bus, from there it is a 2 Minute walk to Cranford Community College Sports Hall.

**Elizabeth Line:**
Take the Elizabeth Line to **Hayes & Harlington Station**.
