e821b2b8-3603-47b1-bcde-f25437a538f1,,Why Leaders Need Pattern Literacy,"Many workplace challenges appear as isolated events: a difficult meeting, resistance to change, silo working, delayed decisions, communication breakdowns or recurring team frustrations.","Many workplace challenges appear as isolated events: a difficult meeting, resistance to change, silo working, delayed decisions, communication breakdowns or recurring team frustrations.
But what if they aren't isolated events? What if they are signals of deeper patterns emerging within teams, organisations and the environments around us?

This introductory BeTeam session explores Pattern Literacy: the ability to recognise recurring patterns and use those insights to make better decisions, collaborate more effectively and respond more thoughtfully to complexity.
Whether you are a leader, coach, HR professional, OD practitioner, facilitator, change professional, or simply curious about how groups function, you are welcome to join us.

**What to Expect**
This will be a small-group, interactive learning session, not a webinar.
Together we will:

• Explore the concept of Pattern Literacy
• Consider the difference between events and patterns
• Work in small groups on a practical challenge
• Reflect on how patterns emerge in teams and organisations
• Share observations and insights
• Meet other professionals interested in leadership, teamwork and organisational life

**Agenda**
7:00pm - Welcome and introductions
7:10pm - Why Pattern Literacy matters
7:30pm - Small group exercise
8:00pm - Group reflection and discussion
8:15pm - Peer insights and networking
8:30pm - Close

**What to Bring**
Curiosity
An open mind; a willingness to contribute to discussion; a real workplace challenge or observation (optional). No preparation is required.

**Online Meeting Information**
This event will be held online using Microsoft Teams.
The Teams joining link will be sent to registered attendees shortly before the event.

Please ensure you can access Microsoft Teams and join from a quiet location where you can participate in the discussion.

**About BeTeam**

BeTeam London is a learning community for people interested in understanding teams, patterns and decision-making. Through practical exercises and collaborative learning, we explore how patterns shape teams, organisations and communities.

To help launch the BeTeam community, we're offering four discounted tickets for those who book at least seven days before the event.

**See the pattern. Understand the system. Make better decisions**

**BeTeam Cancellation Policy**
Cancel 7 or more days before the event: Full refund.
Cancel 2-6 days before the event: Transfer to a future BeTeam event.
Cancel within 48 hours of the event: No refund.
No-show: No refund or transfer.

BeTeam events are intentionally small-group learning experiences. Late cancellations can prevent other members from attending and make it difficult to offer places to people on the waiting list.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/3/highres_536520099.jpeg,2026-11-03 19:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/beteam-london-pattern-literacy-for-leaders/events/316978772/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-24 03:22:25.885011+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/beteam-london-pattern-literacy-for-leaders/events/316978772/,event_316978772@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-24 03:22:25.885011+00,2026-10-28 03:22:27.129706+00,,,meetup:beteam-london-pattern-literacy-for-leaders:why leaders need pattern literacy,"Every 2 weeks on Tuesday until April 6, 2027",f,
15ba6bde-9c1d-4e94-bee2-b54b25cd83a1,,Interview with Guy Davidson on his talks and C++26/7 + C++29,Meeting C++ is hosting an interview with Guy Davidson! He will be giving the talks What to look forward to in C++26…,"Meeting C++ is hosting an interview with Guy Davidson! He will be giving the talks What to look forward to in C++26 (https://meetingcpp.com/mcpp/schedule/talkview.php?th=538405bfda021d35d5d3c5c7653593036c76e5eb) and Profiles are coming (https://meetingcpp.com/mcpp/schedule/talkview.php?th=414814a1f2afc6aca39e237ff200830670c92856) at Meeting C++ 2026 (https://meetingcpp.com/2026)! We'll also discuss the current situation at ISO with C++26 and what the upcoming ISO meeting in Brazil will bring.

Talk description:
The three-year train model continues to deliver as the next version of C++ heaves into view. In Croydon earlier this year the committee waved off the working draft to ISO to publish it as C++26. It will take a while to work its way through the process, but we're ready to start looking at what it delivers for you, the C++ user.
The obvious, big picture items are reflection, contracts and std::execution. These impact hugely on the standard in very different ways. We will spend some time looking at each of these features, but also other smaller items like the hardened standard library.
We'll also look ahead to C++29 and consider what is still to be done. The committee listens and adapts to outside commentary: here you will find out what we've updated.

Bio:
Guy Davidson has been writing games for over 40 years. For half of that time he worked at Creative Assembly, makers of the Total War franchise, where he was the Head of Engineering Practice. He is one of the founders of #include, the diversity and inclusion group for the C++ community. Now he is the Head of Engineering at a company largely based in Ukraine operating in stealth mode. In his ""spare"" time he serves on the C++ standard committee as the convenor. He is also the chair of programming languages for the BSI. In his ""other"" spare time he plays piano, sings for Brighton Festival Chrous, teaches Tai Chi, and involves himself with local politics more than might seem necessary.

Bring your questions!
