eb331303-dc94-454a-810d-0f7df43c6a83,,Get On With It! Bring Your Own Project with optional social chat,"If you find yourself with a pile of unfinished or unstarted projects that you want to get through, look no further.","If you find yourself with a pile of unfinished or unstarted projects that you want to get through, look no further.

We've been running these free online productivity sessions since the first COVID lockdowns in April 2020.

Members have fed back that they get a much-needed productivity boost because, in coming to the session, they make sure they dedicate time to their projects. Read more here: https://suze.dev/blog/get-on-with-it/.

If there's stuff you want to get started, finished or make progress on, but are struggling for motivation, join us! We'll get together to share what we're doing, cheer each other on and generally support each other to kick-start some momentum.

Here are some examples of things people have worked on in previous sessions:

• Writing blog posts
• Learning how to build a mobile app
• Sorting out Lego
• Photography projects
• Working on an online art gallery
• Preparing for a talk
• Decluttering
• Fixing a child's broken electronic toy
• Putting up shelving
• Sewing projects
• Building mobile apps
• IoT projects with Raspberry Pi and Arduino
• Online tutorials
• Assembling a treadmill
• Painting by numbers

**How to prepare:**

Make sure you have e-mails switched on for this group otherwise you won't receive the Google Meet link. Check your Meetup settings (https://help.meetup.com/hc/en-us/articles/360002879591-Editing-my-email-settings).

**What to expect:**

The session takes place on Google Meet and Slack and the structure is as follows. All times are shown in London UK time:

3.25pm: We e-mail the Google Meet link for this event to all attendees.

 Optional: 3.30pm [Google Meet]: Social chat (not work chat ). If you want to give the social a miss, join the call at 4pm.

4.00pm [Google Meet]: Welcome from Ladies of Code.

4.05pm [Google Meet]: Tell us what you want to work on today. Type it in the chat or switch on your video camera and talk about it :)

4.15pm [Slack]: Get working! Check in / get support on our dedicated Slack channel.

5.15pm [Slack]: Tea break.

5.30pm [Google Meet]: Check back in on Google Meet for show and tells / progress demos.

5.40pm [Slack]: Go back to working on your projects. Check in / get support on our dedicated Slack channel.

6.40pm [Google Meet]: Check in on Google Meet, show and tell/watch and listen!

7.00pm [Google Meet]: Thanks, goodnight and keep up the good work!",,2026-11-01 15:30:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{technology,socialising,arts}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/ladies-of-code-uk/events/316782803/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-28 03:23:34.220625+00,source:a123de80-56fb-42df-942f-e46132c725f9,https://www.meetup.com/ladies-of-code-uk/events/316782803/,event_316782803@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:57.772+00,,2026-10-28 03:23:34.220625+00,2026-10-28 03:23:36.037184+00,,,,,f,
