7a788a8e-773f-486d-a651-0844e3024381,,"Property Investor Networking London Soho | Investors, Developers & Agents","Free monthly property investor networking in London Soho. Bring a deal, find capital, JV partners, agents, lenders and developers.","**Free monthly property investor networking in London Soho.** Bring a deal, find capital, JV partners, agents, lenders and developers.

👉 **Grab your FREE ticket here (required for entry):** https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/property-deal-network-london-soho-pdn-property-investor-networking-event-tickets-1968331789368

Property Deal Network (PDN) is a relaxed monthly meetup for property investors, developers and professionals who want to do business face-to-face.

**What happens at PDN London Soho?**
People bring deals. Others bring capital. Some are sourcing their next project, others are looking for JV partners or professional services. The format is simple: arrive, grab a drink and start conversations. No presentations, no pitches from the front – just direct networking with people who are actively working in property.

**Who attends?**
Investors (from first-timers to portfolio landlords), developers, sourcing agents, brokers, solicitors, architects, lenders and accountants. If you're involved in property – or want to be – you'll find relevant people here.

**Practical details**
• **When:** Tuesday 17 November 2026, from 7pm local time
• **Venue:** Archer St Soho, 3-4 Archer Street, London, W1D 7AP
• **Cost:** Free to attend. The venue asks that everyone buys a drink at full price
• **Dress:** Smart casual (no sportswear). Over 25s only; ID may be requested

This is an established event that runs every month (except December) – if this date doesn't work, there's always next month. All London Soho dates: https://www.propertydealnetwork.com/locations/united-kingdom-networking-events/london-soho-property-networking-event/

**Industry professional?** Paid promotion tickets (max 2 per event) are available on the ticket page for architects, accountants, builders, mortgage brokers, insurance brokers, interior designers, lenders, estate agents and surveyors.

*Property Deal Network – property investor networking in 190 cities worldwide. Join this group to hear about PDN events everywhere.*",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/9/3/6/highres_536786934.jpeg,2026-11-17 19:00:00+00,,America/New_York,in_person,Archer St Soho,"3-4 Archer Street, London, W1D 7AP",London,c78f921f-ce89-4a92-b98f-83bf7cc57102,"{carrer,growth,finance,technology}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/propertydealnetwork/events/317107254/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-25 03:22:33.838204+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/propertydealnetwork/events/317107254/,event_317107254@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-25 03:22:33.838204+00,2026-10-28 03:22:27.129706+00,,,,,f,GB
885f53b1-93c9-4f3a-9755-4b410eace21e,,🇪🇸🎬 LA BOLA NEGRA (FILM & DISCUSSION),🌈 Three lives. Three generations. One shared inheritance...,"🌈 ***Three lives. Three generations. One shared inheritance...***

👋 **Hey guys!** For our next meetup, we’re looking at **La Bola Negra** (The Black Ball), a **Spanish drama** which is easily becoming one of the most talked-about films of the year. The film is directed by the acclaimed duo **Los Javis** and brings together a great cast, including **Penélope Cruz** and **Glenn Close**.

From what I understand, the story itself is a **multi-generational drama** following the interconnected lives and romances of gay men across different eras and it’s actually inspired by an unfinished work by the legendary poet **Federico García Lorca**. The film has already generated **critical acclaim** and picked up some major awards along the way, so let’s check it out!

**The Meetup:** We’ll be meeting for drinks before the film to get acquainted. Then, after the credits roll, we’ll hang around to discuss the movie, share our reviews, and give it our **Letterboxd (https://letterboxd.com/movieroadhouse/)** score. **Full timings and meetup details will be added nearer the date, so check back here for updates.**

It’s not every day we get to see a lost piece of literary history brought to life like this, so there should be plenty for us to talk about afterwards.

**I look forward to seeing you there!**
 Faheem**

