1a705606-ab82-4b34-b8e5-b133dbbb88f2,,Designing Futures: What We Give Forward,"Hosted by Children of the Mekong, Sophie Aldebert and 1 other","**Join us for Designing Futures!**

**⚡ Event Overview**

**Join us for a unique evening blending UX, networking and forward-thinking to champion education. We will explore how design, creativity and technology can help us create more thoughtful futures for the next generations**

All proceeds will support the charity **Children of the Mekong (https://www.childrenofthemekong.org/?utm_source=luma)**, more particularly scholarships for Vietnamese students in higher education (https://www.childrenofthemekong.org/projects/support-students-at-university-and-vocational-training-in-vietnam/). Since 1958, they have provided access to education for children in Southeast Asia, helping them build a brighter future.

**🎙️ Panel Speakers**

• Chaired by **Divya Dinesh Kavungal (https://www.linkedin.com/in/divya-dk/?utm_source=luma)**, Senior UX Designer at Jaguar Land Rover
• **Michael Kibedi (https://www.linkedin.com/in/uxmichaelco/),** Design Researcher and Writer at First and Fifteenth
• **Tashfeen Ahmed (https://www.linkedin.com/in/tashfeen/)**, Senior Product Designer at Microsoft
• **Dr Lesley-Ann Daly (https://www.linkedin.com/in/lesley-ann-daly/),** Lead Design Researcher & Strategist at Tangity
• **Alison Howard (https://www.linkedin.com/in/alisonhoward90/),** Product & Service Design Consultant

**📆 Agenda**

• **6:00-6:30 PM:** Arrival, drinks & food, networking 🍕
• **6:30-6:45 PM:** Welcome and introduction 🎤
• **6:45-7:45 PM:** UX Panel exploring the futures of technology with Q&A 🎨
• **7:45-8:00 PM:** Piano recital 🎹
• **8:00-8:05 PM:** Wrap-up and closure 📝
• **8:05-9:00 PM:** Mingling and more networking 🤝

**📍 About the event**

• **Date and time:** Thursday 5th November, 6-9 PM
• **Location**: French Protestant Church (https://g.co/kgs/7v3tD94?utm_source=luma), 8-9 Soho Square, W1D 3QD London
• Drinks and nibbles will be provided

This event is proudly sponsored by:

• **UX Crunch (https://www.linkedin.com/company/ux-crunch-events/):** Bringing the best thinkers, speakers and leaders from across design together in intimate meet-up environments
• **Owendale Advisory (https://www.owendaleadvisory.com/):** Providing ambitious leaders with independent, tailored guidance and support for end-to-end Intelligence Transformation
• **Tangity (https://www.linkedin.com/company/tangity)** (part of NTT Data)**:** Enabling change through tangible solutions and an international network of strategy, creativity and design studios

We’re also kindly supported by our friends from **PD Ladies (https://www.linkedin.com/company/pdladies/posts/?feedView=all&utm_source=luma)**.

🫂 **Who Should Attend?**

This is a welcoming space for everyone, regardless of experience, gender, religion, identity, ethnicity, or background. While we especially encourage women and non-binary people to attend, all allies who support diversity and inclusion are invited to join us. We foster respect and empowerment in the UX field.

Tickets are non-refundable. Photos may be taken during the event. Please let us know if you would prefer not to be photographed.

