f3a64133-bdd5-423a-9ee6-1660a956ceb6,,Lake District Workshop - 8-days/7-nights (incl transp & acc),Guaranteed departure.,"**Guaranteed departure.**

Join us on this magical **8**-𝐝𝐚𝐲/**7**-𝐧𝐢𝐠𝐡𝐭 tour to explore the picturesque Lake District in colourful autumn with a small group (maximum of 5-6 participants only) guided by a professional photographer, and 𝐢𝐧𝐜𝐥𝐮𝐝𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐚𝐥𝐥 𝐭𝐫𝐚𝐧𝐬𝐩𝐨𝐫𝐭 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐚𝐜𝐜𝐨𝐦𝐦𝐨𝐝𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧!

As a bonus - as if the amazing scenery isn't enough! - The best filter company in the business, **Kase Filters**, is kindly sponsoring our workshop & will be providing multiple sets of their Pro filters just for us - so you can get the most out of this amazing workshop!

𝐒𝐚𝐦𝐩𝐥𝐞 𝐢𝐭𝐢𝐧𝐞𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐲:
𝐃𝐚𝐲 𝟏 – Journey to The Lakes
We’ll collect you from central London & begin the journey to our lovely accommodation in central Keswick.

We'll aim to check in and freshen up, then, if time permitting, head to our first sunset opportunity at the spectacular Castlerigg Stone Circle.

𝐃𝐚𝐲 𝟐 – Ullswater
We’ll begin our first morning with sunrise at the iconic Duke of Portland boathouse, looking down Ullswater towards the distant fells. From there, we’ll pay a visit to Hallin Fell with a gorgeous view down two valleys, with Beda Fell in all its autumnal glory dividing them. During the day, we will visit the powerful Aira Force, the most famous of the Lakes’ waterfalls, falling 70ft below a slate bridge into a rock pool & surrounded by Victorian landscaping.

𝐃𝐚𝐲 𝟑 – Derwent Water
Crow Park will start our day with sunrise, looking down Derwent Water with Borrowdale Valley and the surrounding Fells beyond. Nearby is Isthmus Bay, where you will find the remains of some concrete jetties looking towards the Cumbrian Mountains. Other options for later in the day are Ashness Jetty or Tewet Tarn.

𝐃𝐚𝐲 𝟒 – Buttermere
This morning, we will head for Buttermere and once again put those Kase ND filters to work capturing the famous lone tree with tranquil views across the lake, followed by a short journey up the lake, where we will have views of Char Hut and the autumn colours on the mosaic slopes of Haystacks. Later in the day, we will explore the Southern shore of Crummock Water with several composition options of rocks or trees to choose from.

𝐃𝐚𝐲 𝟓 – Great Langdale
We’ll start the day at the River Brathay near Elterwater, hoping for a touch of mist at sunrise with a couple of oak trees and a small copse reflecting in the calm water. Later, we will head down the Great Langdale Valley towards Side Pike & Blea Tarn, both of which have gorgeous views of the Langdale Pikes.

𝐃𝐚𝐲 𝟔 - Lowther Castle
Our last full day will see us exploring another great attraction in the morning, and our afternoon will be spent visiting Lowther Castle or a similar attraction.

**Day 7 -** We'll look at returning to locations suitable for the weather on the day, with the intent of capturing better shots or images with different conditions.

𝐃𝐚𝐲 8 – Return Journey
For our final day in the stunning Lake District, we will begin with a visit to Tewet Tarn, or even Castlerigg Stone Circle, for sunrise with views towards Blencathra and Skiddaw fells. We'll then say goodbye to Keswick & journey back to London with full memory cards and many happy memories.

𝐈𝐧𝐜𝐥𝐮𝐝𝐞𝐬:
• Return transport from London, & within the Lake District.
• Kase filter sets available to use!
• Professional photo guide & Tuition
• Accommodation - An entire beautiful house! (self-catering - restaurants, pubs, a 5-min walk away) Video of accommodation. (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mFOPMVFMRpU&feature=youtu.be)

𝐍𝐨𝐭 𝐢𝐧𝐜𝐥𝐮𝐝𝐞𝐝: Food & drink. Personal/travel insurance. Any items not stated as included.

𝐏𝐫𝐢𝐜𝐞: (Book through the UK Photo Tours website (https://www.uk-photo-tours.com))

• Includes **accommodation (7-nights)** and **return transport from London!**
• All payments are fully protected by our Tour Operator Insurance.
