6b2129bb-1046-4a21-a24f-3909f8b36a8d,,StitchUp Meetups,"Welcome to StitchUp – a welcoming social group that embraces individuals of all skill levels, providing a shared space for crafting in a social setting.","**Welcome to StitchUp** – a welcoming social group that embraces individuals of all skill levels, providing a shared space for crafting in a social setting.

**Bring your current project**, whether it's knitting, quilting, embroidery, or any other textile craft. Work on your project or piece while having a chat with us. Some people knit, some people mend or just join the conversations. If you are starting new, I’m sure we can give you tips, but generally this is not a class or workshop and you will have to bring your own materials.
Also keep in mind that we sometimes don't have a table, so something that requires table space might be difficult to do.

**Background** – StitchUp began among friends with a shared love for textile crafts, evolving into a thriving group with regular meetups. Unfortunately, the group faced a decline during the COVID-19 pandemic but we would now like to revive these regular meetings in a social, in-person setting.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792725625/orbit/event-covers/sources/ovrcjp7zuzeb9137wb1a.jpg,2026-11-19 18:30:00+00,2026-11-19 21:30:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Barbican Centre,Silk Street,London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,hobbies,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/stitchup/events/315515613/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,0.00,0.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-23 03:19:47.45036+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/stitchup/events/315515613/,event_315515613@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-23 03:19:47.45036+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,51.520206,-0.093786,meetup:stitchup:stitchup meetups,"Every 4th Thursday of the month until December 23, 2026",f,GB
9b09c3b4-31be-4c2c-b1e6-c4864a3355c3,,November Classic: Frankenstein - Mary Shelley,New members are always welcome. :),"New members are always welcome. :)

**Description:**

***Frankenstein; or, The Modern Prometheus*** is an 1818 Gothic novel (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gothic_fiction)[[a]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frankenstein#cite_note-2) written by English author Mary Shelley (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Shelley). It tells the story of Victor Frankenstein (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victor_Frankenstein), a young scientist who creates a sapient (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sapience) creature from different body parts in an unorthodox scientific experiment. Shelley started writing the story when she was 18 and staying in Bath (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bath,_Somerset),[[2]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frankenstein#cite_note-3) and the first edition was published anonymously in London on 1 January 1818, when she was 20. Her name first appeared in a French translation published in Paris in 1821.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792984808/orbit/event-covers/sources/ijtwirix5qxxoqr13vqy.jpg,2026-11-24 18:30:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,The Thirsty Bear,"62 Stamford Street, London, SE1 9LX",London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising,books}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/classics-book-club-london-ages-20-40/events/316844988/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,0.00,0.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-26 03:19:41.089186+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/classics-book-club-london-ages-20-40/events/316844988/,event_316844988@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-26 03:19:41.089186+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,51.50726,-0.107784,,,f,GB
