b2c43f70-b812-4d26-a8d9-36597634978f,,2 Hours to Research Intelligence: Build Your First AI Agent,There are many groups promoting this event.,"There are many groups promoting this event.

Our meetup group is participating by promoting this event.

This event is organized by Albert's List.

This is an online event.

Attendees can be located anywhere in the world!

There is a cost to attend this event.
In order to attend, please register here:
https://www.eventbrite.com/e/2003645521692?aff=oddtdtcreator
You're either looking at a company to join, or you're trying to understand what your competitors are doing. Either way, you're researching blind—reading scattered reviews, googling company news, checking LinkedIn. It takes forever and you miss things.
Stop doing this manually.
In this workshop, you'll customize and deploy a working AI research agent in 3 hours. Fork an existing competitive intelligence agent, wire in your own data sources (RSS feeds, APIs, whatever's available), and run it. Feed it a company or industry keyword. Get back structured intelligence: recent news, hiring patterns, market positioning, gaps, red flags.
**What you'll actually do:**

• Clone a working competitive intelligence agent from GitHub
• Add your own custom data sources (RSS feeds, open APIs, etc.)
• Test it live on a real company or competitor
• Walk away with a deployed agent you can run 100+ times

**Two use cases, one agent:**

1. **Job Seeker Mode** — Research a company before you apply, interview, or accept an offer. Understand growth, hiring, leadership, red flags.
2. **Competitive Mode** — Understand what competitors are doing, market gaps, hiring trends, strategic moves. For employees and side hustlers.

**What you need before the workshop:**

• 10 min of pre-work (optional, but recommended): Clone the GitHub repo, set up your API key, test it runs
• A laptop with a browser (Claude.ai)
• Basic comfort with Claude—you should already be asking it questions and iterating

**After the workshop:**

• Post-work recap doc: What you built, how to iterate, advanced techniques, troubleshooting
• Optional upsell: Advanced agent techniques course (separate paid offering)

**This is NOT:**

• A tutorial on ""how to use AI""
• A guide to corporate strategy
• A tool for stalking or privacy violations (we cover ethical guardrails)

**Price:** $17–27 (one-time, includes materials + post-work doc)
**Pre-work is optional.** If you complete it, you'll hit the ground running. If you skip it, no problem—we'll set up during the first 20 minutes.",,2026-11-12 23:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,growth,careers,technology,ai}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/uk-tech-entrepreneurs-ai-venture-capital/events/317120094/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-28 03:22:26.159151+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/uk-tech-entrepreneurs-ai-venture-capital/events/317120094/,event_317120094@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-28 03:22:26.159151+00,2026-10-28 03:22:28.722536+00,,,,,f,
b3c9f9c2-2fb3-4982-87b4-50577ae03a0e,,Play Badminton for fun... social badminton with a competitive edge!,"Welcome to Grove Park Badminton! Come and play at our bi-weekly sessions, please RSVP your attendance and bring along your racket.","Welcome to Grove Park Badminton! Come and play at our bi-weekly sessions, please RSVP your attendance and bring along your racket.
**MIDDLE INTERMEDIATE LEVEL AND ABOVE ONLY (INCLUDING VISITORS)** - Sorry, NO beginners, this club is not suitable for players who cannot serve, smash, hold a strategic rally and clear a shot from the back of the court. We play with quality, feather shuttlecocks only. Please do not attend Badminton if you are feeling unwell at all, or if you or anyone in your household currently has symptoms of any virus.

**INFORMATION:** Sessions cost: £13 for regulars and 'First Timers'* (cash or bank transfer, always pay before you play) for 2 hours. Please do not attend unless you have RSVP to reserve a space. If circumstances change, update your RSVP 24 hours before the session so others can fill the space. *If you do not attend or cancel after midday on the day of the session, then you will be expected to pay the full £13 cancellation fee on your next visit.*
*First Timers - you will receive a message with bank details to make your first payment of £13. Failure to send payment by midday of the day of your session will result in your name being moved to the 'Not Going' list, this in turn means if there is a 'WaitList', then another player will automatically fill your space.

**TRAVEL:** Free car park and main entrance accessed via Staveley Road. Walk through the side gate, towards sports hall and entrance is on your right hand side. Buses: E3 bus stop opposite the entrance. Chiswick Station: South West Trains - 7 minutes walk Please ring if you get lost - 07811 331030.

**ATTENDANCE, LATE DROP-OUTS AND NO-SHOWS:** Regular players: First no-show - You'll be expected to pay full price for the missed session. Second no-show - £15.00 penalty Third no-show - you will be removed from the group. This is to ensure basic courtesy to those playing and those waiting who can attend and want to play! First Timers: First no-show - you will be removed from the group.

**INSURANCE:** Any injury or loss incurred will be the individual’s responsibilities. The club will hold no responsibility or liability for any loss or injury. Because of this we encourage you to warm up appropriately, wear appropriate clothing including non-marking footwear and STRETCH off before and AFTER the games.
We hope you’ll have fun and an enjoyable time at this session! **PLAYING BADMINTON IS A GREAT WAY TO GET FIT AND HAVE FUN!!!**

**Note:** Please ensure you have all you belongings (and rubbish) before leaving at the end of the evening. There are bins situated just outside the hall for any rubbish. Thank you.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792812087/orbit/event-covers/sources/yzmvuwqk5buczdmcg3ww.jpg,2026-12-29 20:00:00+00,2026-12-29 22:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Grove Park Badminton Club,"Chiswick School Sports Hall, Free Car Park and entrance off Staveley Road",London,c06699ed-62e0-4957-bcb4-080c5271da9a,"{sport,fitness,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/grove-park-badminton-club/events/316408243/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:49:59.056229+00,source:cba1b9d2-d09d-4c19-a89e-50bdbe5525a0,https://www.meetup.com/grove-park-badminton-club/events/316408243/,event_316408243@meetup.com,,2026-10-26 03:20:40.119+00,,2026-10-22 19:49:59.056229+00,2026-10-26 03:21:16.926228+00,,,meetup:grove-park-badminton-club:play badminton for fun social badminton with a competitive edge,"Every week on Tuesday until August 31, 2030",f,GB
