6bcb5e9c-e8ae-4521-853c-ba1c2e8051f3,,November Book Club,Hi everyone!,"Hi everyone!

Welcome to the West London Niche Non Fiction Book Club, so excited you're here!

Join us at the The Drapers Arms in Ealing on Tuesday 24th November to grab a glass or cup of something and chat about the cultural and scientific history of extinction! (And don't worry if you run out of time to finish the book by then; there's lots to chat about even if you haven't quite finished. But please make sure you've read most of it so we can have a good discussion.)

If we reach 10 people attending which is the max Meetup allows and you've not yet signed up but are keen to come, please do still come to the meetup as we usually get some drop outs. Feel free to send me a quick note to let me know you're coming and I look forward to seeing you there!

**This event is also trialling a new online meetup on 26th November alongside the in-person meet up on 24th November for those who aren't able to attend IRL. Both the online and in-person sessions will discuss the same book, and you're welcome to attend both the in-person and online events if you wish to discuss the book with different groups. (The session will not be recorded.) To RSVP to attend the online meet up, please go to: https://calendar.app.google/KsjAYwMF7K2vqLT89**

Feel free to use free or paid-for digital copies of the book - no need to buy a paper copy if you prefer digital. If you do like paper copies and are in Ealing, Oxfam Books on The Green (W5 5DA) is wonderful and may have copies so do pop along there if you can :)",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792984821/orbit/event-covers/sources/iivkwh2511ggsjqq1zwq.jpg,2026-11-24 19:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,The Drapers Arms,"24-25 High St, London W5 5DB",London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,books,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/west-london-niche-non-fiction-book-club/events/316468632/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,0.00,0.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-26 03:19:41.089186+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/west-london-niche-non-fiction-book-club/events/316468632/,event_316468632@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-26 03:19:41.089186+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,51.51176,-0.305094,,,f,GB
1932a4f0-c5fc-4045-abe4-2fb25eb57086,,Film Jam Screening & In Conversation with Ajit Mann,"Film Jam short films, filmmaker conversations and creative connections — featuring an in-conversation Q&A with filmmaker Ajit Mann.","Film Jam short films, filmmaker conversations and creative connections — featuring an in-conversation Q&A with filmmaker Ajit Mann.

Come along for an afternoon of independent film, conversation and creative connections.

The London Film Jam Sunday Screening is a chance to see what our filmmaking community has been creating, meet fellow filmmakers and creatives, catch up with old friends and make some new connections.

**🎥 1 Month Film Jam Premieres**

We’ll be premiering the latest films from our **1 Month Film Jam**, created around this month’s theme, **Childhood Memory**.

Our teams had just one month to take an idea from concept to screen — bringing together writers, directors, actors, crew and other creatives to make their short films.

Come along, see what they created and support the filmmakers behind the work.

**In Conversation with Ajit Mann**

This month, we’ll also be joined by independent filmmaker **Ajit Mann** for a special In Conversation and audience Q&A.

We’ll be talking about the **realities and challenges of independent filmmaking** — the obstacles Ajit has faced along the way, how he has overcome them, creating your own opportunities and what he has learned through the process.

There’ll also be an opportunity to **ask Ajit your own questions** about filmmaking and his experiences in the industry.

**🎬 Meet. Watch. Connect.**

There’ll be plenty of time to mingle, talk films, meet other filmmakers and creatives and build new creative connections.

**Doors open at 12pm. The programme will begin promptly at 12:20pm, so please arrive in good time.**

Everybody is welcome — whether you’ve taken part in Film Jam before, are thinking about joining us, or simply want to come along, watch some films and meet other creatives.

**Venue:**
Whirled Cinema
259–260 Hardess Street
Loughborough Junction
London
SE24 0HN

Vegan food available.
