e513426b-da8b-4e7e-90af-e913d8a45450,,An Evening with Ben Meer - Trafalgar Sq,Join us for an evening of systems and secret habits as we welcome Ben Meer in celebration of his latest book How to be Good at Life.,"Join us for an evening of systems and secret habits as we welcome Ben Meer in celebration of his latest book* How to be Good at Life*. In* How to Be Good at Life*, the hugely popular founder of the Sunday Systems online community, Ben Meer draws from behavioural science and systems thinking to deliver a powerful toolkit for achieving your goals and making your dreams reality. Chaired by business creator Chris Donelly, this is evening is sure to be a success!

***How to Be Good at Life***

From the creator of the massively popular System Sunday community with over two million followers comes a proven method for building systems that make modern life easier.

You’re making thousands of decisions a day. You’re fighting algorithms designed to steal your attention. You’re managing passwords, subscriptions, and deadlines – complexity your brain was never built to handle. And somewhere in there, you’re supposed to exercise, eat well, and maintain friendships.

No wonder life feels harder than it should.

The happiest and most successful people don’t have more willpower than you. They’ve learned a skill most of us were never taught: building systems. This book is the missing manual.

**Ben Meer** is a systems expert, author and coach recognized by Forbes as ‘The Systems Guy’. He is the creator of the popular System Sunday newsletter that has 225k+ subscribers and a social media following of 2 million people. After earning his MBA from Cornell University, he became a management consultant, advising Fortune 500 companies on how to optimize their systems. Tired of ‘non-actionable life advice’, he launched System Sunday to teach others how to live by design, not by default. He lives in Woodstock, Vermont. How to Be Good at Life is his first book.**Chris Donnelly** bootstrapped Verb Brands, from £400 investment to the leading luxury digital marketing agency in the world before selling the business at 29 to private equity. Chris then went on to Co Found Lottie with his brother which is valued at 9 figures in 3 years and became one of Deloittes top 50 revenue growth companies. In 2026 Chris Founded Searchable, which helps businesses to understand how to get found in AI Search and provides a customised agent to help them grow their traffic and revenue. The business reached an $85m valuation in its $6m ARR in 9 months. Along the way, he’s been sharing his journey and became one of the fastest-growing business creators in the world. Growing 3 million followers across LinkedIn, Instagram and YouTube.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792660200/orbit/event-covers/sources/z8sq5l49bjkdgiyqcsqz.jpg,2026-11-05 19:00:00+00,2026-11-05 20:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Waterstones,Trafalgar Square,London,c17c4a77-8c19-42da-a932-7fd57ad27fc7,"{gaming,arts,hobbies,socialising,books}",,external,https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/an-evening-with-ben-meer-trafalgar-sq-tickets-2003141998641,Register on Eventbrite,f,,t,,6.00,20.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 09:09:07.092733+00,source:692118d3-2638-432e-9973-25e783168a55,https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/an-evening-with-ben-meer-trafalgar-sq-tickets-2003141998641,eventbrite-2003141998641,,2026-10-28 03:23:43.538+00,,2026-10-22 09:09:07.092733+00,2026-10-28 03:24:07.409619+00,51.507585,-0.126895,,,f,GB
b78c8d86-189d-456b-91d7-a408ba2f0e36,,How Did Your Model Actually Compute It? Validation from the Run,How Did Your Model Actually Compute It? Validation from the Run,"How Did Your Model Actually Compute It? Validation from the Run

Speaker: Dmitri Goloubentsev, CTO, MatLogica

Model validation needs to establish what pricing code actually computes, not just what the source code and documentation say it should. Yet validating complex models still relies heavily on manual code inspection. As AI accelerates code generation and modification, understanding what actually executes becomes even more important.

In this webinar, Dmitri Goloubentsev, CTO of MatLogica, introduces AADC Tracer, which records calculations as they execute in the production build and links each operation to the source code that performed it.

Using QuantLib as a worked example, including a barrier option whose price depends on more day-count conventions than the engine code suggests, Dmitri will demonstrate how to:

• See the formula actually computed, with each term linked to its source line.
• Trace the inputs, hard-coded constants and market-dependent branches behind a price.
• Replay calculations under different scenarios with exact Greeks, and see where a replay stops being valid.
• Compare what model documentation says with what the run computed.
• Preserve execution records as evidence for validation under PRA SS1/23, SR 26-2 and the ECB guide.
• Use AI to analyse execution evidence, with every claim linked to a source file and line for checking.

The session shows how validation can move beyond reading code to examining what the model actually did.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/5/d/e/e/highres_536724046.jpeg,2026-11-11 18:30:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,c06699ed-62e0-4957-bcb4-080c5271da9a,"{carrer,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/level39-onecanadasquare/events/317070750/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/level39-onecanadasquare/events/317070750/,event_317070750@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,2026-10-28 03:22:27.129706+00,,,,,f,
