89ca4da1-4e99-496d-8d0b-76392bca1407,,"Basketball in King's Cross/Angel every Thursday - full court, 2 hours, £13",Use our sign-up page to join the session:,"Use our sign-up page to join the session:

https://hoop-hub.lovable.app/

Got questions, join our Whatsapp group: [https://chat.whatsapp.com/L8ZtDebGWGfAg97fDihzcQ]
Signups via Google Form and WhatsApp get first priority. Once you signup we will send a confirmation email, letting you know you have reserved a spot.

Note: Majority of our signups are outside of meetup, but the run is active every week.

ABOUT THE SESSION
We run a friendly, competitive basketball session in London every Thursday night. We play near King's Cross St Pancras/Angel from 7pm to 9pm.
HOW THE SESSIONS WORK
We play five-on-five, full court, for two hours. We cap the number of players and rotate subs to ensure everyone gets plenty of court time.
We play a clean game and call our own fouls.
The cost is £13, paid by bank transfer.
WHO CAN PLAY
Our sessions are open to men and women aged 18 and over with at least a basic to intermediate level of basketball skill and understanding of the rules of the game.
VENUE
The court is 10 minutes walk from Angel and King's Cross St Pancras, and is a new indoor court with a wooden floor.
The address is Elizabeth Garrett Anderson School, Rodney Street, London, N1 9QG.

