9ad57f57-a921-4342-aa31-985ec4e8b00c,,October Classic: At the Mountains of Madness - H.P. Lovecraft,New members are always welcome. :),"New members are always welcome. :)

**Description:**

***At the Mountains of Madness*** is a science-fiction (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_fiction) and cosmic horror (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovecraftian_horror) novella (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novella) by the American author H. P. Lovecraft (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/H._P._Lovecraft), written in February–March 1931 and published in three installments in 1936. Rejected that year by *Weird Tales (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weird_Tales)* editor Farnsworth Wright (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farnsworth_Wright) on the grounds of its length,[[1]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/At_the_Mountains_of_Madness#cite_note-FOOTNOTEJoshi2001302-1) it was originally serialized in the February, March, and April 1936 issues of *Astounding Stories (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Analog_Science_Fiction_and_Fact)*. It has been reproduced in numerous collections.
The story details the events of a disastrous expedition to Antarctica (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antarctica) in September 1930, and what is found there by a group of explorers led by the narrator, Dr. William Dyer of Miskatonic University (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Miskatonic_University). Throughout the story, Dyer details a series of previously untold events in the hope of deterring another group of explorers who wish to return to the continent. These events include the discovery of an ancient civilization older than the human race, and realization of Earth's past told through various sculptures and murals.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/c/b/b/1/highres_536452145.jpeg,2026-10-27 18:30:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,The Thirsty Bear,"62 Stamford Street, London, SE1 9LX",London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/classics-book-club-london-ages-20-40/events/316844904/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/classics-book-club-london-ages-20-40/events/316844904/,event_316844904@meetup.com,,2026-10-27 03:19:10.711+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,2026-10-27 03:19:46.36512+00,,,,,f,GB
