995c1862-c401-47c9-bd52-448b9b703539,,British Polish Construction Forum 2026 | London Construction Networking,Kindly note that this is a paid event and the average number of attendees for our events is 60-70 people. You can register on…,"**Kindly note that this is a paid event and the average number of attendees for our events is 60-70 people. You can register on https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/british-polish-construction-forum-2026-london-construction-networking-tickets-1999016890331?aff=meetup**

Join 80+ construction, property, and business professionals for networking, insights, and new opportunities in London.
**London’s Construction, Property & Business Networking Forum Organised by PBLINK – Polish Business Link**

**About the British Polish Construction Forum**

The **British Polish Construction Forum 2026** brings together **80+ construction and property professionals** for a day focused on industry insights, business networking, knowledge exchange, and new commercial opportunities.
Taking place in London, the forum connects **construction companies, property developers, contractors, architects, engineers, investors, suppliers, consultants, and business leaders** from across the UK and the international business community.
Organized by **PBLINK – Polish Business Link**, the event provides an opportunity to build valuable professional relationships, explore current developments in the construction and property market, and discover potential opportunities for collaboration.
While the forum has strong links with the **Polish business community in the UK**, professionals and businesses of all nationalities are welcome to participate and connect with the wider British construction and property sector.

**Construction & Property Networking in London**

The forum is designed for professionals looking to expand their network, gain market knowledge, and connect with people actively involved in the **UK construction, real estate, and property industries**.
Attendees can expect a combination of expert insights, practical discussions, workshops, and dedicated networking opportunities throughout the day.

**Why Attend the British Polish Construction Forum?**

• **Expand your professional network** by meeting construction, property, and business professionals in London.
• **Connect with decision-makers,** including developers, contractors, investors, suppliers, and company directors.
• **Explore new business opportunities** and potential partnerships across construction and real estate.
• **Gain valuable industry insights** through keynote speakers, expert discussions, and practical workshops.
• **Understand market developments** affecting the UK construction and property sectors.
• **Build international connections** with professionals linked to the British and Polish business communities.
• **Create meaningful business relationships** in a professional environment designed for conversation and knowledge exchange.

**Who Should Attend?**

The forum is particularly relevant to:

• Construction companies and contractors
• Property developers and real estate investors
• Architects and architectural practices
• Civil and structural engineers
• Project and construction managers
• Property and real estate professionals
• Building material manufacturers and suppliers
• Construction product distributors
• Quantity surveyors and specialist consultants
• Professional service providers
• Entrepreneurs and business owners
• Investors and company directors
• Businesses seeking opportunities within the UK construction market

**Meet the UK Construction & Property Community**

The **British Polish Construction Forum** offers a valuable opportunity to meet professionals from different areas of the construction and property ecosystem in one setting.
Whether you represent an established construction company, are developing a property business, are looking for investment opportunities, provide professional services, or are seeking new commercial partnerships, the forum provides a platform to **exchange ideas, establish relationships, and explore future collaboration**.

**Connecting British & Polish Business**

With **PBLINK—Polish Business Link—at** the heart of the event, the forum supports stronger connections between businesses and professionals operating across the UK and Polish business communities.
It is an opportunity to meet like-minded professionals, exchange experiences, and discover potential connections that can contribute to long-term business development.

**Event Location**

**Institute of Directors**116 Pall MallLondon SW1Y 5ED, UK

**Forum Agenda**

• **09:30 —** Registration, Coffee & Networking
• **10:00 —** Welcome & Opening Remarks
• **10:10 —** Keynote Address
• **10:30 —** Expert Panel Discussion & Q&A
• **11:30 —** Refreshment Break & Networking
• **11:45 —** Workshop 1
• **12:15 —** Workshop 2
• **13:00 —** Lunch & Networking
• **15:00 —** Closing Remarks

**Organised by PBLINK – Polish Business Link**

**PBLINK – Polish Business Link** connects businesses, entrepreneurs, and professionals, helping create opportunities for networking, collaboration, and international business relationships.
