4f64b358-9cad-489c-8609-f717485b2602,,Building Real Confidence: A Different Approach with Aurore Prefumo,"If you struggle with confidence, overthink often, or find yourself holding back, this session is for you.","If you struggle with confidence, overthink often, or find yourself holding back, this session is for you.

Many of us learned early on that staying quiet or small felt safer. That pattern can serve us well at the time, but later in life, it often shows up as hesitation, self-doubt, or difficulty setting boundaries, even when we consciously want something different.

Journalling and affirmations can help, but they don't always reach the deeper, automatic patterns that drive our behaviour. This live session looks at why that is, and what a different approach can offer.

This is for anyone who's ready to move from thinking about change to actually experiencing it - without a lecture, and without the usual pep talk.

**Why this approach is different**

RTT® (Rapid Transformational Therapy) combines elements of hypnosis, psychology, and NLP, aiming to work at the root of long-standing patterns rather than just managing symptoms. It's been used by people working through:
• Confidence and self-worth
• Anxiety and overthinking
• Burnout and performance pressure
• Patterns around money and self-image

**Reserve your free spot. Limited availability**

Come along and learn more about this approach, and whether it might be useful for you.

**About the speaker**

Aurore Prefumo is a coach and hypnotherapist working with relationships, self-worth, and personal transformation. Her own path included years of emotional overwhelm she once saw as simply part of who she was — until deeper work showed her these were patterns, not identity.
Today, she supports clients in rebuilding self-trust and creating more authentic relationships — with others and with themselves. Drawing on Rapid Transformational Therapy (RTT), NLP, and other mindset-based approaches, she works with clients on confidence, anxiety, stress, and the ways these patterns can show up physically as well as emotionally.
*Disclaimer: This session is for general educational and informational purposes only and is not a substitute for medical or mental health treatment. This Meetup group does not provide financial or medical advice.*",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/8/e/f/b/highres_535656603.jpeg,2026-10-29 20:30:00+00,,Europe/Amsterdam,online,Online event,,,7aa69eeb-df8c-40ae-b929-a4324f936266,"{carrer,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/amsterdam-start-your-online-business-today/events/316994005/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:14:19.427857+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/amsterdam-start-your-online-business-today/events/316994005/,event_316994005@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-21 22:14:19.427857+00,2026-10-28 03:22:26.899552+00,,,,,f,
281fa4bb-dc43-49a1-a7e0-68bb8a536537,,Hyperpolitics: Anton Jäger in conversation with James Schneider - Gower St,"Anton Jäger traces how pub­lic life has become infused with protest, spectacle, and moral urgency.","What happens when politics is everywhere, yet nothing seems to change? From the abandoned dance floors of Thatcher's London to the mass mobilizations of Black Lives Matter, Anton Jäger traces how pub­lic life has become infused with protest, spectacle, and moral urgency - while the old infrastructure of parties, unions, and civic solidarity has been hollowed out.

***Hyperpolitics*** revisits the illusions of the ""end of history"" and dissects the strange energies that replaced them: viral outrage, endless culture wars, and the digital rush of causes that flare and vanish overnight. Jäger shows how the promises of post-Cold War liberalism gave way to a restless, unsteady public sphere where private pas­sions overflow into politics but rarely build enduring power.

**Anton Jäger** will be in conversation with **James Schneider**.

**ANTON JÄGER** is a Lecturer in Politics at Oxford and an opinion writer for the New York Times. He is the co-author (with Arthur Borriello) of The Populist Moment and (with Daniel Zamora) Welfare for Markets.

**JAMES SCHNEIDER** is a writer and political organiser. He serves as the Communications Director for the Progressive International and was Director of Strategic Communications for the Labour Party under the leadership of Jeremy Corbyn.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792660168/orbit/event-covers/sources/syw9iroeqsnsbvdtguqa.jpg,2026-11-08 16:00:00+00,2026-11-08 17:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Waterstones,82 Gower Street,London,7aa69eeb-df8c-40ae-b929-a4324f936266,"{gaming,arts,hobbies,socialising}",,external,https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/hyperpolitics-anton-jager-in-conversation-with-james-schneider-gower-st-tickets-2001528136536,Register on Eventbrite,f,,t,,10.00,15.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 09:09:07.401483+00,source:692118d3-2638-432e-9973-25e783168a55,https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/hyperpolitics-anton-jager-in-conversation-with-james-schneider-gower-st-tickets-2001528136536,eventbrite-2001528136536,,2026-10-28 03:23:43.538+00,,2026-10-22 09:09:07.401483+00,2026-10-28 03:24:07.409619+00,51.522448,-0.132181,,,f,GB
