58a04dfa-a091-40f1-92a0-43f58a483e14,,"Networking with NW London entrepreneurs, community leaders, professionals & busi",Grow Your Network in Colindale and North and North West London,"Grow Your Network in Colindale and North and North West London
Join us for our monthly networking evening, bringing together entrepreneurs, business owners, professionals and community leaders from across Colindale and North London.

Whether you are building a business, leading a local initiative, exploring a new idea or simply looking to meet ambitious and positive people, this event will help you make meaningful new connections in a relaxed and welcoming environment.

Come along if you would like to:
1. Meet local entrepreneurs, business owners and community leaders
2. Promote your business, service, project or community initiative
3. Find potential clients, customers, collaborators or referral partners
4. Exchange knowledge, ideas and opportunities
5. Build relationships with like-minded people in your local area
6. Become part of a growing Colindale business and community network

You do not need to arrive with a polished sales pitch—and you are welcome to attend whether this is your first networking event or you are an experienced networker. Just bring a friendly attitude, an interest in meeting people and enough business cards or contact details to share.

Please note that this is a relationship-building event rather than a high-pressure sales environment. We want attendees to have genuine conversations, support one another and create connections that continue beyond the evening.

When?
Every first Monday per month - Monday 2nd November @ 7:30pm–9:30pm

Where?
The Beaufort Pub, 2 Heritage Avenue, Grahame Park Way, Colindale, London, NW9 5AA
The Beaufort provides a relaxed and informal setting where you can purchase drinks throughout the evening.
The venue is dog-friendly, so well-behaved dogs are welcome to attend with their owners.
Limited parking is available close to the venue. If the nearby spaces are full, there is a larger car park approximately four minutes’ walk from The Beaufort: https://share.google/3GDl4Zp6nzoceZ1iG (https://l.facebook.com/l.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fshare.google%2F3GDl4Zp6nzoceZ1iG%3Ffbclid%3DIwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAcGRvZgFzcnRjBmFwcF9pZBAyMjIwMzkxNzg4MjAwODkyAAEek7p0J0LnnlPOYBVPiSfXZXysYl1L6vJInelURmumqr2Wb9dc3PxoAhzuAf8_aem_YItyBlQdtxhRbLGo4s_Dvg&h=AUDsCPaN0V0NO46oWvUsmabXhT5qxmIkQeHKcAZZQL72AXVc6494K7Eow0hcAf8sA-c7sKDi4hpUjfJHOW03444EX75Von29_5G4mL9Ci6RvCa0Nv2zJkmo5zI68-j82dkpz-OXtW2MUtJEOhsD4ZItuEqggGVbn&**tn**=q&c%5B0%5D=AUDN-tkM7MgdUkwr0ZVSUH9CcShKrEi4Rcsn62iSuzFzYWPhzLRqhsUp5TiCBgwvWPt6FDJph6SsqS6bg3xLjN_5ZYTm4gWjzqnqWiXhIM7B_qt9QtVgHPKZpu7omI5FVPOtbPFG8XFsSGMztFXb7bXO8NBNgs_JHtY)

The schedule for the evening?
7:30pm–8:00pm: Arrival, registration and speed networking

Meet several attendees through short, structured conversations designed to help you make new connections quickly—without the awkwardness of having to approach everyone yourself.
8:00pm–8:30pm: One-minute introductions

Each attendee will have an opportunity to briefly introduce themselves and tell the room about their business, profession, project, skills or the type of connections they would like to make.
8:30pm–9:30pm: Open networking

Continue conversations, exchange contact details and connect with the people most relevant to your interests, goals or business.
The schedule may vary slightly depending on the number of people attending.

Tickets

£5 when booked in advance through Eventbrite here: https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/.../network-with-nw-london... (https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/network-with-nw-london-entrepreneurs-business-owners-community-leaders-tickets-2000591906246?utm_id=97758_v0_s00_e0_tv4_a1den1nkx34sa2&fbclid=IwZXh0bgNhZW0CMTAAcGRvZgFzcnRjBmFwcF9pZBAyMjIwMzkxNzg4MjAwODkyAAEeCbhoJeAMW3ekCznt_pk4_VlizYErc5rVpEowsACdmFcbihwG8ycKjCcAzJ4_aem_3_VO65p-pXmBWBUUJJJ_xA)
£10 when paying at the door, subject to availability
Advance booking is strongly recommended. A maximum of 100 tickets will be available.

