5fe73ac6-0e48-4166-87e7-aa3f718991cd,,Film Discussion: The Life of Chuck,Join us for a friendly discussion of the film The Life of Chuck directed by Michael Flanagan based on Steven King's book with the same name.,"Join us for a friendly discussion of the film The Life of Chuck directed by Michael Flanagan based on Steven King's book with the same name.

• Free film (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nn6jXnUfC54)

We'll primarily discuss the film, just because it's freely available. You are welcome to come tell us your thoughts about the book if you read it.

**Proceedings:**
These will be roundtable discussions where everyone will have equal standing and equal opportunity to contribute to the discussion.

We like to keep the tone of our discussions warm and casual and to approach these conversations with playfulness, kindness, open-mindedness, and respectfulness. In that spirit, we appreciate reflective questioning, critical thinking, and debate too.

We'll vote on what to read for the next meeting at the start of this meeting.

Please feel free to bring suggestions for readings that we can add to the list of alternatives to vote on. Please note that we prefer readings which are in the public domain and freely accessible online.

Please do the agreed reading beforehand.

If for any reason you can't make the meeting, please update your RSVP in a timely manner.

If you will be joining us, please be punctual.

Thank you! Looking forward to the discussion!",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/d/7/e/highres_530591646.jpeg,2026-12-12 15:00:00+00,2026-12-12 17:00:00+00,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,creative,socialising,books}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/reasoned-reads-round-table/events/314349208/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:37.169472+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/reasoned-reads-round-table/events/314349208/,event_314349208@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:37.169472+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,meetup:reasoned-reads-round-table:film discussion the life of chuck,"Every 2 weeks on Saturday until March 1, 2027",f,
7954de83-2dc4-41ef-b77c-1e20d102eb2b,,The End of the World as We Know It: Various authors (Online Meetup),This will be a joint meeting with the Horror Book Club - if you want to attend in person then please join the Horror Book Club event on Wednesday 4th November.,"This will be a joint meeting with the Horror Book Club - if you want to attend in person then please join the Horror Book Club event on Wednesday 4th November.

We will be focusing on the below 10 stories

• In a Pig's Eye - Joe R Lansdale
• Wrong Fucking Place, Wrong Fucking Time - Robert C Cargill
• Grace - Tim Lebbon
• The African Painted Dog - Catriona Ward
• The Boat Man - Tananarive Due and Steven Barnes
• The Story I Tell is the Story of Some of Us - Paul Tremblay
• He's a Righteous Man - Ronald Malfi
• Came the Last Night of Sadness - Catheryn M Valente
• The Devil's Children - Sarah Langdon
• The Unfortunate Convalescence of the Super Lawyer - Nat Cassidy

Book blurb follows:
Since its initial publication in 1978, *The Stand* has been considered Stephen King's seminal masterpiece of apocalyptic fiction. It has sold millions of copies and has been adapted twice for television. Generations of writers have been impacted by its dark yet ultimately hopeful vision of the end and new beginning of civilisation, and its stunning array of characters.

Now for the first time, Stephen King has fully authorised a return to the harrowing world of *The Stand* through this original short story anthology, as presented by award-winning authors and editors Christopher Golden and Brian Keene. Bringing together some of today's greatest and most visionary writers, *The End of the World As We Know It* features unforgettable, all-new stories set during and after (and some perhaps long after) the events of *The Stand*—brilliant, terrifying, and painfully human tales that will resonate with readers everywhere as an essential companion to the classic, bestselling novel..

