69fd1bfe-509e-4ce5-9991-95a203d3dd8f,,LINO BLOCK PRINTING,Bookable via our website ➡️ https://www.thegoodlifecentre.co.uk/events/lino-block-printing-7/,"**Bookable via our website ➡️** https://www.thegoodlifecentre.co.uk/events/lino-block-printing-7/

**⋆⋆⋆**

**Suitable for:** Suitable for beginners. No prior experience is required.
**About:** Spend a day learning to cut a lino block, ink up and print onto fabric.

On this one day workshop you will gain an introduction to the lino printing technique onto fabric.

You will create your own one color lino print on fabric, an artwork ready to hang on your wall or perhaps as a gift for someone.

Taking inspiration from natural objects, plants and images provided and learn to free your hand and mind with the process of mark making itself. Katharine will guide you through the process of carving your own piece of natural linoleum which you will then ink up and print onto your prepared piece of fabric multiple times using a brayer roller.

You will make your own creative decisions as you go with as much or little guidance as you need, while always bearing in mind mistakes can lead to positive and new outcomes!",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792898408/orbit/event-covers/sources/hsqrvz1mgrzupt3vbpxr.jpg,2026-10-25 10:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,The Goodlife Centre,49/55 Great guildford Street,London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising,hobbies}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/thegoodlifecentre/events/316781030/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,150.00,150.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-25 03:19:47.028458+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/thegoodlifecentre/events/316781030/,event_316781030@meetup.com,,2026-10-25 03:19:10.667+00,,2026-10-25 03:19:47.028458+00,2026-10-25 03:20:08.704815+00,51.503124,-0.096614,,,f,GB
3f83c820-4345-4b49-8789-0d592cf79db6,,THREE LEGGED STOOL,Bookable via our website ➡️ https://www.thegoodlifecentre.co.uk/milking-stool/,"Bookable via our website ➡️ https://www.thegoodlifecentre.co.uk/milking-stool/
⋆⋆⋆

A wonderful 5-day project using basic carpentry woodwork skills and woodturning skills to make three-legged milking stool.

In this workshop you will learn the skills of how to measure accurately, cut precisely to join planks together using dowels. Use the ‘spindle method’ on a woodturning lathe to create the legs and use hand tools to finalise the shape of the seat. You will learn to use a drill guide to ensure the joinery is drilled at a consistent angle. The legs will be joined using the wedged tenon method.

During this 5 day workshop you will:

• Make a seat, glue 2 pieces of timber using the dowel method and roughly shape on using the band saw.
• Make a brace for the legs.
• Using the lathe you will turn 3 legs
• Create the finished shape of the seat using a spokeshave
• Use a reamer to make leg mortices conical for strength
• Use a tapered tenon cutter to make tapered tenon for strength

Stool dimensions approximately: 360mm high, diameter of the seat around 300mm.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1793157596/orbit/event-covers/sources/ohhd16nkui81h50a9eoz.jpg,2026-11-16 10:00:00+00,2026-11-16 17:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,The Goodlife Centre,"49-55 Great Guildford St, London SE1 0ES, UK",London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising,hobbies}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/thegoodlifecentre/events/317158220/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,595.00,595.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-28 03:19:46.398197+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/thegoodlifecentre/events/317158220/,event_317158220@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-28 03:19:46.398197+00,2026-10-28 03:20:15.72495+00,51.50314,-0.096736,meetup:thegoodlifecentre:three legged stool,"Every week on Monday until December 7, 2026",f,GB
85897d26-9234-4bbc-8816-aaa250d5b7f8,,The Monsters Among Us,"How a Hidden Minority Preys on Organisations, Societies, and Nations — and How We Stop Them","How a Hidden Minority Preys on Organisations, Societies, and Nations — and How We Stop Them

There are people in this world whose psychology is profoundly abnormal — organisational predators driven by extreme psychopathy and narcissism. They are few in number, perhaps less than one percent of the population, yet their impact is devastating. They infiltrate organisations, manipulate culture, erode trust, and quietly seize influence. When enabled, they become monsters — unseen, applauded, protected — leaving destruction in their wake.

For decades, Gearóid Carey has studied these individuals and the catastrophic effects they have on teams, communities, governments, and entire nations. In this groundbreaking book, he reveals their psychology, their methods, and the predictable pattern of infiltration, grooming, and colonisation that they use to gain power.

But The Monsters Among Us is not a book about despair — it is a book about the cure.
Carey introduces two revolutionary frameworks capable of stopping organisational predators: Organisational Hygiene and Anti-Tyrannical Measures. When these principles are applied, predators lose their power, organisations recover, and societies thrive. When they are absent, corruption spreads, misery rises, and tyrannous rule emerges.

Inside this book, you will learn:
• How organisational predators think, behave, and manipulate
• Why good people fail to recognise them until it’s too late
• The three stages of organisational capture: infiltration, grooming, colonisation
• How networks of predators coalesce into the powerful superclass
• Why tyranny has been the default condition of civilisation for 10,000 years
• Why liberal democracy is the first real antidote — and why it is under attack
• The essential anti-tyrannical safeguards every free society must defend
• How to apply organisational hygiene to protect teams, institutions, and nations

A warning. A diagnosis. A blueprint for victory.
This book exposes how the superclass manipulates economies, healthcare, food systems, education, and government to serve their own interests — regardless of human suffering. Yet it also offers a path to rebuild integrity and restore freedom.

A call to action
If we understand the monsters, we can defeat them. If we defend liberal democracy and organisational hygiene, their age ends — and the age of human flourishing begins.
This is the end of tyranny — if we are brave enough to defend the light.

For readers of:
Matt Goodwin, Ayaan Hirsi Ali, Jordan Peterson, Douglas Murray, and Robert F. Kennedy Jr.

About the Author
Gearóid Carey is a counsellor, researcher, and writer with over 20 years of experience helping people recover from trauma, addiction, and mental-health crises. He is the creator of the Recovery Tracker and an advocate for transforming society through measurable wellbeing, integrity, and freedom.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792698511/orbit/event-covers/sources/stcimytiovboslu05wwi.jpg,2026-11-22 19:00:00+00,2026-11-22 19:30:00+00,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/journey-to-democracy/events/fvrpbvyjcpbdc/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:37.169472+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/journey-to-democracy/events/fvrpbvyjcpbdc/,event_fvrpbvyjcpbdc@meetup.com,,2026-10-27 03:19:10.711+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:37.169472+00,2026-10-27 03:19:46.873136+00,,,meetup:journey-to-democracy:the monsters among us,"Every week on Sunday until October 8, 2028",f,
