a6bcedf0-ca03-4d1c-bda2-51b19bcca15a,,Journey to Democracy: The End of Tyranny,"How did humanity discover liberal democracy? Why do some nations become free, peaceful and prosperous while others remain trapped under tyranny? And could we one day live in a world without…","**How did humanity discover liberal democracy? Why do some nations become free, peaceful and prosperous while others remain trapped under tyranny? And could we one day live in a world without dictatorships?**
*Journey to Democracy: The End of Tyranny* is a weekly discussion group based on the book of the same name by Gearóid Carey.
Throughout history, most people lived under kings, emperors, dictators and other rulers they had little or no power to remove. Then something extraordinary happened. Humanity began developing a new way of organising society: liberal democracy.
Today, hundreds of millions of people enjoy freedoms, rights, opportunities and levels of prosperity that earlier generations could scarcely have imagined. Yet billions still live under authoritarian governments, and even established democracies face serious challenges.
**Can we build a future in which every person lives in a free and democratic society?**

What we'll explore

Each week, we'll explore ideas, historical events and contemporary issues, including:

• What liberal democracy is and why it matters.
• How different countries made the journey from tyranny to democracy.
• Why some democracies succeed while others fail.
• The institutions and principles that protect our freedom.
• The threats facing liberal democracies today.
• How we can support the spread of liberal democracy around the world.
• Whether a worldwide federation of liberal democracies could help bring about the end of tyranny.

What to expect

This is an informal, friendly and thought-provoking discussion group.
We'll introduce a topic, explore some of the ideas from the book and open the conversation to everyone.
You don't need to have read the book or have any previous knowledge of politics or history. All you need is curiosity and a willingness to think, listen and contribute.
Different perspectives are welcome. The aim is not to tell people what to think, but to explore ideas, question assumptions and learn from one another.

Who is this for?

Anyone interested in democracy, freedom, politics, history, human rights, international relations or the future of civilisation.
Whether you're passionate about democracy, sceptical about how it works or simply curious about how societies change, you're very welcome.

Our bigger question

**Could the 21st century be the century in which humanity finally brings tyranny to an end?**
Come along, join the conversation and help explore what a freer, safer and more prosperous world might look like.

Important note

This is an independent educational and discussion event, not affiliated with any political party or campaign. Participants are encouraged to express their views freely, listen respectfully and challenge ideas rather than attack individuals. Disagreement is welcome; personal abuse, intimidation and harassment are not.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/a/1/2/highres_536519922.jpeg,2026-11-01 20:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/journey-to-democracy/events/316951910/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:37.169472+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/journey-to-democracy/events/316951910/,event_316951910@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:37.169472+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.776315+00,,,meetup:journey-to-democracy:journey to democracy the end of tyranny,"Every week on Sunday until April 9, 2027",f,
bd7f5553-f88e-4ac0-b775-787764248553,,Nordic Walking Brockwell Park,Ready to get outside? Our Friday morning Nordic Walk in Brockwell Park is back!,"Ready to get outside? Our Friday morning Nordic Walk in Brockwell Park is back!

At this moment we can meet with up to 30 people (of more than two households) to do outdoor exercise and walks. However, i like to keep our exercise groups small, so I have set the maximum participants at 12.

For now this walk is for our experienced Nordic Walkers only, who already used to Nordic Walk with us regularly before Covid 19 kept us indoors, and who have their own Nordic Walking poles.

As this session is outdoors, we will not ask you to wear a face mask, but we do ask you to keep 2 meters apart. Some of our walkers might be immune compromised or more at risk, so please help us keep everyone safe!

Please do not come to the session and stay at home if:
• you know you have been in contact - in the last 2 weeks- with someone with symptoms of possible Covid, or if you have been in contact with someone who tested positive.
• you have any of the following symptoms: (new) Loss of smell/taste, Persistent cough, Fatigue, Loss of appetite, Skin rash, Hives, Fever, Severe muscle pain, Shortness of breath, Diarrhoea, Delirium, Abdominal pain, Chest pain, Hoarse voice, Eye soreness, Sore or painful throat, Nausea or vomiting, Headache, Dizziness or light headedness

We meet by the Blackbird bakery in Herne Hill, between the station and the park.

Session Price: £10 per session, £89 for a 10-session card or £70 unlimited sessions per month. Session cards and Pay Monthly can be used in any of our outdoor walks or indoor Zoom classes sessions (except for the Parkinson's sessions).

Pay What Works:
The price shown above is the “true” value of the session that best reflects the work I put into preparing and leading your session. However, I understand that not everyone can afford to pay full price, and I don’t want that to stop you from joining us.

In an effort to find a balance between more financial accessibility and sustainable pricing, I now offer a “Pay What Works” model. This allows for financial flexibility while still valuing and respecting the work and energy I provide in creating and delivering these classes.

Then send an email to ailien@fitandhappyoutdoors.com with the heading “INVOICE please”- followed by “FAHO 1” to pay full price as quoted below, “FAHO 2”, for 20% off, or “FAHO 3” for 50% off.

Please do tell me if you want to pay for 10 sessions, or if you’d like to pay monthly.
I prefer payment by bank transfer, but if that is not possible you could pay in cash. No cheques please, the queues by the banks are just too long.

We walk in all safe weather conditions – if a walk is cancelled, we will contact you to let you know. Please check for text messages or Meetup messages before leaving home!",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792698887/orbit/event-covers/sources/v0emjd6ekqqgxwve3ka1.jpg,2026-11-06 10:00:00+00,2026-11-06 11:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Blackbird Bakery,230 Railton Road,London,8827b689-2637-4245-8ba7-214b35948ea2,"{sport,travel,fitness}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/fit-and-happy-outdoors/events/317022662/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,10.00,10.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:54:30.136455+00,source:f26eb5d4-b239-4813-8e0c-3cf689eed4bd,https://www.meetup.com/fit-and-happy-outdoors/events/317022662/,event_317022662@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:22:30.379+00,,2026-10-22 19:54:30.136455+00,2026-10-28 03:22:55.486349+00,51.452682,-0.102277,meetup:fit-and-happy-outdoors:nordic walking brockwell park,Every week on Friday,f,GB
