43cad5b2-ef67-4474-962b-0361bebbbcb8,,When Everyone Knows by Steven Pinker,"In this event, we will discuss about a science or philosophy book chosen by London Science and Philosophy Book Club. The attendees will be divided into groups and each of them will focus on a…","In this event, we will discuss about a science or philosophy book chosen by London Science and Philosophy Book Club. The attendees will be divided into groups and each of them will focus on a chapter or one of the main ideas in the book. This month we will discuss about a fascinating book called When Everyone Knows That Everyone Knows by Steven Pinker. If you haven't read the book, it's no problem. I will bring you up to speed with the discussion materials.

We will meet in a nice lounge area at 6 p.m for introductions. Please come on time so you will not miss out on valuable discussion midway. If you end up in the waitlist, feel free to show up.

Book Description:
As a cognitive scientist, the ultimate subject of Steven Pinker’s fascination is how we think about each other’s thoughts, ad infinitum. It sounds impossible, but Steven Pinker shows that we do it all the time. This awareness, which we experience as something that is public or “out there,” is called common knowledge, and it has a momentous impact on our social, political, and economic lives.

Common knowledge, Pinker shows, can make sense of many of life’s enigmas: financial bubbles and crashes, revolutions that come out of nowhere, the posturing and pretence of diplomacy, the eruption of social media shaming mobs and academic cancel culture, the awkwardness of a first date. But people also go to great lengths to avoid common knowledge―to ensure that even if everyone knows something, they can’t know that everyone else knows they know it. And so we get rituals like benign hypocrisy, veiled bribes and threats, sexual innuendo, and pretending not to see the elephant in the room.

In exploring the paradoxes of human behaviour, When Everyone Knows that Everyone Knows… invites us to understand the ways we try to get into each other’s heads, and the harmonies, hypocrisies, and outrages that result.

Agenda
6 p.m to 7 p.m: Introduction and Socializing
7 p.m to 9:30 p.m: Book Discussion
9:30 p.m to late night: Drinks, Dinner or Feel free to go hom",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/9/4/1/highres_536459713.jpeg,2026-11-07 18:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Middle Eight,66 Great Queen Street,London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising,books}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/science-and-philosophy-book-club/events/316849549/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/science-and-philosophy-book-club/events/316849549/,event_316849549@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,,,f,GB
247f3994-2c9d-430d-83f6-7296f8ea9ac3,,🤝 Founders Meetup by F4F,Founders for Founders brings you Real conversations for Entrepreneurs building Startups around the world. Every Week.,"***Founders for Founders* brings you Real conversations for Entrepreneurs building Startups around the world. Every Week.**
*Talk it out, build it better.*

• This is a special FREE weekly event for founders around the world: you can check out The Founders for Founders Website (https://f4f.vc/) for more info.

Building something is a rollercoaster, and it's a whole lot better with people who *get it*. Founders for Founders is our weekly get-together where you meet other entrepreneurs, talk through what you're working on, and leave with fresh ideas and new connections.
Here's how it works:

• **⏱️ One hour, once a week:** an easy, energising break in your week
• **🤝 Meet 4 different founders:** we personally put you in touch with four others, so every conversation counts
• **💬 Real talk (English):** share your ideas, talk through your blockers, and get honest opinions from people who've been there
• **🌱 Connections that last:** many of the founders you meet become sounding boards, collaborators, and friends long after the hour is up

**Talk it out, build it better.**

This is a FREE event. No one to impress, just peers who *get it*.
Whether you're deep in the build, just starting out, or somewhere in between, for-profit, nonprofit, or a project you believe in, you're welcome here.

**Where:** We meet on SpeakDuo (https://speakduo.onelink.me/DlwG/meetup), built for live online group events with advanced matching, so you're paired with the right founders for focused, meaningful conversations instead of getting lost in a crowded call.

**RSVP to save your spot:** bring what you're working on, and let's
unite. You can also check upcoming events at f4f.vc/events (http://f4f.vc/events). 🚀",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/9/3/0/f/highres_535297647.jpeg,2026-11-24 18:00:00+00,2026-11-24 19:00:00+00,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,entrepreneurship,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/founders-london/events/316957925/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:14:19.427857+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/founders-london/events/316957925/,event_316957925@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-21 22:14:19.427857+00,2026-10-28 03:22:26.899552+00,,,meetup:founders-london:founders meetup by f4f,"Every week on Tuesday until July 11, 2031",f,
