87e2e028-8098-4152-8aba-b19ce749430e,,City Photowalk,"We had a great turnout last time and would love to keep the momentum. Given that the weather is getting a bit iffy, I’m going to come up with a Plan A for the actual walk and Plan B if it literally…","We had a great turnout last time and would love to keep the momentum. Given that the weather is getting a bit iffy, I’m going to come up with a Plan A for the actual walk and Plan B if it literally rains on our photography parade.
See you guys soon!

**Photowalk Code of Conduct**

Our club is a welcoming, inclusive and judgment-free space for photographers of every background and experience level.

1. Everyone is equal. Treat every member with the same respect, regardless of age, race, ethnicity, nationality, religion, gender, sexuality, disability, appearance, experience or equipment.
2. Be kind. Bullying, harassment, discrimination, intimidation, exclusion or deliberately making someone uncomfortable will not be tolerated.
3. No shaming. Never shame anyone for their photographs, ability, camera, phone, editing style, knowledge or level of experience.
4. Do not make negative comments about ability. Everyone is here to enjoy photography and develop at their own pace. Constructive feedback should only be given when someone asks for it, and it must be respectful and helpful.
5. Respect different styles. Photography is subjective. You do not have to like someone’s work, but you must respect their creative choices.
6. Help, don’t compete. Celebrate other people’s progress, share knowledge generously and make newer members feel welcome. This club is a community, not a competition.
7. Respect personal boundaries. Ask before photographing another member or sharing an identifiable photograph of them. If someone asks not to be photographed, respect that immediately.
8. Include everyone. Do not form cliques, deliberately leave people behind during walks or make anyone feel that they do not belong.
9. Take responsibility for your impact. Jokes and comments should not come at somebody else’s expense. If someone tells you that your behaviour made them uncomfortable, listen and respond respectfully.
10. Speak to an organiser if something happens. Concerns will be taken seriously and handled as fairly and discreetly as possible. Serious or repeated breaches may result in removal from the club.

The basic rule: be kind, be inclusive and never make another person feel small.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/5/c/highres_535502652.jpeg,2027-04-03 13:00:00+00,2027-04-03 15:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Liverpool Street,Liverpool Street,London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,creative,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/photowalk-club/events/wmhcbvykcgbfb/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/photowalk-club/events/wmhcbvykcgbfb/,event_wmhcbvykcgbfb@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,meetup:photowalk-club:city photowalk,Every 1st Saturday of the month,f,GB
49df92e0-1bae-4c67-b13d-2da811a1ee9f,,Free Public Speaking: Beginners to Advanced – Central London Toastmasters,🎤 Join Our Free Public Speaking Class in Central London,"🎤 **Join Our Free Public Speaking Class in Central London**

• 🌟 Are you struggling with public speaking or experiencing anxiety about it?
• 👉 Attend our in-person public speaking class, suitable for beginners to advanced speakers, absolutely FREE as a guest!

*You don't need to speak - just observe and learn, or participate if you feel ready.*

**Why Attend Our Public Speaking Class?**

• 💪 **Overcome Public Speaking Fear**
Central London Toastmasters is the premier weekly public speaking club, offering a relaxed and supportive environment. Practice in a safe space where no one judges you, and start your journey to becoming a confident speaker.
• ✨ **Become a Charismatic Speaker**
Enhance your public speaking skills and develop the charisma you've always wanted. Impress your colleagues with smooth, polished presentations and wow your friends with newfound confidence and storytelling abilities.
• 💼 **Improve Business Speaking Skills**
Our meetings are friendly and informal, making them the perfect starting point for building confidence in public speaking. Many of our members began with anxiety, but now speak with total confidence. As a guest, you’ll see firsthand how warm and welcoming our club is, and you can chat with members about their experiences.
• 🏆 **Develop Leadership Skills**
Public speaking is not just about presenting; it's also about leading. Our club provides opportunities to take on leadership roles, helping you to develop crucial skills like team management, decision-making, and strategic thinking that can benefit your personal and professional life.

📅 **Location and Time**

• 📍 Location: Cittie of Yorke pub, Holborn
• ⏰ Time: 6:30 PM – 8:30 PM (Feel free to arrive late and quietly take a seat)

🔄 **What to Expect at Our Meetings**

• The meeting is divided into two halves, each lasting approximately 50 minutes, with a 10-minute break.
• 🎯 First Half: Members participate in impromptu speeches, and guests are invited to introduce themselves by name.
• 📈 Second Half: Members deliver prepared speeches followed by evaluations.
• After the meeting, we enjoy drinks and informal chats, providing a great opportunity to network and learn more about the club.

🎟️ **Interested in Becoming a Member?**
Membership includes access to our online course, Pathways, guiding you step-by-step through your public speaking journey. A full year’s membership, covering 50 weekly meetings, is just £168, plus a one-time £30 registration fee.

**💬 Testimonials from Our Members**

• **“Toastmasters transformed my life!”**
""I went from fearing public speaking to leading meetings at work. This newfound confidence even earned me a promotion!"" – **Alexander**
• **""A warm and supportive club!""**
""From the first meeting, I felt welcomed. The constructive feedback boosted my confidence both in public speaking and daily life."" – **Sarah**
• **""Overcoming my fear was easier than I thought.""**
""The support here made my sales presentations more impactful and less stressful. It's been a game-changer for me professionally."" – **David**
• **""A fun and rewarding experience.""**
""I look forward to every meeting. The sessions are engaging, and I love the socializing afterward."" – **Lucy**
• **""I've grown as a speaker and leader.""**
""Taking on roles in the club has sharpened my leadership skills, making me more effective at work."" – **James**",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/e/1/6/highres_523151798.jpeg,2026-11-17 18:30:00+00,2026-11-17 20:30:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Cittie of Yorke,22 High Holborn,London,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,growth,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-xkeapfpj/events/312459743/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-xkeapfpj/events/312459743/,event_312459743@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-22 19:53:33.497215+00,2026-10-28 03:22:26.899552+00,,,meetup:meetup-group-xkeapfpj:free public speaking beginners to advanced central london toastmasters,"Every week on Tuesday until December 15, 2026",f,GB
b2f0b7db-4756-451e-ad24-f2cddd81a8fd,,"Health, Fitness, Beauty & Wellness - Business and Startups Networking Event",PLEASE MAKE SURE TO BOOK YOUR TICKET IN ADVANCE TO ATTEND THE EVENT. YOU CAN RESERVE YOUR SPOT HERE.…,"**PLEASE MAKE SURE TO BOOK YOUR TICKET IN ADVANCE TO ATTEND THE EVENT. YOU CAN RESERVE YOUR SPOT HERE. https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/health-fitness-beauty-wellness-business-and-startups-networking-event-tickets-2002210787363**

Step into a room full of innovators, founders, and professionals from across the **health, fitness, beauty, and wellness industries**. This networking event is designed to bring together individuals building brands, launching startups, investing in the sector, or offering services that support business growth and transformation in the wellness space.
Whether you're launching a skincare line, developing a fitness app, running a wellness clinic, or building a health-tech startup, this event is your opportunity to **connect with like-minded professionals**, explore partnerships, and share ideas with others who are passionate about helping people feel and live better.
The evening will feature **casual yet focused networking**, **1-minute elevator pitches**, and plenty of opportunities to meet future collaborators, co-founders, clients, or supporters.

**What to expect?**
**1-Minute Elevator Pitches** – Founders, startups, and professionals can briefly introduce themselves and what they’re looking for (e.g. clients, partners, investment, services).
**High-Quality Networking** – Meet people from across the health, wellness, beauty, and fitness space in a relaxed, friendly setting.
**Business Development Opportunities** – Discover potential partnerships, clients, or new ventures.
**Industry Diversity** – From wellness coaches and skincare founders to fitness tech developers and product designers—everyone’s welcome.

**Who should attend?**
This event is ideal for anyone working in or building a business within the health, fitness, beauty, or wellness industries, whether you're launching something new or already established and looking to grow. It's a curated space for collaboration, business development, and meaningful networking.

• **Startup Founders & Entrepreneurs** – From early-stage concepts to scaling brands in fitness, beauty, wellness, or health-tech.
• **Wellness Coaches & Practitioners** – Including life coaches, yoga teachers, breathwork facilitators, holistic therapists, and alternative health professionals.
• **Beauty Brand Founders & Product Developers** – Skincare, haircare, clean beauty, cosmetic products, and beauty tech innovations.
• **HealthTech & FitTech Innovators** – Founders and developers building apps, wearables, platforms, or software focused on physical or mental wellbeing.
• **Nutritionists, Dietitians & Wellness Experts** – Offering services, products, or platforms related to food, supplements, and health optimisation.
• **Personal Trainers & Fitness Professionals** – Gym owners, performance coaches, online fitness entrepreneurs, or boutique studio founders.
• **Investors & VCs** – Actively looking for promising startups in wellness, health, fitness, or beauty.
• **Product Designers & Formulators** – Working on physical wellness products, supplements, or cosmetics.
• **Consultants & Agencies** – Legal, branding, PR, marketing, e-commerce, or operations specialists working with wellness businesses.
• **Retailers & Distributors** – Boutique shop owners, wellness marketplaces, or professionals exploring new product partnerships.
• **Influencers, Creators & Content Strategists** – Focused on health, beauty, fitness, and lifestyle, looking to connect with brands and startups.
• **Medical & Clinical Wellness Practitioners** – Functional medicine doctors, physiotherapists, and others bridging the gap between traditional and modern wellness.
• **Students & Career Changers** – Looking to explore opportunities in the wellness space or build connections to launch their own brand.

**Why attend?**
This event is your opportunity to connect with others who are shaping the future of health, fitness, beauty, and wellness. Whether you're just starting out or already running a successful venture, surrounding yourself with the right people can make all the difference.
Attending means:

• **Expanding your network** with people who work in your industry and speak your language
• **Meeting potential collaborators, clients, or partners** you wouldn’t come across in your daily routine
• **Sharing your story** in a relaxed and welcoming environment where everyone’s here to connect
• **Learning what others are building** and gaining insight into emerging trends across wellness, beauty, fitness, and health
• **Building visibility and credibility** by being part of an active, forward-thinking business community

If you’re serious about growing your brand, exploring new ideas, or simply meeting others in the space, this event gives you a place to be seen, heard, and supported. You never know who you’ll meet—or where one good conversation might lead.
**Spaces are limited—register now to join a community passionate about shaping the future of wellness and personal wellbeing.**
