bcf8ff58-a5be-4db2-9c2c-5ae034031a39,,"Deeper Discussion: Men vs Women, how different are they?","Men vs Women, how different are they?","Men vs Women, how different are they?

Are the differences between men and women mostly cultural stories we tell ourselves—or are they rooted in biology, brains, hormones, and evolutionary history?

We’ll examine the evidence on physical and cognitive differences, personality traits, interests, emotional processing, risk-taking, and social behavior. We’ll also dig into how much of the gap is shaped by culture, upbringing, and modern environments—and where the data still leaves room for debate.

This Deeper Discussion gathering invites a serious, open, and unhurried examination of the topic. We will move past slogans and surface talking points to explore the harder terrain. The atmosphere we will encourage is one of curiosity, logic, critical thinking and less ideological emotional outburst.

This is not a debate with predetermined sides or a lecture. It is a facilitated conversation designed for people willing to sit with complexity, hear opposing perspectives, and think carefully about what kind of future is possible—and desirable—for our societie

Expect thoughtful exchange, rigorous questioning, and space for disagreement without virtuous performance.

Agenda:
6 p.m to 7 p.m: Introduction and Socializing
7 p.m to 9:30 p.m: Topic Discussion
9:30 p.m to late night: Drinks, Dinner or Feel free to go home.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/b/7/d/8/highres_535607064.jpeg,2026-11-14 18:00:00+00,,Europe/London,in_person,Hilton Doubletree Holborn,92 Southampton Row Tube: Holborn,WC1B 4BH London,7aa69eeb-df8c-40ae-b929-a4324f936266,"{social,socialising,arts}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/science-and-philosophy-book-club/events/317042936/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/science-and-philosophy-book-club/events/317042936/,event_317042936@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,,,f,GB
15d79f4e-ab35-4393-a0aa-b91630713973,,The Artist’s Way – Free Weekly Online Support Group & Book Club for Creatives,"Hi everyone,","Hi everyone,

Thank you for being part of the Playmakers journey — whether you’re brand new or you’ve been with us already, we appreciate you.

Playmakers is a creative community built around one simple idea: play isn’t just for children — it’s a powerful way for adults to connect, recharge, and grow. Over time, we’ll be hosting in-person workshops and events that blend theatre, movement, games, music, writing, and other creative activities to help people develop skills and build community.
For now, we’re keeping things simple.

As a low-barrier entry point into the Playmakers space, we’re running a free weekly online workshop. (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf9mHEnC3L9PpeMpaRVcsNqQ6EpVR7Bb7HJb8OV1UlGrFIhSg/viewform?usp=dialog) It’s a creative book-club-style group centred around *The Artist’s Way*, where we explore ideas together, share reflections, and gently challenge ourselves in a supportive environment.
Each session stands on its own, so you can join at any point in the year. It doesn’t matter how far we are in the book — there’s no catching up required. Just come as you are and start where we are.
It’s relaxed, welcoming, and you can engage at your own pace. No pressure — just curiosity, creativity, and connection.

**New here?** You can find all the details and sign up via This link - Book Club Sign up Form (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf9mHEnC3L9PpeMpaRVcsNqQ6EpVR7Bb7HJb8OV1UlGrFIhSg/viewform?usp=dialog) (you’ll receive the Google Meet link after submitting)

**Returning?** You don’t need to fill the form again — just join using the usual link you’ve already received or keep an eye out for our weekly emails.

**Quick favour:** even if you’re a regular, please hit **Attend / RSVP**. It helps the Meetup algorithm push the event to more people and grow the community

**Event details**
**Sundays | 10:30–11:30am**
**Platform:** Google Meet
**What to bring:** something to write with (notebook + pen or Notes app)

For any questions or further info, hit me up at **Taurean@theplaymakersproject.com**.
Looking forward to building this with you.

— Taurean

The Playmakers Project",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792984815/orbit/event-covers/sources/oabswdi65dy9p5ql41d3.jpg,2027-01-17 10:30:00+00,2027-01-17 12:00:00+00,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,books,creative,socialising,music}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/playmakers-play-creativity-community/events/bsqfwtykccbwb/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,0.00,0.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-26 03:19:41.089186+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/playmakers-play-creativity-community/events/bsqfwtykccbwb/,event_bsqfwtykccbwb@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-26 03:19:41.089186+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,meetup:playmakers-play-creativity-community:the artist s way free weekly online support group book club for creatives,"Every week on Sunday until February 14, 2027",f,
