62d7d3d3-9734-48f4-b15c-b425e1ca89df,,INTRO TO TRADITIONAL UPHOLSTERY – EVENING,Bookable via our website ➡️ https://www.thegoodlifecentre.co.uk/events/intro-to-traditional-upholstery-evening-40/,"**Bookable via our website ➡️** https://www.thegoodlifecentre.co.uk/events/intro-to-traditional-upholstery-evening-40/
⋆⋆⋆

**KEY PROJECT: TRADITIONALLY STITCHED AND SEWN EDGED FOOTSTOOL**
*All of our upholstery classes are for absolute beginners. It doesn’t matter which one you choose to take first. Each technique that is offered is part of all the processes that every upholsterer has to learn.*

6-week workshop. 6:30pm – 9pm.

A perfect course for a beginner. Jumpstart your knowledge of traditional upholstery skills and methods.

Over six Thursday evenings, experienced upholsterers will guide you through the wonderful world of upholstery and help you build a fabulous footstool using traditional methods. You can leave your project at the centre in between classes.

Before the advent of foam in the middle of the twentieth century, the only way to make wooden seats more comfortable was to build up layers using available materials. Our small fabric footstool (above) is built from layers of woven webbing, hessian, vegetable fibre, animal hair and calico and is sewn with specialist needles and stitches. Although this method is more labour-intensive than the modern method of using foam, it is much longer lasting and preferred in more expensive pieces of furniture. This is the method used in many traditional chair seats, so once learned, you can apply this method to your own projects.

We provide everything for the workshop, from the wood frame to the set of natural beech wood legs that are included for you to paint or stain as you wish. Choose from our selection of top fabrics, or bring your own. You will need about a metre of fabric and you will not need it until the final class. The use of all tools and materials is included. We also have a selection of specialist upholstery tools and all the materials that we use in our workshops for sale at the Goodlife Centre for you to continue your new hobby at home.

Beginners welcome.

**Need a different date or time?** You can check our full schedule on the website here: ➡️ https://www.thegoodlifecentre.co.uk/upholstery-traditional-footstool/",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1793071205/orbit/event-covers/sources/pbd3wzsrnykdwhqbvmhj.jpg,2026-11-24 18:30:00+00,2026-11-24 21:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,The Goodlife Centre,"49-55 Great Guildford St, London SE1 0ES, UK",London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising,hobbies}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/thegoodlifecentre/events/vvctbvyjcpbgc/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,380.00,380.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-27 03:19:45.380416+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/thegoodlifecentre/events/vvctbvyjcpbgc/,event_vvctbvyjcpbgc@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-27 03:19:45.380416+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,51.503138,-0.096736,meetup:thegoodlifecentre:intro to traditional upholstery evening,"Every week on Tuesday until December 8, 2026",f,GB
7d1106ef-c25c-456e-810f-dd19aa933ebc,,✨ Sci-Fi STANDALONE: Shroud by Adrian Tchaikovsky 🌑👽🚀,Shroud by Adrian Tchaikovsky (480 pages),"**Shroud by Adrian Tchaikovsky (480 pages)**
**Genre:** Science Fiction • First Contact • Survival Horror

**Summary:**
A commercial expedition travelling through a distant star system discovers Shroud: a pitch-black moon alive with radio activity. Its crushing gravity, immense atmospheric pressure and complete lack of oxygen make it deadly to humans—but potentially incredibly valuable to the corporation hoping to exploit it.
When a catastrophic accident forces scientists Juna Ceelander and Mai Ste Etienne to crash-land on Shroud in a barely adequate escape vehicle, they must cross its hostile surface while their supplies and time rapidly run out. But they soon realise they aren’t alone. Something extraordinary lives in the darkness—and as the two women struggle to understand it, it begins trying to understand them in return.

Tense, atmospheric and deeply unsettling, *Shroud* is a gripping story of survival and first contact that explores communication, intelligence, corporate greed and the terrifying possibility of encountering a form of life completely unlike our own.

Join the Sci-Fi/Fantasy Series Squad! 🚀📚

If you’ve ever gotten halfway through a fantasy or sci-fi series and needed a little group support to finish, this is your crew. We’re reading one book a month together—so you can keep pace, stay motivated and enjoy deep-dive discussions without feeling overwhelmed.

How It Works:

🪐 **Monthly Focus:** We’re tackling one sci-fi or fantasy book per month. This November, we’re venturing into the darkness with *Shroud* by Adrian Tchaikovsky—a tense and terrifying first-contact story set on one of the most hostile worlds imaginable.
🙌 **No Pressure Zone:** Didn’t finish the book? No stress. Come anyway—we’ll chat about Shroud’s alien ecosystem, the characters, the science, our favourite moments and the questions the story raises about intelligence and communication.

📍 **Join us at the Dog & Bull (Surrey Street) in Croydon on Wednesday 25th November at 7:00 PM**
