d611a974-ea1d-42e7-8d67-3af024013435,,"Putting ""Think and Grow Rich"" Into Action","Chapter 5 - Specialized Knowledge, Personal Experiences or Observations","**Chapter 5 - Specialized Knowledge, Personal Experiences or Observations**

Did you know that knowledge alone isn’t power, it’s organized and applied knowledge that creates real success? We are going to dive into Chapter 5 of Think and Grow Rich and explore how specialized knowledge can be the game-changer in achieving your goals. Whether you’re looking to advance your career, build a business, or master a skill, this chapter reveals why knowing how to use what you know is the ultimate key to wealth and success. Don’t miss it. Bring your insights and questions as we uncover the secrets to turning knowledge into action!

Every week, we delve into one of the **13 principles of success**, exploring how to incorporate it into our daily actions to meet our objectives. Our sessions include a live online study group where participants can engage and learn together to gain valuable insights on how to utilize this knowledge for your own success.
Think and Grow Rich was the first book to boldly ask, ""What makes a winner?"" The man who asked and listened for the answer, Napoleon Hill, is now counted in the top ranks of the world's winners himself.

**Group Guidelines:**
This group is meant to be interactive. Having your video on is encouraged but not required. Come with questions and an open mind. My goal is to provide a safe and engaging environment for us to learn from each other and walk away feeling empowered to take action. Please practice kindness and respect. We'll summarize key takeaways from previous weeks, so don't worry if you missed the last one; drop in at any point in the book!

“There’s something really powerful about groups and shared experiences. People might be skeptical about their ability to change if they’re by themselves, but a group will convince them to suspend disbelief. A community creates belief.” — Charles Duhigg
Let's think and grow rich together!

Looking forward to meeting with you,
Dave and Doug",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/0/1/2/highres_536277362.jpeg,2026-10-27 19:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,careers,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/london-e-business-owners-meetup-group/events/316810722/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:14:19.427857+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/london-e-business-owners-meetup-group/events/316810722/,event_316810722@meetup.com,,2026-10-27 03:21:52.243+00,,2026-10-21 22:14:19.427857+00,2026-10-27 03:22:31.70089+00,,,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02:putting think and grow rich into action:online,,f,
e6f4621d-d515-415b-8ee0-15898bcc008d,,"Startups, Entrepreneurs, AI & Investors - Business Networking | Saturday Social","Looking for a startup and business networking event in London for founders, entrepreneurs, investors and B2B professionals?","**Looking for a startup and business networking event in London for founders, entrepreneurs, investors and B2B professionals?**
Join us for a relaxed **Saturday Social Networking Event in Covent Garden** hosted by digital business card app GMax Card (no paper cards needed any more).

**What to Expect**
**Quality conversations, relaxed networking and a live DJ** throughout the evening – a **startup and business crowd in a social setting**.
Meet founders and professionals, exchange ideas, build partnerships, discover new opportunities and grow your network in a welcoming yet professional atmosphere.

Our hosts will **help introduce guests** early in the evening, before the event naturally flows into open networking, drinks and a **live DJ set** (not too loud for conversations).

**Who You'll Meet**

• Startup founders & entrepreneurs
• B2B & SaaS founders and professionals
• Tech founders & startup teams
• Business owners & company directors
• Investors & professionals from the investment ecosystem
• Agencies, consultants & B2B service providers
• Sales, growth & business development professionals
• International founders & business professionals visiting London

**How the Evening Flows**
18:30 - Arrival & welcome
19:00 - Short guest introductions
19:30 - Open socialising/networking with live DJ
21:30 - Close

**Venue - Sycamore Bar, Middle Eight Hotel**
A refined cocktail bar in copper and gold tones. Located inside the 5-star Middle Eight Hotel in Covent Garden, just a short walk from Covent Garden, Holborn and Tottenham Court Road stations.

**Dress Code**
Business or smart attire recommended. Think polished Saturday evening out with a professional touch.

**Tickets & GMax Cards**

• Free RSVP tickets include only the access to the event.
• Selected paid tickets include a premium contactless digital business card by GMax Card. Ask host, not distributed automatically.

**Hosted by:**
• [GMax Card – digital & contactless business cards](www.gmaxcard,com) (no paper cards needed anymore; update details any time)
• [3Edit (beta) - AI vibe coding platform for web design agencies](www.3edit.com); design faster, better and more affordably than Lovalble/Replit.
• [Getshop Today – web design/ecommerce agency](www.getshop.today)

**Important Details**
• 18+ event. ID may be required at the bar.
• Photography and filming may take place for promotional use by [Cine Eye (AudioVisual Production Studio in London).](www.cineeye.co.uk)
