c985c4dc-7f0b-4eb0-a5be-ed8787918aab,,Career Accelerator,Your degree got you this far. Now it’s time to turn your potential into professional momentum.,"Your degree got you this far. Now it’s time to turn your potential into professional momentum.
Breaking into the job market can be difficult. You may have the qualifications, but still find yourself wondering:

• Why isn’t my CV getting results?
• How do I stand out without years of experience?
• How do I build confidence when networking?
• What are employers actually looking for?
• And how do I prove what I can do before someone gives me the opportunity?

CAP Summit is designed to help you start answering those questions.
Join us for an interactive, career-focused event built for graduates, early-career professionals, and ambitious job seekers who want practical guidance, stronger professional confidence, and a clearer route into the career they want.

What to expect

This isn’t an event where you sit and listen.
You’ll take part in practical activities designed around situations you’re likely to face in the real world — from introducing yourself confidently and joining conversations to understanding how to position yourself more effectively in today’s job market.
You’ll explore:
• Networking & Confidence — Learn how to approach people, join conversations naturally and make a stronger first impression.
• Career Positioning — Understand how your CV, LinkedIn presence and professional identity influence how employers see you.
• The Experience Problem — Discover ways to move beyond “I need experience to get experience” and start building evidence of what you can actually do.
• What Employers Look For — Explore the professional behaviours and competencies that help people get hired and succeed once they enter the workplace.
• Practical Career Direction — Leave with a clearer understanding of the areas you need to strengthen and the next steps you can take.

Discover the Career Accelerator Programme

You’ll also be introduced to CAP — the Career Accelerator Programme, a structured 12-week programme designed for people who are serious about building a career, not simply finding their next job.
CAP combines professional development with experience inside a live business. Participants work on real projects, receive weekly one-to-one feedback and develop across seven professional competencies.
The goal is simple: give you the skills, experience and evidence to compete for the career you actually want.

Who should attend?

CAP Summit is particularly relevant if you’re a:
🎓 Graduate trying to break into the professional job market
💼 Job seeker struggling to stand out
🚀 Early-career professional looking to accelerate your development
📈 Ambitious individual who wants practical experience rather than another certificate
If you’ve worked hard to get where you are but still feel stuck, overlooked or unsure what your next move should be, this event is for you.

Come ready to participate.

Meet people. Practice. Ask questions. Challenge yourself.
And leave with a clearer idea of what it takes to move from qualified on paper to credible in the workplace.
Places are limited; reserve your place at CAP Summit today.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792698837/orbit/event-covers/sources/qlrqm1bid4f1t26ib2sw.jpg,2026-11-13 12:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,168d49d1-9456-4c1f-a396-5bc9f2050d9d,"{carrer,growth,careers}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/speed-network-now/events/316511498/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:53:34.160664+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/speed-network-now/events/316511498/,event_316511498@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:21:53.769+00,,2026-10-22 19:53:34.160664+00,2026-10-28 03:22:27.129706+00,,,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02:career accelerator:online,,f,
37a964b0-0a2d-4d16-976c-55e0055ee297,,Artist's Way Free Course,The Artist’s Way – weekly creative circle,"**The Artist’s Way – weekly creative circle**
Each Tuesday we work through one chapter of Julia Cameron’s *The Artist’s Way* together.

**Before each session:**

• Read (or listen to) that week’s chapter
• Keep up your morning pages
• Take your artist date

**Please bring:**
Your book, a notebook and a pen.

**How the session runs:**

• **Check-in:** how your morning pages and artist date went, and anything significant from your week
• **Tasks:** we work through the chapter’s tasks together as quiet writing exercises
• **Reflection:** a short share at the end, only if you’d like to

**A safe space**
This is a peer-led circle, not a class or therapy group. We’re all in it together, including me.
What’s shared here stays here. You don't have to share, and nobody will be fixed or critiqued. Different views are welcome, shared with kindness.

Cameras on, at least during check-in and sharing - seeing each other helps us all feel safe and connected. You can turn them off during quiet writing time. If you need yours off at some point, just let us know at the start of the session.
Sessions are not recorded.

This work can sometimes bring things up. If it does, please be gentle with yourself and reach out to someone you trust, or to a professional if you need more support.

**Schedule**

• 27 Oct – Week 2: Recovering a Sense of Identity
• 3 Nov – Week 3: Power
• 10 Nov – Week 4: Integrity
• 17 Nov – Week 5: Possibility
• 24 Nov – Week 6: Abundance
• 1 Dec – Week 7: Connection
• 8 Dec – Week 8: Strength
• 15 Dec – Week 9: Compassion
• 22 Dec – Week 10: Self-Protection
• 29 Dec – Week 11: Autonomy
• 5 Jan – Week 12: Faith

Dates around Christmas may change; I’ll confirm nearer the time.
However your week went - seven days of pages or none - you are welcome to join. Just come as you are.

**WhatsApp group**
We also have a WhatsApp group for support between sessions - sharing pages done, artist date ideas and little breakthroughs. Please see under **Event Chat** to join. Please note that members can see each other’s phone numbers.

