dd271b9a-1044-47c7-b108-d3bca701c1ca,,❄️ Lapland Adventure with GoXplorers 🌍🤝✈️,❄️ Lapland Adventure with GoXplorers 🌍,"❄️ **Lapland Adventure with GoXplorers** 🌍
Ready to experience the magic of Lapland, chase the Northern Lights, explore frozen waterfalls and create unforgettable memories in the Arctic wilderness?

**📍 Destination**
Rovaniemi, Finnish Lapland

**💰 Price**
£220 Accommodation + £20 GoXplorers Trip Coordination Fee

Join GoXplorers for an unforgettable four-day Arctic adventure in the heart of Finnish Lapland. From hunting the Northern Lights beneath star-filled skies to hiking through frozen canyons and visiting Santa Claus Village, this trip combines breathtaking scenery, unique experiences and great company.
Whether you're travelling solo or with friends, this trip is designed to bring together adventurous people who love exploring new places in a fun, welcoming environment.

✨ **Trip Highlights**

• Witness the magical Northern Lights
• Explore the spectacular Korouoma Frozen Waterfalls
• Visit the world-famous Santa Claus Village
• Optional Husky, Snowmobile and Wildlife experiences
• Meet fellow travellers and make new friends
• Organised group activities with free time to explore
• Stress-free trip coordination by GoXplorers

✨ **What's Included**
✅ 3 nights shared accommodation
✅ Trip coordination and organisation by GoXplorers
✅ Planned group itinerary and activities
✅ Support before and during the trip

**❌ Not Included**
✈️ Flights
🚖 Local transport unless included within booked activities
🎟️ Optional activity costs
🍽️ Food and drinks unless stated otherwise
💳 Personal expenses
⚠️ Participants are responsible for arranging their own travel insurance.

**📅 Itinerary**
**Thursday 5 November** – Welcome to Lapland & Northern Lights Experience
We'll arrive in Rovaniemi, settle into our accommodation and spend the day exploring the capital of Finnish Lapland.
**Highlights include:**
• Exploring Rovaniemi town centre
• Discovering local cafés, shops and Arctic culture
• Meeting the group and enjoying our first evening together
• Optional Northern Lights Hunters Experience (£57 per person)

🌌 **Northern Lights Hunters – £57 per person**
**Includes:**
✅ Return transportation from our accommodation
✅ Visit to two lakes with stunning views
✅ Northern Lights hunting experience
✅ Outdoor campfire BBQ
✅ Finnish sausages and traditional Finnish rice cake
✅ Hot berry drink made from locally picked berries
✅ Sweets and marshmallows by the campfire

**Friday 6 November** – Korouoma Canyon Frozen Waterfalls
One of the highlights of the trip and a truly unforgettable Arctic experience.

**❄️ Korouoma Canyon Frozen Waterfalls – £67 per person**
**Includes:**
✅ Pick-up and drop-off from our Rovaniemi accommodation
✅ Transfers in brand-new 2025 Ford Tourneo 4×4 vans
✅ Certified professional guide (first-aid trained)
✅ Thermal overalls
✅ Guided 4-6 km hike through Korouoma Canyon
✅ Hot drinks and barbecue
✅ Private group experience
**Expect:**
• Frozen waterfalls and dramatic canyon scenery
• Snow-covered forests
• Incredible photo opportunities
• Arctic wilderness landscapes
• Time to enjoy the peaceful beauty of Lapland

**Saturday 7 November** – Santa Claus Village
A magical day exploring one of Lapland's most famous attractions.
**Highlights include:**
🎅 Visit Santa Claus Village
🎅 Cross the Arctic Circle
🎅 Explore local shops and cafés
🎅 Visit Christmas-themed attractions
🎅 Send postcards from Santa's official post office
🎅 Free time to explore at your own pace

**Sunday 8 November** – Optional Arctic Adventure & Departure
Before heading home, participants can choose one of several optional experiences organised through local tour operators.
🐕 Short Husky Ride – £83 per person
🏍️ Arctic Snowmobiling Ride – £83 per person
🦌 Ranua Wildlife Park Tour – £50 per person

**Please note that all activities are completely optional and are booked through local tour operators.**

🏠 **Accommodation Information**
Participants will be staying in shared accommodation.
Where possible, rooms will be allocated as:
• Female-only shared rooms
• Male-only shared rooms
However, depending on final group numbers and accommodation availability, this cannot be guaranteed.
By booking this trip, participants acknowledge they may be sharing a room with other members of the group.

**⚠️ Important Information**
This adventure involves winter conditions, outdoor activities and walking on snow and uneven terrain. Participants should dress appropriately for Arctic weather and be comfortable spending time outdoors in cold temperatures.
Plans may be adjusted due to weather conditions, local circumstances or operational requirements. Any changes will always be made with the best interests and safety of the group in mind.
GoXplorers acts as a trip coordinator and community organiser. All participants remain responsible for ensuring they meet airline, travel and entry requirements, carry adequate travel insurance, and assess their own suitability to participate in planned activities.

