08e3b488-fd2f-4b30-a938-f5be3d882145,,You Can See Everything (2026),"It's been ages since there was a documentary sensation like You Can See Everything, which has just been expanded from the ultra-expensive screenings at the posh chain cinemas to the rank and file…","It's been ages since there was a documentary sensation like You Can See Everything, which has just been expanded from the ultra-expensive screenings at the posh chain cinemas to the rank and file indies. That includes the massive screen 1 at the Genesis, the biggest cinema screen in East London.

Nathan Fielder has become one of the most original and hilarious filmmakers of our time, beginning with fix-your-business TV series Nathan For You (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h0TRpGP8yH4) and expanding into comedy drama with Emma Stone and Benny Safdie in The Curse (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=98XP3t5pGx8) and making some of the most extraordinary TV of the past decade with The Rehearsal (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6CaHP5P4wUc).

This three-hour doc, a collaboration with 'Primetime director Lance Oppenheimer, sees Fielder staying with disgraced medtech founder Elizabeth 'Theranos' Holmes and her husband before she goes to jail. Early reports suggest it is amazing and the fact people seem desperate not to spoil it makes me very excited. It isn't often we go to a brand new movie in this group!

Trailer: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HvW_N5p1q44

