06438bea-1c26-48e8-b614-282ee5a9d65c,,What organisation designers and service designers can learn from each other,"Beautifully designed, broken when implemented?","**Beautifully designed, broken when implemented?**

Every service carries the fingerprint of the organisation behind it. How teams are set up, who decides, and who owns what all show up in the customer's experience. That's why a service can only work as well as the organisation that delivers it.
As service designers, we already look behind the scenes: blueprints show the backstage, the people and processes that make a service work. Organisation design takes us one layer deeper, into roles, decision rights, and ownership.

These are often the questions that decide whether a new service holds up in daily work.

Zsófia Takács has worked on both sides. She trained as an organisation designer (Native in Change, CODP) and as a service designer (MOME). With our host Kornél Csajtai, she'll share real cases, explore:

• How to read a service as a fingerprint of the organisation
• How to bring this view into your projects, by growing your own org design skills or by inviting an org designer onto the team

**For service designers and the leaders who commission their work.**

