f6f348f1-b514-4acc-b20b-feb6e456c757,,City Photowalk,"We had a great turnout last time and would love to keep the momentum. Given that the weather is getting a bit iffy, I’m going to come up with a Plan A for the actual walk and Plan B if it literally…","We had a great turnout last time and would love to keep the momentum. Given that the weather is getting a bit iffy, I’m going to come up with a Plan A for the actual walk and Plan B if it literally rains on our photography parade.
See you guys soon!

**Photowalk Code of Conduct**

Our club is a welcoming, inclusive and judgment-free space for photographers of every background and experience level.

1. Everyone is equal. Treat every member with the same respect, regardless of age, race, ethnicity, nationality, religion, gender, sexuality, disability, appearance, experience or equipment.
2. Be kind. Bullying, harassment, discrimination, intimidation, exclusion or deliberately making someone uncomfortable will not be tolerated.
3. No shaming. Never shame anyone for their photographs, ability, camera, phone, editing style, knowledge or level of experience.
4. Do not make negative comments about ability. Everyone is here to enjoy photography and develop at their own pace. Constructive feedback should only be given when someone asks for it, and it must be respectful and helpful.
5. Respect different styles. Photography is subjective. You do not have to like someone’s work, but you must respect their creative choices.
6. Help, don’t compete. Celebrate other people’s progress, share knowledge generously and make newer members feel welcome. This club is a community, not a competition.
7. Respect personal boundaries. Ask before photographing another member or sharing an identifiable photograph of them. If someone asks not to be photographed, respect that immediately.
8. Include everyone. Do not form cliques, deliberately leave people behind during walks or make anyone feel that they do not belong.
9. Take responsibility for your impact. Jokes and comments should not come at somebody else’s expense. If someone tells you that your behaviour made them uncomfortable, listen and respond respectfully.
10. Speak to an organiser if something happens. Concerns will be taken seriously and handled as fairly and discreetly as possible. Serious or repeated breaches may result in removal from the club.

The basic rule: be kind, be inclusive and never make another person feel small.",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/5/c/highres_535502652.jpeg,2027-02-06 14:00:00+00,2027-02-06 16:00:00+00,Europe/London,in_person,Liverpool Street,Liverpool Street,London,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,creative,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/photowalk-club/events/316040969/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/photowalk-club/events/316040969/,event_316040969@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,meetup:photowalk-club:city photowalk,Every 1st Saturday of the month,f,GB
d1694a59-2d0b-4295-a376-8a6b7131af5b,,How to Follow Up with 10 High-Value Contacts in Under 15 Minutes (Live Workshop),"Please only sign up if you really intend to come. To keep this session interactive and impactful, please arrive on time, camera on and willing to participate.","**Please only sign up if you really intend to come. To keep this session interactive and impactful, please arrive on time, camera on and willing to participate.**

**How to Follow Up with 10 High-Value Contacts in Under 15 Minutes (Live Workshop)**

In this hands-on, 60 minute live workshop, we’re breaking down a practical system to help you streamline your follow-ups, maintain authentic touchpoints, and stay connected with the people who matter most in your career.

**💡 What We’ll Cover & Build Together:**

The 15-Minute Follow-Up Framework: How to categorize and prioritize your key contacts so you never wonder ""Who should I message today?""

• Low-Friction Outreach Scripts: Simple, authentic message templates for warm check-ins, congratulating contacts, or reconnecting after months (or years) of silence.
• Smart Touchpoint Systems: Practical workflows and smart tools to automate reminders and organize your outreach effortlessly.
• Live Implementation (10 Mins): Put the system into practice right during the workshop and send 2–3 low-friction check-ins live on the call!

**🎯 Who Should Attend:**

• Professionals, consultants, and project leaders looking to maintain strong industry visibility.
• Entrepreneurs and specialists who rely on warm relationships for opportunities and advice.
• Anyone who wants a structured, high-efficiency approach to professional networking.

**📋 Prerequisites & What to Bring:**
To get the most value out of this live session, please bring:

• A list of 3–5 contacts you’ve been meaning to catch up with or reconnect with.
• Your preferred messaging tool (LinkedIn, Email, WhatsApp, etc.).
• An open mind to test a fast, low-friction outreach habit!

**📍 Format:**

• Format: Interactive Live Workshop + Quick Implementation + Q&A
• Duration: 60 minutes
• Capacity: Limited to 10 spots to ensure an interactive, high-value experience for everyone.

**Voluntary donation to cover meetup and prepration costs**

