378eb105-e98d-40a2-af2a-636cf4b1043b,,Founders Connect — Show What You're Building,🤓TLDR,"**🤓TLDR**

• A small online session where founders show what they're building, explain what they're trying to solve and get honest, constructive feedback from other founders.

🚀 **BUILDING SOMETHING? SHOW US.**

• Founders Connect is a small, interactive session for founders and entrepreneurs to share what they're building and get feedback from other people building things too.
• No polished pitch deck needed. No investors. No competition. Just useful peer feedback.

👋 **HOW IT WORKS**

• Each founder gets a few minutes to introduce themselves and show us what they're building. You can share your screen and demo a website, app, prototype, landing page, product or even something that's still at idea stage.
• Then the group gets a few minutes to ask questions and give constructive feedback.

**🎟️ FIRST COME, FIRST SERVED**

• Spaces are limited to keep the session small, interactive and ensure everyone gets a chance to share.
• Places will be allocated on a first-come, first-served basis when joining opens, not by Meetup RSVP order.
• Please join promptly to secure your spot. If you can no longer attend, kindly update your RSVP so others know a space may be available.

💡 **GET FEEDBACK ON THINGS LIKE**
• Is the idea clear?
• Would you use or buy it?
• What is confusing?
• What would you improve?
• Who do you think the customer is?
• How would you reach them?
• What would you test next?

🤝 **WHO SHOULD JOIN**

• Anyone actively building a startup, business, product or side project is welcome — from early ideas and prototypes to established businesses.
• You don't need funding, employees or a polished product.

**Show what you're building. Get fresh eyes on it. Help another founder do the same. And maybe you can find someone to collaborate.**",https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/6/c/4/highres_536142692.jpeg,2026-10-26 17:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,4de84854-e351-4122-ab9e-a6ea93b86ee5,"{carrer,entrepreneurship,growth}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/founders-connect-plus/events/317022976/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-21 22:14:19.927193+00,source:93b183a9-4cbd-478c-a97e-334e2b0e1a02,https://www.meetup.com/founders-connect-plus/events/317022976/,event_317022976@meetup.com,,2026-10-26 03:21:52.922+00,,2026-10-21 22:14:19.927193+00,2026-10-26 03:22:29.106722+00,,,,,f,
2c137be6-05b6-4d41-bb24-b1d77599f5c9,,English Language Silent Book Club Paris (online),What is a Silent Book Club?,"**What is a Silent Book Club?**
Silent Book Club is happy hour for introverts. Bring a book and maybe bring a friend. Then settle in for an hour of quiet reading with fellow book lovers. There's no assigned reading or discussion guides - that's the ""silent"" part of our book club - but we do like to share book recommendations and meet like-minded readers.

While some silent reading parties have a strict No Talking! rule, no one will be shushed or shamed at Silent Book Club. All readers are welcome including eReaders and Audible book listeners.

For more info check out the Silent Book Club web site (https://silentbook.club).

**Why English-language?**
I wanted to have two different groups for two different discussions. This is the English-language group where we discuss in English and read books in English. I also manage a French-language Silent Book Club.

Please note that we are using the broad spectrum of *English language* and *anglophone* would perhaps be a better definition. British, American, Canadian, Australian, … you get the idea ... all variants and bastardisations of the English language are warmly accepted with no judgement.

**Why *online-only?***
I wanted to start with the easiest and quickest way possible to see how all of this works and what the interest may be. If everything evolves as planned, I'm sure we'll eventually find ourselves with a mixture of online club meetings and in person meetings at a café or bar. They're not that difficult to find here in Paris...

**How does it work?**
Once every two weeks we meet *online*:

• 19:00 - 19:30 Introductions and general discussion of who's reading what
• 19:30 - 20:30 Quiet reading hour
• 20:30 - 21:00... Optional socialising and general discussion ... or keep reading.

I will currently be using Zoom for our online meetings. But I am open to other possibilities...
Camera off and/or microphone off accepted.

