f7c36f0b-a652-448a-af71-369055f68df7,,English Language Silent Book Club Paris (online),What is a Silent Book Club?,"**What is a Silent Book Club?**
Silent Book Club is happy hour for introverts. Bring a book and maybe bring a friend. Then settle in for an hour of quiet reading with fellow book lovers. There's no assigned reading or discussion guides - that's the ""silent"" part of our book club - but we do like to share book recommendations and meet like-minded readers.

While some silent reading parties have a strict No Talking! rule, no one will be shushed or shamed at Silent Book Club. All readers are welcome including eReaders and Audible book listeners.

For more info check out the Silent Book Club web site (https://silentbook.club).

**Why English-language?**
I wanted to have two different groups for two different discussions. This is the English-language group where we discuss in English and read books in English. I also manage a French-language Silent Book Club.

Please note that we are using the broad spectrum of *English language* and *anglophone* would perhaps be a better definition. British, American, Canadian, Australian, … you get the idea ... all variants and bastardisations of the English language are warmly accepted with no judgement.

**Why *online-only?***
I wanted to start with the easiest and quickest way possible to see how all of this works and what the interest may be. If everything evolves as planned, I'm sure we'll eventually find ourselves with a mixture of online club meetings and in person meetings at a café or bar. They're not that difficult to find here in Paris...

**How does it work?**
Once every two weeks we meet *online*:

• 19:00 - 19:30 Introductions and general discussion of who's reading what
• 19:30 - 20:30 Quiet reading hour
• 20:30 - 21:00... Optional socialising and general discussion ... or keep reading.

I will currently be using Zoom for our online meetings. But I am open to other possibilities...
Camera off and/or microphone off accepted.

If you have any questions please send an email to [englishsilentbookclubparis@gmail.com](mailto:englishsilentbookclubparis@gmail.com)",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1792698414/orbit/event-covers/sources/phyfxbvlvbbhm2skbvmp.jpg,2026-11-09 18:00:00+00,2026-11-09 20:00:00+00,Europe/Paris,online,Online event,,,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,books,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/english-language-silent-book-club-paris/events/314920940/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,,,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/english-language-silent-book-club-paris/events/314920940/,event_314920940@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-22 19:46:36.725985+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.193092+00,,,meetup:english-language-silent-book-club-paris:english language silent book club paris online,Every 2 weeks on Monday,f,
2e6a819d-e40f-41fa-a33f-cdbc13d2536c,,☕ Girls’ Coffee & Support Club,☕ Girls’ Coffee & Support Club,"☕ Girls’ Coffee & Support Club

Real Talk • Real Connections • Supporting Each Other

📅 When: Last Sunday of every month 🕐 Time: 1pm–4pm
📍 Where: White City House,
, next to the BBC Centre
2, Television Centre, 101 Wood Ln, London W12 7FR

Join us on the last Sunday of every month, from 1pm to 4pm, at a cosy café in Soho House, White City, next to the BBC Centre.

Life in London can be busy, balancing work, responsibilities, relationships and personal goals. Sometimes, we just need a space to slow down, enjoy a coffee and have meaningful conversations with like-minded women.

Our monthly girls’ club is all about real conversations, genuine connections and supporting one another through life’s journey. Whether you want to talk about work, share experiences, discuss life’s challenges, exchange ideas or simply meet new friends, you’re welcome here.

💕 No pressure, no judgement — just good coffee, honest conversations and women supporting women.

