037fdc82-c0fc-4107-8836-59d6b32707b6,,Beyond Time Management: A More Natural Way to Organise Creative Work,"For creatives, writers, thinkers, and makers, a project management method that honours creativity rather than stifles it.","**For creatives, writers, thinkers, and makers, a project management method that honours creativity rather than stifles it.**

Most productivity systems assume that creativity works like a factory line: consistent output, linear progress, and endless motivation. And if you’ve ever felt subtly misaligned with those systems, this workshop is for you.

In this 90-minute workshop, we’ll explore a more natural approach to time and energy management that works with your natural rhythms rather than against them.

**This workshop is for creative thinkers of all sorts, and particularly:**

• People juggling multiple creative or personal projects
• Those returning to creative work after burnout or over-structuring
• Anyone who wants structure without losing creative spaciousness

**What We’ll Explore**
This workshop introduces an intuitive framework for organising creative work according to energy, attention, and creative stages.

Together, we’ll look at:

• Why 'time management' often fails creatives
• How energy moves in cycles rather than straight lines
• How projects naturally unfold through distinct creative phases
• How to manage multiple projects without fragmentation or burnout

You’ll also gain language for understanding why certain phases of creative work feel easy, difficult, or mysteriously blocked without turning that insight into self-criticism.

**What to bring:**

