7f7d340f-9bf8-4609-83e4-540e6b36afc0,,The Master and Margarita (on a TUESDAY),"Hi! Join us on a Tuesday to discuss The Master and Margarita (1928-40) by Mikhail Bulgakov, ""a masterpiece of dark humour, fantasy, Soviet satire, and the enduring power of art [⚠️ A.I.]"".","Hi! Join us ***on a Tuesday*** to discuss **The Master and Margarita** (1928-40) by Mikhail Bulgakov, ""a masterpiece of dark humour, fantasy, Soviet satire, and the enduring power of art [⚠️ A.I.]"".

There are multiple English translations (https://welovetranslations.com/2022/10/31/whats-the-best-translation-of-the-master-and-margarita/), but I'll probably be reading the one by Pevear & Volokhonsky (1997) which seems to be available here:

• Pevear & Volokhonsky (1997) (https://files.libcom.org/files/eben002_mastermargarita_pevear.pdf)

Other translations:

• Michael Glenny (1967) (https://www.masterandmargarita.eu/estore/pdf/eben001_mastermargarita_glenny.pdf)

• Mirra Ginsburg (1967) (https://archive.org/details/mastermargarita00bulg_1)

Please read the story before attending the meeting, and be ready to join in with the conversation.

We'll be using Google Meet. If you've booked a place you'll see the meeting link under the Online Event heading on the webpage for the meetup in due course.

If you have problems logging in on the day of the meeting, please leave a message in the Comments section on Meetup. I usually check to see if anyone is having issues.

I hope we'll all enjoy the book and the discussion!

Kind regards,

