3a1e606d-e2fb-4de0-a8b0-91e22092293e,,Thomas Hardy’s The Mayor of Casterbridge (1886) I: chapter 1,"Thomas Hardy (1840-1928) was undoubtedly the greatest English novelist of the final quarter of the nineteenth century. He wrote fourteen novels, a handful of them masterpieces, including The Life…","**Thomas Hardy** (1840-1928) was undoubtedly the greatest English novelist of the final quarter of the nineteenth century. He wrote fourteen novels, a handful of them masterpieces, including ***The Life and Death of The Mayor of Casterbridge: A Story of a Man of Character*** (1886). Set in a fictionalized version of south-west and south-central England he called Wessex, Hardy’s novels offer an often bleak vision of rural and market-town life. At this meeting we will be looking at the early part of the novel and reading the very famous first chapter in which the future mayor, Michael Henchard, sells his wife and child at a country fair.
The text of the novel can be found here: https://www.gutenberg.org/files/143/143-h/143-h.htm
All are welcome. Feel free to take part by joining in discussion or simply by listening to the proceedings.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1793071197/orbit/event-covers/sources/erx6jftnaoooheodciey.jpg,2026-11-24 19:00:00+00,,Europe/Dublin,online,Online event,,,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,books,socialising}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/reading-19th-century-literature/events/317129179/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,0.00,0.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-27 03:19:45.380416+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/reading-19th-century-literature/events/317129179/,event_317129179@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-27 03:19:45.380416+00,2026-10-28 03:19:47.776315+00,,,,,f,
