Book Blurb follows:
A fellow named Richard Bachman wrote Blaze in 1973 on an Olivetti typewriter, then turned the machine over to Stephen King, who used it to write Carrie. Bachman died in 1985 (""cancer of the pseudonym""), but in late 2006 King found the original typescript of Blaze among his papers at the University of Maine's Fogler Library (""How did this get here?!""), and decided that with a little revision it ought to be published.
Blaze is the story of Clayton Blaisdell, Jr. --of the crimes committed against him and the crimes he commits, including his last, the kidnapping of a baby heir worth millions. Blaze has been a slow thinker since childhood, when his father threw him down the stairs--and then threw him down again. After escaping an abusive institution for boys when he was a teenager, Blaze hooks up with George, a seasoned criminal who thinks he has all the answers. But then George is killed, and Blaze, though haunted by his partner, is on his own.",https://res.cloudinary.com/deor01if5/image/upload/v1793157605/orbit/event-covers/sources/alndptvymvm5xlb95fzs.jpg,2026-11-26 19:00:00+00,,Europe/London,online,Online event,,,bbf01bc7-85fe-4d0e-8f0c-8fd50e9ffd7e,"{social,socialising,books,food}",,external,https://www.meetup.com/the-constant-readers-book-club/events/316746660/,Register on Meetup,f,,t,,0.00,0.00,GBP,published,,f,f,2026-10-28 03:19:46.398197+00,source:c243439e-e165-41fe-9fdf-b8e7ca9d670a,https://www.meetup.com/the-constant-readers-book-club/events/316746660/,event_316746660@meetup.com,,2026-10-28 03:19:10.809+00,,2026-10-28 03:19:46.398197+00,2026-10-28 03:20:05.679445+00,,,,,f,
cb0a9e77-c407-42f2-8808-19f880e0131c,,"Meet the people who create, publish, support and play video games.","Meet the people who create, publish, support and play video games.","**Meet the people who create, publish, support and play video games.**
Groop is a newly established startup in stealth mode at Tech Launchpads. We believe there is room for a stronger sense of community among game developers and gamers in London, so we are bringing together people from across the video games industry for an evening of conversations, connections and collaboration.
Whether you are building your first game, running a studio, looking for collaborators or simply passionate about gaming, come along and meet the community.
**Who is it for?**

• Independent developers, programmers and game designers
• Studio founders and owners
• Artists, animators, writers and audio specialists
• Publishers, distributors and gaming investors
• QA testers, localisation specialists and service providers
• Streamers, content creators, esports professionals and gamers
• Students and anyone looking to enter the games industry

**What to expect**
A relaxed networking event where you can share what you are working on, exchange ideas, discuss industry challenges and explore potential collaborations. There will also be a short introduction to Groop and the community we are building.
Come with an idea, a project to talk about or simply a curiosity about games. You do not need a finished game or an established business to join.
