82cef4f9-5c74-42b1-8a01-c10054af80d1,,The 5 Questions Every Founder Must Ask to Work a Four-day Week,https://us06web.zoom.us/meeting/register/b4Y3t-zkQnOP7WHDrIBjpw,"https://us06web.zoom.us/meeting/register/b4Y3t-zkQnOP7WHDrIBjpw

What happens in your business on a day when you’re not available?
If decisions stall, problems pile up, and your team waits for you, this session is for you.

A four-day week isn't about squeezing five days of work into four. It's about building a business that doesn't need you for the fifth day.

In this 45-minute live session, you'll explore five questions that reveal where your business may still depend on you too much, and why the solution might not be what you think.

Through real stories from founders I've advised, you'll discover a different way to look at the challenges keeping you involved in too much. You'll leave with one specific action to take on the following Monday.

No productivity hacks and no delegation tricks, but an approach to deal with the root cause of what keeps you the bottleneck so you can free up time.

Bring: a pen, paper and one real situation from your business for this workshop

