61f24d11-82dc-4340-848b-40c89604f143,,How to Build an AI Employee That Starts Today,"When you are the whole team, every lead you don't qualify and every customer email you answer at 11pm comes out of the hours you should spend building. You can't hire yet. An AI agent can take one…","When you are the whole team, every lead you don't qualify and every customer email you answer at 11pm comes out of the hours you should spend building. You can't hire yet. **An AI agent can take one of those jobs now.** In this live session, Seth Ward, Founder & CEO of 4142, builds an AI agent from start to finish: connected to a real model, doing a single real job like qualifying a lead or drafting a follow-up, and deployed where it actually runs. No slides, and questions are open throughout. **Register now and leave with a clear plan for your first AI hire. (https://fi.co/e/407649/meetup)**

**❯ What You'll Learn:**

• How to pick the one job in your company an AI agent should take on first;
• How to turn that job into instructions an agent can actually follow;
• How to connect the agent to a real AI model and give it the information it needs;
• How to deploy it somewhere it runs on its own, beyond a demo;
• How to repeat the same build for sales, support and follow-ups as your company grows.

**❯ Featured Speaker:**

• **Seth Ward (https://www.linkedin.com/in/sethward/) - Founder & CEO @ 4142 (https://4142.ltd/)**, an AI foundry behind Squidgy, Handled, YEAA and FanatIQ. Through **Squidgy (https://squidgy.ai/)**, his team lets entrepreneurs and small businesses describe a task in plain English and turn it into an AI agent with no code. In 1995 he co-founded i, one of the first web marketing agencies, and went on to work with Vodafone, AOL and News International before serving as CEO of Pynk. Based in London, he runs live AI agent build sessions for founders, including at Nomad Cruise and Bansko Nomad Fest.

**❯ Who Should Attend:**

• Aspiring founders who want to see what an AI agent can do inside a real business;
• Solo founders handling sales, support and admin on their own;
• Professionals with deep industry expertise planning the move from employee to entrepreneur;
• Anyone curious about AI who wants to build with it, not just read about it.

